    "homepage_text": "Kimin Lee\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nKimin Lee\nContact:\nkiminlee@kaist.ac.kr\n(school)\nkimin@config.inc\n(company)\nKimin Lee\nI am an Assistant Professor at the Graduate School of AI at KAIST and Co-founder of\nConfig\n.\nMy research goal is to develop\nsafe and capable decision-making agents\n. Recently, I have focused on the following topics:\nVision-Language Action Models\n[C51, C69, C70]\nR\neinforcement learning from human feedback [P6, C22, C29, C42, C61]\nAI safety evaluation and benchmark [C57, C59, C64, C65]\nHuman-centric AI [C66]\nPreviously, I was a Research Scientist at Google Research. I completed my postdoctoral training at UC Berkeley\nand my PhD at KAIST\n.\nPublications (C: conference / J: journal / P: preprint / *: equal contribution / ^: equal advising)\n202\n6\n[C71] Improving Motion in Image-to-Video Models via Adaptive Low-Pass Guidance\n[\npdf\n][\nwebsite\n]\nJune Suk Choi, Kyungmin Lee, Sihyun Yu, Yisol Choi, Jinwoo Shin,\nKimin Lee\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n2026\n[C70] Learning Multi-View Spatial Reasoning from Cross-View Relations\nSuchae Jeong*, Jaehwi Song*, Haeone Lee, Hanna Kim, Jian Kim, Dongjun Lee, Dong Kyu Shin, Changyeon Kim, Dongyoon Hahm, Woogyeol Jin, Juheon Choi,\nKimin Lee\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n202\n6\n[C6\n9\n]\nQuality over Quantity: Demonstration Curation via Influence Functions for Data-Centric Robot Learning\nHaeone\nLee, Taywon Min, Junsu Kim, Sinjae Kang, Fangchen Liu, Lerrel Pinto,\nKimin Lee\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)\n2026\n[\nC68\n] Learning to generate unit test via adversarial reinforcement learning [\npdf\n]\nDongjun Lee, Changho Hwang,\nKimin Lee\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n202\n6\n[\nC67\n] DEAS: DEtached value learning with Action Sequence for Scalable Offline RL [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nChangyeon Kim, Haeone Lee, Younggyo Seo,\nKimin Lee\n^, Yuke Zhu^\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2026\n[C6\n6\n]\nState Your Intention to Steer Your Attention: An AI Assistant for Intentional Digital Living [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nJuheon Choi, Juyoung Lee, Jian Kim, Chanyoung Kim, Taewon Min, W Bradley Knox^, Min Kyung Lee^,\nKimin Lee\n^\nACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI)\n2026\n[C6\n5\n]\nUnintended Misalignment from Agentic Fine-Tuning: Risks and Mitigation\n[\npdf\n]\nDongyoon Hahm*, Taywon Min*, Woogyeol Jin*\n,\nKimin Lee\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\nAI Alignment Track 2026\n[\nC64\n] MobileSafetyBench: Evaluating Safety of Autonomous Agents in Mobile Device Control [\npdf\n][\ncode\n][\nsite\n]\nJuyong Lee*, Dongyoon Hahm*, June Suk Choi*, W. Bradley Knox,\nKimin Lee\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\nAI Alignment Track 202\n6\n[P13] Adversarial Iterative Unit Test Generation with Large Language Models [\npdf\n]\nDongjun Lee, Juyong Lee, Changho Hwang,\nKimin Lee\nICLR workshop 2026\n202\n5\n[C63] Improbable Bigrams Expose Vulnerabilities of Incomplete Tokens in Byte-Level Tokenizers\n[\npdf\n]\nEugene Jang,\nKimin Lee\n, Jin-Woo Chung, Keuntae Park, Seungwon Shin\nConference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)\n202\n5\n(main)\n[\nC62\n] Benchmarking Mobile Device Control Agents across Diverse Configurations [\npdf\n][\nsite\n][\ncode\n]\nJuyong Lee, Taywon Min, Minyong An, Dongyoon Hahm, Haeone Lee, Changyeon Kim,\nKimin Lee\nConference on Lifelong Learning Agents (CoLLAs)\n2025\n[C6\n1\n] Understanding Impact of Human Feedback via Influence Functions [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nTaywon Min, Haeone Lee, Yongchan Kwon,\nKimin Lee\nAnnual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)\n2025 (main)\n[C60] What Really Matters in Many-Shot Attacks? An Empirical Study of Long-Context Vulnerabilities in LLMs [\npdf\n]\nSangyeop Kim, Yohan Lee, Yongwoo Song,\nKimin Lee\nAnnual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)\n2025 (main)\n[C59]\nEnhancing LLM Agent Safety via Causal Influence Prompting [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nDongyoon Hahm, Woogyeol Jin, June Suk Choi, Sungsoo Ahn\n,\nKimin Lee\nAnnual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)\n2025 (\nfindings\n)\n[C58] Silent Branding Attack: Trigger-free Data Poisoning Attack on Text-to-Image Diffusion Models [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nSangwon Jang, June Suk Choi, Jaehyeong Jo,\nKimin Lee\n^, Sung Ju Hwang^\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n2025\n[\nC57\n] When LLMs Go Online: The Emerging Threat of Web-Enabled LLMs [\npdf\n]\nHanna Kim, Minkyoo Song, Seung Ho Na, Seungwon Shin,\nKimin Lee\nUSENIX Security Symposium\n2025\n[C5\n6\n]\nLearning to Contextualize Web Pages for Enhanced Decision Making by LLM Agents [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nDongjun Lee, Juyong Lee, Kyuyoung Kim, Jihoon Tack, Jinwoo Shin, Yee Whye Teh,\nKimin Lee\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025\n[\nC55\n] Automated Filtering of Human Feedback Data for Aligning Text-to-Image Diffusion Models [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nYongjin Yang*, Sihyeon Kim*, Hojung Jung, Sangmin Bae, SangMook Kim, Se-Young Yun^,\nKimin Lee\n^\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025\n[C5\n4]\nDiffusionGuard: A Robust Defense Against Malicious Diffusion-based Image Editing [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nJune Suk Choi, Kyungmin Lee, Jongheon Jeong, Saining Xie, Jinwoo Shin,\nKimin Lee\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025\n[C5\n3\n] Subtask-Aware Visual Reward Learning from Segmented Demonstrations [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nChangyeon Kim, Minho Heo, Doohyun Lee, Honglak Lee, Jinwoo Shin, Joseph J Lim,\nKimin Lee\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025\n[\nC52\n]\nSpread Preference Annotation: Direct Preference Judgment for Efficient LLM Alignment\n[\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nDongyoung Kim,\nKimin Lee\n, Jinwoo Shin, Jaehyung Kim\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n2025 as\noral presentation (\n207/11672=1.77%)\n[C5\n1\n] Latent Action Pretraining from Videos [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nSeonghyeon Ye*, Joel Jang*, Byeongguk Jeon, Sejune Joo, Jianwei Yang, Baolin Peng, Ajay Mandlekar, Reuben Tan, Yu-Wei Chao, Bill Yuchen Lin, Lars Liden,\nKimin Lee\n^, Jianfeng Gao^, Luke Zettlemoyer^, Dieter Fox^, Minjoon Seo^\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n202\n5\n[C\n50\n]\nDiffExp: Efficient Exploration in Reward Fine-tuning for Text-to-Image Diffusion Models [\npdf\n]\nDaewon Chae*, June Suk Choi*, Jinkyu Kim^,\nKimin Lee\n^\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n202\n5\nas\noral presentation (\n547\n/\n12957\n=\n4\n.\n22\n%)\n[\nC49\n] SelfReplay: Adapting Self-Supervised Sensory Models via Adaptive Meta-Task Replay [\npdf\n]\nHyungjun Yoon, Jaehyun Kwak, Biniyam Aschalew Tolera, Gaole Dai, Mo Li, Taesik Gong,\nKimin Lee\n, Sung-Ju Lee\nACM Conference on Embedded Networked Sensor Systems (SenSys)\n2025\n[\nJ2\n] Prime the Search: Using Large Language Models for Guiding Geometric Task and Motion Planning by Warm-starting Tree Search [\npdf\n]\nDongryung Lee, Sejune Joo,\nKimin Lee\n, Beomjoon Kim\nInternational Journal of Robotics Research\n202\n5\n[P12] Adversarial Reinforcement Learning Framework for ESP Cheater Simulation [\npdf\n]\nInkyu Park, Jeong-Gwan Lee, Taehwan Kwon, Juheon Choi, Seungku Kim, Junsu Kim,\nKimin Lee\nArxiv preprint 2025\n[P11] Revisiting Multi-Agent Debate as Test-Time Scaling: A Systematic Study of Conditional Effectiveness [\npdf\n]\nYongjin Yang*, Euiin Yi*, Jongwoo Ko,\nKimin Lee\n^, Zhijing Jin^, Se-Young Yun^\nArxiv preprint 2025\n[P10] Automated Skill Discovery for Language Agents through Exploration and Iterative Feedback [\npdf\n]\nYongjin Yang*, Sinjae Kang*, Juyong Lee, Dongjun Lee, Se-Young Yun^,\nKimin Lee^\nArxiv preprint 2025\n[P\n9\n] A Definition of AGI [\npdf\n]\nDan Hendrycks, Dawn Song, Christian Szegedy, Honglak Lee, Yarin Gal, Erik Brynjolfsson, Sharon Li, Andy Zou, Lionel Levine, Bo Han, Jie Fu, Ziwei Liu, Jinwoo Shin,\nKimin Lee\n, Mantas Mazeika, Long Phan, George Ingebretsen, Adam Khoja, Cihang Xie, Olawale Salaudeen, Matthias Hein, Kevin Zhao, Alexander Pan, David Duvenaud, Bo Li, Steve Omohundro, Gabriel Alfour, Max Tegmark, Kevin McGrew, Gary Marcus, Eric Schmidt, Yoshua Bengio\nArxiv preprint 2025\n202\n4\n[\nC48\n] Identity Decoupling for Multi-Subject Personalization of Text-to-Image Models [\npdf\n][\nsite\n][\ncode\n]\nSangwon Jang*, Jaehyeong Jo*,\nKimin Lee\n^, Sung Ju Hwang^\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n202\n4\n[C4\n7\n] By My Eyes: Grounding Multimodal Large Language Models with Sensor Data via Visual Prompting [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nHyungjun Yoon, Biniyam Aschalew Tolera, Taesik Gong,\nKimin Lee\n, Sung-Ju Lee\nConference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)\n2024 (main)\n[C46] Margin Matching Preference Optimization: Enhanced Model Alignment with Granular Feedback [\npdf\n][\ncode\n]\nKyuyoung Kim*, Ah Jeong Seo*, Hao Liu, Jinwoo Shin,\nKimin Lee\nConference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)\n2024 (findings)\n[C45] Beyond Thumbs Up/Down: Untangling Challenges of Fine-Grained Feedback for Text-to-Image Generation [\npdf\n]\nKatherine Collins, Najoung Kim, Yonatan Bitton, Verena Rieser, Shayegan Omidshafiei, Yushi Hu, Sherol Chen, Senjuti Dutta, Minsuk Chang,\nKimin Lee\n, Youwei Liang, Georgie Evans, Sahil Singla, Gang Li, Adrian Weller, Junfeng He, Deepak Ramachandran, Krishnamurthy Dvijotham\nConference on AI, Ethics, and Society (AIES)\n2024\n[C44] Promptable Behaviors: Personalizing Multi-Objective Rewards from Human Preferences [\npdf\n][\nsite\n]\nMinyoung Hwang, Luca Weihs, Chanwoo Park,\nKimin Lee\n, Aniruddha Kembhavi, Kiana Ehsani\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n202\n4\n[C4\n3\n]\n