    "homepage_text": "Zhe Feng\nSkip to main content\nSearch\nZhe Feng\nPh.D student,\nHarvard University\nZhe Feng is a student from Zhiyuan College at Shanghai Jiao Tong University in China. He is fortunate to be advised by Xiaotie Deng. His main research interest is in Algorithmic Game Theory, Mechanism Design and Optimization. His major is Mathematics & Applied Mathematics and he focuses on the complexity of games and  algorithm design.\nProgram Visits\nEconomics and Computation\n,\nFall 2015\n,\nVisiting Graduate Student\nlink to homepage\nClose\nlink to homepage\nClose\nSearch"
  },
  "serper::Hongchang Gao": {
    "homepage": "https://hcgao.github.io/index.html",
    "emails": [
      "hongchang.gao@temple.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/gaoghc",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hongchang Gao\nMenu\nHome\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nStudents\nServices\nHongchang Gao\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Computer and Information Sciences\nCollege of Science and Technology\nTemple University\nEmail: hongchang.gao AT temple DOT edu\nOffice: Room 318, Science Education and Research Center (SERC)\nAddress: 1925 N. 12th Street, Philadelphia, PA 19122-1801\n[Google Scholar]\n[Github]\nBrief biography\nHongchang Gao joined the CIS department at Temple University as a tenure-track Assistant Professor in 2020. \nPrior to this, he received his Ph.D. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering from\nUniversity of Pittsburgh\nin 2020, under the supervision of\nDr. Heng Huang\n. He also earned an M.S. degree in Computer Science from\nBeihang University\nin 2014\nand a B.S. degree in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics from\nOcean University of China\nin 2011. He is a recipient of the NSF CAREER award (2024), the AAAI New Faculty Highlights (2023), and the Cisco Faculty Research Award (2023). He regularly serves as an Area Chair for ICML, NeurIPS, and ICLR.\nResearch interests\nMachine/Deep Learning, Optimization\nData Mining, Biomedical Data Science\nRecent news\n03/2026: Honored to serve as an\nAction Editor\nfor Transactions on Machine Learning Research.\n02/2026: One paper on\nQuantum Computing\nwas accepted to IEEE Transactions on Networking.\n02/2026: Honored to receive the\nOutstanding Program Committee Award\nat AAAI 2026.\n11/2025: Delivered an invited talk on\nFederated Muon Optimizer\nat\nKAUST Workshop on Distributed Training in the Era of Large Models\n.\n11/2025: Honored to be recognized as a\nTop Area Chair\nat NeurIPS 2025.\n11/2025: My student, Xinwen Zhang, was selected for the\nICDM Female Student Award in Data Science\n. Congrats, Xinwen!\n11/2025: Delivered a tutorial on\nFederated Optimization\nat ICDM 2025.\n09/2025: One paper on\nCompositional Optimization\nwas accepted to NeurIPS 2025.\n09/2025: One paper on\nMinimax Optimization\nwas accepted to ICDM 2025.\n08/2025: Delivered a tutorial on\nFederated Optimization\nat IJCAI 2025.\n04/2025: One paper on\nFederated Bilevel Optimization\nwas accepted to IJCAI 2025.\n05/2024: Honored to receive the\nNSF CAREER Award\n. Thanks to NSF!\nPage generated 2026-03-11 10:11:08 EDT, by\njemdoc\n."
  },
