    "homepage_text": "Yong Guo\nSearch\nYong Guo\nguoyongcs@gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI am a research scientist at Huawei and lead a creative team. Previously, I was a post-doctoral researcher at\nMax Planck Institute for Informatics\n, working closely with\nProf. Bernt Schiele\n. Before that, I obtained my PhD degree from\nSouth China University of Technology\n, supervised by\nProf. Jian Chen\nand\nProf. Mingkui Tan\n. My research interests include machine learning and computer vision.\n[Hiring!]\nActively recruiting\nresearch interns\n, scientists, and engineers, who would like to work in Shanghai. Please feel free to contact me!\nResearch Interests\nImage Restoration\nModel Compression\nModel Robustness\nRecent News\n2026/02    One paper is accepted by\nTMM 2026\n.\n2026/01    Two papers are accepted by\nICLR 2026\n.\n2025/11    Two papers are accepted by\nTIP\nin 2025.\n2025/11    Three papers are accepted by\nAAAI 2026\n.\n2025/09    Five papers are accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025\n.\n2025/06    Two papers are accepted by\nICCV 2025\n.\n2025/05    Two papers are accepted by\nICML 2025\n.\n2025/02    Four papers are accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n.\nSelected Publications\n[Full List]\nConference Paper\nClosed-loop Matters: Dual Regression Networks for Single Image Super-Resolution\nAccepted by CVPR, 2020\nYong Guo\n,\nJian Chen\n,\nJingdong Wang\n,\nQi Chen\n,\nJiezhang Cao\n,\nZeshuai Deng\n,\nYanwu Xu\n,\nMingkui Tan\nPDF\nCode\nPoster\nSlides\nNAT: Neural Architecture Transformer for Accurate and Compact Architectures\nAccepted by NeurIPS, 2019\nYong Guo\n,\nYin Zheng\n,\nMingkui Tan\n,\nQi Chen\n,\nJian Chen\n,\nPeilin Zhao\n,\nJunzhou Huang\nPDF\nCode\nPoster\nSlides\nMambaIRv2: Attentive State Space Restoration\nAccepted by CVPR, 2025\nHang Guo\n,\nYong Guo\n*\n,\nYaohua Zha\n,\nYulun Zhang\n,\nWenbo Li\n,\nTao Dai\n,\nShu-Tao Xia\n,\nYawei Li\nPDF\nCode\nDiscrimination-aware Channel Pruning for Deep Neural Networks\nAccepted by NeurIPS, 2018\nZhuangwei Zhuang\n,\nMingkui Tan\n,\nBohan Zhuang\n,\nJing Liu\n,\nYong Guo\n,\nQingyao Wu\n,\nJunzhou Huang\n,\nJinhui Zhu\nPDF\nCode\nRobustifying Token Attention for Vision Transformers\nAccepted by ICCV, 2023\nYong Guo\n,\nDavid Stutz\n,\nBernt Schiele\nPDF\nCode\nBreaking the Curse of Space Explosion: Towards Efficient NAS with Curriculum Search\nAccepted by ICML, 2020\nYong Guo\n,\nYaofo Chen\n,\nYin Zheng\n,\nPeilin Zhao\n,\nJian Chen\n,\nJunzhou Huang\n,\nMingkui Tan\nPDF\nCode\nPoster\nSlides\nContrastive Neural Architecture Search with Neural Architecture Comparators\nAccepted by CVPR, 2021 $~~~~$(\nco-first author\n)\nYaofo Chen$^*$\n,\nYong Guo\n$^*$\n,\nQi Chen\n,\nMinli Li\n,\nYaowei Wang\n,\nWei Zeng\n,\nMingkui Tan\nPDF\nCode\nJournal Paper\nTowards Accurate and Compact Architectures via Neural Architecture Transformer\nAccepted by TPAMI, 2021\nYong Guo\n,\nYin Zheng\n,\nMingkui Tan\n,\nQi Chen\n,\nZhipeng Li\n,\nJian Chen\n,\nPeilin Zhao\n,\nJunzhou Huang\nPDF\nCode\nTowards Lightweight Super-Resolution with Dual Regression Learning\nAccepted by TPAMI, 2024\nYong Guo\n,\nMingkui Tan\n,\nZeshuai Deng\n,\nJingdong Wang\n,\nQi Chen\n,\nJiezhang Cao\n,\nYanwu Xu\n,\nJian Chen\nPDF\nCode\nDiscrimination-aware Network Pruning for Deep Model Compression\nAccepted by TPAMI, 2021\nJing Liu\n,\nBohan Zhuang\n,\nZhuangwei Zhuang\n,\nYong Guo\n,\nJunzhou Huang\n,\nJinhui Zhu\n,\nMingkui Tan\nPDF\nCode\nImproving Generative Adversarial Networks with Local Coordinate Coding\nAccepted by TPAMI, 2020 $~~~~$(\nco-first author\n)\nJiezhang Cao$^*$\n,\nYong Guo\n$^*$\n,\nQingyao Wu\n,\nChunhua Shen\n,\nJunzhou Huang\n,\nMingkui Tan\nPDF\nCode\nDriveGPT4: Interpretable End-to-end Autonomous Driving via Large Language Model\nAccepted by IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters, 2024\nZhenhua Xu\n,\nYujia Zhang\n,\nEnze Xie\n,\nZhen Zhao\n,\nYong Guo\n,\nKwan-Yee K. Wong\n,\nZhenguo Li\n,\nHengshuang Zhao\nPDF\nCode\nEnhanced Long-Tailed Recognition with Contrastive CutMix Augmentation\nAccepted by TIP, 2024\nHaolin Pan$^*$\n,\nYong Guo\n$^*$\n,\nMianjie Yu\n,\nJian Chen\nCode\nAuto-Embedding Generative Adversarial Networks for High Resolution Image Synthesis\nAccepted by TMM, 2019\nYong Guo\n,\nQi Chen\n,\nJian Chen\n,\nQingyao Wu\n,\nQinfeng Shi\n,\nMingkui Tan\nPDF\nCode\nHonor & Award\nAssistant Chief Scientist at Huawei\n, 2024\nMSRA Fellowship Nomination Award\n, 2018\nOral Presentation\nat\nECCV\nin Tel Aviv, 2022\nOral Presentation\nat\nICML\nin Stockholm, 2018\nOral Presentation\nat\nAAAI\nin New Orleans, 2018\nNational Scholarship\n, 2019 & 2020\nPrinciple's Scholarship\nof SCUT, 2019 & 2020\nExcellent Doctoral Innovation Fund\nof SCUT, 2019\nExcellent Papers of Computer Academy of Guangdong\n(First Prize), 2021\nExcellent Degree Dissertations of SCUT\n(Bachelor Degree), 2016\nInternship & Collaboration\nI am looking for\nself-motivated intern students\nthat have an interest in my research areas. There is always room for new ideas and projects and I am happy to discuss them with you. When you are highly motivated, please send your CV to my email\nguoyongcs@gmail.com\n.\nWhat you can get as an intern:\nIn-depth guidance\ntowards publishing papers in top-tier conferences/journals\nSufficient computational resources\nCompetitive internship salary\nCite\n×\nCopy\nDownload"
