    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nWelcome to Yulong's Webpage\nI am an assistant profess\nor at the\nSchool of Mathematics, University of Minnesota Twin Cities\n.\nI am also an affiliated faculty at the\nData Science Initiative (DSI)\nin the\nCollege of  Science and Engineering\n.\nBefore that I was an assistant professor at\nthe\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics, University of Massachusetts Amherst\nfrom September 2020 to August 2023.\nI was a Phillip Griffiths Research Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of Mathematics, Duke University\nfrom August 2017 to July 2020. My mentors at Duke are Prof.\nJonathan Mattingly\nand Prof.\nJianfeng Lu\n.  Prior to that, I received my Ph.D. in Mathematics and Statistics at the\nUniversity of Warwick\nunder the supervision of Prof.\nAndrew Stuart\nand Prof.\nHendrik Weber\n.\nOpenings\n:\nI am looking for self-motivated students and postdocs to join my group.\nFor prospective PhD students starting Fall 202\n6\n, please apply through\nhere\n.\nFor prospective postdocs, please apply through\nMathjobs\n.\nSeveral internship positions are available for UMN\nstudents who are interested in theory and scientific applications of deep learning\n, please feel free to email me.\nAddress:\nOffice:\n539 Vincent Hall\nPostal address:\n206 Church St. SE, School of Mathematics, University of Minnesota,\nMinneapolis, MN 55455 USA\nEmail:\nyulonglu at umn dot edu\nYulong Lu  (路玉龙)\nCurriculum Vitae\nReport abuse\nReport abuse"
  },
