    "github": "https://github.com/chongyangma",
    "linkedin": "http://www.linkedin.com/in/chongyangma",
    "homepage_text": "Chongyang Ma's Home Page\nChongyang Ma\nAbout Me\nI'm currently a Tech Lead Manager at\nByteDance\n. Previously I worked as a Research Manager at Kuaishou Technology (\nKwai Inc.\n) and a Senior Research Scientist at\nSnap\nResearch, respectively. Prior to these positions, I was a Senior Research Engineer at\nActivision\nCentral Tech working on facial performance capture for\ngame production\n. From 2012 to 2015, I was a postdoc researcher at\nUBC\nand\nUSC\nworking with Prof.\nAlla Sheffer\nand Prof.\nHao Li\n, respectively.\r\n                I obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Science from\nInstitute for Advanced Study\nof\nTsinghua University\nin 2012, under the supervision of Dr.\nBaining Guo\nand Dr.\nLi-Yi Wei\n. I received my B.S. in Mathematics and Physics from Fundamental Science Class of Tsinghua University in 2007.\nI have been focusing on\ndemocratizing visual content creation\nsince I started my PhD in 2007. My research interests lie in the joint field of\ncomputer graphics\nand\ncomputer vision\n, including but not limited to deep generative models, image & video editing, human digitization, motion capture, face tracking, 3D understanding & reconstruction, physics-based simulation, data-driven animation, procedural modeling, digital geometry processing, and texture synthesis. I have delivered numerous features across Snapchat, Kuaishou/KwaiCut, and TikTok, primarily AI-powered creative tools for image/video generation and manipulation, including the widely popular\nAI Mermaid effect\n, along with advanced techniques for 3D avatars. My work has also received credits from the\nCall of Duty\nfranchise and one of the films in\nthe Hobbit\ntrilogy.\nOur team is hiring full-time research scientists and interns in generative AI, with a focus on\nvideo generation\nand\nworld models\n. Positions are primarily available in San Jose and Seattle. Please feel free to reach out to me via\nemails\nif interested.\nWork Experience\nByteDance\nDec 2023 ~ Present\nTech Lead Manager\nKuaishou Technology\nMar 2019 ~ Dec 2023\nResearch Lead/Manager\nSnap Inc.\nNov 2016 ~ Feb 2019\nSenior Research Engineer/Scientist\nActivision Publishing, Inc.\nJuly 2015 ~ Nov 2016\nSenior Computer Vision Research Engineer\nUniversity of Southern California\nOct 2013 ~ June 2015\nPostdoctoral Scholar in Geometric Capture Lab\nThe University of British Columbia\nSep 2012 ~ Sep 2013\nPostdoctoral Fellow in\nImager Laboratory\nOther Positions\nWeta Digital\nJune 2014 ~ Aug 2014\nResearch and Development Intern\nINRIA Nancy Grand-Est\nAug 2011 ~ Feb 2012\nVisiting student in\nALICE team\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nMar 2012 ~ July 2012\nResearch intern in\nInternet Graphics Group\nApr 2008 ~ Aug 2011\nPublications\nProfessional Activities\nNote:\nDue to an increasing daily workload and my commitment to maintaining high-quality reviews, I am currently unable to accept review invitations from conferences or journals where I have not previously published.\nAssociate Editor\nComputer Animation and Virtual Worlds\n(CAVW) 2022--2025\nProgram Committee\nACM SIGGRAPH Technical Papers 2024, 2025\nACM SIGGRAPH Asia Technical Papers 2023, 2026\nComputer Graphics International (CGI) 2023\nComputational Visual Media (CVM) 2023--2026\nShape Modeling International (SMI) 2018--2023\nComputer Animation and Social Agents (CASA) 2017--2022\nACM SIGGRAPH Asia Technical Briefs and Posters 2019\nACM Symposium on Interactive 3D Graphics and Games (I3D) 2015--2018\nACM/Eurographics Symposium on Computer Animation (SCA) 2015, 2016\nPacific Graphics 2015, 2016\nPaper Reviewer\nNeural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV)\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)\nIEEE International Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME)\nACM SIGGRAPH\nACM SIGGRAPH Asia\nEurographics\nPacific Graphics\nCAD/Graphics\nComputer Graphics International (CGI)\nAsian Conference on Computer Vision (ACCV)\nIEEE VR\nACM Transactions on Graphics\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\nIEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics\nIEEE Computer Graphics and Applications\nComputer Graphics Forum (Wiley Blackwell)\nVisual Informatics (Elsevier)\nComputers & Graphics (Elsevier)\nThe Visual Computer (Springer)\nSignal, Image and Video Processing (Springer)\nJournal of Computer Science and Technology (Springer)\nJournal of Electronic Imaging\nJournal of Computer Graphics Techniques\nMiscellaneous\nHow to pronounce my name: [\n'tÊÉ:Å jÊÅ 'ma:\n]\nMy academic \"ancestors\" (according to\nthe Mathematics Genealogy Project\n):\nChongyang Ma ←\nBaining Guo\n←\nJohn Hopcroft\n←\nRichard Mattson\n←\nBernard Widrow\n←\nWilliam Linvill\n←\nErnst Guillemin\n←\nArnold Sommerfeld\n←\nFerdinand von Lindemann\n←\nFelix Klein\n←\nJulius PlÃ¼cker\n&\nRudolf Lipschitz\n← …\nMy film and game credits\nThe Hobbit: The Battle of the Five Armies\n(Weta Digital), 2014\nSkylanders Battlecast\n(Activision), 2016\nCall of Duty: Infinite Warfare\n(Activision), 2016\nCall of Duty: Modern Warfare Remastered\n(Activision), 2016\nCall of Duty: WWII\n(Activision), 2017\nMy unprofessional sports record\n(Running) 3000 metres: 12'10\"\n(Basketball) most consecutive free throws made: 12\n(Basketball) most consecutive three-point field goals: 6\nCopyright © 2010 - 2025 Chongyang Ma | Last updated: 11/02/2025"
