    "homepage_text": "Zinan Lin at Microsoft Research\nSkip to main content\nMicrosoft\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nSearch\nSearch Microsoft Research\nNo results\nCancel\nZinan Lin\nSenior Researcher\nAbout\nMy name is Zinan Lin (林梓楠 in Chinese). I am a Principal Researcher at\nAlgorithms group\n,\nMicrosoft Research\n. I received my Ph.D. from\nCarnegie Mellon University\n(opens in new tab)\nin 2023, where I am fortunate to be advised by\nGiulia Fanti\n(opens in new tab)\nand\nVyas Sekar\n(opens in new tab)\n. Before that, I obtained my B.E. from\nTsinghua University\n(opens in new tab)\nin 2017. I am interested in the theoretical foundations of machine learning (especially generative models), and the applications in privacy, security, and networking.\nMore information is at my\nhomepage\n(opens in new tab)\n.\nOpens in a new tab\nResearch areas\nArtificial intelligence\nSecurity, privacy, and cryptography\nSystems and networking\nResearch groups\nAlgorithms (Redmond)\nPrivacy Preserving Machine Learning Innovation\nFollow us:\nFollow on X\nLike on Facebook\nFollow on LinkedIn\nSubscribe on Youtube\nFollow on Instagram\nSubscribe to our RSS feed\nShare this page:\nShare on X\nShare on Facebook\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on Reddit"
  },
