    "homepage_text": "Fisher Yu Lab |\nSelect Page\nApplied Nano & Bio Photonic Group\nUniversity of Arkansas\nOur Research\nW\nelcome to the home page of the Applied Nano & Bio Photonics Group at the\nUniversity of Arkansas\n. We are located in the Engineering Research Center which is about two miles away from Fayetteville campus. The group is led by Professor Shui-Qing (Fisher) Yu of the\nDepartment of Electrical Engineering\n,\nCollege of Engineering\n.\nSee our most recent\nMURI award weblink\nfeaturing collaborative efforts with the Department of Defense (DoD) through the Air Force Office of Scientific Research (AFOSR).\nTo learn more about us, our facilities, and our capabilities, please explore our website. We hope you find these pages useful and informative and welcome any feedback you may have!\nNew!\nCurrently, our group has a few position openings of Graduate Research Associates, Postdoctoral Research Associates, and Undergraduate Research Associates. Find out the\nresearch opportunities\nin the group.\nLast updated on 11/25/2025\nLearn More\nShui-Qing “Fisher” Yu\n: 2022 Faculty Distinguished Achievement in Research Award\nMore News\nResearch Areas\nDeveloping novel electrical and photonic materials & Developing novel optoelectronics\nFacilities\nSemiconductor laser characterization system, FTIR and Low Temperature Controller.\nResources\nHiDEC\n,\nMBE lab\n,\nJEOL JBX-5500ZD electron beam lithography system\nPublications\nJournal Papers, Conference Presentations, Patents, Proceeding Papers\nTo learn more about us, our facilities, and our capabilities, please explore our website.\nWe hope you find these pages useful and informative and welcome any feedback you may have!\nContact Us"
  },
