    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nDr. Ding Xinghao, Professor, Deputy Director of the Department-School of Information Science and Engineering\nEnglish\n|\nä¸­æç\nHome\nAbout\nSchool of Information Science and Engineering\nXiamen University\nHistory\nFacts&Figures\nAnnual Report\nContact Us\nPrograms\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nDoctoral Programs\nMaster Programs\nAdmission\nProfessional Students\nCenter of Collaborative Education in Information Science\nPeople\nFaculty\nProfessor\nAssociate Professor\nAssistant Professor\nAdjunct Professor\nHonorary Professor\nDistinguished Professor\nStaff\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Communication Science\nDepartment of Cognitive Science and Technology\nDepartment of Cyber Space Security\nAlumni\nWork Opportunity\nDepartments\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Communication Science\nDepartment of Cognitive Science and Technology\nDepartment of Cyber Space Security\nResearch\nKey Labs\nResearch Institutes\nResearch Centers\nNews&Events\nNews\nEvents\nProfessor\nFaculty\nProfessor\nAssociate Professor\nAssistant Professor\nAdjunct Professor\nHonorary Professor\nDistinguished Professor\nStaff\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Communication Science\nDepartment of Cognitive Science and Technology\nDepartment of Cyber Space Security\nAlumni\nWork Opportunity\nHome\n>>\nPeople\n>>\nFaculty\n>>\nProfessor\n>>\r\n                Content\nDr. Ding Xinghao, Professor, Deputy Director of the Department\nResearch Interestsï¼Deep Learning, machine learning, medical image processing and analysis, computer vision, smart data analysis and processing\nEmailï¼dxh(AT)xmu.edu.cn\nResumeï¼\nDegrees\nPhD,  Precision Instrument and Machinery, Hefei University of Technology, 2003\nBSc, Precision Instrument, Hefei University of Technology, 1998\nProfessional Activities\nLocal Chair, 2015 IEEE International Workshop on Multimedia Signal Processing, Xiamen, China, 19-21 October 2015\nPublication Co-Chairsï¼Internation al Symposium on Intelligent Signal Processing and Communication Systems, Xiamen, 2017\nProjects\nBayesian nonparametric methods for compressed sensing MRI using partial k-space decompositionscourse Analysis (NNSF 2016)\nSelected Publications\n[1] Fu X, Zeng D, Huang Y, Zhang XP, Ding X*, 2016. A weighted variational model for simultaneous reflectance and illumination estimation. In Proceedings of Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR2016), Las Vegas, NV, USA (IEEE: EI).\n[2] Jiang Y, Ding X*, Zeng D, Huang Y, Paisley J, 2015. Pan-sharpening with a Hyper-Laplacian penalty. In Proceedings of IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV2015), Santiago, Chile, pp. 540-548 (IEEE: EI).\n[3] Ding X*, Jiang Y, Huangand Y, Paisley J, 2014. Pan-sharpening with a Bayesian nonparametric dictionary learning model. In Proceedings of International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS2014), Reykjavik, Iceland, pp. 176-184 (EI).\n[4] Fu X, Liao Y, Zeng D, Huang Y, Zhang XP, Ding X*, 2015. A probabilistic method for image enhancement with simultaneous illumination and reflectance estimation. IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, 24(12): 4965-4977 (IEEE: SCI/EI).\n[5] Huang Y, Paisley J, Lin Q, Ding X*, Fu X, Zhang XP, 2014. Bayesian nonparametric dictionary learning for compressed sensing MRI. IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, (23)12: 5007-5119 (IEEE: SCI/EI).\n[6] Ding X*, He L, Carin L, 2015. Bayesian robust principal component analysis, IEEE Transactions on Image Processing, 20(12): 3419-3430, 2011. (IEEE: SCI/EI).\n[7] Huang Y, Wu R, Sun Y, Wang W, Ding X*, 2015. Vehicle logo recognition system based on convolutional networks with a pre-training strategy. IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Transportation Systems, 16(4): 1951-1960 (IEEE: SCI/EI).\n[8] Chai J*, Chen Z, Chen H, Ding X, 2016. Designing bag-level multiple-instance feature-weighting algorithms based on the large margin principle. Information Sciences, 367: 783â808 (Elsevier: SCI/EI).\n[9] Chai J*, Ding X, Chen H, Lia T, 2014. Multiple-instance discriminant analysis. Pattern Recognition, 47(7): 2517-2531 (Elsevier: SCI/EI).\n[10] Fu X, Zeng D, Huang Y, Liao Y, Ding X*, Paisley J, 2016. A fusion-based enhancing method for weakly illuminated images. Signal Processing, 129: 82-96 (Elsevier: SCI/EI).\n[11] Zhuang P, Fu X, Huang Y, Zeng D, Ding X*, 2016. A novel framework method for non-blind deconvolution using subspace images priors. Signal Processing: Image Communication, 46: 17-28 (Springer: SCI/EI).\n[12] Zhuang P, Huang Y, Zeng D, Ding X*, 2016. Mixed noise removal based on a novel non-parametric Bayesian sparse outlier model. Neurocomputing, 174: 858-865 (Elsevier: SCI/EI).\n[13] Fu X, Wang J, Zeng D, Huang Y, Ding X*, 2015. Remote sensing image enhancement using regularized-histogram equalization and DCT. IEEE Geoscience and Remote Sensing Letters, 12(11): 2301-2305 (IEEE: SCI/EI).\n[14] Ding X, Chen L, Zheng X, Huang Y, Zeng D*, 2016.  Single image rain and snow removal via guided L0 smoothing filter. Multimedia Tools and Applications, 75(5): 2697-2712 (Springer: SCI/EI).\n[15] Huang Y, Chen X, Ding X*, 2016. A harmonic means pooling strategy for structural similarity index measurement in image quality assessment. Multimedia Tools and Applications, 75(5): 2769-2780 (Springer: SCI/EI).\n[16] Huang Y, Chen X, Zhang J, Zeng D, Zhang D, Ding X*, 2015. Single-trial ERPs denoising via collaborative filtering on ERPs images. Neurocomputing, 149: 914-923 (Elsevier: SCI/EI).\nQuick Links\nXiamen University\nSchool of Information Science and Engineering\nAdmission Office of Xiamen University\nCenter of Collaborative Education in Information Science\nOverseas Education College of Xiamen University\nCopyright Â© School of Information Science and Engineering\nTop"
