  "serper::Jiaoyan Chen": {
    "homepage": "https://chenjiaoyan.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "firstname4ai@gmail.com",
      "firstname.lastname@manchester.ac.uk"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/KRR-Oxford",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/jiaoyan-chen-00822b26/",
    "homepage_text": "Jiaoyan Chen\nJiaoyan Chen\nContact Information\nOffice: 2.91, Kilburn Building\n,\nOxford Road\n,\nManchester\n,\nUK\n,\nM13 9PL\nEmail: firstname.lastname@manchester.ac.uk, firstname4ai@gmail.com\nHome\n,\nLinkedIn\n,\nCV\n,\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nDBLP\nBiography\nJiaoyan is a Senior Lecturer (~Associate Professor) in Department of Computer Science, The University of Manchester.\n    Before that, he was a Lecturer in Manchester from 2022, a Senior Researcher in Department of Computer Science, University of Oxford from 2017 (with\nProf. Ian Horrocks\n), and a postdoctoral in Heidelberg University.\n    Jiaoyan got his PhD and bachelor degrees both in Zhejiang University on Computer Science and Technology. He was a visiting PhD in Department of Informatics, Zurich University from 2014 to 2015.\nNews!\n3 Mar: give a seminar on ontology embedding on The Open University\n13 Jan: one paper on LLM-based KG embedding and one paper on LLM for OWL reasoning accepted by WWW'26\n4 Jan: one paper on RAG with incomplete KG accepted by EACL'26\nResearch Interests\nKnowledge Representation\n: construction and curation of knowledge graphs and ontologies, semantic techniques.\nMachine Learning\n: knowledge representation learning, semantic embedding, neural-symbolic integration.\nData and Knowledge Management for AI\n: evaluating and augmenting large language models (LLMs) with knowledge graphs, ontologies and structured data.\nPhD / MPhil Recruiting\nPlease email me before applying online, if you have interests in the following PhD projects\nRAG project\n,\nLLM explanability and evaluation project\n, or other topics that fall into my scope.\n        MPhil (research-oriented master, usually self-funded) applications are also welcomed.\n        I am also open to application of visiting PhD, but only consider topics within my interests.\n        As there are so many enquires and applicants, I will not be able to respond to all of them, but only those qualified (e.g., oversee PhD applicants require outstanding academic performance evidenced by more than one of the following: excellent transcripts, degree from top universities, top publications with key contributions, and outstanding final-year project mark). I apologize for that in advance.\nRecent Projects / Grants\nEPSRC New Investigator Award \"OntoEm: Semantic Embeddings for Ontologies\" (EP/Y017706/1), 2024 - 2027, PI.\nThe Manchester-Melbourne-Toronto (MMT) Research Fund, \"AI-Driven Solutions for Child Protection: Utilizing LLMs and Knowledge Graph\" (collaborative research initiatives), 2024 - 2026, PI with Jia Xue from University of Toronto.\nEPSRC \"ConCur: Knowledge Graph Construction and Curation\" (EP/V050869/1), 2021 - 2025, Research Co-Investigator.\nTuring Innovation Catalyst Manchester (TICM) funded Collaborative R&D Project \"Multi-modal Semantic Search with Ontologies and Modern AI Techniques\", 2024 - 2025, PI.\nTuring-Manchester Feasibility Project \"Knowledge Graph for Explainability, Guidance and Human-in-the-loop in Machine Learning\", 2022 - 2023, PI.\nRecent Services\nAssociate Editor of\nThe Knowledge Engineering Review\n(KER) (2025 - ).\nAssociate Editor of\nTransactions on Graph Data and Knowledge\n(TGDK) (2023 - ).\nEditor Board of Data Intelligence (2021 - ).\nMembership of EPSRC Peer Review College (2023 - )\nCo-organiser of the OAEI Track\nBio-ML\nin ISWC (2022 - 2024).\nPC/SPC/Area Chair of ISWC, The Web Conference, NeurIPS, ARR, etc.\nProposal reviewer for grant bodies including ERC, RAEng, DFG, NWO, etc.\nPublications\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nDBLP\n,\nSelected\nSelective Invited Talks and Tutorials\nEmbedding Complex Knowledge: From Geometric to Language Models. Invited report in Shanxi University, Shanxi, China. 10/11/2025.\nSlides\nIntegrating Knowledge Graphs and Large Language Models for Advancing Scientific Research. Tutorial at ICDCS 2025, Glasgow, UK. 20/07/2025.\nSlides\nOntology Embedding and Construction in the Large Language Model Era. Invited Talk in Southeast University, Nanjing. 10/01/2025.\nSlides\nIntegrating Knowledge Graphs and Large Language Models for Advancing Scientific Research. Tutorial at Learning on Graph Conference (LoG), 26/11/2024.\nSlides\nData Intensive Question Answering with Large Language Models. Invited Talk at University of Stuttgart. 31/10/2024.\nSlides\nKnowledge Engineering meets (Large) Language Models. Amazon Search Research Talk Series. 12/07/2024.\nSlides\nNeural-symbolic Knowledge Representation and Reasoning with Ontology and Knowledge Graph Embeddings. Seminar at King Abdullah University of Science and Technology (KAUST), 04/2024.\nSlides\nKnowledge-aware Zero-shot Learning (K-ZSL): Concepts, Methods and Resources\n. Tutorial in IJCAI 2023 (August 19 - 25).\nSoftware\nOWL2Vec*\n(an OWL ontology embedding framework)\nDeepOnto\n(a library for ontology engineering with language models and machine learning)\nTeaching in Manchester\n\"Data Engineering Technologies (COMP63502)\". 2025-2026.\n\"Advanced Topics in Knowledge Representation and Reasoning (COMP64602)\". 2025-2026.\n\"Data Engineering (COMP60711)\". 2024-2025.\n\"Querying Data on the Web (COMP62421)\". 2023-2024, 2024-2025.\nCurrent Research Students / Associates\nHui Yang\n(Postdoctoral, 06/2024 - )\nBeiyu Xu (PhD, 01/2026 - )\nHira Beril Kucuk (PhD, 04/2025 - )\nHanhua Hong (PhD, 09/2024 - )\nYiping Song (PhD, 04/2024 - )\nIan Hyland (half-time PhD, 04/2024 - )\nZhenyu Wu (PhD, 09/2022 - )\nPast Research Students / Associates\nJonathon Dilworth\n(Research Assistant, Department of Computer Science, The University of Manchester, 2025 - 2026)\nTianzhe Zhao (visiting PhD from Xi'an Jiaotong University, 2024 - 2025)\nHang Dong\n(Postdoctoral, Department of Computer Science, University of Oxford, 2022 - 2024)\nYuan He\n(PhD, Department of Computer Science, University of Oxford, 2020 - 2024)\nMelis Kupeli (Research Assistant, Alliance Manchester Business School, The University of Manchester, 2022 - 2023)\nYuxia Geng\n(PhD, College of Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang University, 2018 - 2023)\nErik Bryhn Myklebust\n(PhD, NIVA & SIRIUS, University of OSLO, 2019 - 2022) (external co-supervisor)\nMathias Jackermeier (MSc, Department of Computer Science, University of Oxford, 2022)\nYan Zhou (MSc, GIScience, University of Heidelberg, 2016 - 2017)"
