    "homepage_text": "Cheng-Fu Chen | Ole Miss\nSkip to main site navigation\nSkip to main content\nGive\nSearch\nCheng-Fu Chen\nAssociate Professor of Modern Languages\nFaculty\nStaff\nEmail:\ncchen5@olemiss.edu\nOffice Location:\n1848 University Circle\nPhone:\n662-915-6792\nDr. Cheng-Fu Chen is an Associate Professor of Chinese in the Department of Modern Languages at the University of Mississippi.\nResearch Interests\nMandarin Chinese, Rukai (Austronesian, Taiwan), syntax, semantics\nBiography\nDr. Cheng-Fu Chen teaches Mandarin Chinese at all levels. His current research focuses on eventuality, argument structure, and related morphosyntactic and syntactic-semantic issues across typologically diverse languages.\nCourses Taught\nChin 313\nMedia Chinese I: Newspapers and Internet\nChin 314\nMedia Chinese II: Broadcast News\nChin 325\nThe Chinese Writing System\nChin 330\nIntroduction to Chinese Linguistics\nChin 401\nAdvanced Chinese I\nChin 402\nAdvanced Chinese II\nChin 425\nChinese Narratives and Storytelling\nChin 450\nDomain Knowledge\nChin 550\nAdvanced Domain Knowledge\nOffice, Department or Center\nDepartment of  Modern Languages\nSchool\nCollege of Liberal Arts\nCampuses\nOxford\nAreas of Expertise\nMandarin Chinese, Rukai (Austronesian, Taiwan), syntax, semantics\nEducation\nM.A. Linguistics, National Taiwan University (1999)\nM.A. Linguistics, The University of Texas at Austin (2004)\nPh.D. Linguistics, The University of Texas at Austin (2008)\nTake The Next Steps\nVisit Campus\nRequest Information\nApply"
  },
