    "homepage_text": "Haozhi Qi's Homepage\nHaozhi Qi\nCV\n&\nGoogle Scholar\n&\nGitHub\n&\nTwitter\nI am a Research Scientist at Amazon Frontier AI & Robotics (FAR).\nMy research lies at the intersection of robot learning, computer vision, and tactile sensing.\n        My Ph.D. thesis focused on\nMultisensory Dexterity for Robotics\n.\nI received my Ph.D. from UC Berkeley, where I worked with\nProf. Yi Ma\nand\nProf. Jitendra Malik\n. I received my\n        Bachelor's degree from Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST), where I was advised by\nProf. Chi-Keung Tang\n. I also spent two years at\n        Microsoft Research Asia (MSRA), working on computer vision with\nDr. Jifeng Dai\nand\nDr. Yichen Wei\n.\nRecent News\n[26/06] Upcoming invited talk at ICRA 2026 Workshop on\nManipulation Robustness: Towards Human-Level Robustness in the Real World\n.\n[26/01] Two papers accepted at ICRA 2026.\n[25/11] Serving as Area Chair for RSS 2026.\nWorkshop Series:\nDexterous Manipulation\n. I have been organizing the long-running Workshop on Dexterous Manipulation series. We are committed to open science; please find the video archives and proceedings for each year below:\nUpcoming Workshop at ICRA 2026:\n[Website]\nRSS:\n[2025]\n[2024]\nCoRL:\n[2025]\n[2024]\nICRA:\n[2025]\nTouch Processing\n.\n[NeurIPS 2024]\n[NeurIPS 2023]\nPapers\n(*Equal Technical Contribution, †Equal Advising)\nHandelBot: Real-World Piano Playing via Fast Adaptation of Dexterous Robot Policies\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\nTech Report, Mar 2026\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nLearning Dexterous Manipulation Skills from Imperfect Simulations\n*,\n*,\n*,\n,\n,\n†,\nHaozhi Qi\n†\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n), 2026\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nDexterity from Smart Lenses: Multi-Fingered Robot Manipulation with In-the-Wild Human\n        Demonstrations\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n), 2026\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nCoordinated Humanoid Manipulation with Choice Policies\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n*,\n,\n,\n,\n†,\n†\nTech Report, Dec 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nOSMO: Open-Source Tactile Glove for Human-to-Robot Skill Transfer\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n*,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\nTech Report, Dec 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nSPIDER: Scalable Physics-Informed Dexterous Retargeting\n,\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\n†,\n†,\n†,\n†\nTech Report, Nov 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nFrom Simple to Complex Skills: The Case of In-Hand Object Reorientation\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n), 2025\nPaper\nWebsite\nLearning Visuotactile Skills with Two Multifingered Hands\n,\n*,\n*,\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n), 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nLearning In-Hand Translation Using Tactile Skin With Shear and Normal Force Sensing\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n), 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nHand-Object Interaction Pretraining from Videos\n*,\n*,\n,\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n), 2025\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nLessons from Learning to Spin “Pens”\n*,\n*,\n*,\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n,\n,\nConference on Robot Learning (\nCoRL\n), 2024\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nTwisting Lids Off with Two Hands\n*,\n*,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\nConference on Robot Learning (\nCoRL\n), 2024\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nSummary\nNeural feels with Neural Fields: Visuo-tactile Perception for In-Hand Manipulation\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\nScience Robotics\n, Nov 2024 (\nJournal Cover\n)\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nDigitizing Touch with an Artificial Multimodal Fingertip\n,\n,\n        Ali Sengül,\n        Victoria Rose Most,\n        Nolan Black,\n        Kevin Sawyer,\n        Romeo Mercado,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n        Alexander Sohn,\n        Byron Taylor,\n        Norb Tydingco,\n        Gregg Kammerer,\n        Dave Stroud,\n        Jake Khatha,\n        Kurt Jenkins,\n        Kyle Most,\n        Neal Stein,\n        Ricardo Chavira,\n        Thomas Craven-Bartle,\n        Eric Sanchez,\n        Yitian Ding,\n,\nTech Report, Nov 2024\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nGeneral In-Hand Object Rotation with Vision and Touch\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\nConference on Robot Learning (\nCoRL\n), 2023\nPaper\nWebsite\nVideo\nSummary\nPerceiving Extrinsic Contacts from Touch Improves Learning Insertion Policies\n,\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\nTech Report, Sep 2023\nPaper\nCode\nVideo\nSummary\nIn-Hand Object Rotation via Rapid Motor Adaptation\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n*,\n,\n,\nConference on Robot Learning (\nCoRL\n), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nSummary\nOutstanding Demo Award\nat NeurIPS 2023 Robot Learning Workshop\nCoupling Vision and Proprioception for Navigation of Legged Robots\n*,\n*,\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nSummary\nReduNet: A White-box Deep Network from the Principle of Maximizing Rate Reduction\n*,\n*,\n*,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (\nJMLR\n), accepted in 2022\nPaper\nCode\nSummary\nOurs\nGT\nLearning Long-term Visual Dynamics with Region Proposal Interaction Networks\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2021\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nSummary\nDeep Isometric Learning for Visual Recognition\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2020\nPaper\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nSummary\nNeurVPS: Neural Vanishing Point Scanning via Conic Convolution\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\nNeural Information Processing System (\nNIPS\n), 2019\nPaper\nCode\nLearning to Reconstruct 3D Manhattan Wireframes from a Single Image\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\n,\n,\n,\n,\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV\n), 2019\n      (\nOral, 4.3% acceptance rate\n)\nPaper\nCode\nEnd-to-End Wireframe Parsing\n,\nHaozhi Qi\n,\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV\n), 2019\nPaper\nCode\nDeformable Convolutional Networks\n*,\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n*,\n*,\n*,\n,\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (\nICCV\n), 2017 (\nOral, 2.1% acceptance rate\n)\nPaper\nCode\nFully Convolutional Instance-aware Semantic Segmentation\n*,\nHaozhi Qi\n*,\n,\n,\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2017 (\nSpotlight, 8.0% acceptance rate\n)\nPaper\nCode\nI highly value open-source and reproducible research. I aim to open-source all of my project code; the current progress is 24 / 26 (92.3%).\n      In addition, my CV template is open-sourced\nhere\n,\n      and its design is inspired by\nthis\n.\n      This website is also open-sourced\nhere\n.\n      Its design is inspired by\nthis\nand\nthis\n,\n      with a few adapted elements.\n★\n★\n★\n★\n★"
