    "homepage_text": "About me - Xiaofei Xieâs HOMEPAGE\nXiaofei Xie (è°¢èé£)\nAssistant Professor, School of Computing and Information Systems (SCIS), Singapore Management University (SMU)\nFollow\nSMU, Singapore\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI am an Assistant Professor in School of Computing and Information Systems, Singapore Management University, Singapore (2022-). Previously, I was a postdoc at Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (2018-2021).\nMy current research mainly focuses on program analysis, software testing, vulnerability detection and quality assurance of AI systems.\nI am looking for highly motivated PhD students. Please send me an email with your CV if you are interested.\nSMU is ranked No. 9 ï¼No. 5 in Asia) in the Software Engineering category, No. 37 (No. 16 in Asia) in the broad AI category and No. 85 (No. 14 in Asia) in the overall CS discipline in CSRanking (based on publications from 2014 to 2024).\nNews\n(04/2023) Our paper âBehAVExplor: Behavior Diversity Guided Testing for Autonomous Driving Systemsâ is accepted by ISSTA 2023\n(04/2023) Our paper âMulti-target Backdoor Attacks for Code Pre-trained Modelsâ is accepted by ACL 2023\n(02/2023) Our paper âEvading DeepFake Detectors via Adversarial Statistical Consistencyâ is accepted by CVPR 2023\n(01/2023) Our paper âNeural Episodic Control with State Abstractionâ is accepted by ICLR 2023\n(12/2022) Our paper âGraphSearchNet: Enhancing GNNs via Capturing Global Dependencies for Semantic Code Searchâ is accepted by TSE 2023.\n(12/2022) Our paper âGameRTS: A Regression Testing Framework for Video Gamesâ is accepted by ICSE 2023\n(12/2022) Our paper âContraBERT: Enhancing Code Pre-trained Models via Contrastive  Learningâ is accepted by ICSE 2023\n(12/2022) Our paper âEfficient Testing of Deep Neural Networks via Labeling-Free Accuracy Estimationâ is accepted by ICSE 2023\n(12/2022) Our paper âWidget Detection-based Testing for Industrial Mobile Gamesâ is accepted by ICSE SEIP 2023\n(12/2022) Our paper âCodeS: Towards Code Model Generalization Under Distribution Shiftâ is accepted by ICSE NIER 2023\n(8/2022) Our paper âTransRepair: Context-aware Program Repair for Compilation Errorsâ is accepted by ASE 2022\n(8/2022) Our paper âTowards Understanding the Faults of JavaScript-Based Deep Learning Systemsâ is accepted by ASE 2022\n(8/2022) Our paper âDeep Learning for Coverage-Guided Fuzzing: How Far Are We?â is accepted by TDSC 2022\n(8/2022) Our paper âSelf-Checking Deep Neural Networks for Anomalies and Adversaries in Deploymentâ is accepted by TDSC 2022\n(8/2022) Our paper âEnhancing Security Patch Identification by Capturing Structures in Commitsâ is accepted by TDSC 2022\n(7/2022) Our paper âDecompiling x86 Deep Neural Network Executablesâ is accepted by USENIX 2023\n(7/2022) Our paper âCross-Lingual Transfer Learning for Statistical Type Inferenceâ won ACM SIGSOFT Distinguished Paper Award (ISSTAâ22)\n(6/2022) Our paper âA3GAN: Attribute-Aware Anonymization Networks for Face De-identificationâ is accepted by ACM-MM 2022.\n(6/2022) Our paper âLarge-Scale Analysis of Non-Termination Bugs in Real-World OSS Projectsâ is accepted by ESEC/FSE 2022.\n(4/2022) Our team won 3rd place in AI Singaporeâs Trusted Media Challenge (Deepfake detection).\n(4/2022) Our paper âNeuron Coverage-Guided Domain Generalizationâ is accepted by TPAMI 2022\n(4/2022) Our paper âCross-Lingual Transfer Learning for Statistical Type Inferenceâ is accepted by ISSTA 2022\n(4/2022) Our paper âDemystifying Performance Regressions in String Solversâ is accepted by TSE 2022\n(3/2022) Our paper âGraphCode2Vec: Generic Code Embedding via Lexical and Program Dependence Analysesâ is accepted by MSR 2022\n(2/2022) Our paper âGBGallery : A Benchmark and Framework for Game Testingâ is accepted by EMSE 2022\n(1/2022) Our paper âAn Empirical Study on Data Distribution-Aware Test Selection for Deep Learning Enhancementâ is accepted by TOSEM 2022\n(12/2021) Our paper âLearning Program Semantics with Code Representations: An Empirical Studyâ is accepted by SANER 2021\n(5/2021) Our paper âAutomatic RNN Repair via Model-based Analysisâ is accepted by ICML 2021\n(5/2021) Our paper âAVA: Adversarial Vignetting Attack against Visual Recognitionâ is accepted by IJCAI 2021\n(4/2021) Our paper âTowards Exploring the Limitations of Active Learning: An Empirical Studyâ is accepted by ASE 2021\n(4/2021) Our paper âBreaking Neural Reasoning Architectures with Metamorphic Relation-Based Adversarial Examplesâ is accepted by TNNLS\n(3/2021) Our paper âBias Field Poses a Threat to DNN-based X-Ray Recognition!â is accepted by ICME 2021\n(2/2021) Our paper âStealing Deep Reinforcement Learning Models for Fun and Profitâ is accepted by AsiaCCS 2021\n(1/2021) Our paper âRetrieval-Augmented Generation for Code Summarization via Hybrid GNNâ is accepted by ICLR 2021 (spotlight)\n(12/2020) Our paper âAutomatic Web Testing using Curiosity-Driven Reinforcement Learningâ is accepted by ICSE 2021\n(12/2020) Two papers are accepted by AAAI 2021\n(11/2020) Our paper â An Empirical Study on Robustness of DNNs with Out-of-Distribution Awarenessâ won the Best Paper Award in APSEC 2020\n(09/2020) Our paper âWatch out! Motion is Blurring the Vision of Your Deep Neural Networksâ is accepted by NeurIPS 2020.\n(09/2020) Our paper âA Performance-Sensitive Malware Detection System Using Deep Learning on Mobile Devicesâ is accepted by TIFS.\n(08/2020) Our paper âCan We Trust Your Explanations? Sanity Checks for Interpreters in Android Malware Analysisâ is accepted by TIFS.\n(07/2020) Four papers are accepted by ASE 2020.\n(07/2020) Four papers are accepted by ACM MM 2020.\n(07/2020) Our paper âRegression Testing of Massively Multiplayer Online Role-Playing Gamesâ is accepted at ICSME 2020, NIER Track.\n(07/2020) Our paper âJSCSP: a Novel Policy-Based XSS Defense Mechanism for Browsersâ is accepted at TDSC.\n(07/2020) Our paper âSPARK: Spatial-aware Online Incremental Attack Against Visual Trackingâ is accepted at ECCV 2020.\n(07/2020) I was awarded the ACM Tianjin Doctoral Dissertation Award 2019.\n(05/2020) Our paper âFakeSpotter: A Simple yet Robust Baseline for Spotting AI-Synthesized Fake Facesâ is accepted at IJCAI 2020.\n(03/2020) Our paper âHow are Deep Learning Models Similar? An Empirical Study on Clone Analysis of Deep Learning Softwareâ is accepted at ICPC 2020.\n(12/2019) Three papers âTowards Characterising Adversarial Defects of Deep Learning Software from the Lens of Uncertaintyâ, âTypestate-Guided Fuzzer for Discovering Use-after-Free Vulnerabilitiesâ and âMemLock: Memory Usage Guided Fuzzingâ are accepted at ICSEâ2020.\n(11/2019) Our papers âStealthy and Efficient Adversarial Attacks against Deep Reinforcement Learningâ is accepted at AAAI 2020.\n(10/2019) Our paper âWuji: Automatic Online Combat Game Testing Using Evolutionary Deep Reinforcement Learningâ receives the ACM SIGSOFT Distinguished Paper Award in ASEâ19.\n(10/2019) I was awarded ACM SIGSOFT CAPS Travel Funds for ASE 2019.\n(08/2019) Three papers including DeepHunter, DeepStellar and DeepMutation++ are accepted by ASE 2019.\n(08/2019) Two papers âAn Empirical Study towards Characterizing Deep Learning Development and Deployment across Different Frameworks and Platformsâ and âWuji: Automatic Online Combat Game Testing Using Evolutionary Deep Reinforcement Learningââ are accepted by ASE 2019.\n(07/2019) Two papers âSafe Inputs Generation for Black-box Systemsâ and âMobiDroid: A Performance-Sensitive Malware Detection System on Mobile Platformâ are accepted by ICECCS 2019.\n(05/2019) Three papers âDeepStellar: Model-Based Quantitative Analysis of Stateful Deep Learning Systemsâ, âLocating Vulnerabilities in Binaries via Memory Layout Recoveringâ and âCerebro: Context-aware Adaptive Fuzzing for EffectiveVulnerability Detectionâ are accepted by ESEC/FSE 2019.\n(05/2019) Our paper âDiffChaser: Detecting Disagreements for Deep Neural Networksâ is accepted by IJCAI 2019.\n(05/2019) Our paper âDeepHunter: A Coverage-Guided Fuzz Testing Framework for Deep Neural Networksâ is accepted by ISSTA 2019."
