    "homepage_text": "Chen  Wang\nChen  Wang\nI am a final-year PhD student at Stanford CS, advised by\nFei-Fei Li\nand\nKaren Liu\n.\nMy research goal is to build robots with human-like dexterity and capability in handling everyday tasks. To that end, I focus on robot learning for dexterous manipulation, imitation learning from human motion, and long-horizon planning and control.\nPreviously, I have spent time researching at\nGoogle DeepMind\n(2024),\nNVIDIA Research\n(2022) and\nMIT CSAIL\n(2019).\nRecent\nAug, 2024\nObj-Dex\n,\nReKep\n,\nTRANSIC\naccepted to CoRL 2024\nMay, 2024\nDexCap\naccepted to RSS 2024\nNov, 2023\nMimicPlay\nselected as Best Paper/Student Paper/Systems Paper Awards Finalist at CoRL 2023\nAug, 2023\nSeqDex\n,\nMimicPlay\n,\nVoxPoser\n,\nNOIR\naccepted to CoRL 2023\nDec, 2022\nGot into NVIDIA Graduate Fellowship Finalist\nSep, 2022\nTwo papers accepted to CoRL 2022\nJun, 2022\nGenTP\naccepted to RA-L 2022\nSep, 2021\nCo-GAIL\nand\nrobomimic\naccepted to CoRL 2021\nJun, 2021\nHAN\naccepted to IROS 2021\nOct, 2020\nSwingBot\nreceived\nbest paper award\nat IROS 2020\nResearch\nDexCap: Scalable and Portable Mocap Data Collection System for Dexterous Manipulation\nChen Wang\n,Â Haochen Shi,Â Weizhuo Wang,Â Ruohan Zhang,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â andÂ C. Karen Liu\nRobotics: Science and Systems, RSS 2024\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nSequential Dexterity: Chaining Dexterous Policies for Long-Horizon Manipulation\nYuanpei Chen*,Â\nChen Wang*\n,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â andÂ C. Karen Liu\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2023\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nMimicPlay: Long-horizon Imitation Learning by Watching Human Play\nChen Wang\n,Â Linxi Fan,Â Jiankai Sun,Â Ruohan Zhang,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â Danfei Xu,Â Yuke Zhu*,Â andÂ Anima Anandkumar*\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2023\nOral presentation\nFinalist - Best Paper/Best Student Paper Awards\nFinalist - Best Systems Paper Award\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nObject-Centric Dexterous Manipulation from Human Motion Data\nYuanpei Chen,Â\nChen Wang\n,Â Yaodong Yang,Â andÂ C Karen Liu\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2024\nPDF\nWebsite\nReKep: Spatio-Temporal Reasoning of Relational Keypoint Constraints for Robotic Manipulation\nWenlong Huang,Â\nChen Wang*\n,Â Yunzhu Li*,Â Ruohan Zhang,Â andÂ Li Fei-Fei\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2024\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nTRANSIC: Sim-to-Real Policy Transfer by Learning from Online Correction\nYunfan Jiang,Â\nChen Wang\n,Â Ruohan Zhang,Â Jiajun Wu,Â andÂ Li Fei-Fei\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2024\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nVoxPoser: Composable 3D Value Maps for Robotic Manipulation with Language Models\nWenlong Huang,Â\nChen Wang\n,Â Ruohan Zhang,Â Yunzhu Li,Â Jiajun Wu,Â andÂ Li Fei-Fei\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2023\nOral presentation\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nNOIR: Neural Signal Operated Intelligent Robot for Everyday Activities\nSharon Lee*,Â Ruohan Zhang*,Â Minjune Hwang*,Â Ayano Hiranaka*,Â\nChen Wang\n,Â Wensi Ai,Â Jin Jie Ryan Tan,Â Shreya Gupta,Â Yilun Hao,Â Gabrael Levine,Â Ruohan Gao,Â Anthony Norcia,Â Jiajun Wu*,Â andÂ Li Fei-Fei*\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2023\nPDF\nWebsite\nBEHAVIOR-1K: A Benchmark for Embodied AI with 1,000 Everyday Activities and Realistic Simulation\nChengshu Li*,Â Ruohan Zhang*,Â Josiah Wong*,Â Cem Gokmen*,Â Sanjana Srivastava*,Â Roberto Martin-Martin*,Â\nChen Wang*\n,Â Gabrael Levine*,Â Michael Lingelbach,Â Jiankai Sun,Â Mona Anvari,Â Minjune Hwang,Â Manasi Sharma,Â Arman Aydin,Â Dhruva Bansal,Â Samuel Hunter,Â Kyu-Young Kim,Â Alan Lou,Â Caleb R. Matthews,Â Ivan Villa-Renteria,Â Jerry Huayang Tang,Â Claire Tang,Â Fei Xia,Â Silvio Savarese,Â Hyowon Gweon,Â C. Karen Liu,Â Jiajun Wu,Â andÂ Li Fei-Fei\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2022\nOral presentation\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nGeneralizable Task Planning through Representation Pretraining\nChen Wang\n,Â Danfei Xu,Â andÂ Li Fei-Fei\nRobotics and Automation Letters, RA-L 2022\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nCo-GAIL: Learning Diverse Strategies for Human-Robot Collaboration\nChen Wang\n,Â Claudia PÃ©rez-DâArpino,Â Danfei Xu,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â C. Karen Liu,Â andÂ Silvio Savarese\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2021\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nWhat matters in learning from offline human demonstrations for robot manipulation\nAjay Mandlekar,Â Danfei Xu,Â Josiah Wong,Â Soroush Nasiriany,Â\nChen Wang\n,Â Rohun Kulkarni,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â Silvio Savarese,Â Yuke Zhu,Â andÂ Roberto MartÄ±Ìn-MartÄ±Ìn\nConference on Robot Learning, CoRL 2021\nOral presentation\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nGeneralization through hand-eye coordination: An action space for learning spatially-invariant visuomotor control\nChen Wang*\n,Â Rui Wang*,Â Ajay Mandlekar,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â Silvio Savarese,Â andÂ Danfei Xu\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems, IROS 2021\nPDF\nWebsite\nVideo\nSwingbot: Learning physical features from in-hand tactile exploration for dynamic swing-up manipulation\nChen Wang*\n,Â Shaoxiong Wang*,Â Branden Romero,Â Filipe Veiga,Â andÂ Edward Adelson\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems, IROS 2020\nBest Paper Award\nPDF\nWebsite\nVideo\nPatent\n6-PACK: Category-level 6d pose tracker with anchor-based keypoints\nChen Wang\n,Â Roberto MartÄ±Ìn-MartÄ±Ìn,Â Danfei Xu,Â Jun Lv,Â Cewu Lu,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â Silvio Savarese,Â andÂ Yuke Zhu\nInternational Conference on Robotics and Automation, ICRA 2020\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nDensefusion: 6d object pose estimation by iterative dense fusion\nChen Wang\n,Â Danfei Xu,Â Yuke Zhu,Â Roberto MartÄ±Ìn-MartÄ±Ìn,Â Cewu Lu,Â Li Fei-Fei,Â andÂ Silvio Savarese\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition, CVPR 2019\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nVideo\nTransferable force-torque dynamics model for peg-in-hole task\nJunfeng Ding*,Â\nChen Wang*\n,Â andÂ Cewu Lu\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems, IROS 2019\nPDF\nVideo\nTendencyRL: Multi-stage discriminative hints for efficient goal-oriented reverse curriculum learning\nChen Wang*\n,Â Junfeng Ding*,Â Xiangyu Chen,Â Zelin Ye,Â Jialu Wang,Â Ziruo Cai,Â Shixiang Gu,Â andÂ Cewu Lu\nDeep Reinforcement Learning Symposium, NIPS Symposium 2017\nPoster\nVideo"
