    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYong Zhang\nCV\nDr. Yong Zhang (張勇) has broad research interests including Corporate Governance, Financial Regulations, Executive Compensation, Insider Trading, and the role of media in financial markets. His research has been published in leading research journals in both accounting and finance (\nJournal of Accounting Research\n,\nManagement Science, Contemporary Accounting Research, Review of Accounting Studies, Journal of Banking and Finance, Journal of Accounting Auditing and Finance,\nand\nJournal of Accounting and Public Policy\n).\nHis work has been featured in\nHarvard Law School Forum on Corporate Governance and Financial Regulation\nand\nColumbia Law School's Blog on Corporations and the Capital Markets\nand presented in conferences such as NBER and AFA\n.\n***I am currently accepting applications for Postdoctoral Fellows, Research Assistants/Associates and\nPhD students\n.\nPostdoctoral Fellows\n:\nInitial employment period will be 6-12 months, with possible extensions. Compensation will be competitive. Preferred candidates should have doctoral degrees in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or related quantitative research areas. Please send your CV and related supporting documents (e.g., working papers) to\nyongzhang@polyu.edu.hk\n.\nResearch Assistants/Associates\n: Current research master students or PhD students with exceptional capabilities and a strong desire to conduct top-tier research may submit applications for the positions of Research Assistants and Research Associates.\nPhD students\n: C\nandidates for PhD studentship need to have excellent research background\nand a strong desire to conduct top-tier research.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
