    "homepage_text": "Tengda Han\nTengda Han\n(韩腾达)\n/tən-daː/\ntengda@google.com\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\n/\nTwitter\nI am a research scientist at\nGoogle DeepMind\n.\n            I was a post-doctoral research fellow in\nVGG\nat the University of Oxford. \n            I obtained my PhD degree in the same group, supervised by\nAndrew Zisserman\n.\n    I train neural networks to understand videos.\nI obtained a Bachelor of Engineering degree in\nAustralian National University\n,\n    with a major in mechanical & material engineering.\nI had chance to work on deep learning projects with\nBasura Fernando\n,\nAnoop Cherian\n,\nMehrtash Harandi\n,\nStephen Gould\nand\nRichard Hartley\n.\nBefore that, I studied business administration and law in\nRenmin University of China\n, \n    Beijing, for one year.\nOriginally, I am from the suburbs of\nHangzhou\n, China.\nNews\n[Jan. 2026] 1 paper \"\nDynamic Reflection\n\" accepted by ICLR! Congrats Tyler!\n[Jul. 2025] 1 paper on \"\nAD for animations\n\" accepted by ACMMM! Congrats Zhongrui!\n[Jun. 2025] 1 paper \"\nShot-by-Shot\n\" accepted by ICCV! Congrats Junyu!\n[Apr. 2025] Co-organizing the \"\nSLoMo\n\"  workshop on Movie Understanding at ICCV25.\n[Feb. 2025] 1 paper \"\nOrthogonal Optimizer\n\" accepted by CVPR!\n[Dec. 2024] Co-organizing the\nSelf-Supervised Learning workshop\nat NeurIPS!\n[Dec. 2024] Our paper on\nUnique Video Captioning\ngets the Best Paper Award at ACCV! Big congrats to Toby!\n[Sep. 2024] 2 papers \"\nAutoAD-Zero\n\" and \n    \"\nUnique Video Captioning\n\" accepted by ACCV, \n    1 paper \"\nCountGD\n\" accepted by NeurIPS! Great work from Junyu, Toby and Niki!\n[Apr. 2024] Published\nStale Diffusion: Hyper-realistic 5D Movie Generation Using Old-school Methods\non April 1st. Enjoy reading!\n[Mar. 2024] Join Google DeepMind in London, as a research scientist.\nMore\n[Mar. 2024] 2 papers \"\nAutoAD-III\n\" and \"\nUnsupervised Counting\n\" accepted by CVPR2024.\n[Feb. 2024] Give a talk at\nÉcole des Ponts ParisTech\non Movie Audio Description.\n[Jan. 2024] Co-organizing the\nLearning from Procedural Videos and Language\n. See you in Seattle!\n[Jan. 2024] Co-organizing the\nBMVA Symposium on Vision and Language\nwith\nMichael Wray\nand\nDavide Moltisanti\n. See you in London!\n[Dec. 2023] Give talks at\nShanghai Jiao Tong University\nand\nThe AI Talks\non Long Video Understanding.\n[Nov. 2023] Our paper \"\nOpen-world Text-specified Object Counting\n\" received \n    the Best Poster Award at BMVC2023. Congrats to Niki!\n[Nov. 2023] Received the BMVA\nSullivan Doctoral Thesis Prize Runner-up\n.\n[Aug. 2023] 1 paper \"\nOpen-world Text-specified Object Counting\n\" accepted by BMVC2023.\n[Jul. 2023] 1 paper \"\nAutoAD II\n\" accepted by ICCV2023.\n[Jul. 2023] Our workshop \"\nSelf-Supervised Learning - Theory and Practice\n\" jointly organised with\nIshan Misra\n,\nMathilde Caron\n,\nHilde Kuehne\nand\nPengtao Xie\nis accepted by NeurIPS'23! We are accepting paper submissions!\n[Jun. 2023] Give a talk on\nThe First Edinburgh Workshop on Affordable Machine Learning\n.\n[Slides pdf]\n[Apr. 2023] Our workshop \"\nBigMAC: Big Model Adaptation for Computer vision\n\"\n    jointly organised with\nYuki Asano\n,\nMathilde Caron\n,\nPhillip Isola\nand\nSerge Belongie\n,\n    is accepted by ICCV'23. See you in Paris!\n[Mar. 2023] 1 paper \"\nAutoAD: Movie Description in Context\n\"\n    accepted by CVPR2023 with Highlight.\n[Nov. 2022] Passed my PhD with \"no corrections\" (\nthesis pdf\n). \n    My examiners are\nCarl Vondrick\nand\nAndrea Vedaldi\n.\n[Sept. 2022] 1 paper \"Turbo Training with Token Dropout\" accepted by BMVC2022.\n[Jul. 2022] 1 paper \"\nPrompting Visual-Language Models for Efficient Video Understanding\n\" accepted by ECCV2022.\n[Mar. 2022] 1 paper \"\nTemporal Alignment Networks\n\" \n    accepted by CVPR2022 as an oral.\n[Aug. 2021 - Dec. 2021] Research Scientist Intern at DeepMind hosted by\nJean-Baptiste Alayrac\n. \n    I am in the\nFlamingo project\n.\n[Sep. 2020] 1 paper \"\nSelf-supervised Co-Training (CoCLR)\n\"\n    accepted by NeurIPS2020.\nPublications\nMisc\nA\ntemplate\nto produce your PhD thesis from arXiv zip files, \n    liked by a few Oxford PhDs.\nA\nweb server\nto monitor\nSLURM\nresource, internally used in VGG."
  },
