    "homepage_text": "Welcome to My Space - Feng Gao\nFeng Gao\nI’m an activitist, researcher and practitioner promoting and builiding an open digital future in China.  Co-Founder of Open Data China, and SODA. Proudly on the board of Open Supply Hub, and Shanghai Association of AI and Social Development.\nFollow\nLinkedin\nTwitter (not personal account)\nGitHub\nWelcome to My Space\nRecent News\nI am appointed as a member of “Digital SuZhou” Advisory Committee by the SuZhou City Government.\nA new series of blogs “剖析公共数据授权运营” were published on the Open Data China Wechat Account\nA new invited op-ed as part of\n“The Impact of the Establishment of the National Data Bureau on the Future of Big Data”\nwas published on Journal of Documentation, Information&Knowledge\nThe new paper\n“Investigation into Authorized Public Data Operation: Its Positioning and Nature”\nwas published on the Journal of Big Data\nFeatured Works\nODI Fridays: Open data and China – a ten year review\n(Vdieo)\n,\nMay 2021, Open Data Institute\nOpen A Can of SODA – Driving Urban Data Innovation with Openness as its Principle\n，2017, Paris Innovation Review\nData Institutions in China:stewarding data in the cultural and migrant population sectors\n, Feb 2023, Open Data Institute Research Fellowship Report\nAdvancing Data Justice Research and Practice: China Report\n, March 2022, Advancing Data Justice Project led by Alan Turing Institute\nEnter your search term..."
