  "serper::Weiran Shen": {
    "homepage": "https://www.weiran-shen.info/",
    "emails": [
      "shenweiran@ruc.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Weiran Shen\n中文\nWeiran Shen\nTenure-Track Associate Professor\nGaoling School of Artificial Intelligence\nRenmin University of China\nAddress:\n59 Zhongguancun St.\nHaidian District\nBeijing, China\nEmail:\nshenweiran AT ruc DOT edu DOT cn\nAbout me\nI am an tenure-track associate professor at Gaoling School of Artificial Intelligence, Renmin University of China. Before joining Renmin University, I was a post doctoral researcher at ISR, Carnegie Mellon University, working with\nFei Fang\n. I obtained my Ph.D. at IIIS, Tsinghua University, advised by Pingzhong Tang, and my B.E. at Department of Electronic Engineering, Tsinghua University.\nMy research interest lies in the interface of economics and computation, especially auction and mechanism design, game theory, multi-agent systems and machine learning.\nPublications\n2026\n[\nPDF\n]\nThe Power of Initial Investigation in Audit Games. AAAI-2026\nRen Liu, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nIBCB: Efficient Inverse Batched Contextual Bandit for Behavioral Evolution History. IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI)\nYi Xu, Weiran Shen, Jun Xu, Xiao Zhang, Ji-Rong Wen.\n2025\n[\nPDF\n]\nMultiplayer General Lotto Game. WINE-2025\nYan Liu, Bonan Ni, Weiran Shen, Zihe Wang, Jie Zhang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nStackelberg vs. Nash in the Lottery Colonel Blotto Game. IJCAI-2025\nYan Liu, Bonan Ni, Weiran Shen, Zihe Wang, Jie Zhang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nPublic Signaling in Markets with Information Asymmetry Using a Limited Number of Signals. IJCAI-2025\nXu Zhao, Ren Liu, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nOptimizing Revenue through User Coupon Recommendations in Truthful Online Ad Auctions. WWW-2025\nXiaodong Liu, Yiming Ding, Xiao Lin, Changcheng Li, Peng Jiang, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nTwo-stage Auction Design in Online Advertising. WWW-2025\nZhikang Fan, Lan Hu, Ruirui Wang, Zhongrui Ma, Yue Wang, Qi Ye, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nBalancing Revenue and Privacy with Signaling Schemes in Online Ad Auctions. WSDM-2025\nHongtao Liu, Luxi Chen, Yiming Ding, Changcheng Li, Han Li, Peng Jiang, Weiran Shen.\n2024\n[\nPDF\n] [\nOnline version\n]\nLTP-MMF: Towards Long-term Provider Max-min Fairness Under Recommendation Feedback Loops. ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS)\nChen Xu, Xiaopeng Ye, Jun Xu, Xiao Zhang, Weiran Shen, Ji-Rong Wen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nSRAP-agent: Simulating and Optimizing Scarce Resource Allocation Policy with LLM-based Agent. EMNLP-2024 (Findings)\nJiarui Ji, Yang Li, Hongtao Liu, Zhicheng Du, Zhewei Wei, Qi Qi, Weiran Shen, Yankai Lin.\n[\nPDF\n] [\nOnline version\n]\nAn Extensive Study of Security Games with Strategic Informants. Artificial Intelligence (AIJ)\nSubsumes the IJCAI conference version.\nWeiran Shen, Minbiao Han, Weizhe Chen, Taoan Huang, Rohit Singh, Haifeng Xu, Fei Fang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nOptimal Auction Design with User Coupons in Advertising Systems. IJCAI-2024\nXiaodong Liu, Zhikang Fan, Yiming Ding, Yuan Guo, Lihua Zhang, Changcheng Li, Dongying Kong, Han Li, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n] [\nOnline version\n]\nA mechanism design approach for multi-party machine learning. Theoretical Computer Science (TCS)\nSubsumes the IJTCS-FAW conference version.\nMengjing Chen, Yang Liu, Weiran Shen, Yiheng Shen, Pingzhong Tang, Qiang Yang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nA Fast Algorithm for k Memory Messaging Scheme Design in Dynamic Environments with Uncertainty. ICAPS-2024\nZhikang Fan, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nSimultaneous Optimization of Bid Shading and Internal Auction for Demand-Side Platforms. AAAI-2024\nYadong Xu, Bonan Ni, Weiran Shen, Xun Wang, Zichen Wang, Yinsong Xue, Pingzhong Tang.\n2023\n[\nPDF\n]\nAuto-bidding with Budget and ROI Constrained Buyers. IJCAI-2023\nXiaodong Liu, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nRevenue Maximization Mechanisms for an Uninformed Mediator with Communication Abilities. IJCAI-2023\nZhikang Fan, Weiran Shen.\n[\nPDF\n]\nDeep Generative Modeling on Limited Data with Regularization by Nontransferable Pre-trained Models. ICLR-2023\nYong Zhong, Hongtao Liu, Xiaodong Liu, Fan Bao, Weiran Shen, Chongxuan Li.\n[\nPDF\n]\nP-MMF Provider Max-min Fairness Re-ranking in Recommender System. WWW-2023\nChen Xu, Sirui Chen, Jun Xu, Weiran Shen, Xiao Zhang, Gang Wang, Zhenhua Dong.\n2022\n[\nPDF\n]\nInverse Game Theory for Stackelberg Games: the Blessing of Bounded Rationality. NeurIPS-2022\nJibang Wu, Weiran Shen, Fei Fang, Haifeng Xu.\n[\nPDF\n]\nA Mechanism Design Approach for Multi-Party Machine Learning. IJTCS-FAW-2022\nMengjing Chen, Yang Liu, Weiran Shen, Yiheng Shen, Pingzhong Tang, Qiang Yang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nOptimal pricing policy design for selling cost-reducing innovation in Cournot games. Theoretical Computer Science (TCS)\nMengjing Chen, Haoqiang Huang, Weiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang, Zihe Wang, Jie Zhang.\n2021\n[\nPDF\n] [\nOnline version\n]\nCoalitional permutation manipulations in the Gale-Shapley algorithm. Artificial Intelligence (AIJ)\nSubsumes the AAMAS conference version.\nWeiran Shen, Yuan Deng, Pingzhong Tang.\n[\narXiv version\n]\nOptimal Pricing of Information. EC-2021\nShuze Liu, Weiran Shen, Haifeng Xu.\n[\nPDF\n]\nCoupon Design in Advertising Systems. AAAI-2021\nWeiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang, Xun Wang, Yadong Xu, Xiwang Yang.\n2020\n[\nPDF\n]\nHarnessing the Power of Deception in Attack Graph-Based Security Games. GameSec-2020\nStephanie Milani, Weiran Shen, Kevin S. Chan, Sridhar Venkatesan, Nandi O. Leslie, Charles Kamhoua and Fei Fang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nWhen to Follow the Tip: Security Games with Strategic Informants. IJCAI-2020\nWeiran Shen, Weizhe Chen, Taoan Huang, Rohit Singh and Fei Fang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nGreen Security Game with Community Engagement. AAMAS-2020\nTaoan Huang, Weiran Shen, David Zeng, Tianyu Gu, Rohit Singh and Fei Fang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nLearning to Design Coupons in Online Advertising Markets. AAMAS-2020\nWeiran Shen, Xun Wang, Yadong Xu, Xiwang Yang and Pingzhong Tang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nBayesian Nash Equilibrium in First-Price Auction with Discrete Value Distributions. AAMAS-2020\nZihe Wang, Weiran Shen and Song Zuo.\n[\nPDF\n]\nReinforcement Mechanism Design: With Applications to Dynamic Pricing in Sponsored Search Auctions. AAAI-2020\nWeiran Shen, Binghui Peng, Hanpeng Liu, Michael Zhang, Ruohan Qian, Yan Hong, Zhi Guo, Zongyao Ding, Pengjun Lu and Pingzhong Tang.\n2019\n[\nPDF\n]\nDispatching through pricing: modeling ride-sharing and designing dynamic prices. IJCAI-2019\nMengjing Chen, Weiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang and Song Zuo.\n[\nPDF\n]\nLearning to clear the market. ICML-2019\nWeiran Shen, Sébastien Lahaie and Renato Paes Leme.\n[\nPDF\n] [\narXiv version\n]\nAutomated mechanism design via neural networks. AAMAS-2019\nWeiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang and Song Zuo.\n[\nPDF\n]\nBuyer signaling games in auctions. AAMAS-2019\nWeiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang and Yulong Zeng.\n[\nPDF\n]\nLearning optimal strategies to commit to. AAAI-2019\nBinghui Peng, Weiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang and Song Zuo.\n2018\n[\nPDF\n]\nEx-post IR dynamic auctions with cost-per-action payments. IJCAI-2018\nWeiran Shen, Zihe Wang and Song Zuo.\n[\nPDF\n]\nCoalitional permutation manipulations in the Gale-Shapley algorithm. AAMAS-2018\nYuan Deng, Weiran Shen and Pingzhong Tang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nA closed-form characterization of buyer signaling schemes in monopoly pricing. AAMAS-2018\nWeiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang and Yulong Zeng.\n[\nPDF\n]\nBuyer-optimal distribution. AAMAS-2018\nWeiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang and Yulong Zeng.\n[\nPDF\n]\nCoalition manipulation of Gale-Shapley algorithm. AAAI-2018\nYuan Deng, Weiran Shen and Pingzhong Tang.\n2017\n[\nPDF\n]\nPractical versus optimal mechanisms. AAMAS-2017\nWeiran Shen, Pingzhong Tang.\n[\nPDF\n]\nHotelling-Downs model with limited attraction. AAMAS-2017\nWeiran Shen, Zihe Wang."
  },
  "serper::Dawen Liang": {
    "homepage": "https://dawenl.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Dawen Liang\nDawen Liang\nEmail:\nI am a member of technical staff at\nxAI\n. Before that, I was a research scientist at\nNetflix\nand worked on personalization, policy learning, and LLM post-training. I completed my Ph.D. in the\nElectrical\nEngineering Department\nat\nColumbia University\n, \nas part of the\nLabROSA\n,\nworking with\nProfessor Dan\nEllis\nand\nProfessor David Blei\n.\nPrior to that, I completed my master's degree in\nMusic and Technology program\nat\nCarnegie Mellon University\n, working with\nProfessor Roger Dannenberg\nin the\nSchool of Computer Science\n, where I was part of the\nComputer Music Group\n.\nPapers\nFor the most up-to-date information please see my\nGoogle Scholar\npage.\nMiscellaneous\nHere are some (very old) notes regarding some topics I found interesting. \nI wrote these just for fun (and I hope they can be useful to someone in the future).\nTherefore, there might be mistakes/errors in these notes. \nIf you find any problems, please let me know.\nA proof\nthat Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) is\nbiased for variance estimator.\nA note\nthat shows some useful properties for matrix\nderivative.\nSome technical details\nfor the Expectation Maximization (EM)\nalgorithm.\nPage generated 2025-11-25 21:41:02 PST, by\njemdoc\n."
  },
  "serper::Xiaojie Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/xjwang/home",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Xiaojie Wang's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nXiaojie Wang's Homepage\nWelcome to Xiaojie Wang's Homepage\nBibliography\nI am with Qualcomm Inc. New Jersey Research Center since 2020, conducting\nwireless research on\nphysical and MAC layer\nfor\n5G/6G and beyond (i\nncluding 3GPP RAN1 standardization\n).\nI obtained my B.Sc,  M.Sc (with Honors), PhD (Summa Cum Laude) in Electrical and Communication Engineering at University of Stuttgart in 2012, 2014 and 2019, respectively. My research focus is novel multi-carrier waveform, massive MIMO, iterative detection and decoding, and non-orthogonal multiple access techniques.\nI am passionate about doing research for communication systems and gathered research and development experience in the physical layer of wireless and optical communications systems, particularly, error control codes, waveform design, multi-user detection and digital signal processing.\nPublications\nPatent\nT. Wild,\nX. Wang\nand F. Schaich,\nChoice of filter sideband supression according to channel quality in universal filtered multicarrier\n,\ngranted 2016.\nOver 200 pending patents on 5G/6G wireless.\nPapers\nP. Gupta, S. Fong,\nX. Wang\n, et. al.,\nEnhancing 5G URLLC for Industrial IoT with Device-to-Device Communication\n,\nIEEE I\nnt. Sym. on Wireless Comm. Systems (ISWCS), 2021.\nX. Wang\nand S. ten Brink,\nSINR Analysis of Different Multicarrier Waveforms over Doubly Dispersive Channels,\nIEEE Trans. Veh. Technol., 2020.\nB. Peng,\nX. Wang\nand S. ten Brink,\nOn Receive Window Design for UF-OFDM Signals over Multipath Channels,\nIEEE Wireless Comm. Letters, 2020.\nX. Wang\n, C. Liang, L. Ping and S. ten Brink,\nAchievable Rate Region for Iterative Multi-User Detection via Low-cost Gaussian Approximation\n, IEEE Trans. Wireless Comm., 2020.\nM. Arnold,\nX. Wang\nand S. ten Brink,\nExploiting Sparsity in Measured Massive MIMO: Compressive Sensing vs Codebook based Precoding,\nUnder Review, Trans. Wireless Comm., 2019.\nD. Verenzuela, E. Björnson,\nX. Wang\n, M. Arnold and S. ten Brink,\nMassive-MIMO Iterative Channel Estimation and Decoding (MICED) in the Uplink\n,  IEEE Trans. Comm., 2019.\nX. Wang\n, S. Cammerer and S. ten Brink,\nNear-Capacity Detection and Decoding: Code Design for Dynamic User Loads in Gaussian Multiple Access Channels\n, IEEE Trans. Comm., 2019.\nS. Cammerer,\nX. Wang\nand S. ten Brink,\nSpatially Coupled LDPC Codes and the Multiple Access Channel\n, Conf. on Inform. Sciences and Syst., Baltimore, USA, 2019.\nX. Wang\n, C. Liang, L. Ping and S. ten Brink,\nAchievable Rate Region for Iterative Multi-User Detection via Low-cost Gaussian Approximation\n, Int. Symp. Inform. Theory, Paris, French, 2019.\nX. Wang\n, M. Arnold and S. ten Brink,\nTDD and FDD Massive MIMO: Channel Coherence and Operation Region\n, Workshop on Smart Antennas, Wien, Austria, 2019.\nX. Wang\n, S. Cammerer and S. ten Brink,\nNear Gaussian Multiple Access Channel Capacity Detection and Decoding\n, Int. Symp. Turbo Codes and Iterative Inform. Process., Hongkong, China, 2018.\nX. Wang\n, S. Burkert and S. ten Brink,\nOptimally Combining Active Interference Cancellation and FIR-Filtering for Spectral Shaping of Multicarrier Waveforms\n, Asilomar Conf. on Signals, Syst. and Computers, Pacific Grove, USA, 2018.\nM. Arnold,\nX. Wang\nand S. ten Brink,\nSubcarrier-interlaced FDD for faster-than-TDD channel tracking in massive MIMO systems\n, Worshop on Smart Antennas Bochum, Germany, 2018.\nX. Wang\n, S. Burkert and S. ten Brink,\nOn Peak to Average Power Ratio of Universal Filtered OFDM Signals\n, Int. Sym. Personal, Indoor and Mobile Radio Comm., Montreal, Canada, 2017.\nX. Wang\nand S. ten Brink,\nIterative MIMO Subspace Detection based on Parallel Interference Cancellation\n, Wireless Comm. and Networking Conf., San Francisco, USA, 2017.\nX. Wang\n, K. Kienzle and S. ten Brink,\nOn Spectral Shaping of Multicarrier Waveforms Employing FIR-Filtering and Active Interference Cancellation\n, Int. Conf. on Syst., Comm. and Coding, Hamburg, Germany, 2017.\nX. Wang\n, B. Leible, W. Wang, D. Rörich and S. ten Brink,\nJoint IQ Imbalance Compensation and Channel Estimation in Coherent Optical OFDM Systems\n, Int. Conf. on Signal Process. and Comm. Syst., Gold Coast, Australia, 2016.\nX. Wang\n, T. Wild, F. Schaich and S. ten Brink,\nPilot-aided Channel Estimation for Universal Filtered Multi-Carrier\n, Veh. Techno. Conf. Fall, Bosten, USA, 2015.\nX. Wang\n, T. Wild and F. Schaich,\nFilter Optimization for Carrier-Frequency- and Timing-Offset in Universal Filtered Multi-Carrier Systems\n, Veh. Techno. Conf. Spring, Glasgow, UK, 2015.\nX. Wang\n, T. Wild, F. Schaich and A. Santos,\nUniversal Filtered Multi-Carrier with Leakage-Based Filter Optimization\n, European Wireless Conf., Barcelona, Spain, 2014.\nD. Rörich,\nX. Wang\n, M. Bernhard and J. Speidel,\nOptimal Modulation Index of the Mach-Zehnder Modulator in a Coherent Optical OFDM System Employing Digital Predistortion\n,\nITG Symposium Photonic Networks, Leipzip, Germany, 2013.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
