    "homepage_text": "Rui Zhang | Homepage\nRui Zhang\nPostdoc Research Fellow\nThe University of Hong Kong\nOffice: P207, Graduate House, HKU\nAbout\nI am a\nPostdoc Research Fellow\nat the HKU Musketeers Foundation Institute of Data Science (IDS), The University of Hong Kong (HKU), working with Prof.\nHo Chen\n. Before that, I obtained my Ph.D. in Computer Science from The Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU). My research interests include\nAI security & privacy\n,\ntrustworthy machine learning\n,\ndistributed learning\n, and\nLLM-based applications\n.\nPlease feel free to reach out if you have any questions or would like to collaborate on research projects!\nNews\nJun 2025:\nOur paper \"Geminio: Language-Guided Gradient Inversion Attacks in Federated Learning\" has been accepted to ICCV 2025! 🎉\nMay 2025:\nI have successfully received my Ph.D. from The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. 🎓\nMar 2025:\nI have successfully completed my Ph.D. oral defense! Thanks to my supervisors, committee members and everyone who supported me throughout this journey. 🎉🙏\nDec 2024:\nI have received the 3rd prize in the Four Minute Thesis (4MT) Competition at IEEE GLOBECOM 2024. 🎉\nPublications\nThe full list of publications is on\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nSelected\nAll\nBuilding Gradient Bridges: Label Leakage from Restricted Gradient Sharing in Federated Learning\nRui Zhang\n, Ka-Ho Chow, Ping Li\narXiv preprint, 2025\nPaper\nGeminio: Language-Guided Gradient Inversion Attacks in Federated Learning\nJunjie Shan, Ziqi Zhao, Jialin Lu,\nRui Zhang\n, Siu Ming Yiu, Ka-Ho Chow\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2025\nPaper\nCode\nGradFilt: Class-wise Targeted Data Reconstruction from Gradients in Federated Learning\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo, Ping Li\nThe Web Conference (WWW), 2024\nPaper\nVideo\nPosterior Probability-based Label Recovery Attack in Federated Learning\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo, Ping Li\nICLR PML Workshop, 2024\nPaper\nA Survey on Gradient Inversion: Attacks, Defenses and Future Directions\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo, Junxiao Wang, Xin Xie, Dacheng Tao\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI), 2022\nPaper\nVideo\nCycle: Sustainable Off-Chain Payment Channel Network with Asynchronous Rebalancing\nZicong Hong, Song Guo,\nRui Zhang\n, Peng Li, Yunfeng Zhan, Wuhui Chen\nInternational Conference on Dependable Systems and Networks (DSN), 2022\nPaper\nVideo\nBuilding Gradient Bridges: Label Leakage from Restricted Gradient Sharing in Federated Learning\nRui Zhang\n, Ka-Ho Chow, Ping Li\narXiv preprint, 2025\nPaper\nGeminio: Language-Guided Gradient Inversion Attacks in Federated Learning\nJunjie Shan, Ziqi Zhao, Jialin Lu,\nRui Zhang\n, Siu Ming Yiu, Ka-Ho Chow\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2025\nPaper\nCode\nGradFilt: Class-wise Targeted Data Reconstruction from Gradients in Federated Learning\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo, Ping Li\nThe Web Conference (WWW), 2024\nPaper\nVideo\nPosterior Probability-based Label Recovery Attack in Federated Learning\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo, Ping Li\nICLR PML Workshop, 2024\nPaper\nPrivacy Inference for Data Auditing\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo\nInternational Symposium on AI, Data and Digitalization (SAIDD), 2023\nPaper\nMGIA: Mutual Gradient Inversion Attack in MultiModal Federated Learning (Student Abstract)\nXuan Liu, Siqi Cai, Lin Li,\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI), 2023\nPaper\nA Survey on Gradient Inversion: Attacks, Defenses and Future Directions\nRui Zhang\n, Song Guo, Junxiao Wang, Xin Xie, Dacheng Tao\nInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI), 2022\nPaper\nVideo\nCycle: Sustainable Off-Chain Payment Channel Network with Asynchronous Rebalancing\nZicong Hong, Song Guo,\nRui Zhang\n, Peng Li, Yunfeng Zhan, Wuhui Chen\nInternational Conference on Dependable Systems and Networks (DSN), 2022\nPaper\nVideo\nA Novel Pseudonym Linking Scheme for Privacy Inference in VANETs\nRui Zhang\n, Xin Wang, Peng Cheng, Jiming Chen.\nVehicular Technology Conference (VTC), 2020\nPaper\nAn Industrial Control System Testbed for the Encrypted Controller\nXing Li, Mengxiang Liu,\nRui Zhang\n, Peng Cheng, Jiming Chen\nInternational Conference on Cyber-Physical Systems (ICCPS), 2018\nPaper\nA Simulation-based Platform for Privacy Preservation Research in VANETs\nPeng Cheng,\nRui Zhang\n, Linkang Du, Jiming Chen\nChinese Patent (No. CN110189517B), 2020\nPaper\nExperiences\nThe University of Hong Kong\n2025 - now\nPostdoc Research Fellow\nMusketeers Foundation Institute of Data Science\nThe Hong Kong Polytechnic University\n2020 - 2025\nPh.D. Student\nComputer Science\nZhejiang University\n2017 - 2020\nM.Eng. Student\nControl Science and Engineering\nZhejiang Lab\nSummer 2019\nResearch Scientist, Intern\nResearch Center for Intelligent Equipment\nNortheastern University\n2013 - 2017\nB.Eng. Student\nAutomation\nFirst Class Honors\nServices\nConference Reviewer\nJournal Reviewer\nProgram Committee\nACL\n(2025)\nICCV\n(2025)\nICLR\n(2025-2026)\nAAAI\n(2025-2026)\nCVPR\n(2024-2026)\nIJCAI\n(2024-2025)\nINFOCOM\n(2022-2024)\nIEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems (TPDS)\nACM Computing Surveys (CSUR)\nJournal of Sensors\nIEEE Access\nAAAI\n(2025-2026)\nIJCAI\n(2024-2025)\nTeachings\nTeaching Assistant\nat PolyU:\nMachine Learning (COMP4432)\n- Spring 2023\nArtificial Intelligence (COMP4431)\n- Fall 2022\nArtificial Intelligence (COMP4431)\n- Fall 2021\nWireless Network and Mobile Computing (COMP5327)\n- Spring 2021\nAcknowledgement\nThis webpage was built based on a template by\nMartin Saveski\n.\n  Thanks for the author's contribution.\nRui Zhang\nUpdated: November 15, 2025"
