    "homepage_text": "Sen Yang | Homepage\n🧐\nSen Yang\nPhD Candidate in Computer Science\nYale University\nAbout Me\nI am a fourth-year PhD candidate in the Computer Science Department at Yale University. I am very fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Fan Zhang\n. Previously, I obtained my Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees from Fudan University.\nMy research focuses on analyzing potential issues in decentralized systems, especially those related to\nMaximal Extractable Value (MEV)\n. Feel free to reach out if you are interested in my work or in collaborating with me!\nPublications\nManuscripts\nBoost+: Equitable, Incentive-Compatible Block Building\nMengqian Zhang*,\nSen Yang*\n, Kartik Nayak, Fan Zhang.\narXiv\nLifefin: Escaping Mempool Explosions in DAG-based BFT.\nJianting Zhang,\nSen Yang\n, Alberto Sonnino, Sebastián Loza, Aniket Kate.\narXiv\nGeographical Centralization Resilience in Ethereum’s Block-Building Paradigm.\nSen Yang\n, Burak Öz, Fei Wu, Fan Zhang.\narXiv\n,\nblog post\n,\ndemo\nInsecurity Through Obscurity: Veiled Vulnerabilities in Closed-Source Contracts.\nSen Yang\n, Kaihua Qin, Aviv Yaish, Fan Zhang.\narXiv\n,\nblog post\nPublished Papers\nRediSwap: MEV Redistribution Mechanism for CFMMs.\nMengqian Zhang,\nSen Yang\n, Fan Zhang. In DeFi'25.\nACM DL\n,\narXiv\n,\ncode\nAgora: Trust Less and Open More in Verification for Confidential Computing.\nHongbo Chen, Quan Zhou,\nSen Yang\n, Sixuan Dang, Xing Han, Danfeng Zhang, Fan Zhang, XiaoFeng Wang. In OOPSLA'25.\nACM DL\n,\narXiv\n,\nposter\n,\ncode\nDecentralization of Ethereum’s Builder Market.\nSen Yang\n, Kartik Nayak, Fan Zhang. In IEEE S&P'25.\narXiv\n,\nIEEE Xplore\n,\nblog post\n,\ncode & dataset\nSoK: MEV Countermeasures.\nSen Yang\n, Fan Zhang, Ken Huang, Xi Chen, Youwei Yang, Feng Zhu. In DeFi'24.\nfull version on arXiv\n,\nACM DL\nMISO: Legacy-compatible Privacy-preserving Single Sign-on using Trusted Execution Environments.\nRongwu Xu,\nSen Yang\n, Fan Zhang, Zhixuan Fang. In EuroS&P'23.\narXiv\n,\nIEEE Xplore\nAnalyzing Ground-Truth Data of Mobile Gambling Scams.\nGeng Hong, Zhemin Yang,\nSen Yang\n, Xiaojing Liao, Xiaolin Du, Min Yang, Haixin Duan. In IEEE S&P'22.\nIEEE Xplore\nCoverage-Guided Tensor Compiler Fuzzing with Joint IR-Pass Mutation.\nJiawei Liu, Yuxiang Wei,\nSen Yang\n, Yinlin Deng, Lingming Zhang. In OOPSLA'22.\nACM DL\n,\ncode\nApp in the Middle: Demystify Application Virtualization in Android and its Security Threats.\nLei Zhang, Zhemin Yang, Yuyu He, Mingqi Li,\nSen Yang\n, Min Yang, Yuan Zhang, Zhiyun Qian. In SIGMETRICS'19.\nACM DL\nHow You Get Shot in the Back: A Systematical Study about Cryptojacking in the Real World.\nGeng Hong, Zhemin Yang,\nSen Yang\n, Lei Zhang, Yuhong Nan, Zhibo Zhang, Min Yang, Yuan Zhang, Zhiyun Qian, Haixin Duan. In ACM CCS'18.\nACM DL\n,\ncode\nTeaching\nTeaching Assistant, 2025 Fall, Full Stack Web Programming, Yale University\nTeaching Assistant, 2025 Spring, Full Stack Web Programming, Yale University\nTeaching Assistant, 2024 Fall, Computer System Security, Yale University\nTeaching Assistant, 2022 Spring, Compilers, Fudan University\nTeaching Assistant, 2021 Fall, Computer Network, Fudan University\nTeaching Assistant, 2018 Spring, Web Fundamentals, Fudan University\nServices\nProgram Committee\nCAAW 2026\nOOPSLA 2026 Artifact\nReviewer\nACM Transactions on the Web\nSub-Reviewer\nFC 2026\nIEEE ICDCS 2025\nUSENIX Security 2024/25\nAFT 2023/24\nACM CCS 2018/22\nAsiaCCS 2020"
