    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "é­åä¸°ä¸ªäººä¸»é¡µ----ä¸­ç§é¢ç½ç»æ°æ®ç§å­¦ä¸ææ¯éç¹å®éªå®¤\nJiafeng Guo\nï¼é­åä¸°ï¼\nä¸­ç§é¢è®¡ç®æç ç©¶åï¼åäº¬æºæºå­¦èï¼èæ³éå¹´ç§å­¦å®¶\nProfessor\nInstitute of Computing Technology (ICT),Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS)\nCAS Key Lab of Web Data Science and Technology\nEmail :\nguojiafeng@ict.ac.cn\nOffice :\n(8610)62600936\nAddress :\nNO. 6 Kexueyuan South Road, Haidian District, Beijing, P.R.China,\nBiography\nPublication\nProjects & ToolKits\nStudents & Talks\nJiafeng Guo is currently a Researcher ofâInstitute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences, a Professor ofâUniversity of Chinese Academy of Sciences, as well as a PI ofâBeijing Academy of Artificial Intelligence. He is the director ofâthe CAS key lab of network data science and technology. He received his B.E. in Computer Science and Technology from the University of Science and Technology of China, Hefei, China, in 2004 and earned his Ph.D. in Computer Software and Theory from the University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China, in 2009.\nDr. Guo has worked on a number of topics related to web search and data mining, including query representation and understanding, learning to rank, and text modeling. His current research is focused onâneural models for information retrieval (Neural IR)âandânatural language understanding. He has won theâBest Paper Award in ACM CIKM (2011), Best Student Paper Award in ACM SIGIR (2012), Best Full Paper Runner-up Award in ACM CIKM (2017), Best Paper Award in ACM WSDM (2022) and Best Paper Award in EMNLP (2024).\nHighlight:â\nOpen ToolKit for Deep Text Matching & Neural IR\nâ\nMatchZoo\n3,608\nâ\nMatchZoo-py\n445\nâ\nAwesome-resources\n727\nââ\nHighlight:â\nA Deep Look into Neural Ranking Models for Information Retrieval\nâ(NeuIR Survey)\nHighlight:â\nä¿¡æ¯æ£ç´¢ä¸æ·±åº¦å­¦ä¹\nâ(ä¸è)\nNews\n[Mar. 2025] I will co-organize\nThe First Workshop on Robust Information Retrieval\nââat SIGIR 2025. Looking forward to seeing you in Padova, Italy.\n[Mar. 2025] I co-organized a tutorial on\nRobust Information Retrieval\nat WSDM 2025. The survey on robust information retrieval is available\nhere\n.\n[Nov. 2024] Our paper\nPretraining Data Detection for Large Language Models: A Divergence-based Calibration Method\nwon the Best Paper Award in EMNLP 2024. We presented a new dataset and method for black-box detection of pre-training data.\nHonors and Awards\nNational Awards:â\nSecond Prize for the National Technological Invention Award (2021)\n,â\nSecond Prize for the National Science and Technology Progress (2013)\nProvincial Awards: First Prize of the China Institute of Electronics Science and Technology Progress Award (2024), First Prize of the Qian Weichang Chinese Information Processing Science and Technology Award by the Chinese Information Processing Society of China (2024), First Prize of the China Institute of Electronics Science and Technology Progress Award (2011)\nBest Paper Awards:â\nACM WSDM 2022 Best Paper Award\n,\nACM CIKM 2017 Best Full Paper Runner-up Award\n,â\nACM SIGIR 2012 Best Stuedent Paper Award\n,â\nACM CIKM 2011 Best Paper Award\nPersonal Awards: National Natural Science Foundation--Outstanding Youth Foundation (2017),â\nQian Weichang Chinese Information Processing Science and Technology Award Hanwang Youth Innovation Prize (2012)\n, Excellent Award of Youth Innovation Promotion Associationï¼CAS (2016), the CAS-ICT Outstanding Star Award (2011), the CAS-ICT One-Hundred Research Stars Award (2011), the CAS-ICT Excellent Employee Award (2011)\nOther Awards: Second Prize for the CAS Mobile Innovation Competition on Utility Applications (2013), The CAS-ICT Excellent Team Award (2010), Silver prize for the National Open Source Software Competition (2006)\nAcademic Services\nChairs/Co-Chairs: Reproducibility Paper Co-chair of the 46th ACM SIGIR conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR'23), Workshop Co-chair of the 44th ACM SIGIR conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR'21), Short Paper Co-chair of the 43rd ACM SIGIR conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR'20), Short Paper Co-chair of the 5th ACM SIGIR International Conference on the Theory of Information Retrieval (ICTIR'19), Publicity Co-chair of the 4th ACM SIGIR International Conference on the Theory of Information Retrieval (ICTIR'18), Program Co-chair of the 24th China Conference on Information Retrieval (CCIR'18), Workshop Co-chair of the 8th ACM International WSDM Conference (WSDM'15), Co-chair of the 20th China Conference on Information Retrieval Young Scholar Forum (CCIR'14-CCIR'16)\nSecretary-General: Information Retrieval Technical Committeeï¼Chinese Information Processing Society of China\nAssociate Editor: ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS), Information Retrieval Journal (IRJ), Communication of ACM (China)\nSenior PC Member: SIGIR2022, KDD2022, CIKM2021, AAAI2019, WWW2019, SIGIR 2019\nPC Member: WWW2020. WSDM2020, WSDM2019, EMNLP2019, NLPCC2019, SIGIR2018, EMNLP2018, KDD2018, WWW2018, AAAI2018, WSDM2018, SIGIR2017, AAAI2017, WSDM2017, EMNLP2017, CIKM2017, ACML2017, SIGIR 2016, CIKM 2016, WSDM 2016, EMNLP 2016, ACML 2016, ICTIR 2016, IJCAI 2015, ACL 2014, WSDM 2014, CIKM 2013, ICDM 2013, WSDM 2013, ACL 2013, WSDM 2012, CIKM 2012, SIGIR 2012, ACL 2012\nReviewer: IEEE TKDE, ACM TOIS, ACM TKDD, Information Retrieval Journal (IRJ), Neurocomputing, International Journal of Machine Learning and Cybernetics (JMLC)\nPlease find more publications on\nmy Google Scholar profile\n.\n2025\nYubao Tang, Ruqing Zhang, Jiafeng Guo, Maarten de Rijke, Yixing Fan and Xueqi Cheng.â\nBoosting Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Generation-Augmented Retrieval: A Co-Training Approach\n. The 48th International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR 2025).\nYu-an Liu, Ruqing Zhang, Jiafeng Guo, Maarten de Rijke, Yixing Fan and Xueqi Cheng.â\nOn the Scaling of Robustness and Effectiveness in Dense Retrieval\n. The 48th International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR 2025).\nNing Xian, Yixing Fan, Ruqing Zhang, Maarten de Rijke and Jiafeng Guo.â\nAn Empirical Study of Evaluating Long-form Question Answering\n. The 48th International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval (SIGIR 2025).\nJiafeng Guo, Yinqiong Cai, Keping Bi, Yixing Fan, Wei Chen, Ruqing Zhang and Xueqi Cheng.â\nCAME: Competitively Learning a Mixture-of-Experts Model for First-stage Retrieval\n. ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS).\nJiafeng Guo, Changjiang Zhou, Ruqing Zhang, Jiangui Chen, Maarten de Rijke, Yixing Fan and Xueqi Cheng.â\nCorpusBrain++: A Continual Generative Pre-Training Framework for Knowledge-Intensive Language Tasks\n. ACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS).\nZhilei Hu, Zixuan Li, Xiaolong Jin, Long Bai, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nLarge Language Model-Based Event Relation Extraction with Rationales\n. The 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics (COLING 2025).\nJiyao Wei, Saiping Guan, Xiaolong Jin, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nInductive Link Prediction in N-ary Knowledge Graphs\n. The 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics (COLING 2025).\nYihang Wang, Bowen Tian, Yueyang Su, Yixing Fan and Jiafeng Guo.\nMDPO: Customized Direct Preference Optimization with a Metric-based Sampler for Question and Answer Generation\n. The 31st International Conference on Computational Linguistics (COLING 2025).\nGaoyu Zhu, Wei Shao, Xichou zhu, Lei Yu, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nText2Sql: Pure Fine-Tuning and Pure Knowledge Distillation\n. 2025 Annual Conference of the Nations of the Americas Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (NAACL 2025).\nMingkun Zhang, Keping Bi, Wei Chen, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nCLIPure: Purification in Latent Space via CLIP for Adversarially Robust Zero-Shot Classification\n. The Thirteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR 2025).\nLulu Yu, Keping Bi, Jiafeng Guo, Shihao Liu, Dawei Yin and Xueqi Cheng.\nUnbiased Learning to Rank with Query-Level Click Propensity Estimation: Beyond Pointwise Observation and Relevance\n. The ACM Web Conference 2025 (WWW 2025).\nYu-An Liu, Ruqing Zhang, Jiafeng Guo, Changjiang Zhou, Maarten de Rijke and Xueqi Cheng.\nOn the Robustness of Generative Information Retrieval Models: An Out-of-Distribution Perspective\n. The 47th European Conference on Information Retrieval (ECIR 2025).\nWanqing Cui, Rui Cheng, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nMVAM: Multi-View Attention Method for Fine-grained Image-Text Matching\n. The 47th European Conference on Information Retrieval (ECIR 2025).\nYu-An Liu, Ruqing Zhang, Jiafeng Guo, Maarten de Rijke, Yixing Fan and Xueqi Cheng.\nAttack-in-the-Chain: Bootstrapping Large Language Models for Attacks against Black-box Neural Ranking Models\n. The 39th Annual AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2025).\nYubao Tang, Ruqing Zhang, Jiafeng Guo, Maarten de Rijke, Shihao Liu, Shuaiqiang Wang, Dawei Yin and Xueqi Cheng.\nGenerative Retrieval for Book Search\n. 31st ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (KDD 2025).\n2024\nYubao Tang, Ruqing Zhang, Jiafeng Guo, Maarten de Rijke, Wei Chen and Xueqi Cheng.\nGenerative Retrieval Meets Multi-Graded Relevance\n. The Thirty-eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024, Spotlight).\nMingkun Zhang, Keping Bi, Wei Chen, Quanrun Chen, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nCausalDiff: Causality-Inspired Disentanglement via Diffusion Model for Adversarial Defense\n. The Thirty-eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024).\nMingkun Zhang, Jianing Li, Wei Chen, Jiafeng Guo and Xueqi Cheng.\nClassifier Guidance Enhances Diffusion-based Adversarial Purification by Preserving Predictive Information\n. The 27th European Conference on Artificial Intelligence (ECAI 2024).\nWeich...[truncated]"
