    "homepage_text": "Yuanyu Wan at ZJU\nYuanyu Wan (宛袁玉)\nResearcher (浙江大学百人计划研究员)\nSchool of Software Technology\nZhejiang University\nI am also a member of the\nVIPA\ngroup.\nEmail: wanyy@zju.edu.cn or wanyy9@gmail.com.\nResearch Interest\nOnline Learning, Distributed Optimization\nEducation Experiences\nNanjing University\n, Nanjing, China\nPh.D., Computer Science and Technology, Sep., 2019 — Jun., 2022 (Advisor: Prof.\nLijun Zhang\n)\nM.S., Computer Science and Technology, Aug., 2016 — Jun., 2019 (Advisor: Prof.\nLijun Zhang\n)\nSun Yat-Sen University\n, Zhuhai, China\nB.E., Software Engineering, Sep., 2012 — Jun., 2016\nSelected Papers (\nPublications by Year\n)\nBlack-Box Reductions for Decentralized Online Convex Optimization in Changing Environments\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\nIn Proceedings of the 38th Annual Conference on Learning Theory (\nCOLT'25\n), pages 5605-5631, 2025.\nImproved Regret for Bandit Convex Optimization with Delayed Feedback\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\n, Chang Yao, Mingli Song, and Lijun Zhang\nIn Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 37 (\nNeurIPS'24\n), pages 169-196, 2024.\nNearly Optimal Regret for Decentralized Online Convex Optimization\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\n, Tong Wei, Mingli Song, and Lijun Zhang\nIn Proceedings of the 37th Annual Conference on Learning Theory (\nCOLT'24\n), pages 4862-4888, 2024.\nNon-stationary Online Convex Optimization with Arbitrary Delays\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\n, Chang Yao, Mingli Song, and Lijun Zhang\nIn Proceedings of the 41st International Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML'24\n), pages 49991-50011, 2024.\nImproved Dynamic Regret for Online Frank-Wolfe\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\n, Lijun Zhang, and Mingli Song\nIn Proceedings of the 36th Annual Conference on Learning Theory (\nCOLT'23\n), pages 3304 - 3327, 2023.\nProjection-free Distributed Online Learning with Sublinear Communication Complexity\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\n, Guanghui Wang, Wei-Wei Tu, and Lijun Zhang\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (\nJMLR\n), 23(172):1 - 53, 2022.\nEfficient Adaptive Online Learning via Frequent Directions\n[\nPDF\n]\nYuanyu Wan\n, and Lijun Zhang\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n), 44(10): 6910 - 6923, 2022.\nAcademic Service\nArea Chair: NeurIPS 2025\nSenior Program Committee Member: IJCAI 2021, 2025; ECAI 2024, 2025\nProgram Committee Member: COLT 2026; ALT 2024, 2025; AAAI 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2026; IJCAI 2020; ICONIP 2020\nConference Reviewer: ICML 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026; NeurIPS 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024; ICLR 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025; AISTATS 2023, 2025; PAKDD 2022; CICAI 2022; ACML 2021; PRCV 2021; IJCNN 2021; KDD 2020\nJournal Reviewer: TPAMI; TIT; Artificial Intelligence; TSP; TMLR; TNNLS; SCIS; TETCI; Machine Learning; Optimization Methods and Software; IEEE/CAA JAS; IEEE Networking Letters; Neurocomputing; Information Sciences; Machine Intelligence Research; ESWA; 软件学报; 中国科学信息科学\nStudents\nName\nYear of Entry\nYear of Graduation\nProgram\nFirst Job/Employer\nYu He\n2025\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nYuxi Li\n2025\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nHao Zhou\n2024\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nLan Xue\n2024\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nYu Shen\n2024\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nXiaoyu Wang\n2023\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nYitao Ma\n2023\nin progress\nMaster\n---\nKailong Chen*\n2021\n2024\nMaster\nDu Xiaoman, Beijing\nChenxu Zhang*\n2021\n2024\nMaster\n---, Beijing\nXu Yang*\n2021\n2024\nMaster\nAlibaba, Hangzhou\n* K. Chen, C. Zhang, and X. Yang started working with me since 2022"
