    "homepage_text": "Xueyan Niu\nXueyan Niu\nAddress:\nTheory Lab, 2012 Labs\nHuawei Technologies Co., Ltd.\n3 Xinxi Road, Haidian District, Beijing\nEmail:\nniuxueyan at gmail dot com\nMy last name is pronounced \"new\"\nAbout\nI have been a Principal Engineer with the Theory Lab at Huawei 2012 Labs since 2022. Prior to that, I was a researcher at the Cognitive Computing Lab, Baidu Research, in 2021. I received my Ph.D. degree in operations research from Purdue University, West Lafayette, IN, USA, in 2021 and the B.S. degree in mathematics and applied mathematics from Peking University, Beijing, China, in 2016.\nI am looking for highly self-motivated student interns with aligned research interests. Applications from individuals from underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged. Please send me an email if interested.\nResearch Interests\nMy research lies at the intersection of machine learning, information theory, and communications. I focus on foundational aspects of generative modeling and efficient data representation, with applications in large language models, image, and video processing. My work has been published in leading information theory venues such as IEEE Transactions on Information Theory as well as top artificial intelligence conferences such as NeurIPS and ICLR. Notably, my research on partial information decomposition received the Outstanding Early Career Researcher Paper Award at ISITA 2020."
  },
