    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Yinfei Yang\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYinfei Yang\nYinfei Yang (杨寅飞）\n\"\nK.I.S.S.\n- Keep it simple, Stupid! \" -- by\nKelly Johnson\nEmail: yangyin7 AT gmail DOT com\nShort Biography\nYinfei Yang is a research scientist at Apple AI/ML working on vision and language foundation models. Before Apple, He worked at Google research on various natural language processing problems including semantic retrieval, multilingual representation, and multimodal representation. Prior to that, He also worked at Redfin and Amazon as research engineers for machine learning and computer vision problems. His research focuses on image and text representation learning for retrieval and transferring tasks. He is generally interested in problems in Computer Vision, Natural Language Processing, or combined.\nTopics:\nEmbedding model.\nVision foundation model.\nVision language model.\nMultimodal LLM.\nPreviously worked on:\nLong text semantic representation, sentence embedding.\nQuestion-answering.\nSummarization and text generation.\nSentiment analysis.\nRecommendation;\nHouse value estimation.\nPrior Experience\n2017-2021\nResearch Scientist @ Google Research\n2015-2017     Data Science Engineer @ Redfin\n2013-2015     Software Engineer @ Amazon / Lab126\n2008               Intern @ Sun Microsystems.\nSelected Publications\n(\nGoogle Scholar\n)\nDaniel Cer,\nYinfei Yang\n, Sheng-yi Kong, Nan Hua, Nicole Limtiaco, Rhomni St. John, Noah Constant, Mario Guajardo-Céspedes, Steve Yuan, Chris Tar, Yun-Hsuan Sung, Brian Strope, Ray Kurzweil.\nUniversal Sentence Encoder for English\n.\nEMNLP 2018, demo paper\nYinfei Yang\n, Steve Yuan, Daniel Cer, Sheng-Yi Kong, Noah Constant, Petr Pilar, Heming Ge, Yun-hsuan Sung, Brian Strope and Ray Kurzweil,\nLearning Semantic Textual Similarity from Conversations\n,\n3rd workshop on RepL4NLP, ACL 2018,\nBest Paper Runner up\nYinfei Yang\n, Ani Nenkova,\nDetecting information-dense texts in multiple news domains\n. The 28th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n, 2014\nOthers\nReviewer\nConference: ICRA-2014, ICRA-2015, AAAI-2016, AAAI-2017, EMNLP-2017\nJournal: Computer Speech & Language, Pattern Recognition\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
