    "homepage_text": "Chang Tang (ååçä¸ªäººä¸»é¡µ,åä¸­ç§æå¤§å­¦) - Homepage\nHOME\nPUBLICATIONS\nTEACHING\nREADING\nRESOURCES\nCHANG TANG\nProfessor, PhD Supervisor \n\t\tSchool of Software Engineering \n\t\tHuazhong University of Science and Technology (\nHUST page\n)\nIEEE/CCF/CSIG Senior Member, ACM/CAAI/CSIAM Member\nNo. 1037 Luoyu Road, Wuhan, P.R. China Postcode: 430074.\nGoogle Scholar\ndblp\nBIBs\nEmail:\ntangchang[shift+2]hust.edu.cn\nI am looking for new MS/BS students to join my research project working on machine learning and computer vision. If you have a\ngood personality & solid mathematical & English background and happen to be interested in my research\n, please contact me!\nABOUT ME:\nI obtained my master degree (supervised by\nZhanjie Song\n) and PhD degree (supervised by\nChunping Hou\n) from Tianjin University in 2016 (master-doctor continuous study program). From Sep 2014-Sep 2015, I was a visiting student in University of Wollongong, Australia, supervised by\nWanqing Li\n, and I have got lots of supervision from professor\nXinwang Liu\nduring my visiting in Australia and the subsequent academic career.\nMy recent research interests lie in the areas of pattern recognition and machine learning. I am recently interested in building machine learning models for solving computer vision and data mining problems. I am a member of\nVision and Learning Representation Group (VLR Lab)\nleaded by Prof.\nXiang Bai\n.\nSOME INTERESTING PROJECTS:\nMulti-view/modal learning theories, methods and applications\nMedical AI\nLarge Language Models (LLM) and applications\nRECENT NEWS:\n2026-02-24: One paper was accepted by IEEE Signal Processing Letters.\n2026-02-06: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Emerging Topics in Computational Intelligence.\n2025-11-08: Five papers were accepted by AAAI 2026.\n2025-11-03: One paper was accepted by SCIENCE CHINA Information Sciences.\n2025-09-19: Two papers were accepted by NeurIPS 2025.\n2024-09-06: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (IEEE T-KDE) (CCF-A).\n2024-09-01: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics (IEEE T-CBB) (CCF-B).\n2025-07-01: One paper was accepted by IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics.\n2025-06-18: One paper was accepted by MICCAI 2025.\n2025-04-29: Two papers were accepted by IJCAI 2025.\n2025-02-23: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (IF: 8.3).\n2025-02-07: One paper was accepted by IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics (IF: 6.7).\n2025-01-19: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Multimedia.\n2024-12-31: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (IF: 10.2).\n2024-12-03: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Multimedia.\n2024-12-27: Associate editor of IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics (IF: 7.7).\n2024-12-21: Two co-authored paper were accepted by ICASSP 202 (CCF-B).\n2024-11-25: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (IF: 8.3).\n2024-11-16: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (IF: 8.3).\n2024-08-22: One papers was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (IEEE T-KDE) (CCF-A, IF 8.9).\n2024-07-16: Two papers were accepted by ACM MM 2024 (CCF-A).\n2024-06-26: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\n2024-06-23: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (IEEE T-KDE) (CCF-A, IF 8.9).\n2024-05-04: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (IEEE T-KDE) (CCF-A, IF 8.9).\n2024-04-09: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing (IEEE T-GRS) (CCF-B, IF 8.13).\n2024-04-07: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (CCF-A, IF: 23.6).\n2024-03-26: One co-authored paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing (IEEE T-GRS) (CCF-B, IF 8.13).\n2024-03-11: Two papers were accepted by ä¸­å½ç§å­¦ï¼ä¿¡æ¯ç§å­¦ and Journal of Computer Science and Technology, respectively.\n2024-02-26: One paper was accepted by Information Fusion (IF: 18.6).\n2024-02-03: One paper was accepted by IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics (IF: 7.7).\n2024-01-24: One paper was accepted by Expert Systems With Applications (IF: 8.5).\n2024-01-12: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (IEEE T-NNLS) (CCF-B, IF 11.9).\n2023-12-19: One paper was accepted by Computers in Biology and Medicine (IF: 7.7).\n2023-12-19: Associate editor of Neural Networks (IF: 7.8).\n2023-12-05: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering (IEEE T-KDE) (CCF-A, IF 8.9).\n2023-12-05: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (IEEE T-NNLS) (CCF-B, IF 11.9).\n2023-10-24: Associate editor of CAAI Transactions on Intelligence Technology (IF: 5.1).\n2023-10-08: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing (IEEE T-GRS) (CCF-B, IF 8.13).\n2023-09: CCF Senior Member.\n2023-08-17: One paper was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing (IEEE T-GRS) (CCF-B, IF 8.13).\n2023-08-04: One paper was accepted by Information Sciences (CCF-B).\n2023-07-26: Two papers were accepted by ACM MM 2023 (CCF-A).\n2023-03-13: One paper was accepted by ICME 2023 (CCF-B).\n2023-02-28: One paper was accepted by CVPR 2023 (CCF-A).\n2023-02-25: IEEE Senior Member\nPROJECTS:\nNational Natural Science Foundation of China (General Project): PI, 2020.\nOpen Research Project of Key Laboratory of Information Perception and Systems for Public Security \nof MIIT: PI, 2020.\nOpen Research Project of Guangdong Key Laboratory for Biomedical Measurements and Ultrasound Imaging: PI, 2020.\nNational Natural Science Foundation of China (Youth Project): PI, 2017.\nFundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities, China University of Geosciencesï¼Wuhanï¼: PI, 2017.\nOpen Research Project of The Hubei Key Laboratory of Intelligent Geo-Information Processing: PI, 2018.\nRECENT PUBLICATIONS:\nPre-print\n2024\nWeiqing Yan, Yuanyang Zhang,\nChang Tang\n*, Wujie Zhou, Weisi Lin, \"Anchor-Sharing and Clusterwise Contrastive Network for Multiview Representation Learning\", IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems, 2024. [\nCODE\n]\nWenqi Yang, Minhui Wang,\nChang Tang\n*, Xiao Zheng, Xinwang Liu, Kunlun He*, \"Trustworthy Multi-view Clustering via Alternating Generative Adversarial Representation Learning and Fusion\", Information Fusion, 107:102323, 2024. [\nCODE\n]\nShuhan Huang, Minhui Wang, Xiao Zheng, Jiajia Chen,\nChang Tang\n*, \"Hierarchical and Dynamic Graph Attention Network for Drug-disease Association Prediction\", IEEE Journal of Biomedical and Health Informatics, 1-12, 2024. [\nCODE\n]\nZixiao Jin, Minhui Wang, Xiao Zheng, Jiajia Chen,\nChang Tang\n*, \"Drug Side Effects Prediction via Cross Attention Learning and Feature Aggregation\", Expert Systems With Applications, 248: 123346, 2024. [\nCODE\n]\nZixiao Jin, Minhui Wang,\nChang Tang\n, Xiao Zheng, Wen Zhang, Xiaofeng Sha, Shan An, \"Predicting miRNA-disease association via graph attention learning and multiplex adaptive modality fusion\", Computers in Biology and Medicine, 169: 107904, 2024. [\nCODE\n]\nWei Feng, Minhui Wang,\nChang Tang\n, Weiying Xie, Xianju Li, Xiao Zheng, Jiangfeng Xu, \"Hyperspectral band selection via region-wise latent feature fusion and graph filter embedded subspace clustering\", Engineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence, 132:107911, 2024. [\nCODE\n]\n2023\nChang Tang\n, Jun Wang, Xinwang Liu, Weiying Xie, Xianju Li, Wei Zhang, Xinzhong Zhu, \"Spatial and Spectral Structure Preserved Self-representation for Hyperspectral Band Selection\", IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing, 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nXiao He,\nChang Tang\n*, Xinwang Liu, Wei Zhang, Kun Sun, Jiangfeng Xu, Object Detection in Hyperspectral Image via Unified Spectral-Spatial Feature Aggregation, IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing, 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nJun Wang,\nChang Tang\n*, Xiao Zheng, Xinwang Liu, Wei Zhang, En Zhu, Xinzhong Zhu, \"Fast Approximated Multiple Kernel K-means\", IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering, 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nShengju Yu, Suyuan Liu, Siwei Wang,\nChang Tang\n*, Zhigang Luo, Xinwang Liu, En Zhu, \"Sparse Low-Rank Multi-View Subspace Clustering With Consensus Anchors and Unified Bipartite Graph\", IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems, 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nWeiqing Yan, Long Xu, Hao Liu, Chang Tang, Wujie Zhou, \"High-order Structural Relation Distillation Networks from LiDAR to Monocular Image 3D Detectors\", IEEE Transactions on Intelligent Vehicles, 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nXiao He,\nChang Tang\n*, Xin Zou, Wei Zhang, Multispectral Object Detection via Cross-Modal Conflict-Aware Learning, ACM International Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM 2023), 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nXin Zou,\nChang Tang\n*, Xiao Zheng, Zhenglai Li, Xiao He, Shan An, Xinwang Liu, DPNET: Dynamic Poly-attention Network for Trustworthy Multi-modal Classification, Proceedings of the 31th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM), 2023. [\nCODE\n]\nJun Wang,\nChang Tang\n*, Zhiguo Wan, Wei Zhang, Kun Sun, Albert Zomaya. \"Efficient and Effective One-step Multi-view Clustering\", IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems, 2023.\nWeiqing Yan, Yuanyang Zhang, Chenlei Lv,\nChang Tang\n*, Guanghui Yue, Liang Liao, Weisi Lin, \"GCFAgg: Global and Cross-view Feature Aggregation for Multi-view Clustering\", IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023.\nXin Zou,\nChang Tang\n*, Xiao Zheng, Kun Sun, Wei Zhang, Deqiong Ding, \"Inclusivity induced adaptive graph learning for multi-view clustering\", Knowledge-Based Systems, 267:110424, 2023.\nXin Zou,\nChang Tang\n*, Wei Zhang, Kun Sun, Liangxiao Jiang, Hierarchical Attention Learning for Multimod...[truncated]"
