    "homepage_text": "ZHU ZHANG's Homepage - Research\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZHU ZHANG's Homepage\nResearch\nPublication and Preprints\nwith C.-J. Liu, M. Ma, and D. Wu\n,\nUnstable mode around the 3D boundary layer flow\n. arXiv. 2509.06089.\nwith S. Li and T. Yang,\nStructural stability of subsonic boundary layers in the entire subsonic regime\n. arXiv.\n2501.16268\nWith R.-J. Duan,\nSolutions to a moving boundary problem on the Boltzmann equation,\nJ.  Statistical Physics,\n192 (10), 1-37, 2025.\nwith\nT\n.\nYang,\nLinear instability analysis on compressible Navier-Stokes equations with strong boundary layer,\nArch. Ration. Mech. Anal.\n, 247, 2023.\nwith C.-J. Liu and T. Yang,\nValidity of Prandtl expansions for steady MHD in the Sobolev framework\n,\nSIAM. J. Math. Anal.\n55 (3) 2377-2410, 2023.\nwith C.-J. Liu and T. Yang,\nAnalysis of the Tollmien-Schlichting wave in the Prandtl-Hartmann regime\n,\nJ. Math. Pure. Appl.\n165, 58-105, 2022.\nwith R.-J. Duan,  and S.-Q. Liu,\nIon-acoustic shock in a collisional plasma\n,\nJ. Differential Equations\n269 (2020), 3721-3768.\nwith R.-J. Duan, F.-M. Huang and Y. Wang,\nEffects of soft interaction and non-isothermal boundary upon long-time dynamics of rarefied gas,\nArch. Ration. Mech. Anal\n.\n234 (2019), 925-1006.\nInstability in a Vlasov-Fokker-Planck binary mixture\n,\nJ. Differential Equations\n266 (2019), 1514-1535.\nwith R.-J. Duan, S.-Q. Liu and T. Yang, Heat transfer problem for the Boltzmann equation in a channel with diffusive boundary condition.\nChin. Ann. Math, Ser. B\n, (2022), Dedicated to the Memory of Professor Chaohao Gu.\nAwards and Grants\nPI.\nGeneral Research Fund, Hong Kong RGC, No. 15300225. (2025)\nPI\n. General Research Fund\n,  Hong Kong RGC,  No. 15300024. (2024)\nPI\n.\nEarly Career Scheme,  Hong Kong RGC,  No. 25303523. (2023)\nCo-I.\nGeneral Research Fund, Hong Kong RGC,  No. 11318822. (2022)\nInvited speaker at HYP2024 (19th International Conference on Hyperbolic Problems).\nHKMS Young Scholars Award, Hong Kong Mathematical Society (2024)\nBest Thesis Award, Hong Kong Mathematical Society, 2020.\nService:\nI serve as a referee for the following journals:\nJ. London Math. Soc., J. Differential Equations,\nScience China Math.,\nSIAM J. Math. Anal., Kinetic and Related Models, among others.\nEditorial\nKinetic and Related Models\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Bingxin Zhou": {
    "homepage": "https://www.bingxinzhao.com/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Bingxin Zhao\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBingxin Zhao\nWelcome to my website.\nI am an assistant professor in Statistics and Data Science at the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania, with a secondary appointment in the Department of Medicine at the Perelman School of Medicine.\nMy research develops statistical and AI methods for science and medicine, with a focus on integrating multimodal data, such as imaging, genomics, and knowledge graphs, to enable discovery and translation. I’m also working on unifying statistical rigor, software engineering, and agentic AI to build practical systems for scientific and medical research.\nMy work has advanced understanding of the brain and inter-organ connections (e.g., heart–brain links) in relation to brain disorders and healthy aging, recognized by the\ninaugural UK Biobank Scientific Impact Awards\n. Our agentic AI platform was recently selected as a finalist for the\nAlzheimer’s Insights AI Prize\n, a $1M award supporting the use of agentic AI in Alzheimer’s disease research.\nWharton Faculty Page\nGoogle Scholar Page\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
