    "homepage_text": "About Me - Chao Qin\nChao Qin\nResearcher\nFollow\nPalo Alto, CA\nStanford University\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nAbout Me\nI am a postdoctoral scholar at Stanford Graduate School of Business, where I have the privilege of working with\nGuido Imbens\n,\nStefan Wager\n, and\nKuang Xu\n, and collaborating with\nRamesh Johari\nand\nAirbnb\n. Previously, I received my Ph.D. degree in Decision, Risk, and Operations from Columbia Business School, where I was very fortunate to be advised by\nDaniel Russo\n.\nOutside academia, I have worked on research teams at\nGoogle DeepMind, Scale AI, Amazon AI, and Adobe Research\n.\nMy research interests include\nMethodologies:\nExperimental Design, Bandits and Reinforcement Learning, Causal Inference, (Statistical) Machine Learning, Optimization, Game Theory\nApplications:\nExperimentation and Personalization, Large-Scale Resource Allocation, Pricing, Service Operations, Supply Chain Management, Advertising Measurement, Ranking.\nThe\nsyllabus\nof my mini-course at Northwestern Kellogg School of Management provides an overview of my recent work on Adaptive Experimentation.\nExcited to be on the academic job market for the first time!\nContact\nEmail:\nchaoqin@stanford.edu\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nLinkedIn"
  },
