    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Chen Zhao - homepage\nChen Zhao\nAssistant Professor\nComputer Science, NYU Shanghai\nAffiliated Assistant Professor\nCenter for Data Science, New York University\n567 West Yangsi Road, Shanghai, China\nEmail: cz1285 [at] nyu [dot] edu\nI am an assistant professor at\nthe Department of Computer Science, NYU Shanghai\n(Starting at Fall 2023). \n                I am also affiliated at\nCenter for Data Science, New York University\n.\nI was a postdoctoral researcher at the Department of Computer Science, New York University, mentored by Prof.\nKyunghyun Cho\nand Prof.\nHe He\n.\n                    I am a member of the\nML\n2\nlab and the\nCILVR\ngroup.\nI received my Ph.D. at the Department of Computer Science, University of Maryland, College Park,\n                    advised by Prof.\nJordan Boyd-Graber\nand Prof.\nHal Daumé III\n.\n                    Throughout my graduate studies, I spent several summers doing internships in industry, including\nMicrosoft Semantic Machines\n,\nDMX group\nand\nIDEAS group\nat Microsoft Research.\nMy main research interest is in\nnatural language processing\n. \n                    My goal is to equip language model based intelligent agents with external tools to make them more reliable and interpretable in real scenarios. Some directions I'm excited recently include:\n(1)\nAgentic Search and RL\n:\n                    Real-world tasks often require agents to perform multiple, iterative searches across diverse sources. How to effectively retrieve and incorporate external knowledge, especially when the task demands intensive reasoning capabilities?\n(2)\nDiffusion Language Models\n:\n                    Diffusion language models show strong potential in both reasoning and efficiency, but how can they be integrated into agentic scenarios?\n(3)\nUnderstanding Language Models in knowledge and reasoning\n: \n                    How language models internally acquire knowledge, reason about it, and adopt quickly with new information (i.e. Knowledge Editing)?\n(4)\nHuman-centered NLP in Healthcare\n: How to have both language model and human in-the-loop to reliably solve real-world healthcare problems (e.g., Radiology Report Generation, Medical Agents)?\nPhDs and Visitors:\nI am looking for 1-2 PhD students to join the group this coming cycle (2025 - 2026), see my\nadvising statement\nand\nthe NYU Shanghai PhD program\nfor details.\n                I am also looking for predoctoral researchers and visiting researchers (start time could be flexible). If you are interested in working with me, please send me an email.\nUndergrads:\nI really enjoy working with undergrads, and have made some success over the years. I usually look for 1-2 undergrads at NYU Shanghai to join my group every year, please take machine learning class first then send me an email if you are interested.\nPapers\n(\"_\" means our awesome undergrads at NYU Shanghai! * indicates equal contribution)\nDiffusion vs. autoregressive language models: A text embedding perspective\nSiyue Zhang, Yilun Zhao,\nLiyuan Geng\n, Arman Cohan, Anh Tuan Luu,\nChen Zhao\nEMNLP 2025\nRPDR: A Round-trip Prediction-Based Data Augmentation Framework for Long-Tail Question Answering\nYiming Zhang, Siyue Zhang, Junbo Zhao,\nChen Zhao\nEMNLP 2025\nLimRank: Less is More for Reasoning-Intensive Information Reranking\nTingyu Song, Yilun Zhao, Siyue Zhang,\nChen Zhao\n, Arman Cohan\nEMNLP 2025\nFinTrust: A Comprehensive Benchmark of Trustworthiness Evaluation in Finance Domain\nTiansheng Hu\n, Tongyan Hu,\nLiuyang Bai\n, Yilun Zhao, Arman Cohan,\nChen Zhao\nEMNLP 2025\nSportReason: Evaluating Retrieval-Augmented Reasoning across Tables and Text for Sports Question Answering\nKaiyue Feng\n, Siyue Zhang, Bingsen Chen, Yilun Zhao,\nChen Zhao\nEMNLP 2025\nMRAG: A Modular Retrieval Framework for Time-Sensitive Question Answering\nSiyue Zhang, Yuxiang Xue, Yiming Zhang, Xiaobao Wu, Anh Tuan Luu,\nChen Zhao\nFindings of EMNLP 2025\nFinLFQA: Evaluating Attributed Text Generation of LLMs in Financial Long-Form Question Answering\nYitao Long*,\nTiansheng Hu*\n, Yilun Zhao, Arman Cohan,\nChen Zhao\nFindings of EMNLP 2025\nMCTS-RAG: Enhancing Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Monte Carlo Tree Search\nYunhai Hu, Yilun Zhao,\nChen Zhao\n, Arman Cohan\nFindings of EMNLP 2025\nReasoning Models Know When They’re Right: Probing Hidden States for Self-Verification\nAnqi Zhang, Yulin Chen, Jane Pan,\nChen Zhao\n, Aurojit Panda, Jinyang Li, He He\nCOLM 2025\n[code/data]\nInter-Passage Verification for Multi-evidence Multi-answer QA\nBingsen Chen, Shengjie Wang, Xi Ye,\nChen Zhao\nFindings of ACL 2025\n[code/data]\nPHYSICS: Benchmarking Foundation Models on University-Level Physics Problem Solving\nKaiyue Feng\n, Yilun Zhao, Yixin Liu, Tianyu Yang,\nChen Zhao\n, John Sous, Arman Cohan\nFindings of ACL 2025\n[code/data]\nAre Multimodal LLMs Robust Against Adversarial Perturbations? RoMMath: A Systematic Evaluation on Multimodal Math Reasoning\nYilun Zhao, Guo Gan, Chengye Wang,\nChen Zhao\n, Arman Cohan\nNAACL 2025\n[code/data]\nMMVU: Measuring Expert-Level Multi-Discipline Video Understanding\nYilun Zhao, Lujing Xie, Haowei Zhang, Guo Gan, Yitao Long, Zhiyuan Hu, Tongyan Hu, Weiyuan Chen, Chuhan Li, Junyang Song, Zhijian Xu, Chengye Wang, Weifeng Pan, Ziyao Shangguan, Xiangru Tang, Zhenwen Liang, Yixin Liu,\nChen Zhao\n, Arman Cohan\nCVPR 2025\n[code/data]\nFinDVer: Explainable Claim Verification over Long and Hybrid-content Financial Documents\nYilun Zhao, Yitao Long, Tintin Jiang, Chengye Wang, Weiyuan Chen, Hongjun Liu, Xiangru Tang, Yiming Zhang,\nChen Zhao\n, Arman Cohan\nEMNLP 2024\n[code/data]\nSynTQA: Synergistic Table-based Question Answering via Mixture of Text-to-SQL and E2E TQA\nSiyue Zhang, Anh Tuan Luu,\nChen Zhao\nFindings of EMNLP 2024\n[code/data]\nTAPERA: Enhancing Faithfulness and Interpretability in Long-Form Table QA by Content Planning and Execution-based Reasoning\nYilun Zhao, Lyuhao Chen, Arman Cohan,\nChen Zhao\nACL 2024\n[code/data]\nParallel Structures in Pre-training Data Yield In-Context Learning\nYanda Chen,\nChen Zhao\n, Zhou Yu, Kathleen McKeown, He He\nACL 2024\n[code/data]\nKnowledgeMath: Knowledge-Intensive Math Word Problem Solving in Finance Domains\nYilun Zhao*, Hongjun Liu*, Yitao Long, Rui Zhang,\nChen Zhao\n, Arman Cohan\nACL 2024\n[code/data]\nYour Co-Workers Matter: Evaluating Collaborative Capabilities of Language Models in Blocks World\nGuande Wu,\nChen Zhao\n, Claudio Silva, He He\nFindings of ACL 2024\n[code/data]\nDo models explain themselves? counterfactual simulatability of natural language explanations\nYanda Chen, Ruiqi Zhong, Narutatsu Ri,\nChen Zhao\n, He He, Jacob Steinhardt, Zhou Yu, Kathleen McKeown\nICML 2024\n[code/data]\nLarge Language Models Help Humans Verify Truthfulness--Except When They Are Convincingly Wrong\nChenglei Si, Navita Goyal, Sherry Tongshuang Wu,\nChen Zhao\n, Shi Feng, Hal Daumé III, Jordan Boyd-Graber\nNAACL 2024\n[code/data]\nTwo Failures of Self-Consistency in the Multi-Step Reasoning of LLMs\nAngelica Chen, Jason Phang, Alicia Parrish, Vishakh Padmakumar,\nChen Zhao\n, Samuel R. Bowman, Kyunghyun Cho\nTMLR 2024\n[code/data]\nMixture of Prompt Experts for Generalizable and Interpretable Question Answering\nChenglei Si, Weijia Shi,\nChen Zhao\n, Luke Zettlemoyer, Jordan Boyd-Graber\nFindings of EMNLP 2023\n[code/data]\nOn the Relation between Sensitivity and Accuracy in In-context Learning\nYanda Chen,\nChen Zhao\n, Zhou Yu, Kathleen McKeown, He He\nFindings of EMNLP 2023\n[code/data]\nARGUS: Visualization of AI-Assisted Task Guidance in AR\nSonia Castelo, Joao Rulff, Erin McGowan, Bea Steers, Guande Wu, Shaoyu Chen, Iran Roman, Roque Lopez, Ethan Brewer,\nChen Zhao\n, Jing Qian, Kyunghyun Cho, He He, Qi Sun, Huy Vo, Juan Bello, Michael Krone, Claudio Silva\nIEEE Vis 2023\n[code/data]\nRobuT: A Systematic Study of Table QA Robustness Against Human-Annotated Adversarial Perturbations\nYilun Zhao,\nChen Zhao\n, Linyong Nan, Zhenting Qi, Wenlin Zhang, Boyu Mi, Xiangyu Tang, Dragomir Radev\nACL 2023\n[code/data]\nRevisiting Calibration for Question Answering\nChenglei Si,\nChen Zhao\n, Sewon Min, Jordan Boyd-Graber\nFindings of EMNLP 2022\n[code/data]\nBridging the Generalization Gap in Text-to-SQL Parsing with Schema Expansion\nChen Zhao\n, Yu Su, Adam Pauls, Emmanouil Antonios Platanios\nACL 2022\n[code/data]\nDistantly-Supervised Evidence Retrieval Enables Question Answering without Annotated Evidence Pieces\nChen Zhao\n, Chenyan Xiong, Jordan Boyd-Graber, Hal Daumé III\nEMNLP 2021\n[code/data]\nWhat's in a Name? Answer Equivalence for Open-Domain Question Answering.\nChenglei Si,\nChen Zhao\n, Jordan Boyd-Graber\nEMNLP 2021 short\n[code/data]\nMulti-Step Reasoning Over Unstructured Text with Beam Dense Retrieval\nChen Zhao\n, Chenyan Xiong, Jordan Boyd-Graber, Hal Daumé III\nNAACL 2021 short\n[code/data]\nOn the Potential of Lexico-logical Alignments for Semantic Parsing to SQL Queries\nTianze Shi*,\nChen Zhao*\n, Jordan Boyd-Graber, Hal Daumé III, Lillian Lee\nFinding of EMNLP 2020 (* indicates equal contributuon)\n[code/data]\nTransformer-XH: Multi-evidence Reasoning with Extra Hop Attention\nChen Zhao\n, Chenyan Xiong, Corby Rosset, Xia Song, Paul Bennett, Saurabh Tiwary\nICLR 2020\n[code]\nComplex Factoid Question Answering with a Free-Text Knowledge Graph\nChen Zhao\n, Chenyan Xiong, Xin Qian, Jordan Boyd-Graber\nWWW 2020\n[website]\n[video]\nAuto-EM: End-to-end Fuzzy Entity-Matching using Pre-trained Deep Models and Transfer Learning\nChen Zhao\n, Yeye He\nWWW 2019\nA dataset and baselines for sequential open-domain question answering\nAhmed Elgohary*,\nChen Zhao*\n, Jordan Boyd-Graber\nEMNLP 2018 short (* indicates equal contributuon)\n[dataset]\nLightNet: A Versatile, Standalone Matlab-based Environment for Deep Learning\nChengxi Ye,\nChen Zhao\n, Yezhou Yang, Cornelia Fermüller, Yiannis Aloimonos\nACMMM 2016\nAtom Decomposition with Adaptive Basis Selection Strategy for Matrix Completion\nYao Hu,\nChen Zhao\n, Deng Cai, Xiaofei He, Xuelong Li\nTOMM 2016\nPhD Students\nYulin Chen\n(NYU CDS PhD, w/ He He)\nHongjun Liu\n(NYU CDS PhD)\nBale Chen\n(NYU Courant CS PhD)\nYihuai Hong\n(NYU Courant CS PhD)\nZiyun Yu\n(NYU Courant CS PhD)\nVisitors\nSiyue Zhang\n(PhD student a...[truncated]"
