    "homepage_text": "Henghui Ding\nHenghui Ding\nProfessor\nOffice: Room 813, Building C, 579 Guoquan Rd, Fudan University\nEmail: henghui.ding[AT]gmail.com\nHenghui Ding is currently a Professor at Fudan University. Prior to that, he was a Presidential Postdoctoral Fellow (Principal Investigator) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU) in Singapore, a Postdoctoral Researcher at ETH Zürich in Switzerland, and a Research Scientist at ByteDance AI Lab in Singapore. He received the Ph.D. degree (winner of the Best Thesis Award) from NTU in 2020, and the B.E. degree from Xi’an Jiaotong University in 2016. His research interests broadly include machine learning and computer vision. Specifically, he focuses on scene understanding (e.g., video/image segmentation, detection), AIGC (e.g., video/image generation/editing), multi-modal learning (e.g., vision-language), low-shot learning, and human–computer interaction. He serves/served as an Area Chair for CVPR’(24-26), NeurIPS’(24-26), ICML’(25-26), ICLR’(25-26), ECCV’26, AAAI’26, ACM MM’(24-26), BMVC’(24-25), and a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for AAAI’(22-25), IJCAI’(23-25). He serves as an Associate Editor for IEEE Transactions on Image Processing (TIP) and Pattern Recognition (PR).\nOpenings: We are looking for self-motivated graduate (Master/Ph.D.) students and undergraduate interns to join our group. If you are interested, please email me with your resume and transcript.\nNews\nMar 2026\nServing as an\nArea Chair for NeurIPS 2026\n.\nMar 2026\nCall for Papers\n:\nCVPR 2026 PVUW Workshop\n.\nFeb 2026\nServing as an\nArea Chair for ACM MM 2026\n.\nFeb 2026\n3 papers accepted to\nCVPR 2026\n. Congratulations to Xincheng and Yang!\nFeb 2026\nServing as an\nAssociate Editor for Pattern Recognition\n.\nJan 2026\nFISS\naccepted to\nTPAMI\n.\nJan 2026\nGREx\naccepted to\nIJCV\n.\nDec 2025\nServing as an\nArea Chair for ECCV 2026\n.\nNov 2025\nServing as an\nArea Chair for ICML 2026\n.\nNov 2025\n3 papers accepted to\nAAAI 2026\n, 1 Oral. Congratulations to Hengrui and Xincheng!\nSep 2025\n2 papers accepted to\nNeurIPS 2025\n, 1 Spotlight. Congratulations to Zhenyuan!\nAug 2025\nServing as an\nArea Chair for CVPR 2026\n. Serving as an\nArea Chair for ICLR 2026\n.\nAug 2025\nMOSEv2 Dataset\nis released.\nEvaluation server\nis online.\nAug 2025\nMeViSv2 Dataset\naccepted to IEEE TPAMI.\nJul 2025\nServing as an Area Chair for\nAAAI 2026\n.\nJun 2025\n6 papers accepted to\nICCV 2025\n. Congratulations to Xincheng, Kaining, and Ziye!\nMay 2025\n7th LSVOS Workshop@ICCV 2025\n.\nMay 2025\nServing as an Area Chair for\nBMVC 2025\n.\nMay 2025\n1 paper accepted to\nICML 2025 as Oral\n.\nMar 2025\nCall for Papers\n:\nCVPR 2025 PVUW Workshop\n.\nFeb 2025\n3 papers accepted to\nCVPR 2025\n.\nFeb 2025\nServing as an Area Chair for\nACM MM 2025\n.\nFeb 2025\nServing as an Area Chair for\nNeurIPS 2025\n.\nDec 2024\nServing as an\nAssociate Editor for IEEE TIP\n.\n3 papers accepted to\nAAAI 2025\n.\nServing as an Area Chair for\nICML 2025\n.\nNov 2024\nServing as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nIJCAI 2025\n.\nSep 2024\nServing as an\nArea Chair for CVPR 2025\n.\n3 papers accepted to\nNeurIPS 2024\n.\nAug 2024\nServing as an\nArea Chair for ICLR 2025\n.\nJul 2024\n2 papers accepted to\nECCV 2024\n.\n3 papers accepted to\nACM MM 2024\n.\nTransformer-based Segmentation Survey\naccepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nJun 2024\nServing as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nAAAI 2025\n.\nImage Editing Survey\n.\nCVPR 2024 MOSE & MeViS\nChallenge Report\n.\nMay 2024\nServing as an Area Chair for\nBMVC 2024\n.\nApr 2024\n1 paper on Video Segmentation accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nServing as an Area Chair for\nNeurIPS 2024\n.\nMar 2024\nCall for Papers\n:\nCVPR 2024 PVUW Workshop\nJan 2024\nOpen Vocabulary Learning Survey\naccepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\n3 papers accepted to\nCVPR 2024\n.\nDec 2023\n1 paper accepted to\nAAAI 2024\n.\nNov 2023\n1 paper accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n, 1 paper accepted to\nIEEE TMM\n.\nServing as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nIJCAI 2024\n.\nSep 2023\nSeveral papers accepted, 1\nNeurIPS\n, 1\nIEEE TIFS\n, 1\nPR\n.\nAug 2023\nMeViS Dataset\nis released.\nEvaluation server\nis online.\nServing as an Area Chair for\nCVPR 2024\n.\nJul 2023\n5 papers accepted to\nICCV 2023\n.\nMOSE Dataset\naccepted to ICCV 2023.\nServing as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nAAAI 2024\n.\nJun 2023\n1 paper accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nMay 2023\n2 paper accepted to\nIEEE TIP\n.\nNamed\nCVPR 2023 Outstanding Reviewer\n.\nMar 2023\n6 papers accepted to\nCVPR 2023\n, 1 Highlight.\nFeb 2023\nMOSE Dataset\nis released.\nEvaluation server\nis online..\nJan 2023\n3 papers accepted to\nICLR 2023\n, 1 paper accepted to\nISBI 2023\n.\nDec 2022\nServing as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nIJCAI 2023\n.\nNov 2022\nServing as an Associate Editor for\nIET Computer Vision\n.\nOct 2022\n2 papers accepted to\nIEEE TPAMI\n.\nSep 2022\n2 papers accepted to\nNeurIPS 2022\n.\nJul 2022\n2 papers accepted to\nECCV 2022\n.\nMar 2022\n4 papers accepted to\nCVPR 2022\n.\nSep 2021\nServing as a Senior Program Committee (SPC) member for\nAAAI 2022\n.\n2 papers accepted to\nNeurIPS 2021\n.\nJul 2021\n8 papers accepted to\nICCV 2021\n.\nSelected Publications\narXiv\nMOSEv2: A More Challenging Dataset for Video Object Segmentation in Complex Scenes\nHenghui Ding\n, Kaining Ying, Chang Liu, Shuting He, Xudong Jiang, Yu-Gang Jiang, Philip HS Torr, and Song Bai\narXiv preprint arXiv:2508.05630\n(\narXiv\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\narXiv\nLearning to Model the World: A Survey of World Models in Artificial Intelligence\nJiahua Dong, Qi Lyu, Baichen Liu, Xudong Wang, Wenqi Liang, Duzhen Zhang, Jiahang Tu, Hongliu Li, Hanbin Zhao,\nHenghui Ding\n, Yulun Zhang, Zhi Han, Nicu Sebe, Fahad Shahbaz Khan, Salman Khan, and\n4 more authors\nTechRxiv\n(\narXiv\n),\n          \n          \n          2026\nPDF\nCode\nTPAMI\nMeViS: A Multi-Modal Dataset for Referring Motion Expression Video Segmentation\nHenghui Ding\n, Chang Liu, Shuting He, Kaining Ying, Xudong Jiang, Chen Change Loy, and Yu-Gang Jiang\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(\nTPAMI\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\narXiv\nMultimodal Referring Segmentation: A Survey\nHenghui Ding\n, Song Tang, Shuting He, Chang Liu, Zuxuan Wu, and Yu-Gang Jiang\narXiv preprint arXiv:2508.00265\n(\narXiv\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nWebsite\nCVPR\nEffectErase: Joint Video Object Removal and Insertion for High-Quality Effect Erasing\nYang Fu, Yike Zheng, Ziyun Dai, and\nHenghui Ding†\nIn IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n),\n          \n          \n          2026\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nCVPR\nGlyphPrinter: Region-Grouped Direct Preference Optimization for Glyph-Accurate Visual Text Rendering\nXincheng Shuai*, Ziye Li*,\nHenghui Ding†\n, and Dacheng Tao\nIn IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n),\n          \n          \n          2026\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nIJCV\nGREx: Generalized Referring Expression Segmentation, Comprehension, and Generation\nHenghui Ding\n, Chang Liu, Shuting He, Xudong Jiang, and Yu-Gang Jiang\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision\n(\nIJCV\n),\n          \n          \n          2026\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nICLR\nAutoFly: Vision-Language-Action Model for UAV Autonomous Navigation in the Wild\nXiaolou Sun, Wufei Si, Wenhui Ni, Yuntian Li, Dongming Wu, Fei Xie, Runwei Guan†, He-Yang Xu,\nHenghui Ding†\n, Yuan Wu, Yutao Yue, Yongming Huang†, and Hui Xiong\nIn International Conference on Learning Representations\n(\nICLR\n),\n          \n          \n          2026\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nAAAI\nSegment Anything Across Shots: A Method and Benchmark\nHengrui Hu, Kaining Ying, and\nHenghui Ding†\nIn AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nAAAI\n),\n          \n          \n          2026\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nNeurIPS Spotlight\nSceneDesigner: Controllable Multi-Object Image Generation with 9-DoF Pose Manipulation\nZhenyuan Qin, Xincheng Shuai, and\nHenghui Ding†\nIn Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(\nNeurIPS Spotlight\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nNeurIPS\nSAMA: Towards Multi-Turn Referential Grounded Video Chat with Large Language Models\nYe Sun, Hao Zhang,\nHenghui Ding†\n, Tiehua Zhang, Xingjun Ma†, and Yu-Gang Jiang\nIn Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(\nNeurIPS\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nICCV\nTowards Omnimodal Expressions and Reasoning in Referring Audio-Visual Segmentation\nKaining Ying,\nHenghui Ding†\n, Guangquan Jie, and Yu-Gang Jiang\nIn IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nICCV\nMOVE: Motion-Guided Few-Shot Video Object Segmentation\nKaining Ying*, Hengrui Hu*, and\nHenghui Ding†\nIn IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nICCV\nFree-Form Motion Control: Controlling the 6D Poses of Camera and Objects in Video Generation\nXincheng Shuai,\nHenghui Ding†\n, Zhenyuan Qin, Hao Luo, Xingjun Ma, and Dacheng Tao\nIn IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nICCV\nAnyI2V: Animating Any Conditional Image with Motion Control\nZiye Li, Hao Luo, Xincheng Shuai, and\nHenghui Ding†\nIn IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nICCV\nCharaConsist: Fine-Grained Consistent Character Generation\nMengyu Wang,\nHenghui Ding†\n, Jianing Peng, Yao Zhao, Yunpeng Chen, and Yunchao Wei\n†\nIn IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nWebsite\nICML Oral\nReferSplat: Referring Segmentation in 3D Gaussian Splatting\nShuting He, Guangquan Jie, Changshuo Wang, Yun Zhou, Shuming Hu, Guanbin Li, and\nHenghui Ding†\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning\n(\nICML Oral\n),\n          \n          \n          2025\nPDF\nCode\nTPAMI\nTransformer-based Visual Segmentation: A survey\nXiangtai Li,\nHenghui Ding\n, Haobo Yuan, Wenwei Zhang, Guangliang Cheng, Jiangmiao Pang, Kai Chen, Ziwei Liu, and Chen Change Loy\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(\nTPAMI\n...[truncated]"
