    "homepage_text": "Zhaoning Yu [余兆宁] | Home\nZhaoning Yu [余兆宁]\nZhaoning Yu, 余兆宁\nznyu [AT] iastate [dot] edu\nBio\n大家好！Hi everyone! I am currently a 5th year Ph.D. Candidate in\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat Iowa State University. My advisor is\nDr.Hongyang Gao\n. Before arriving at the Iowa State University, I completed my master degree from\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat the George Washington Unversity in 2020. I obtained my Bachelor degree from\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat Wuhan University in 2018, supervised by\nDr.Xiaoliang Meng\n.\nMy research generally centers around graph deep learning. More specifically, I am currently working on\n(1) Graph Neural Networks(GNNs). (2) Explainable GNNs. (3) LLM on graph understanding.\nNews\n01/2026\nOur paper\nRESTRAIN: From Spurious Votes to Signals — Self-Driven RL with Self-Penalization\nhas been accepted to\nICLR 2026\n.\n01/2025\nOur paper\nMAGE: Model-Level Graph Neural Networks Explanations via Motif-based Graph Generation\nhas been accepted to\nICLR 2025\n.\n05/2022\nOur paper\nMolecular Representation Learning via Heterogeneous Motif Graph Neural Networks\nhas been accepted to\nICML 2022\n.\n12/2021\nI am so proud to receive a\nTeaching Excellence Award\n05/2021\nI won a\nseed funding\nfrom the Department of Computer Science at Iowa State University\nPublications\nComplete list of publications on\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nRESTRAIN: From Spurious Votes to Signals — Self-Driven RL with Self-Penalization\nZhaoning Yu\n, Will Su, Leitian Tao, Haozhu Wang, Aashu Singh, Hanchao Yu, Jianyu Wang, Hongyang Gao, Weizhe Yuan, Jason Weston, Ping Yu, Jing Xu\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2026\nPaper\nMAGE: Model-level graph neural networks explanations via motif-based graph generation\nZhaoning Yu\n, Hongyang Gao\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2025\nPaper\nMolecular Representation Learning via Heterogeneous Motif Graph Neural Networks\nZhaoning Yu\n, Hongyang Gao\nThirty-ninth International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nServices\nProgram Committee Member & Reviewer & External Reviewer\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n)\n2024, 2025, 2026\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n2024, 2025, 2026\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n2023, 2024, 2025\nAssociation for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n)\n2025, 2026\nLearning on Graphs Conference (\nLoG\n)\n2022, 2023, 2024\nArtificial Intelligence and Statistics (\nAISTATS\n)\n2026\nACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management (\nCIKM\n)\n2024, 2025\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining (\nKDD\n)\n2022\nRésumé\nMeta\nFeb '26 - Present\nAdvisor: Fujun Liu\nResearch Scientist\nIowa State University\nJan '21 - May '26\nAdvisor: Dr.Hongyang Gao\nPh.D. Student\nComputer Science\nGoogle\nAug '25 - Nov'25\nAdvisor: Xin Ma, John Holler\nPh.D. SWE Intern\nMeta\nMay '25 - Aug'25\nAdvisor: Will Su, Jing Xu\nPh.D. SWE Intern\nGenentech\nMay '24 - Aug'24\nAdvisor: Wenyi Wang\nML Intern\nGeorge Washington University\nSep '18 - Jun '20\nM.S. Student\nComputer Science\nWuhan University\nSep '14 - Jun '18\nAdvisor: Dr.Xiaoliang Meng\nB.E. Student\nSoftware Engineering\nZhaoning Yu\nbased on the template by\nMartin Saveski\nand\nPaul J. Wright"
  },
