    "homepage_text": "Haoran Liu\nHome\nEducation\nExperiences\nPublications\nAwards\nServices\nHaoran Liu  (刘浩然)\nPh.D Student\nat\nTexas A&M University\nResearch Interests:\nGraph-infused LLMs, Graph Learning\nAbout me:\nHowdy\n👋\n! I am currently an Applied Scientist at Amazon. Prior to joining Amazon, I graduated from Department of Computer Science & Engineering at Texas A&M University, advised by Dr.\nJames Caverlee\n. \n\t\t\t\tBefore coming to TAMU, I received master's and bachelor's degrees from Waseda University, Japan, and Southeast University, China. \n\t\t\t\tMy current research focuses on Graph Reasoning for LLM and LLM for Marketing Science. \n\t\t\t\tI enjoy running and rock climbing when not doing research.\nE-mail:\nliuhr99@tamu.edu\nGoogle Scholar |\nGithub |\nTwitter |\nLinkedIn\nCV[PDF]\nEducation\nPh.D. Student\nat\nDepartment of Computer Science & Engineering\n,\nTexas A&M University\nJune 2021 - Now\n&nbspCollege Station, TX\nAdvised by Prof.\nJames Caverlee\n.\nMaster of Engineering\nat\nInformation Engineering\n,\nWaseda University\nSep 2017 - Sep 2019\nTokyo, Japan\nAdvised by Prof.\nKamata Sei-ichiro\n.\nBachelor\nat\nSchool of Information Science and Engineering\n,\nSoutheast University\nSept 2014 - July 2018\nNanjing, China\nSpecial Class for the Gifted Young, Chien-Shiung Wu Honor College.\nExperiences\nApplied Scientist Intern\nat\nAmazon\nAutomated Marketing and Engineering Team\nSep 2024 - Nov 2024\n&nbspSeattle, WA\nResearch Intern\nat\nNEC Labs America\nMachine Learning Department\nMay 2024 - Aug 2024\n&nbspPrinceton, NJ\nMentor: Dr.\nMartin Renqiang Min\nand Dr.\nChristopher Malon\n.\nResearch Intern\nat\nNEC Labs America\nMachine Learning Department\nMay 2023 - Aug 2023\n&nbspPrinceton, NJ\nMentor: Dr.\nMartin Renqiang Min\n.\nResearch Intern\nat\nBaidu Research\nBig Data Lab\nJune 2020 - Aug 2020\n&nbspBeijing, China\nMentored by Dr.\nHaoyi Xiong\nand Prof.\nDejing Dou\n.\nPublications\n(* indicates equal contribution.)\nA Survey on LLMs for Story Generation.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nGithub\n]\nMaria Teleki, Vedangi Bengali*, Xiangjue Dong*, Sai Tejas Janjur*,\nHaoran Liu*\n, Tian Liu, Cong Wang, Ting Liu, Yin Zhang, Frank Shipman, James Caverlee\nEMNLP 2025 Findings.\nLLMs for Customized Offsite Marketing Content Generation and Evaluation at Scale.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nHaoran Liu\n, Amir Tahmasbi, Ehtesham Sam Haque, Purak Jain.\nKDD LLM4ECommerce Workshop 2025.\nMKG-Rank: Enhancing Large Language Models with Knowledge Graph for Multilingual Medical Question Answering.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nFeiyang Li, Yingjian Chen,\nHaoran Liu\n, Rui Yang, Han Yuan, Yuang Jiang, Tianxiao Li, Edison Marrese Taylor,\nHossein Rouhizadeh, Yusuke Iwasawa, Douglas Teodoro, Yutaka Matsuo, Irene Li\nPreprint.\nGraphCheck: Breaking Long-Term Text Barriers with Extracted Knowledge Graph-Powered Fact-Checking.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nYingjian Chen*,\nHaoran Liu*\n, Yinhong Liu, Rui Yang, Han Yuan, Yanran Fu, Pengyuan Zhou, Qingyu Chen,\nJames Caverlee, Irene Li.\nACL 2025 Main.\nLearning Disentangled Equivariant Representation for Explicitly Controllable 3D Molecule Generation.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nHaoran Liu\n, Youzhi Luo, Tianxiao Li, James Caverlee, Martin Renqiang Min\nAAAI 2025.\nMasculine Defaults via Gendered Discourse in Podcasts and Large Language Models.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nProject Website\n] [\nPaper\n]\nMaria Teleki, Xiangjue Dong,\nHaoran Liu\n, James Caverlee\nICWSM 2025. Also selected as\nparallel talk\nin IC2S2.\nKG-Rank: Enhancing Large Language Models for Medical QA with Knowledge Graphs and Ranking Techniques. \n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nRui Yang,\nHaoran Liu\n, Edison Marrese-Taylor, Qingcheng Zeng, Yu He Ke, Wanxin Li, Lechao Cheng, Qingyu Chen,\nJames Caverlee, Yutaka Matsuo, Irene Li\nBioNLP@ACL 2024.\nEverything Perturbed All at Once: Enabling Differentiable Graph Attacks.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nHaoran Liu\n, Bokun Wang, Jianling Wang, Xiangjue Dong, Tianbao Yang, James Caverlee\nWWW 2024.\nGradient-Guided Importance Sampling for Learning Binary Energy-Based Models.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nMeng Liu,\nHaoran Liu\n, Shuiwang Ji\nICLR 2023\nLearning Hierarchical Protein Representations via Complete 3D Graph Networks.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nCode\n]\nLimei Wang*,\nHaoran Liu*\n, Yi Liu, Jerry Kurtin, Shuiwang Ji\nICLR 2023\nComENet: Towards Complete and Efficient Message Passing for 3D Molecular Graphs.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nCode\n]\nLimei Wang*, Yi Liu*, Yuchao Lin,\nHaoran Liu\n, Shuiwang Ji\nNeurIPS 2022\nDIG: A Turnkey Library for Diving into Graph Deep Learning Research.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nCode\n]\nMeng Liu, Youzhi Luo, Limei Wang, Yaochen Xie, Hao Yuan, Shurui Gui, Haiyang Yu, Zhao Xu, Jingtun Zhang, Yi Liu, Keqiang Yan,\nHaoran Liu\n, Cong Fu, Bora Oztekin, Xuan Zhang, Shuiwang Ji\nJournal of Machine Learning Research (JMLR), 2022\nExploring the Common Principal Subspace of Deep Features in Neural Networks.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nHaoran Liu\n, Haoyi Xiong, Yaqing Wang, Haozhe An, Dejing Dou\nMachine Learning Journal (MLJ), 2022\nEdge-guided Hierarchically Nested Network for Real-time Semantic Segmentation.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nYuqi Li, Sei-Ichiro Kamata,\nHaoran Liu\nICSIPA 2019\nBest Paper Award\nHybrid Featured based Pyramid Structured CNN for Texture Classification.\n\t\t\t\t\t[\nPaper\n]\nHaoran Liu\n, Sei-Ichiro Kamata, Yuqi Li\nICSIPA 2019\nAwards\nDepartment of Computer Science & Engineering Travel Award\n. 2023, 2024, 2025\nCRA-WP Grad Cohort for Women\n. 2024\nD. E. Shaw Research Graduate and Postdoctoral Fellowship\n. 2023\nBest Paper Award\n. ICSIPA. 2019.\nIPS Special Scholarship for International Student\n. Waseda University. 2017-2018.\nFoundation for the Advancement of Industry, Science and Technology (FAIS) Scholarship\n. 2017-2018.\nSecond Prize in National Undergraduate Electronics Design Contest.\n2016.\nServices\nConference reviewer:\nNeurIPS (23', 24'), ICLR (23', 24', 25'), ICML (24', 25'), KDD (23'), SIGIR(23'), LoG (22', 23', 24'), NeurIPS Dataset and Benchmark Track (22', 23', 24'), CVPR (24', 25'), ICDM (20'), etc.\nJounal reviewer:\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems, IEEE Transactions on Cybernetics.\nSince Sep, 2022\nProudly powered by Bootstrap\nOk, done!\nPrivate\nGroup\nSave\nCancel\n+Share to a new group\n+Share to a new group\nPost\nCancel\nPost\nCancel"
