    "homepage_text": "Homepage of Yuan Zhang\nYuan Zhang\nPh.D. Candidate\nCenter on Frontiers of Computing Studies, Peking University\nEmail:\nzhangyuan [at] alumni.pku.edu.cn\nBiography\nYuan Zhang is a Ph.D. Candidate at\nPeking University (PKU)\n, \r\n\tadvised by Prof. Shanghang Zhang and Prof. Kuan Cheng. Previously, he received his M.Eng. degree from\r\n\tPeking University and B.Eng. degree from\nHohai University (HHU)\n. \r\n\tHe used to intern at SenseTime Research, Alibaba (DAMO Academy), ByteDance (Seed Foundation Model), and UC Berkeley (BAIR).\nHis major research interests lie within efficient machine learning algorithms, like\nEfficient AI (KD, Pruning, Quantization)\nMultimodal Large Language Model\nEducation\nPeking University (PKU)\n, Beijing, China\nPhD Candidate at\nCenter on Frontiers of Computing Studies.\nSep. 2024 – Jun. 2028\nRank: 5/52\nResearch: Efficiency for Multimodal Large Language Model\nPeking University (PKU)\n, Beijing, China\nMaster Degree.\nSep. 2020 – Jun. 2023\nRank: 3/110\nNational Scholarship of China\nHohai University (HHU)\n, Nanjing, China\nBachelor Degree.\nSep. 2016 – Jun. 2020\nRank: 1/112\nNational Scholarship of China\nSelected Publications\nFirst-author:\nICML\nx 1,\nNeurIPS\nx 1,\nCVPR\nx 1,\nACM MM\nx 1\nAll\nFirst author\nKnowledge distillation\nVision language model\nC1\nSparseVLM: Visual Token Sparsification for Efficient Vision-Language Model Inference\nYuan Zhang\n, ChunKai Fan, Junpeng Ma, and\n7 more authors,\nShanghang Zhang\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning\n(\nICML\n), 2025.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nPanasonic Press\nC2\nUnveiling the Tapestry of Consistency in Large Vision-Language Models\nYuan Zhang\n, Fei Xiao, Tao Huang, and\n6 more authors,\nHaoyuan Guo\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(\nNeurIPS\n), 2024.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nVideo\nByteDance Seed Press\nC3\nFreeKD: Knowledge Distillation via Semantic Frequency Prompt\nYuan Zhang\n, Tao Huang, Jiaming Liu, Tao Jiang, Kuan Cheng, Shanghang Zhang\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n), 2024.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nC4\nAvatar Knowledge Distillation: Self-ensemble Teacher Paradigm with Uncertainty\nYuan Zhang\n, Weihua Chen, Yichen Lu, Tao Huang, Xiuyu Sun, Jian Cao\nACM International Conference on Multimedia\n(\nACM MM\n), 2023.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nVideo\nC5\nDistilling Cross-Modal Knowledge via Feature Disentanglement\nJunhong Liu,\nYuan Zhang\n, Tao Huang, Wenchao Xu, Renyu Yang\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nAAAI\n), 2025.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nC6\nMoVE-KD: Knowledge Distillation for VLMs with Mixture of Visual Encoders\nJiajun Cao,\nYuan Zhang\n, Tao Huang, Ming Lu, Qizhe Zhang, Ruichuan An, Ningning Ma, Shanghang Zhang\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n), 2025.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nC7\nKnowledge Diffusion for Distillation\nTao Huang,\nYuan Zhang\n, Mingkai Zheng, Shan You, Fei Wang, Chen Qian, Chang Xu\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n(\nNeurIPS\n), 2023.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nC8\nMasked Distillation with Receptive Tokens\nTao Huang*,\nYuan Zhang*\n, Shan You, Fei Wang, Chen Qian, Jian Cao, Chang Xu\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations\n(\nICLR\n), 2023.\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nVideo\nManuscripts\nResearch\nSparseVLM+: Visual Token Sparsification with Improved Text-Visual Attention Pattern\nYuan Zhang\n, Junpeng Ma, Qizhe Zhang, Chun-Kai Fan, Wenzhao Zheng, Kuan Cheng, Jiwen Lu, Shanghang Zhang\nResearchGate preprint (2025).\nPDF\nBib\nCode\narXiv\nChainV: Atomic Visual Hints Make Multimodal Reasoning Shorter and Better\nYuan Zhang\n, Ming Lu, Junwen Pan, Tao Huang, Kuan Cheng, Qi She, Shanghang Zhang\narXiv preprint arXiv:2511.17106 (2025).\nPDF\nBib\narXiv\nLoss-Oriented Ranking for Automated Visual Prompting in LVLMs\nYuan Zhang\n, Chun-Kai Fan, Tao Huang, Ming Lu, Sicheng Yu, Junwen Pan, Kuan Cheng, Qi She, Shanghang Zhang\narXiv preprint arXiv:2506.16112 (2025).\nPDF\nBib\narXiv\nDAMO-YOLO: A Report on Real-Time Object Detection Design\nXianzhe Xu*, Yiqi Jiang*, Weihua Chen*, Yilun Huang*,\nYuan Zhang*\n, Xiuyu Sun\narXiv preprint arXiv:2211.15444 (2022).\nPDF\nBib\nCode\nVideo\nResearch Experience\nBerkeley Artificial Intelligence Research Lab (BAIR)\n, California, USA\nRemote Research Intern  (Advisor:\nWenzhao Zheng\n).\nSep. 2024 – Dec. 2024\nVision Foundation Model.\nEfficiency in LVLMs and propose SparseVLM.\nByteDance Seed Foundation Model\n, Beijing, China\n(S1) Researcher  (Advisor:\nHaoyuan Guo\n).\n(S2) Research Intern  (Advisor:\nMing Lu\n).\nJul. 2023 – Jul. 2024, Jan. 2025 – Now\nVision Foundation Model.\nResearch on Consistency in LVLMs and propose\nConBench\n.\nAlibaba DAMO Academy\n, Beijing, China\nResearch Intern  (Advisor:\nWeihua Chen\n).\nJun. 2022 – Feb. 2023\nResearch on knowledge distillation (KD) and propose AvatarKD.\nDistill for DAMO-YOLO.\nSenseTime Research\n, Beijing, China\nResearch Intern  (Advisor:\nTao Huang\n).\nMar. 2022 – Jun. 2022\nResearch on knowledge distillation (KD) and propose MasKD.\nDevelop on MMRazor.\nAcademic Services\nReviewer for Conferences:\nCVPR\n2024 |\nECCV\n2024 |\nACM MM\n2024 |\nNeurIPS\n2024\nICLR\n2025 |\nAISTATS\n2025 |\nCVPR\n2025 |\nICML\n2025 |\nICCV\n2025 |\nNeurIPS\n2025\nWACV\n2026 |\nAAAI\n2026 |\nAISTATS\n2026 |\nICLR\n2026 |\nCVPR\n2026 |\nICML\n2026\nReviewer for Journals:\nIJCV\n|\nT-IP\n|\nT-MLR\n|\nT-MM\n|\nT-CSVT\n|\nT-NNLS\nOpen Source Projects\nYOLOv5-Multibackbone-Compression\nDuty: Owner.\nOct. 2021 – Mar. 2022\nDescription: YOLOv5 Series Multi-backbone(TPH-YOLOv5, Ghostnet, ShuffleNetv2, Mobilenetv3Small, EfficientNetLite, PP-LCNet, SwinTransformer YOLO), \r\n\tModule(CBAM, DCN), Pruning (EagleEye, Network Slimming), Quantization (MQBench) and Deployment (TensorRT, ncnn) Compression Tool Box.\nDAMO-YOLO\nDuty: Distill and Deployment.\nJun. 2022 – Sep. 2022\nDescription: First make distillation great again on all size models of YOLO series (1.0 AP+), especially on the small size.\nAwards and Honor\nTencent Scholarship\nPh.D. period (¥ 20,000).\nSep. 2025\nNational Scholarship of China\nMaster period (¥ 20,000).\nNov. 2021\nNational Scholarship of China\nUndergraduate period (¥ 8,000).\nNov. 2018\nVisitors\n© Yuan Zhang | Last updated: Nov. 15, 2025"
