  "serper::Phoebe Lin": {
    "homepage": "https://www.phoebezlin.com/",
    "emails": [
      "phoebe.lin93@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/phoebelin/",
    "homepage_text": "Phoebe Lin, Product Designer and Researcher\nHome\nAbout\nCV\nWriting\nI'm Phoebe,\nProduct designer & researcher, driven by curiosity\nI care about the way people learn and questions like \"How do we create rich environments that allow children to develop powerful ideas?\" I'm good at taking complex, ambiguous spaces, and turning it into things that are intuitive and simple. I thrive in collaborative teams.\nScroll to see my latest work\nInteraction Design\nIdeation\nInteraction Design\nUX Visioning\nUI Design\nProduct Strategy\nStorytelling\nUser Research\nSummit Learning Onboarding\nCompany\nRole\nProject\nChan Zuckerberg Initiative\nLead Designer\nPlatform Retention / Journey Mapping / Visioning\nThe Onboarding & Training team co-created an onboarding vision with our education partner, Gradient Learning, to streamline new teacher and school-leader experiences on the Summit Learning Platform and reduce time to true engagement. The new onboarding provides teachers with a range of low- to high-touch learning experiences, including contextualized walkthrough videos, a course and data \"sandbox\", a \"My Summit Assistant\", and more. We also reimagined the teacher home page to provide teachers with immediate access to relevant information.\nSummit Learning Platform Redesign\nCompany\nRole\nProject\nChan Zuckerberg Initiative\nSr Product Designer\nInformation Architecture / Org Strategy\nAfter an org-wide strategy shift, the Summit Learning Platform was finally ready for a redesign that was long overdue. The core instructional and projects flow were clunky, and the new platform needed to accommodate any type of curricula and assessments. We came up with six novel IA approaches, and prioritized two with engineering to move forward with.\nThe first model is the curriculum-based model where information is primarily organized by curriculum structure. This model prioritizes helping teachers understand their students' progress and identify differentiation opportunities.\nThe second model is a modal-based model where information is primarily organized by what the user is doing in the moment. This model prioritizes all the JTBDs in Differentiation, Giving feedback, Internalization, and Planning equally.\nSelf-Directed Learning\nCompany\nRole\nProject\nChan Zuckerberg Initiative\nSr Product Designer\nProduct Innovation / Field Research / Org Strategy\nHow do we empower students to take charge of their own learning in a classroom? One challenge we found students faced was not knowing what their interests are and how material in school is relevant to their interests. We set out to create an interest exploration tool that exposed students to new fields and ideas, and then connected established interests to skills they practiced in class.\nFull case studies\nCreating an Empowering Student Experience on an LMS\nHow do you make a reporting tool used in schools an empowering experience for students? The SchoolCity student portal allows students to track their own progress, understand what is expected, and engage with learning in the classroom.\nTeaching Children Machine Learning through a Conversational Agent\nHow do you design an effective and engaging learning experience to teach children what AI is? Zhorai is a novel conversational AI learning experience that utilizes the glass-box and question-and-answer pedagogies.\nGet in touch and let’s collaborate.\nlinkedin\n\nemail\n\nHome\nAbout\nCV\nWriting"
  },
