    "homepage_text": "Lixin WANG\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nLixin WANG\nDoctor of Philosophy (Student)\n,\nDepartment of Chemistry\nh-index\n121\nScopus Citations\n2\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2024\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 7\nAffordable and Clean Energy\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Lixin WANG is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n12\nSimilar Profiles\nTransition Metal Dichalcogenide\nMaterial Science\n100%\nNanostructured Material\nMaterial Science\n62%\nNanosheet\nMaterial Science\n50%\nMonolayers\nMaterial Science\n50%\nHydrogen Evolution\nMaterial Science\n50%\nTransition Metal\nChemical Engineering\n50%\nHydrogen\nChemical Engineering\n50%\nPlatinum\nMaterial Science\n37%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n3\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\nUnconventional-Phase 1T′-Transition Metal Dichalcogenide Monolayers Grown on Amorphous Templates for Highly Efficient Hydrogen Evolution\nLi, Z.\n(Co-first Author),\nYang, H.\n(Co-first Author), Sun, M. (Co-first Author), Zhang, A. (Co-first Author), Ge, Y.,\nLong, X.\n,\nHuang, B.\n,\nZhai, L.\n,\nZhai, W.\n,\nLi, L.\n,\nWang, L.\n,\nWang, C.\n,\nXu, Y.\n, Cai, Y., Liu, P., Chen, B., Gu, L., Qiao, P., Zhang, Q. & Ding, F.\n& 1 others\n,\nZhang, H.\n,\n25 Feb 2026\n,\nIn:\nJournal of the American Chemical Society.\n148\n,\n7\n,\np. 7342-7354\n13 p.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nMonolayers\n100%\nHydrogen Evolution\n100%\nTransition Metal Dichalcogenide\n100%\nTransition Metal\n100%\nHydrogen\n100%\n2H-Au Nanosheet-Templated Growth of PdFe for Electrocatalytic Methanol Oxidation\nWang, J. (Co-first Author), Zhang, A. (Co-first Author), Niu, W. (Co-first Author), Liu, G. (Co-first Author),\nZhou, X.\n(Co-first Author),\nWang, L.\n, Liu, X.,\nLi, L.\n,\nLi, Z.\n,\nZhai, L.\n,\nYang, Q.\n,\nHuang, B.\n,\nWa, Q.\n, Yun, Q., Cheng, H., Ge, Y., Huang, J., Hu, Z., Chen, B. & Zhang, Q.\n& 3 others\n,\nFan, Z.\n, Gu, L. &\nZhang, H.\n,\n22 May 2025\n,\nIn:\nAdvanced Functional Materials.\n35\n,\n21\n,\n7 p.\n, 2405073.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nNanosheet\n100%\nNanostructured Material\n25%\nCrystalline Material\n25%\nElectrocatalysts\n25%\nAlloy\n12%\n12\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n6\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nPhase Engineering of Nanomaterials: Transition Metal Dichalcogenides\nZhai, W.\n,\nLi, Z.\n,\nWang, Y.\n,\nZhai, L.\n,\nYao, Y.\n,\nLi, S.\n,\nWang, L.\n,\nYang, H.\n,\nChi, B.\n,\nLiang, J.\n,\nShi, Z.\n, Ge, Y., Lai, Z., Yun, Q., Zhang, A.,\nWu, Z.\n,\nHe, Q.\n, Chen, B., Huang, Z. &\nZhang, H.\n,\n10 Apr 2024\n,\nIn:\nChemical Reviews.\n124\n,\n7\n,\np. 4479-4539\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nTransition Metal Dichalcogenide\n100%\nNanostructured Material\n100%\nFerroelectric Material\n12%\nCatalysis\n12%\nCrystal Structure\n12%\n109\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)"
