    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nXibin ZHAO-School of Software, Tsinghua University\nä¸­æ\nHome\nAbout\nIntroduction\nContact Us\nNews\nNotice\nNews\nPeople\nFaculty\nVisiting Professor\nPost-doctoral\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nInstitutions & Centers\nResearch Awards\nResearch Projects\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate Courses\nGraduate courses\næç´¢\nç«ç¹å¯¼èª\nHome\nAbout\nIntroduction\nContact Us\nNews\nNotice\nNews\nPeople\nFaculty\nVisiting Professor\nPost-doctoral\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nInstitutions & Centers\nResearch Awards\nResearch Projects\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate Courses\nGraduate courses\nShare to\nFaculty\nName:\nXibin ZHAO\nTitle:\nlong-term associate professor\nEmail:\nzxb@tsinghua.edu.cn\nAddress:\n11-313, East Main Building, Tshinghua University\nResearch Fields:\nXibin Zhao has been dedicated to research in network security anomaly detection and attack tracing, focused on building a comprehensive network security defense system that covers the entire life cycle of data perception, processing, and analysis. \r\nIn the field of anomaly detection, he is devoted to entity behavior feature modeling, out-of-distribution data analysis, and new attack detection algorithms based on deep learning. \r\nIn terms of attack tracing, he studies construction of multi-host and full-system tracing diagrams by unified modeling based on multi-level logging and further explores the diagramsâ compression, repre-sentation, and modeling methods and establishment of a set of tracing diagram collection and manage-ment algorithms for different data sources and systems, and effective reconstruction of the attacker's complete attack chain through approaches such as attack entry point analysis and link restoration. \r\nHis research areas include information system security, industrial networks and control, enterprise in-formationization, artificial intelligence, intelligent manufacturing, and knowledge automation.\nEDUCATION\nPh.D., Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, Jiangsu University, 2004\nM.S., Computer Science, Jiangsu University, 2000\nB.S., Computer Science, Jiangsu University, 1994\nEMPLOYMENT\n2013-Present, School of Software, Tsinghua University, Associate Professor\n2011-2011, Computer Science, Hong Kong University of Science and Technology, Visiting Scholar\n2007-2013, School of Software, Tsinghua University, Assistant Professor\n2005-2007, School of Software, Tsinghua University, Postdoc\nOTHER TITLES\nMember, The Ministry of Science and Technology's \"12th Five-Year Plan\" 863 Advanced Manufac-turing Field Major Project \"Core Software\" Experts Group\nMemberï¼The Ministry of Science and Technology's \"14th Five-Year Plan\" National Key R&D Pro-gram \"Social Governance and Smart Society Technology Support\" Experts Group\nDeputy director, Key Laboratory of Information System Security, Ministry of Education\nDirector, Tsinghua University-China Central Depository & Clearing Co., Ltd. Joint Institute for Fi-nancial Information Technology Innovation\nDeputy director, Tsinghua University - CRRC Sifang Institute of Intelligent Equipment Industrial Internet of Things Joint Research Center\nSenior member, China Automation Association\nMember, China Automation Society Intelligent Manufacturing Committee\nMember, Equipment Certification Technical Committee of China Urban Rail Transit AssociationPC member, International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI'2020)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI'2022)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR'2022)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI'2021)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI'2020)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI'2020)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR'2020)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI'2019)ï¼CCF Aï¼\nPC member, IEEE International Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME'2019) ï¼CCF Bï¼\nPC member, IEEE International Conference on Multimedia and Expo (ICME'2018) ï¼CCF Bï¼\nPC member, IEEE Real-Time and Embedded Technology and Applications Symposium (RTAS'2018)ï¼CCF Bï¼\nCOURSES TAUGHT\nApplied Cryptography\nInternet and Information Security Technologies\nRESEARCH PROJECTS\n1. Research on general models, theories and application methods of industrial software components, Guangdong Provincial Joint Foundation, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. U20A6003 (sub-project leader)\n2. Research on self-adaptive detection of multi-source heterogeneous data anomalies in industrial scenarios, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. 62076146 (project leader)\n3. Data Space Construction Method and Technology for Rail Transit Equipment Manufacturing Enterprises Supporting Personalized Business Chain, National Key Research and Development Projects, project No. 2018YFB1703404 (sub-project leader)\n4. Research on innovation and development of industrial Internet platforms for business groups, Chinese Academy of Engineering\n5. Artificial intelligence-driven optimization and control in discrete manufacturing, Guangdong Provincial Joint Foundation, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. U1801263 (sub-project leader)\n6. Research and development of basic software and supporting tools for rail transit equipment, sub-project of National Key Research and Development Project (core electronic devices, high-end general-purpose chips and basic software products), project No. 2016ZX01038101-002 (project leader)\n7. Real-time collection of industrial process data and knowledge automation, Guangdong Provincial Joint Fund, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. U1701262\n8. Data perception, transmission and big data processing of IoT in intelligent manufacturing, Guangdong Provincial Joint Fund, project No. U1201251 (sub-project leader)\n9. Research on common technology and standard specification of MES of discrete manufacturing, key project of 863 Program, project No. 2012AA040906 (project leader)\n10. Reliability investigation of hybird wireless mesh network for airport surface communications, joint project of Tsinghua University and Boeing ( (main researcher)\n11. Research on domestic basic software security testing technology, sub-project of National Key Research and Development Projects (core electronic devices, high-end general-purpose chips and basic software products), project No. 2010ZX01045-002-3 (main researcher)\n12. Multi-scale cross-sensing computing theory and key technologies for mobile social networks, key project of National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. 61133016 (sub-project leader)\n13. Research on reliability of domain-oriented MANET service access, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. 61073168 (Principal Investigator)\n14. \"A demonstrative information security project at China Minzu Securities\", Demonstrative Information System Security Project under National Development and Reform Commission (deputy leader)\n15. Research on reliability assurance mechanisms of product design processes, sub-project of 973 Program Project \"Research on Reliability of Large-scale Application Software for Modern Design\", project No. 2010CB328000 (the backbone of the project)\n16. Research and development and application of reconfigurable information integration platforms for business groups, goal-oriented project of 863 program, project No. 2009AA04Z153 (main researcher)\n17. Configurable MES products and industry solutions for discrete manufacturing, key project of 863 Program, project No. 2007AA040701-1 (leader)\n18. Development and demonstrative application of digitalized integrated integrated systems for large-scale electrical business groups in Jiangsu Province, Major Research Project Funded by Jiangsu Provincial Government, project No. BE2007071\n19. Development and demonstrative application of digital integration technology for design in rail transit industry, Major Research Project Funded by Jiangsu Provincial Government, project No. BE2007003\n20. China Postdoctoral Science Foundation (40th batch, second-class funding)\n21. Security mechanism for multi-user collaborative computing in grid computing, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. 90412007\n22. Research on identification, control and application of disturbed systems in complex thermal systems, National Natural Science Foundation of China, project No. 60474026\n23. E-commerce-oriented customer relationship management development tools, 863 Program, project No. 2001AA414220\n24. XML-based e-commerce platform, 863 Program, subject No. 2001AA414020\n25. Research, development and application of a new generation of ERP software, major software project of 863 Program, project No. 2003AA4Z3210\n26. Development and application of integrated systems for informatization of small and medium-sized manufacturing enterprises, 863 Program, project No. 2003AA414030\n27. Research on complex authorization mechanism in grid computing, sub-project of 863 Program, project No. 2003AA148020 (deputy leader)\n28. Research on complex authorization mechanisms in distributive enterprise information system, sub-project of 863 Program, project No. 2003AA414031 (leader)\n29. Research on requirements modeling and conversion tools for ERP of manufacturing enterprises, sub-project of 863 Program, project No. 2003AA414031 (deputy leader)\n30. Research on CRM Application Model (funded by Key Science and Technology Foundation under Jiangsu Provincial Department of Education)\n31. Research and development of information integration system for discrete manufacturing enterprises and its application in switching and electrical industry, major project of 863 Program, project No. 2003AA411020 (deputy leader)\n32. ERP system of East China Electric Power Equipment Manufacturing Plant (Demonstrative Informatization Project for Sm...[truncated]"
