    "homepage_text": "Buyu Liu\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nBuyu Liu\nWelcome to\nBuyu Liu\n's Homepage\nAbout Me\nI am\nan\nAssociate\nProfessor at\nZhejiang University\nfrom Jan. 2024, after the five-year cheerful experience at\nNEC Laboratories America\nas\na senior researcher\n. Prior to this, I was postdoc researcher in the\nschool of informatics\nat the\nUniversity of Edinburgh\n, working with\nVittorio Ferrari\n. I was a PhD candidate in\nCollege of Engineering and Computer Science\nin\nAustralian National University\nfrom 2012 to 2016, working with\nXuming He\n(supervisor) and\nStephen Gould\n(advisor).\nI was also working in\nComputer Vision Group\n, Canberra Research Laboratory,\nNational ICT of Australia (NICTA)\n.  (my previous homepage can be found\nhere\n)\nResearch Interests\n3D Scene Understanding and its Security: road layout estimation; indoor scene understanding and trajectory prediction\nSemantic Video/Image Parsing\nDynamic Holistic Scene Understanding\nEfficient Inference and Test-time Aware Learning\nActive Learning for Structured Output\nGetting involved\n🙋\nI am always looking for well-motivated and hard-working students who are interested in doing research with me. You can read some of my selected\nPublication\nto get a feel for the type of work that I do. I encourage students to contact me but please read the following before doing so:\nTo Potential PhD students:\nYou must have good mathematical and computational skills, preferably with prior experience in machine learning and/or computer vision. Strong programming skills in Python and/or C++, and familiarity with software revision control (e.g., GitHub) is also required. When contacting me include a copy of your\nacademic transcript\nand\nresume.\nA\nproposed research topic\n(\nas a minimum, please include (i) the research question, (ii) its relationship to previous work, and (i\nii\n) a timeline and milestones\n) is also preferred.\nWhat do you expect:\nWhy do you want to pursue a Ph.D.? This is the first question applicants need to ask themselves. Whether it's to continue\nyour career in academia\nor to be more competitive in the industry, we are committed to providing assistance in four aspects: theory, programming, writing, and presentation.\nJoin us, and you will expect:\nWeekly/Bi-weekly one-one meetings 🧑‍🏫 : discuss individual research progress.\nSmall-scale reading groups 📖 : share research highlights in different domains.\nResearch activities 🧳 : participate in top-tier conferences.\nRich team-wise activities 🏸 : if you would like to.\nNote: All applications for PhD or Masters should come through the Department applications system.\nContact\nEmail\nbuyu.zju at outlook dot com\nor\nbuyu.liu at zju.edu.cn\nNews\nWe have three papers submitted to CVPR 24\nWe have one paper\naccepted\nin\nNeurIPS 24\nmain track\n. See you at\nVancouver :)\nWe have\none paper accepted\nin\nACM MM24\nWe have two papers accepted in CVPR 24.\nWe have\none\npaper accepted in ACM MM23\n.\nPresented our work on trajectory prediction in Berkeley Deep Drive 2023.\nWe have\none\npaper\naccepted\nin\nCVPR23.\nServed as SPC in IJCAI 2023\nWe have three papers\naccepted\nin CVPR22\nWe have two papers submitted to TIP (We\nrank\nthe\nfirst\non\nGaze Estimation Benchmark\n(See either results or Within-Dataset and search for\nHDU_CS\n)\n! Our code can be found\nhere\n)\nWe have\none\npaper accepted\nin\nCVPR21\n...\nLast updated: 01/14/2024.   © 2024 Buyu Liu. All Rights Reserved.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Y. Zhang": {
