    "homepage_text": "Yuankai Huo |   Vanderbilt Institute for Surgery and Engineering | Vanderbilt University\nSkip to main content\nlink\nVanderbilt Institute for Surgery and Engineering\nHome\n»\nPersonnel\n»\nYuankai Huo\nYuankai Huo\nAssistant Professor in Computer Science\nEducation:\nPh.D., Electrical Engineering\nVanderbilt University, 2018\nM.S., Computer Science,\nColumbia University, New York, NY, 2013-2014\nThesis title:\n“Structural Medical Image Analyses using Consistent Volume and Surface Image Processing”\nDefense date:\nMay 02 2018\nCommittee:\nBennett A. Landman, Ph.D. Benoit M. Dawant, Ph.D. Richard Alan Peters, Ph.D. Hakmook Kang, Ph.D. Richard G. Abramson, M.D. Warren D. Taylor, M.D.\nArea/Interests:\nMedical image analysis, machine learning\nLab:\ntHe biomedical data Representation and Learning laB (HRLB)\nyuankai.huo@vanderbilt.edu\nWebsite\nLab Website\nSeminar sign-up\nEmail\nmichelle.bukowski@vanderbilt.edu\nto receive seminar announcements.\nNIH Grant Writing – Miga June 2022\nNIH Grant Writing – Johnson June 2022\nNIH Workshop Short Talks April 2023\nLearn more about the\nMaster of Engineering Degree (ESI)\nDownload the ESI degree\nprogram guide\nVISE Partners\nVanderbilt School of Engineering\nVanderbilt School of Medicine\nMedical Innovators Development Program (MIDP)"
