    "homepage_text": "Yen-Chun Chen\n      -  National Taiwan Normal University\nNational Taiwan Normal University  Home\nHelp & FAQ\nLink opens in a new tab\nEnglish\n中文\nSearch content at National Taiwan Normal University\nView Scopus Profile\nYen-Chun Chen\nAssociate Professor\nCollege of Management\nEmail\nbluekikochen\nntnu.edu\ntw\nh-index\nh10-index\nh5-index\n579\nCitations\n14\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n308\nCitations\n11\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n62\nCitations\n4\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2009\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 9\nIndustry, Innovation, and Infrastructure\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Yen-Chun Chen is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n12\nSimilar Profiles\norientation\nINIS\n100%\nperformance\nINIS\n84%\nmarket\nINIS\n55%\ninteractions\nINIS\n40%\nmarketing\nINIS\n38%\nSimultaneous Engineering\nSocial Sciences\n31%\nvalues\nINIS\n30%\nEntrepreneurial Orientation\nSocial Sciences\n29%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n22\nArticle\n5\nChapter\nDoes organizational ambidextrous learning matter for digital transformation?\nChen, Y. C.\n& Lin, Y. H.,\n2025\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nManagement Decision.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nlearning\n100%\ntransformations\n100%\nperformance\n36%\nvalues\n27%\nEntrepreneurial Action\n10%\n2\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nUnderstanding the role of entrepreneurial orientation in creating ambidextrous competitive advantage: a comparative-design, longitudinal study\nChen, Y. C.\n, Arnold, T., Liu, P. Y. & Huang, C. Y.,\n2023 Jan 4\n,\nIn:\nEuropean Journal of Marketing.\n57\n,\n1\n,\np. 89-124\n36 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\ndesign\n100%\norientation\n100%\nCompetitive Advantage\n100%\nLongitudinal Analysis\n100%\nEntrepreneurial Orientation\n100%\n19\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nDoes alliance orientation matter for new product success? An empirical study of Taiwanese electronics firms\nChen, Y. C.\n& Arnold, T.,\n2022 Nov 30\n,\nIn:\nEuropean Journal of Marketing.\n56\n,\n12\n,\np. 3347-3380\n34 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\norientation\n100%\nSimultaneous Engineering\n100%\nNew Product Development\n100%\nDecision Making\n60%\nInnovativeness\n60%\n7\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nUnderstanding the interplay between competitor and alliance orientations in product innovativeness: An integrative framework\nChen, Y. C.\n, Lin, Y. H., Li, P. C. & Chen, C. J.,\n2022 Feb\n,\nIn:\nTechnological Forecasting and Social Change.\n175\n, 121358.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nRegression Analysis\n100%\nAnalysis of Covariance\n100%\nQuantile Regression\n100%\nPartial Least Squares Structural Equation Modeling\n100%\norientation\n100%\n11\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nCustomer involvement, business capabilities and new product performance\nChen, Y. C.\n, Arnold, T. & Tsai, H. T.,\n2021 Oct 6\n,\nIn:\nEuropean Journal of Marketing.\n55\n,\n10\n,\np. 2769-2793\n25 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nperformance\n100%\ninformation\n100%\nbusiness\n100%\nMarketing\n100%\nmarketing\n71%\n23\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 27 research outputs"
