  "serper::Zixing Song": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/zxsong",
    "emails": [
      "songzixingbristol@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zixing Song\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZixing Song\nZixing Song\nLecturer\nSchool of Engineering Mathematics and Technology\nUniversity of Bristol\n🏢:\nAda Lovelace Building, Bristol BS8 1TW, UK\n📧:\nsongzixingbristol[at]\ngmail.com\n🎓\n:\nGoogle Schola\nr\nI am currently a Lecturer (equivalent to Assistant Professor in the US) at the\nSchool of Engineering Mathematics and Technology\n,\nUniversity of Bristol\n. Before that, I was a postdoctoral research associate in the\nMachine Learning Group\nat the\nDepartment of Engineering\n,\nUniversity of Cambridge\n. I was lucky to work with\nProf. José Miguel Hernández-Lobato\nat the\nComputational and Biological Learning Lab\n. I obtained my PhD degree from the\nComputer Science and Engineering Department\n,\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK)\n, where I was fortunate to be supervised by\nProf. Irwin King\n. Prior to that, I received my BEng in Computer Science from\nSoutheast University\n, Nanjing, China.\nMy research focuses on data-efficient learning for graph-structured data, with a central goal of ensuring trustworthiness—specifically explainability, fairness, and robustness—across its cross-disciplinary applications in social network analysis, natural science, and financial services.\n🔥 I am looking for self-motivated students to work with me on the following topics. Details can be found under the\nRecruitment\nPage.\nLLMs for graph data, Graph foundation models (alignment, agent, RAG, distillation, reasoning, ...)\nDeep generative models for graphs in drug discovery (molecular generation, dynamics simulation, ...)\nTrustworthy graph machine learning with weak supervision (robustness, fairness, explainability, ...)\nCross-disciplinary Graph Neural Networks applications in time-evolving areas (transaction networks, knowledge graphs, ...)\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
