    "homepage_text": "Kai Yao's Homepage\nPublications\nNews\nBio\nKai Yao\nSenior Algorithm Engineer\nAnt Group\nHangzhou, China\njiumo.yk (at) antgroup.com\nShort Bio\nI’m a researcher at Ant Group, working on Large Language Models. My research journey began with a B.Eng. from\nXi’an Jiaotong-Liverpool University\n, followed by a PhD from\nUniversity of Liverpool\n. I then completed my PostDoc at\nZhejiang University\nunder Prof.\nJianke Zhu\n’s guidance. My research background lies in computer vision, language models and transfer learning.\nResearch Interest\nLarge Language Model\nTransfer Learning\nImage Generation\nMedical Image Analysis\nAutonomous Driving Systems\nEducation\nPh.D. in Computer Science\n, 2019.12 - 2023.11,\nUniversity of Liverpool\nB.Eng. in Computer Science\n, 2014.9 - 2018.6,\nXi’an Jiaotong-Liverpool University\nResearch Experience\nPostdoctoral Fellow\n, 2024.1 - 2026.1,\nZhejiang University\nWork Experience\nSenior Algorithm Engineer\n, 2024.1 - Present, Ant Group\nReview Experience\nACL, EMNLP, ICLR, NeurIPS, CVPR, ECCV, ICCV, Nature Communication\nHonors and Awards\nTop 5 in\nCrossMoDa Challenge 2021\n.\nThe third prize of 2020-2021 Outstanding Academic Papers of Suzhou Natural Science.\nFull Doctoral Scholarship, University of Liverpool, 2019.\nNews\n[JAN. 2026]\nOur conference paper accepted in EACL 2026 as Oral presentation.\n[SEG. 2025]\nOur paper accepted in IJCV and ACM MM 2025.\n[AUG. 2025]\nOur conference paper accepted in CIKM 2025.\n[APR. 2025]\nOur conference paper accepted in ACL 2025.\n[DEC. 2024]\nOur conference paper accepted in AAAI 2025 as Oral presentation.\n[NOV. 2024]\nI am happy to attend EMNLP 2024 in person at Miami.\n[SEP. 2024]\nOur conference paper accepted in EMNLP24.\n[DEC. 2023]\nOur conference paper accepted in AAAI24.\n[Aug. 2023] Our papers accepted as Oral Presentation in ACM CIKM 2023.\n[May. 2023] Our two journal papers accepted in IEEE TETCI and IJB.\n[Nov. 2022] Our conference paper accepted in AAAI 2023. We propose a novel augmentation for medical image domain generalization. The code released at\nhere\n.\n[Jul. 2022] Our conference paper accepted in ECCV 2022. We propose a novel hybrid vision-transformer-based GAN for image outpainting. The code released at\nhere\n.\n[Jun. 2022] Our journal paper accepted in IEEE-JBHI (IF: 7.0).\n[Dec. 2021] Our team PremiLab wins 5th in the Challenge\nCrossMoDa 2021 (MICCAI workshop)\n.\n[Dec. 2021] Our journal paper accepted in International Journal of Bioprinting (IF: 7.4).\n[Nov. 2021] Our journal paper accepted in Cognitive Computation (IF: 4.9).\n[Dec. 2019] I started my PhD course at UoL PremiLab Lab with full scholarship.\nshow more\nPublications\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nEACL 2026 Oral\nGAST:Gradient-aligned Sparse Tuning of Large Language Models with Data-layer Selection\nKai Yao\n, Zhenghan Song, Kaixin Wu, mingjie zhong, Danzhao Cheng, Zhaorui Tan, Yixin Ji, Penglei Gao\nEuropean Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics\nNLP Top\nIJCV\nUnlock Pose Diversity:Accurate and Efficient Implicit Keypoint-based Spatiotemporal Diffusion for Audio-driven Talking Portrait\nChaolong Yang*,\nKai Yao*\n, Yuyao Yan, Chenru Jiang, Weiguang Zhao, Jie Sun, Guangliang Cheng, Yifei Zhang, Bin Dong, Kaizhu Huang\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision\nPDF\nCode\nCCF-A, CV Top\nACM MM 2025\nKDTalker++:Controllable Talking Portrait Generation with Audio, Text, and Expression Editing\nChaolong Yang, Yinuo Guo,\nKai Yao\n, Yuyao Yan, Jie Sun, Kaizhu Huang\nACM Multimedia\nCode\nCCF-A, CV Top\nCIKM 2025\nTowards Instance-wise Personalized Federated Learning via Semi-Implicit Bayesian Prompt Tuning\nTiandi Ye, Wenyan Liu,\nKai Yao\n, Lichun Li, Shangchao Su, Cen Chen, Xiang Li, Shan Yin, Ming Gao\nACM International Conference on Information and Knowledge Management\nPDF\nCCF-B\nACL 2025\nGradOT:Training-free Gradient-persevering Offsite-tuning for Large Language Models\nKai Yao*\n, Zhaorui Tan*, Penglei Gao, Lichun Li, Kaixin Wu, Yinggui Wang, Yuan Zhao, Yixin Ji, Wei Wang, Jianke Zhu\nAnnual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics\nPDF\nCCF-A, NLP Top\nUnder Review\nTest-time Compute:from System-1 Thinking to System-2 Thinking\nYixin Ji, Juntao Li, Hai Ye, Kaixin Wu,\nKai Yao\n, Jia Xu, Linjian Mo, Min Zhang\nPDF\nUnder Review\nTNNLS\nSCMix:Stochastic Compound Mixing for Open Compound Domain Adaptation in Semantic Segmentation\nKai Yao*\n, Zhaorui Tan*, Zixian Su, Xi Yang, Jie Sun, Kaizhu Huang\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems\nPDF\nCCF-B\nAAAI 2025 Oral\nScaleOT:Privacy-utility-scalable Offsite-tuning with Dynamic LayerReplace and Selective Rank Compression\nKai Yao\n, Zhaorui Tan, Tiandi Ye, Lichun Li, Yuan Zhao, Wenyan Liu, Wei Wang, Jianke Zhu\nProceedings of Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence\nPDF\nCCF-A\nEMNLP 2024\nLayer-wise Importance Matters:Less Memory for Better Performance in Parameter-efficient Fine-tuning of Large Language Models\nKai Yao*\n, Penglei Gao*, Lichun Li, Yuan Zhao, Xiaofeng Wang, Wei Wang, Jianke Zhu\nProceedings of Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\nPDF\nCode\nCCF-B, NLP Top\nECCV 2024\nUnleashing the Power of Prompt-driven Nucleus Instance Segmentation\nZhongyi Shui, Yunlong Zhang,\nKai Yao\n, Chenglu Zhu, Yuxuan Sun, Lin Yang\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision\nPDF\nCode\nCCF-B, CV Top\nUnder Review\nOPa-Ma:Text Guided Mamba for 360-degree Image Out-painting\nPenglei Gao*,\nKai Yao*\n, Tiandi Ye, Steven Wang, Yuan Yao, Xiaofeng Wang\nPDF\nUnder Review\nAAAI 2024 Oral\nUnraveling Batch Normalization for Realistic Test-Time Adaptation\nZixian Su, Jingwei Guo,\nKai Yao\n, Xi Yang, Qiufeng Wang, Kaizhu Huang\nProceedings of Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence\nPDF\nCode\nCCF-A\nCIKM 2023 Oral\nExplore Epistemic Uncertainty in Domain Adaptive Semantic Segmentation\nKai Yao\n, Zixian Su, Xi Yang, Jie Sun, Kaizhu Huang\nACM International Conference on I