    "homepage_text": "Xiwen Yao\n      -  Northwestern Polytechnical University\nNorthwestern Polytechnical University Home\nEnglish\n中文\nSearch content at Northwestern Polytechnical University\nView Scopus Profile\nYao Xiwen\nProfessor\nSchool of Automation\nh-index\n7907\nCitations\n39\nh-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2013\n2026\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 11\nSustainable Cities and Communities\nSDG 13\nClimate Action\nSDG 15\nLife on Land\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Xiwen Yao is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n12\nSimilar Profiles\nObject Detection\nComputer Science\n100%\nRemote Sensing Image\nComputer Science\n97%\nRemote Sensing\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n53%\nConvolutional Neural Network\nComputer Science\n41%\nImage Segmentation\nComputer Science\n27%\nOptical Remote Sensing\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n20%\nSynthetic Aperture Radar\nEarth and Planetary Sciences\n17%\nDeep Learning Method\nComputer Science\n14%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations and top research areas from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration on country/territory level. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a country/territory to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a country/territory from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n68\nArticle\n17\nConference contribution\n2\nConference article\n1\nPaper\nDomain Adaptation for Object Detection Based on Domain-Aware Prompting in Remote Sensing Imagery\nZhang, X.,\nYao, X.\n,\nCheng, G.\n&\nHan, J.\n,\n2026\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing.\n64\n, 5607916.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nObject Detection\n100%\nDomain Adaptation\n100%\nPerformance Degradation\n33%\nSuperior Performance\n33%\nInvariant Domain\n33%\nDual-perspective filter pruning via diversity and independence collaboration\nGao, C., Cao, Q.,\nYao, X.\n, Feng, X. &\nCheng, G.\n,\nSep 2026\n,\nIn:\nPattern Recognition.\n177\n, 113321.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nConvolutional Neural Network\n100%\nCompression Efficiency\n100%\nGlocalDualNet: Disentangling Scale and Representation for Few-Shot Remote Sensing Segmentation\nTang, H., Jia, Y., Cheng, J., Mu, Y., Wu, Y. &\nYao, X.\n,\n2026\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Applied Earth Observations and Remote Sensing.\n19\n,\np. 8018-8030\n13 p.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nImage Segmentation\n100%\nsegmentation accuracy\n33%\nRepresentation Learning\n16%\nLearning Process\n16%\nIntrinsic Property\n16%\nIntroducing WSOD-SAM Proposals and Heuristic Pseudo-Fully Supervised Training Strategy for Weakly Supervised Object Detection in Remote Sensing Images\nQian, X., He, Z., Wang, W., Yue, W.,\nYao, X.\n&\nCheng, G.\n,\n2026\n,\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing.\n64\n, 5602412.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nRemote Sensing Image\n100%\nObject Detection\n100%\nSegment Anything Model\n100%\nSuperior Performance\n7%\nAnnotation\n7%\nPrototype Decoupled Knowledge Distillation\nLiu, Y., Qu, Z., Liu, N.,\nYao, X.\n&\nHan, J.\n,\n2026\n, (Accepted/In press)\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology.\nResearch output\n:\nContribution to journal\n›\nArticle\n›\npeer-review\nKnowledge Distillation\n100%\nInstance Level\n42%\nSuperior Performance\n14%\nKnowledge Transfer\n14%\nView all 88 Research outputs"
