    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Hongzhan Lin - Daniel Lin / Homepage\nHongzhan Lin\nPositive Pessimist. Here I want to express my highest respect to my grandpa, for his endless love that will guide me forever.\nFollow\nSingapore\nNUS\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nHongzhan Lin\n☀️About Me\nThis is Hongzhan Lin (林鸿展 in Chinese). I will be joining\nCTIC\nresearch centre at National University of Singapore (NUS) as a research fellow in 2026, working with\nProf. Mong-Li Lee\n,\nProf. Wynne Hsu\n, and\nProf. Tat-Seng Chua\n. Currently, I am going to finish my PhD in NLP group at Hong Kong Baptist University (HKBU), advised by\nProf. Jing Ma\n. I visited\nNExT++\nresearch centre at NUS, working under the guidance of\nProf. Tat-Seng Chua\nfrom 2024 to 2025. Before, I obtained both of my Bachelor and Master degrees from PRIS lab at Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications (BUPT) in 2019 and 2022 respectively, advised by\nProf. Guang Chen\n. Early on I was working as an NLP research intern in Tencent AI Lab.\nMy research interests lie in Natural Language Processing, Multimodal Reasoning, and Social Computing, etc. I am open for possible collaborations. For those who are interested in working with me, please feel free to email me. Remote collaboration is also welcome!\n📚Academic Appointments\nResearch Fellow in School of Computing, NUS, Singapore [2026 - Present]\nPhD in Department of Computer Science, HKBU, Hong Kong [2022 - 2026]\nVisiting Scholar in School of Computing, NUS, Singapore [2024 - 2025]\nMaster in School of Artiticial Intelligence, BUPT, Beijing [2019 - 2022]\n📑Selected Publications\n“FACT-AUDIT: An Adaptive Multi-Agent Framework for Dynamic Fact-Checking Evaluation of Large Language Models”,\nACL 2025\n. [\nPaper\n]\n“Towards Explainable Harmful Meme Detection through Multimodal Debate between Large Language Models”,\nWWW 2024 (Oral)\n. [\nPaper\n]\n“Zero-Shot Rumor Detection with Propagation Structure via Prompt Learning”,\nAAAI 2023\n. [\nPaper\n]\n“Detect Rumors in Microblog Posts for Low-Resource Domains via Adversarial Contrastive Learning”,\nNAACL 2022 (Findings)\n. [\nPaper\n]\n“Rumor Detection on Twitter with Claim-Guided Hierarchical Graph Attention Networks”,\nEMNLP 2021\n. [\nPaper\n]\n💁‍♂️Professional Services\nConference Area Chair: ACL, EMNLP, NeurIPS\nConference Reviewer: ACL, EMNLP, WWW, AAAI, NeurIPS, ICLR, CVPR, NAACL, COLING, ACM MM, IJCAI, ECAI\nJournal Reviewer: TPAMI, TKDE, TOIS, CL, TOMM, TCSS, TCSVT, TALLIP, JAIR, EAAI, ESWA"
  },
