    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nDing Changxing\nStudy\nä¸­æ\nä¸¨\nSCUT\nMENU\nSearch\nAbout\nAbout SCUT\nAbout GZIC\nNEWS & EVENTS\nNews Highlights\nLatest News\nEvents at GZIC\nStudy\nUndergraduate Programmes\nGraduate Programmes\nSupervisors\nOutbound Programmes\nInbound Programmes\nResearch\nInstitutes & Centers\nSchools\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nInnovation Factory\nInnovation Achievement\nJoin Us\nhomepage\nStudy\nSupervisors\nSchool of Future Technology\nStudy\nUndergraduate Programmes\nGraduate Programmes\nSupervisors\nSchool of Biomedical Sciences and Engineering\nShien-Ming Wu School of Intelligent Engineering\nSchool of Emergent Soft Matter\nSchool of Microelectronics / School of Integrated Circuits\nSchool of Future Technology\nSchool of Marine Science and Engineering\nOutbound Programmes\nInbound Programmes\nDing Changxing\nTitle\nResearcher, Doctoral Supervisor,School of future technology\nE-mail\nchxding@scut.edu.cn\nHonor\nSelected as a national-level young talent and a top-notch scientist of Guangdong Province\nAdmission Programs/Majors\nMEng: 1) Electronic Information\nMSï¼1)Intelligent Science and Technology\nPh.D: 1) Electronic Information; 2) Intelligent Science and Technology;\nPersonal Profile\nGraduated with a doctorate from the University of Technology Sydney in 2016 and joined South China University of Technology as an associate researcher in the same year. In 2021, I was exceptionally promoted to researcher (with a senior professional title). The research field is computer vision and embodied intelligence, with a focus on solving the problems of understanding and generating human interactive movements, serving applications such as intelligent robots and virtual digital humans. More than 60 papers have been published in top journals and conferences such as TPAMI, IJCV, and CVPR, among which 5 are ESI highly cited papers as the first author. In the past five years, I have guided the postgraduate students of my research group to publish more than 30 papers as the first author in top journals such as IEEE T-PAMI, T-IP, IJCV, and top conferences such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, and ACM MM.\nSelected as a national-level young talent and a Guangdong Provincial Outstanding Youth. The research work won the First Prize of Natural Science of Guangdong Province in 2023, the Best Paper Award for Young Authors of the IEEE Signal Processing Society (SPS) in 2023 (only three papers were selected from thousands of top journals such as TIP/TSP/TIFS/TASLP in this year), the title of one of the top 2% of global scientists released by Stanford University, and 2021 The ACM China Rising Star Award (Guangzhou Chapter). Won the championship of the Video-based Face Recognition Challenge held by the National Institute of Standards and Technology in the United States and the top-level conference MICCAI The champion of the brain tumor segmentation competition held, and the double champion of the action Recognition Challenge and the action Expectation Challenge held by the top conference CVPR.'\nResearch Interests\nComputer vision, embodied intelligence, multimodal learning\nRepresentative Research Achievements\nJiayu Jiang, Changxing Ding*, Wentao Tan, Junhong Wang, Jin Tao, Xiangmin Xu, âModeling Thousands of Human Annotators for Generalizable Text-to-Image Person Re-identificationâ, CVPR, 2025 (CCF A).\nGuowei Wang, Changxing Ding*, âEffortless Active Labeling for Long-Term Test-Time Adaptationâ, CVPR, 2025 (CCF A).\nMengqing Xue, Yifei Liu, Ling Guo, Shaoli Huang, Changxing Ding*, âGuiding Human-Object Interactions with Rich Geometry and Relationsâ, CVPR, 2025 (CCF A).\nYupeng Hu, Changxing Ding*, Chang Sun, etc., Bilateral Collaboration with Large Vision-Language Models for Open Vocabulary Human-Object Interaction Detection, ICCV, 2025 (CCF A).\nXu Yang, Shaoli Huang, Shenbo Xie, Xuelin Chen, Yifei Liu, Changxing Ding*, Democratizing High-Fidelity Co-Speech Gesture Video Generation, ICCV, 2025 (CCF A).\nYiyang Chen, Shanshan Zhao, Lunhao Duan, Changxing Ding*, Dacheng Tao, Harnessing Text-to-Image Diffusion Models for Point Cloud Self-Supervised Learning, ICCV, 2025 (CCF A).\nGuowei Wang, Changxing Ding*, Wentao Tan, Mingkui Tan, âDecoupled Prototype Learning for Reliable Test-Time Adaptationâ, IEEE Trans. Multimedia (T-MM), 2025.\nXu Yang, Changxing Ding*, Zhibin Hong, Junhao Huang, Jin Tao, Xiangmin Xu, Texture-Preserving Diffusion Models for High-Fidelity Virtual Try-On, CVPR, 2024 (CCF A).\nWentao Tan, Changxing Ding*, Jiayu Jiang, Fei Wang, Yibing Zhan, Dapeng Tao, Harnessing the Power of MLLMs for Transferable Text-to-Image Person ReID, CVPR, 2024 (CCF A).\nZhuolong Li, Xingao Li, Changxing Ding*, Xiangmin Xu, Disentangled Pre-training for Human-Object Interaction Detection, CVPR, 2024 (CCF A).\nContact\nFor Collaborations, Tel: +86-20-81181636/1631   Email: global@scut.edu.cn\nFor Study at SCUT, Tel: +86-20-81182580/2585   Email: sieinfo@scut.edu.cn\nFor Jobs, please click\nhttps://www2.scut.edu.cn/gzic_en/2025/0820/c44854a599684/page.htm\nto find job vacancies.\nLinks\nPlease Click\nSchool of International Education, SCUT\nMinistry of Education\nChina Scholarship Council\nChina Education Association for International Exchange\nGZIC Global\nGZIC\nSCUT\n2018 Â© Guangzhou International Campus, SCUT. All Rights Reserved"
  },
