    "homepage_text": "Kui JIANG\n      -  CityUHK Scholars\nCityUHK Scholars Home\nResearcher Login\nLink opens in a new tab\nSearch content at CityUHK Scholars\nMr. Kui JIANG, 蔣奎\n(Former), (Former)\nh-index\n14772\nScopus Citations\n42\nScopus h-index\nCalculated based on number of publications stored in Pure and citations from Scopus\n2012\n2025\nResearch activity per year\nPersonal profile\nAuthor IDs\nORCID iD:\n0000-0003-1007-1315\nScopus Author ID:\n56411571500\nResearcherID:\nY-3635-2019\nGoogle Scholar Profile:\nLai4x-UAAAAJ\nPrizes/Honours\nHighly Cited Researcher 2019 by Clarivate Analytics;\nResearch Interests/Areas\nOrganic Photovoltaics\nExpertise related to UN Sustainable Development Goals\nIn 2015, UN member states agreed to 17 global\nSustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\nto end poverty, protect the planet and ensure prosperity for all. This person’s work contributes towards the following SDG(s):\nSDG 7\nAffordable and Clean Energy\nSDG 9\nIndustry, Innovation, and Infrastructure\nFingerprint\nDive into the research topics where Kui JIANG is active. These topic labels come from the works of this person. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n12\nSimilar Profiles\nOrganic Solar Cells\nMaterial Science\n100%\nPolymer\nMaterial Science\n82%\nPerovskite Solar Cell\nMaterial Science\n53%\nPolymer Solar Cell\nMaterial Science\n53%\nFullerene\nMaterial Science\n45%\nSolar Cell\nMaterial Science\n23%\nHeterojunction\nMaterial Science\n20%\nMorphology\nMaterial Science\n16%\nView full fingerprint\nCollaborations from the last five years\nRecent external collaboration based on locations. Dive into details by clicking on the dots or\nSelect a place from the list\nDive into details\nSelect a place to view shared publications and projects\nClose\nSelect a place from the list\nExplore network further\nResearch output\n52\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n1\nErratum\nPhotoluminescent delocalized excitons in donor polymers facilitate efficient charge generation for high-performance organic photovoltaics\nJiang, K.\n, Westbrook, R. J. E. (Co-first Author),\nXia, T.\n, Zhong, C., Lu, J., Khasbaatar, A., Liu, K., Lin, F. R., Jang, S.-H., Zhang, J., Li, Y., Diao, Y., Wei, Z.,\nYip, H.-L.\n, Ginger, D. S. &\nJen, A.K.-Y.\n,\nDec 2025\n,\nIn:\nNature Communications.\n16\n,\n1\n, 3176.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nFile\nDonor\n100%\nPhotoluminescence\n100%\nExciton\n100%\nOrganic Solar Cells\n100%\nPolymer\n100%\n14\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\n87\nDownloads (CityUHK Scholars)\nA hot carrier perovskite solar cell with efficiency exceeding 27% enabled by ultrafast hot hole transfer with phthalocyanine derivatives\nGong, S., Qu, G., Qiao, Y., Wen, Y., Huang, Y., Cai, S., Zhang, L.,\nJiang, K.\n, Liu, S., Lin, M., Beard, M. C., Xu, Z.-X. & Chen, X.,\n21 Jul 2024\n,\nIn:\nEnergy & Environmental Science.\n17\n,\n14\n,\np. 5080-5090\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nSun Illumination\n100%\nPerovskite Solar Cells\n100%\nSolar Cell\n100%\nTransportation\n100%\nHot Carrier\n100%\n52\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nConjugated linker-boosted self-assembled monolayer molecule for inverted perovskite solar cells\nQu, G., Cai, S., Qiao, Y.,\nWang, D.\n, Gong, S., Khan, D., Wang, Y.,\nJiang, K.\n, Chen, Q., Zhang, L., Wang, Y.-G., Chen, X.,\nJen, A. K.-Y.\n& Xu, Z.-X.,\n17 Jul 2024\n,\nIn:\nJoule.\n8\n,\n7\n,\np. 2123-2134\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nOpen Access\nSelf Assembled Monolayer\n100%\nPerovskite Solar Cell\n100%\nIndium Tin Oxide\n20%\nCharge Carrier\n20%\nUltrafast Spectroscopy\n20%\n160\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nMorphologically engineered multi-component organic solar cells with stratified donor distribution and alloyed acceptors for enhanced efficiency and stability\nZhang, N.\n,\nJiang, K.\n, Lin, F. R., An, Y.,\nDu, G.\n,\nXia, T.\n,\nJen, A.K.-Y.\n&\nYip, H.-L.\n,\nJun 2024\n,\nIn:\nMaterials Today Energy.\n42\n, 101548.\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nMorphology\n100%\nOrganic Solar Cells\n100%\nHeterojunction\n25%\n9\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nRedox mediator-stabilized wide-bandgap perovskites for monolithic perovskite-organic tandem solar cells\nWu, S.\n, Yan, Y., Yin, J.,\nJiang, K.\n,\nLi, F.\n,\nZeng, Z.\n,\nTsang, S.-W.\n&\nJen, A.K.-Y.\n,\nApr 2024\n,\nIn:\nNature Energy.\n9\n,\n4\n,\np. 411-421\nResearch output\n:\nJournal Publications and Reviews\n›\nRGC 21 - Publication in refereed journal\n›\npeer-review\nRedox Mediator\n100%\nSolar Cell\n100%\nBand Gap\n100%\nHalide\n100%\nTandem Solar Cell\n100%\n132\nLink opens in a new tab\nCitations\n(Scopus)\nView all 53 research outputs\nPrizes\nStanford's top 2% most highly cited scientists 2023\nJIANG, K.\n(Recipient),\nOct 2023\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes and awards\nScientific Field\n100%\nHighly Cited Paper\n100%\nStanford's top 2% most highly cited scientists 2022\nJIANG, K.\n(Recipient),\nNov 2022\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes and awards\nScientific Field\n100%\nHighly Cited Paper\n100%\nHighly Cited Researcher 2019\nJIANG, K.\n(Recipient),\n19 Nov 2019\nPrize\n:\nRGC 64B - Prizes and awards\nFile\nResearch Performance\n100%\nPress/Media\nCityU scientists discover a novel photophysical mechanism that has achieved record-breaking efficiency for organic photovoltaics\nJIANG, K.\n&\nJEN, A.\n21/12/22\n1 item of Media coverage\nPress/Media\n:\nPress / Media\nThesis\nRegulating Exciton Dynamics Facilitate Efficient Change Generation for High-performance Organic Photovoltaics\nJIANG, K.\n(Author),\nJEN, A.\n(Supervisor),\n2 Apr 2025\nStudent thesis\n:\nMaster's Thesis"
