    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home - Luiz Chamon\nLuiz Chamon\n© 2020–2026. All rights reserved.\nHello there!\nI am an assistant professor (tenure-track) and\nHi!PARIS\nchair holder\nin the center for applied math (\nCMAP\n) of\nÉcole polytechnique\n.\nMy group develops tools that enable intelligent systems\nto\nextract\n,\nprocess\n, and\nact\non information.\nNews\nMar 17th, 2026\n– I will give a talk at HEC's \"Law, Society & AI\" seminar series\nNov 27th, 2025\n– Check out our papers at NeurIPS 2025:\n\"Learning (approximately) equivariant networks via constrained optimization\"\n(oral)\n[\npaper\n]\n\"Learning with statistical equality constraints\"\n[\npaper\n]\nKeynote:\n\"The 5 W's and H of constrained learning\"\nat\nCOML@NeurIPS\nNov 24th, 2025\n– I received the\nShiing-Shen Chern Young Faculty award\n,\na recognition of talented young mathematicians at École polytechnique.\nJul 21st, 2025\n– I was interviewed about my research within my\nHi!PARIS\nchair. Check out the full article and video pitch\nhere\n.\nJul 17th, 2025\n– Funded 4-year grant on\n\"Beyond (Robust) Learning: Striking Compromises in Machine Learning\"\n(\nANR JCJC\n). PhD and postdoc positions will be announced soon.\nJul 20th, 2025\n– Invited keynote speaker at the NeurIPS 2025 workshop on\n\"Constrained Optimization for Machine Learning\"\n. Submit your contributions\nhere\n.\nJul 16th, 2025\n– Paper accepted at IEEE CDC 2025:\n\"A Lagrangian Framework for Safe Cooperative Reinforcement Learning\"\nwith S. Das, S. Paternain, and C. Eksin [\npaper\n].\nJun 29th, 2025\n– Invited talk at\nEUROPT 2025\nin Southampton, UK.\nJun 26th, 2025\n– Seminar at\nENS Ulm\nin Paris, France.\nJun 20th, 2025\n– New preprint:\n\"Learning (Approximately) Equivariant Networks via Constrained Optimization,\"\nwith A. Manolache and M. Niepert (\narXiv\n).\nJun 11th, 2025\n– Seminar at\nRice Paris Summit\n.\nApr 3rd, 2025\n– Seminar at\nGIPSA\n-\nLJK\n, Grenoble, France.\nMar 20th, 2025\n– Seminar at\nUC3M\n, Madrid, Spain.\nMar 14th, 2025\n– New preprint:\n\"The Lagrangian method for solving constrained Markov games,\"\nwith S. Das, S. Paternain, and C. Eksin (\narXiv\n).\nMar 11th, 2025\n– New preprint:\n\"Benign overfitting and the geometry of the ridge regression solution in binary classification,\"\nwith A. Tsigler, S. Frei, and P.L. Bartlett (\narXiv\n).\nJan 27th, 2025\n– Our paper\n\"Solving differential equations with constrained learning\"\nhas been accepted to ICLR 2025 [\npaper\n].\nJan 1st, 2025\n– I have been appointed to\nELLIS scholar\n.\n© 2020–2026. All rights reserved."
