    "homepage_text": "Guy Van den Broeck - News\nGuy Van den Broeck\nUCLA - Computer Science Department\nEngineering VI Room 368A\n404 Westwood Plaza\nLos Angeles, CA  90095-1596\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\nPronounce my name\nguyvdb@cs.ucla.edu\nguy@sigmoid.social\n@guyvdb\nI am a Professor of\nComputer Science\nand \n                    Samueli Fellow at\nUCLA\n, \n                    where I direct the\nStatistical and Relational Artificial Intelligence (StarAI) lab\n.\n                    My research interests are in \n                    Machine Learning (Tractable Deep Generative Models, Statistical Relational Learning, Probabilistic Programming), \n                    Knowledge Representation and Reasoning (Probabilistic Inference, Probabilistic Databases), \n                    and Artificial Intelligence in general.\nRecent Publications\n2026\n[239]\nPrateek Anand\n,\nAnji Liu\n,\nMeihua Dang\n,\nBoyang Fu\n,\nXinzhu Wei\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\nand\nSriram Sankararaman\n.\nGPC: Deep generative model of genetic variation data improves imputation accuracy in private populations\n,\nIn\nICLR Workshop on Generative AI in Genomics (Gen2): Barriers and Frontiers\n,\n2026\n.\n[238]\nAnji Liu\n,\nZilei Shao\nand\nGuy Van den Broeck\n.\nRethinking Probabilistic Circuit Parameter Learning\n,\nIn\nProceedings of the 29th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics (AISTATS)\n,\n2026\n.\nOral full presentation, acceptance rate 0.5%\n[237]\nDaniel Israel\n,\nTian Jin\n,\nEllie Cheng\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\n,\nAditya Grover\n,\nSuvinay Subramanian\nand\nMichael Carbin\n.\nPlanned Diffusion\n,\nIn\nProceedings of the 14th International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n,\n2026\n.\n[236]\nZheng Luo\n,\nWim Van den Broeck\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\nand\nYisu Remy Wang\n.\nAlgorithms for Optimizing Acyclic Queries\n,\nIn\nProceedings of the 29th International Conference on Database Theory (ICDT)\n,\n2026\n.\n[235]\nDaniel Israel\n,\nAditya Grover\nand\nGuy Van den Broeck\n.\nEnabling Autoregressive Models to Fill In Masked Tokens\n,\nIn\nFindings of the 19th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (EACL)\n,\n2026\n.\n[234]\nWilliam Zhao\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\nand\nBenjie Wang\n.\nHow to Marginalize in Causal Structure Learning?\n,\nIn\n5th Workshop on Graphs and more Complex Structures For Learning and Reasoning (GCLR)\n,\n2026\n.\n[233]\nAnjunyi Fan\n,\nXuejie Liu\n,\nAnji Liu\n,\nQiuping Wu\n,\nJiaqi Yang\n,\nYuchao Qin\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\n,\nYitao Liang\nand\nBonan Yan\n.\nESTroM: Element-Flow Architecture For Processing Sparse Tractable Probabilistic Models\n,\nIn\nProceedings of the 32nd International Symposium on High-Performance Computer Architecture (HPCA)\n,\n2026\n.\n2025\n[232]\nDaniel Israel\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\nand\nAditya Grover\n.\nAccelerating Diffusion LLMs via Adaptive Parallel Decoding\n,\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 38 (NeurIPS)\n,\n2025\n.\nOral spotlight presentation, acceptance rate 688/21575 = 3.1%\n[231]\nXuejie Liu\n,\nAnji Liu\n,\nYitao Liang\nand\nGuy Van den Broeck\n.\nPlug-and-Play Context Feature Reuse for Efficient Masked Generation\n,\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 38 (NeurIPS)\n,\n2025\n.\n[230]\nVinh Tong\n,\nTrung-Dung Hoang\n,\nAnji Liu\n,\nGuy Van den Broeck\nand\nMathias Niepert\n.\nRao-Blackwell Gradient Estimators for Equivariant Denoising Diffusion\n,\nIn\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems 38 (NeurIPS)\n,\n2025\n.\nMore Publications\nRecent Talks\nInvited Talk\n— Mar 2026\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\nWallenberg Advanced Scientific Forum on the Foundations of Neurosymbolic Artificial Intelligence\nTalk\n— Mar\nPolynomial semantics of probabilistic circuits and the limits of tractable marginalization\nDagstuhl Seminar on Tensor Factorizations Meet Probabilistic Circuits\nInvited Talk\n— Feb 2026\nInjecting Logical Knowledge in Autoregressive Models\nSapienza University of Rome\nInvited Talk\n— Feb 2026\nWeighted Model Counting Problems in the Context of LLMs\nShonan Meeting - Model Counting: Theory meets Practice\nInvited Talk\n— Jan 2026\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\nAAAI Bridge Program: Making Embodied AI Reliable with Testing and Formal Verification\nInvited Talk\n— Jan 2026\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\nNational University of Singapore\nInvited Talk\n— Oct 2025\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\nAmazon\nInvited Talk\n— Sep 2025\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\nNVIDIA\nInvited Talk\n— Sep 2025\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\nUPenn ASSERT Center Seminar\nKeynote\n— Sep 2025\nSymbolic Reasoning in the Age of Large Language Models\n19th Conference on Neurosymbolic Learning and Reasoning (NeSy 2025)\nMore Talks"
