    "homepage_text": "Seyed Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\nSeyed\nMohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\nResearch Scientist\nI am a Staff Machine Learning Researcher at Apple Zurich. Prior to that, I was an Assistant Professor at\nImperial College London\nin the Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering. Before joining Imperial College, I was a postdoctoral researcher in the\nInstitute for Machine Learning\nat the\nETH Zurich\n. I received my PhD in Computer and Communication Sciences under the supervision of\nPascal Frossard\nat the\nÉcole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL)\n, Switzerland in November 2019. My PhD research focused on the analysis of the robustness of classifiers and its connection with the geometry of deep neural networks. I was also fortunate to intern for the Apple AI Research in 2017, working on autonomous technologies.\nI got my M.Sc. degree in Communication Systems from the EPFL, in 2014, and my B.Sc. in Electrical Engineering from\nTehran Polytechnic\n, Iran, in 2012.\nNews\nJun 2024\nI have joined Apple Zurich as an AI/ML researcher!\nAug 2022\nI gave an invited talk on various aspects of robustness and generalization at Apple MLR/MI.\nJul 2022\nI attended\nDagstuhl Seminar on Security of Machine Learning\n. That was amazing!\nJun 2022\nOur work on data augmentationt for common corruptions,\nPRIME\n, got accepted at ECCV 2022!\nMar 2022\nMy joint work with\nEPFL’s VITA lab\non robustness of vehicle trajectory prediction models is accepted at CVPR 2022.\nSelected Publications\nICLR\nReducing Excessive Margin to Achieve a Better Accuracy vs. Robustness Trade-off\nRahul Rade,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                and\nSeyed-Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\nIn International Conference on Learning Representations\n2022\nPDF\nICML\nUniform Convergence, Adversarial Spheres and a Simple Remedy\nGregor Bachmann,\nSeyed-Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Thomas Hofmann\nIn International Conference on Machine Learning\n2021\narXiv\nNeurIPS\nNeural Anisotropy Directions\nGuillermo Ortiz-Jimenez,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Apostolos Modas,\nSeyed-Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Pascal Frossard\nIn Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems\n2020\narXiv\nBlog\nCode\nVideo\nCVPR\nGeoDA: a geometric framework for black-box adversarial attacks\nAli Rahmati,\nSeyed-Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Pascal Frossard,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Huaiyu Dai\nIn IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n2020\narXiv\nCode\nVideo\nCVPR\nRobustness via curvature regularization, and vice versa\nSeyed-Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Alhussein Fawzi,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  Jonathan Uesato,\n                \n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Pascal Frossard\nIn IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n2019\narXiv\nCode\nCVPR\nGeometric robustness of deep networks: analysis and improvement\nCan Kanbak,\nSeyed-Mohsen Moosavi-Dezfooli\n,\n              \n            \n          \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n            \n              \n                \n                  and Pascal Frossard\nIn IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n2018\narXiv\nCode"
