    "homepage_text": "Home\nPublications & preprints\nStudents\nTeaching\nVita\nJean-Michel Loubes\nInstitut de Mathématiques de Toulouse\nHome\nResearch Director at INRIA\non leave from Professor of Mathematics\nAffiliated to\nInstitut de Mathématiques de Toulouse\n&  associate\nToulouse School of Economics\nProjet INRIA\nRegalia\nPrincipal Investigator Chair TRIAL (Trustworthy AI & Machine Learning)\npreviously chair : Fair and Robust Machine Learning\nat Artificial and Natural Intelligence Toulouse Institute (\nANITI\n)\nResearch :\nMathematical Statistics, Machine Learning & Optimal Transport\nFairness, Robustness and Explainability of Artificial Intelligence\nIndustrial Applications\nPublications : link to my\ngoogle page\nCurrent Projects :\nAudit of AI’s models : Bias Analysis, Robustness & Explainability – Head of ANR  Regulation of AI &  Principal Investigator in ANITI’s CHAIR Trust and Responsibility in AI  & Scientifi PI of REGALIA Team\nMember of AFNOR CEN-CENELEC on AI Regulations norms (2024-..)\nPrincipal Investigator in the Explainability Project\nGEMS\n(CNRS Prize for innovation 2019) with\na video\nSport & Artificial Intelligence\nActualités :\nCours :\nFairness and statistics (IHP 2025)\nWorld AI Summit 2025\nRetrouver mes formations sur l’IA et la régulation :\nCNRS FORMATION\nPast & Current Duties\nMember of Scientifi Comitee of ANITI (2019- … )\nMember of National Council of University CNU 26 (2016-2020)\nMember of  Scientific Comitee of\nCNRS Mathematical Institute\n(2020-2024)\nDeputy President\nof Toulouse 3 University in charge of Innovation for Industry (2019-2023)\nHead of\nMaster 2 Mathematics and Applications\n(2019-2024)\nMember of the founder team of\nMaths-Industry CNRS Project AMIES\nand Head for Occitanie region 2010-2016 (Toulouse, Montpellier,\nPau\n, Perpignan, …). National Expert member on Machine Learning and Data Science\nDirector of Research Team (Statistics and Probability) and Member of Directoire de l’Institut de Mathématiques (2008-2012)\nQuelques interventions sur l’IA et la confiance dans les décisions algorithmiques\nBiais et explicabilité en IA :\nCNRS Formation\nANITI DAYS :\nTrust and Reliability\nLes biais et l’IA :\nUsine Nouvelle\nLa confiance dans l’IA :\nLe Monde\nLe dictionnaire du numérique\nInterventions at\nEuropean Network  NeEDS\n,\nBias in Medicine\n,\nBCAM\n,\nCNRS Innovation\n,\nANITI\nMail:\nloubes »at »math.univ-toulouse.fr\nHome\nPublications & preprints\nStudents\nTeaching\nVita\nCopyright © 2026 Jean-Michel Loubes. All rights reserved. WordPress Theme by\nWPZOOM\nMentions Légales"
