    "homepage_text": "Jonathan Ragan-Kelley\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nAssociate Professor\nComputer Science & Artificial Intelligence Lab\nDepartment of Electrical Engineering & Computer Science\nMassachusetts Institute of Technology\njrk@mit.edu\n32-D462\n32 Vassar St.\nCambridge, MA 02139\nBio\nI am an associate professor of\nElectrical Engineering & Computer Science\nat\nMIT\n.\nI was previously an assistant professor of\nEECS\nat\nUC Berkeley\n, a postdoc in\ncomputer science\nat\nStanford\n, where I worked with\nPat Hanrahan\nand\nMark Horowitz\n, and a visiting researcher at\nGoogle\n. My work focuses on high-efficiency computer graphics, at the intersection of graphics with systems, architecture, and compilers. I did my PhD with\nFrÃ©do Durand\nand\nSaman Amarasinghe\nat\nMIT CSAIL\n, developing the\nHalide language\ntogether with\nAndrew Adams\n, have worked at three\nmajor\nGPU\nvendors\nin architecture, compilers, and research, and built a\nreal-time preview system\nfor the special effects industry in collaboration with\nIndustrial Light & Magic\n.\nCurrent Advisees\nRahul Goel\n(with FrÃ©do Durand)\nDavid Akeley\nManya Bansal\n(with Saman Amarasinghe)\nKartik Chandra\n(with Josh Tenenbaum)\nYuka Ikarashi\nTian Jin\n(with Michael Carbin)\nAmanda Liu\n(with Adam Chlipala)\nAhmed Mahmoud\n(postdoc, jointly with Justin Solomon)\nWilliam Brandon (on leave at Anthropic)\nFormer Students & Postdocs\nGilbert Bernstein\nâ Assistant Professor at University of Washington\nSamir Droubi â Jump Trading\nKarl Krauth\nâ Postdoc at Stanford\nTzu-Mao Li\nâ Assistant Professor at UC San Diego\nKarima Ma\n- Researcher at Adobe\nKenneth Moon - Citadel Securities\nKevin Mu â PhD student at University of Washington\nAnne Ouyang â PhD student at Stanford\nKevin Qian â Jane Street, incoming PhD student at Stanford\nAlex Reinking\nâ Researcher at Adobe\nAJ Root\nâ PhD student at Stanford\nVaishaal Shankar\nâ Researcher at Anthropic\nPublications\nLightweight and Locality-Aware Composition of Black-Box Subroutines\nManya Bansal,\nDillon Sharlet\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n,\nSaman Amarasinghe\nProceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages (PLDI 2025)\nExo 2: Growing a Scheduling Language\nYuka Ikarashi\n, \n                Kevin Qian, \n                Samir Droubi,\nAlex Reinking\n, \n                Gilbert Louis Bernstein,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nASPLOS 2025\nSketching With Your Voice: \"Non-Phonorealistic\" Rendering of Sounds via Vocal Imitation\nMatthew Caren,\nKartik Chandra\n, \n                Joshua B. Tenenbaum,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n,\nKarima Ma\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2024\nReducing Transformer Key-Value Cache Size with Cross-Layer Attention\nWilliam Brandon, \n                Mayank Mishra, \n                Aniruddha Nrusimha, \n                Rameswar Panda,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nNeurIPS 2024\nFast Matrix Multiplications for Lookup Table-Quantized LLMs\nHan Guo, \n                William Brandon, \n                Radostin Cholakov,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n, \n                Eric P. Xing, \n                Yoon Kim\nEMNLP 2024\nHydra: Sequentially-Dependent Draft Heads for Medusa Decoding\nZachary Ankner, \n                Rishab Parthasarathy, \n                Aniruddha Nrusimha, \n                Christopher Rinard,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n, \n                William Brandon\nConference on Language Modeling (COLM 2024)\nA Verified Compiler for a Functional Tensor Language\nAmanda Liu\n, \n                Gilbert Louis Bernstein,\nAdam Chlipala\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nProceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages (PLDI 2024)\nStorytelling as Inverse Inverse Planning\nKartik Chandra\n,\nTzu-Mao Li\n, \n                Joshua B. Tenenbaum,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nTopics in Cognitive Science (2024)\nDistributions for Compositionally Differentiating Parametric Discontinuities\nJesse Michel, \n                Kevin Mu, \n                Xuanda Yang, \n                Sai Praveen Bangaru, \n                Elias Rojas Collins,\nGilbert Bernstein\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n, \n                Michael Carbin,\nTzu-Mao Li\nProceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages (OOPSLA 2024)\nFast Instruction Selection for Fast Digital Signal Processing\nAlexander J Root,\nMaaz Bin Safeer Ahmad\n,\nDillon Sharlet\n,\nAndrew Adams\n,\nShoaib Kamil\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nProceedings of the ACM International Conference on Architectural Support for Programming Languages and Operating Systems (ASPLOS 2024)\nSLANG.D: Fast, Modular and Differentiable Shader Programming\nSai Praveen Bangaru, \n                Lifan Wu,\nTzu-Mao Li\n, \n                Jacob Munkberg,\nGilbert Bernstein\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n,\nFrÃ©do Durand\n, \n                Aaron Lefohn, \n                Yong He\nACM Transactions on Graphics (SIGGRAPH Asia 2023)\nInferring the Future by Imagining the Past\nKartik Chandra\n, \n                Tony Chen,\nTzu-Mao Li\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n, \n                Josh Tenenbaum\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2023)\nSemantics and Scheduling for Machine Knitting Compilers\nJenny Lin, \n                Vidya Narayanan,\nYuka Ikarashi\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n,\nGilbert Bernstein\n, \n                James McCann\nACM Transactions on Graphics (Proc. SIGGRAPH 2023)\nActing as Inverse Inverse Planning\nKartik Chandra\n,\nTzu-Mao Li\n, \n                Joshua B. Tenenbaum,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nSIGGRAPH 2023\nGradient Descent: The Ultimate Optimizer\nKartik Chandra\n, \n                Audrey Xie,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\n, \n                Erik Meijer\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (distinguished paper, NeurIPS 2022)\nDesigning Perceptual Puzzles by Differentiating Probabilistic Programs\nKartik Chandra\n,\nTzu-Mao Li\n,\nJoshua Tenenbaum\n,\nJonathan Ragan-Kelley\nSIGGRAPH 2022\nExocompilation for productive programming of hardware accelerators\nYuka Ikarashi\n,\nGilbert Bernstein\n,\nAlex Reinking\n,\nHasan Genc\