  "serper::Toh Kar-Ann": {
    "homepage": "https://milab.yonsei.ac.kr/professor",
    "emails": [
      "katoh@yonsei.ac.kr",
      "katoh@ieee.org"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Professor\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nProfessor\nKar-Ann Toh\nProfessor, Ph.D., Senior Member, IEEE\nSchool of Electrical & Electronic Engineering,\nYonsei University, Seoul, Korea\nTel: +82-2-2123-5864, Fax: +82-2-312-4584\nOffice: #216, Engineering Building C\nEmail:\nkatoh(AT)yonsei.ac.kr\nor\nkatoh\n(AT)\nieee.org\nBrief Biography\nKar-Ann Toh received the Ph.D. degree from Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore. He then worked for two years in the aerospace industry, prior to his postdoctoral appointments at research centers in NTU, from 1998 to 2002. He was with the Institute for Infocomm Research, Singapore, from 2002 to 2005. He is a full Professor with the School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Yonsei University, South Korea. His research interests include biometrics, pattern classification, machine learning, optimization, and neural networks. Besides being active in publication, he has served as a member of advisory board and technical program committee for international conferences related to biometrics and artificial intelligence. He has served as an Associate Editor for the IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security from 2013 to 2016, the Pattern Recognition Letters from 2011 to 2021, and the Journal of The Franklin Institute from 2018 to 2020. He is currently an Associate Editor of the IEEE Transactions on Biometrics, Behavior, and Identity Science, and an\nEditorial Board Member of\nIET Biometrics.\nProfessional Activities\n(last-modified: 18 Mar 2022)\n- Senior Member of IEEE (since 2003).\n-\nEditorial\n:\nAssociate Editor, IEEE Transactions on Biometrics, Behavior and Identity Science (Nov 2018 - present)\nEditorial Board Member, IET Biometrics (March 2012 - present)\nAssociate Editor, IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security (2013 - 2016)\nAssociate Editor, Journal of The Franklin Institute: Engineering and Applied Mathematics (Jan 2018 - Jan 2020)\nAssociate Editor, Pattern Recognition Letters, Elsevier (March 2011 - September 2021)\nEditorial Board of IEEE Biometrics Council Newsletter (2013 - 2015)\nGuest editorial\n:\nJiankun Hu, Vijayakumar Bhagavatula, Mohammed Bennamoun and Kar-Ann Toh, Special Issue on Biometric Security for Mobile Computing, Security and Communication Networks Journal, John Wiley, 2011.\nGuang-Bin Huang, Erik Cambria, Kar-Ann Toh, Bernard Widrow, Zongben Xu, Special Issue on New Trends of Learning in Computational Intelligence, IEEE Computational Intelligence Magazine, 2015.\nBook editorial\n:\nHaizhou Li, Kar-Ann Toh, and Liyuan Li, Advanced Topics in Biometrics, World Scientific Publishing Co. Pte. Ltd., 2011.\nFuchen Sun, Kar-Ann Toh, Manuel Grana Romay and Kezhi Mao, Extreme Learning Machines 2013: Algorithms and Applications, Springer, Mar 5, 2014.\n-\nInternational Advisory Board\n:\nThe 5th IAPR/IEEE International Conference on Biometrics, Mar 30-Apr01, 2012, New Delhi, India, (ICB'12)\nInternational Joint Conference on Biometrics, October 2011, Washington DC, USA, (IJCB'11)\nIEEE International Conference on Signal and Image Processing Applications, November 2011, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, (ICSIPA'11)\nIEEE International Conference on Signal and Image Processing Applications, November 2009, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, (ICSIPA'09)\n-\nAwards\n:\nBest Paper Award, for the paper \"Learning from the Kernel and the Range Space\" which was presented in the 17th IEEE/ACIS International Conference on Computer and Information Science, 2018.\nOutstanding Teaching Award for 20\n21\nacademic year, School of EEE Yonsei University.\nOutstanding Teaching Award for 2014 academic year, School of EEE Yonsei University.\nOutstanding Teaching Award for 2013 academic year, School of EEE Yonsei University.\n-\nConference Committee\n:\nInternational Joint Conference on Biometrics (IJCB 2022), October 10-13, 2022, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates (https://ijcb2022.org/).\n14th International Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Information Retrieval, October 25-27, 2022 (KDIR), Valletta, Malta (https://kdir.scitevents.org/Home.aspx)\nTrack Chair of Signal Processing, 15th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 16--19 December 2022, Chengdu, China (ICIEA 2022)\n35th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI 2021) February 2-9, 2021, Virtual\\\\ (\nhttps://aaai.org/Conferences/AAAI-21/\n)\n2021 IEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP 2021) September 19-22, 2021, Anchorage, Alaska, USA (https://www.2021.ieeeicip.org/www.2021.ieeeicip.org/index.html)\nIEEE International Symposium on Circuits and Systems (ISCAS 2021), May 23-26, 2021, On-Site \\& Virtual, Daegu, Korea (https://iscas2021.org/)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, 15th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 21–25 June 2020, Kristiansand, Norway (ICIEA 2020)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, 14th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 19–21 June 2019, Xi’an, China (ICIEA 2019)\nKar-Ann Toh, Area Chair, The 11th IAPR International Conference on Biometrics (ICB 2018), February 20 - 23, 2018, Madrid, Queensland, Australia (http://icb2018.org/) (one of major conferences in biometrics.)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, 13th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 31 May–2 June 2018, Wuhan, China (ICIEA 2018)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal and Information Processing, 12th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 18-20 June 2017, Siem Reap, Cambodia (ICIEA 2017)\nKar-Ann Toh, Area Chair, IEEE Eighth International Conference on Biometrics: Theory, Applications and Systems, 6-9 September 2016, Niagara Falls, USA (BTAS 2016). (one of major conferences in biometrics.)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, 11th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 5-7 June 2016, Hefei, China, (ICIEA 2016)\nKar-Ann Toh and Michele Nappi, Publication Co-Chair, The 8th IAPR International Conference on Biometrics (ICB 2015), May 19 - 22, 2015 Phuket, Thailand (http://http://icb2015.org/) (one of major conferences in biometrics.)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, 10th International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 15-17 June 2015, Auckland, New Zealand (ICIEA 2015)\nKar-Ann Toh, Area Chair, International Joint Conference on Biometrics, September 29 - October 2, 2014, Florida, USA (IJCB’14) (http://www.ijcb2014.org/) (a major conference in biometrics.)\nKar-Ann Toh, Area Chair, The 6th IAPR International Conference on Biometrics (ICB 2013), June 4 - 7, 2013 Madrid, Spain (http://atvs.ii.uam.es/icb2013/) (one of major conferences in biometrics.)\nDong Sun, Yiguang Hong, Stan Li, and Kar-Ann Toh, Program Co-Chairs, The 12th International Conference on Control, Automation, Robotics and Vision, December 2012, Shenzhen, China (ICARCV 2012) Call for Papers\nAndrew Teoh, Pong C. Yuen, Jiankun Hu, Jaihie Kim and Kar-Ann Toh, ICIEA Invited Session on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, Seventh International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 18-20 July 2012, Singapore (ICIEA 2012) Call for Papers\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, Seventh International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 18-20 July 2012, Singapore (ICIEA 2012) Call for Papers\nAndrew Teoh, Kwanghoon Sohn, Jiankun Hu, Arun Ross, and Kar-Ann Toh, ICIEA Invited Session on Biometrics and Pattern Recognition, 21-23 June 2011, Beijing, China (ICIEA 2011)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, Sixth International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 21-23 June 2011, Beijing, China (ICIEA 2011)\nArun Ross, Kar-Ann Toh and Sudeep Sarkar, Program chairs, IEEE Fourth International Conference on Biometrics: Theory, Applications and Systems (BTAS 2010), 27-29 September 2010, Washington DC, USA (BTAS 2010)\nKar-Ann Toh, Jiankun Hu and Andrew Teoh, ICIEA Invited Session on Biometrics, 15-17 June 2010, Taichung, Taiwan (ICIEA 2010)\nKar-Ann Toh, Kwanghoon Sohn and Sangyoun Lee, Special Session on Vision, Recognition and Biometrics, IEEE TENCON 2009, 23-26 November 2009, Singapore (TENCON 2009)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, Fifth International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 15-17 June 2010, Taichung, Taiwan (ICIEA 2010)\nKar-Ann Toh, Andrew Teoh and Kwanghoon Sohn, ICIEA Invited Session on Pattern Analysis and Biometrics, 25-27 May 2009, Xi’an, China (ICIEA 2009)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, Fourth International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications, 25-27 May 2009, Xi’an, China (ICIEA 2009)\nKar-Ann Toh, Technical Track Chair, The Tenth International Conference on Control, Automation, Robotics and Vision, 17-20 December 2008, Hanoi, Vietnam (ICARCV 2008)\nKar-Ann Toh, Zujun Hou and Andrew Teoh, ICIEA Invited Session on Pattern Analysis and Biometrics, 3-5 June 2008, Singapore (ICIEA 2008)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair of Signal Processing, Third International Conference on Industrial Electronics and Applications 3-5 June 2008, Singapore (ICIEA 2008)\nKar-Ann Toh, Track Chair, IEEE International Conferences on Cybernetics & Intelligent Systems (CIS) and Robotics, Automation & Mechatronics (RAM), 3-6 June, 2008, Chengdu, China (CIS-RAM 2008) Call for papers\nKar-Ann Toh, and Andrew B. J. Teoh, Chair/Vice Chair of ISATC Outreach Task Force 2007-2008, IEEE Computational Intelligence Society.\nKar-Ann Toh, Sangyoun Lee, and Jaihie Kim, ICIEA Invited Session on Biometrics, Fusion and Pattern Recognition, 23-25 May, 2007, Harbin, China (ICIEA 2007)\nKar-Ann Toh, Technical Track Chair, The Ninth International Conference on Control, Automation, Robotics and Vision, 5-8 December 2006, Singapore (ICARCV 2006)\nKar-Ann Toh and Ke Chen, ICIEA Invited Session on Pattern Analysis and Biometrics, 24-26 May, 2006, Singapore (ICIEA 2006)\nKe Chen, Kar-Ann Toh and Peter Tino, Special Session on Natural Co...[truncated]"
