    "homepage_text": "Media IC & System Lab\nMedia IC & System Lab\nIntroduction\nResearch\nMembers\nCourses\nPublication\nMembers only\nProfessor\nGroup Picture\nPostdoc\nPh.D. Students\nMaster Students\nRA\nAlumni\nProfessor\nShao-Yi Chien (簡韶逸)\nResearch Summary:\nProf. Chien directs Media IC & System Design Lab. The research area includes multimedia signal processing systems, multimedia VLSI design, and System-on-a-Chip design methodology. The research level is from algorithm level, hardware architecture level, to system level. The current research directions of Media IC & System Design Lab are intelligent video signal processing systems, image signal processing systems, graphics processing unit design, and image/video coding systems.\nSee Prof. Shao-Yi Chien's Homepage\nGroup Picture\nPostdoc\nPh.D. Students\nLi-Yang Huang (黃立洋)\nResearch Area:\nPose Estimation/Tracking, Pose Engine Design\nEmail:\nlyhuang@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nPo-Hsien Yu (喻柏憲)\nResearch Area:\nDNN accelerator architecture\nEmail:\nmichaelyu@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nFu-Sheng Yu (于富昇)\nResearch Area:\nMulti-task learning\nEmail:\nfushengyu@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nMaster\nYung-Wei Fan (范詠為)\nResearch Area:\nLandmark detection/gesture recognition/Human reconstruction\nEmail:\nywfan@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nYu-Kai Hsieh (謝郁楷)\nResearch Area:\nNN based visual odometry\nEmail:\nykhsieh@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nTzu-Hsuan Lin (林子軒)\nResearch Area:\nEfficient Video Inference/ Efficient Hardware Backbone for Distributed Intelligence\nEmail:\nzslin@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nTang-I Wang (王瑭毅)\nResearch Area:\nLocalization in Wide Area for Augmented Reality Systems\nEmail:\ntiwang@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nHeng-Hsiu Hu (胡珩秀)\nResearch Area:\nSuper-resolution for Oshawott\nEmail:\nderekpigg@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nMeng-Ping Lin (林孟平)\nResearch Area:\nEye-tracking Guided Beamforming\nEmail:\nmplin@media.ee.ntu.edu.tw\nTzu-Ching Huang (黃子青)\nResearch Area:\nRemote Eye Tracking for DMS/Landmark Detection\nEmail:\ntchuang@media.ee.ntu.edu.