    "homepage_text": "Chunjing Xiao's Homepage\nChunjing Xiao\nAssociate Professor\nSchool of Computer and Information Engineering\nHenan University\nEmail: chunjingxiao@gmail.com\nAddress: Jinming Road, Henan University, Kaifeng, China\nI received my Ph.D. degree from the\nUniversity of Electronic Science and\n        Technology of China\nin Chengdu, China.\n        Currently, I hold the position of an Associate Professor at the\nSchool of\n        Computer and Information Engineering\n,\nHenan University\nin Kaifeng,\n        China. During my academic journey, I had the privilege of being a visiting scholar with the Department of\n        Electrical Engineering and Computer Science at Northwestern University, located in Evanston, IL, USA.\n        My research interests lie in the fields of recommender systems, anomaly detection, and the Internet of Things.\n        These areas have captivated my passion, and I am constantly seeking ways to contribute to their advancements. As\n        an academic and researcher, I am dedicated to exploring innovative solutions and making meaningful contributions\n        to these domains. More information about my experience and research can be found on\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nPublications\n2024:\nMotif-Consistent Counterfactuals with Adversarial Refinement for Graph-Level Anomaly Detection.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Shikang Pang, Wenxin Tai, Yanlong Huang, Goce Trajcevski, Fan Zhou.\nACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining.\nCounterfactual data augmentation with denoising diffusion for graph anomaly detection.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Shikang Pang, Xovee Xu, Xuan Li, Goce Trajcevski, Fan Zhou.\nIEEE Transactions on Computational Social Systems.\nNatural Evolution-based Dual-Level Aggregation for Temporal Knowledge Graph Reasoning.\nBin Chen,\nChunjing Xiao*\n, Fan Zhou.\nConference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing.\nDiffusion model-based contrastive learning for human activity recognition.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Yanhui Han, Wei Yang, Yane Hou, Fangzhan Shi, Kevin Chetty.\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal.\nGraph anomaly detection with diffusion model-based graph enhancement .\nShikang Pang,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Wenxin Tai, Zhangtao Cheng, Fan Zhou.\nProceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence.\n2023:\nCounterfactual Graph\n                    Learning for Anomaly Detection on Attributed Networks.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Xovee Xu, Yue Lei, Kunpeng Zhang, Siyuan Liu, Fan Zhou.\nIEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering.\nMean Teacher-based\n                    Cross-Domain Activity Recognition using WiFi Signals.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Yue Lei, Chun Liu, Jie Wu.\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal.\nExploring\n                    indirect entity relations for knowledge graph enhanced recommender system.\nZhonghai He, Bei Hui, Shengming Zhang,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Ting Zhong, Fan Zhou.\nExpert Systems with Applications.\nUncertainty-Aware\n                    Heterogeneous Representation Learning in POI Recommender Systems.\nFan Zhou, Tangjiang Qian, Yuhua Mo, Zhangtao Cheng,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Jin\n                Wu, Goce Trajcevski.\nIEEE Transactions on Systems, Man, and Cybernetics: Systems.\n2022:\nSelf-Supervised Few-Shot\n                    Time-series Segmentation for Activity Recognition.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Shiming Chen, Fan Zhou, Jie Wu.\nIEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing.\nDeep\n                    metric learning for accurate protein secondary structure prediction.\nWei Yang, Yang Liu,\nChunjing Xiao\n.\nKnowledge-Based Systems.\nCombining\n                    Imputation Method and Feature Weighting Algorithms to Improve the Classification Accuracy of\n                    Incomplete Data.\nYue Wang, Cong Guo,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Wei Yang.\nJournal of Physics: Conference Series.\nConnecting the Hosts:\n                    Street-Level IP Geolocation with Graph Neural Networks.\nZhiyuan Wang, Fan Zhou, Wenxuan Zeng, Goce Trajcevski,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Yong Wang, Kai Chen.\nProceedings of the 28th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining, 4121-4131.\n2021:\nA Real-time Activity\n                    Recognition System based on Dynamic Adaptive Windows using WiFi Signals.\nShiming Chen,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Yanhui Han, Xianghe Du.\nProceedings of the 2021 5th International Conference on Computer Science and Artificial\n                Intelligence, 122-127.\nMetaRisk:\n                    Semi-supervised few-shot operational risk classification in banking industry.\nFan Zhou, Xiuxiu Qi,\nChunjing Xiao\n, Jiahao Wang.\nInformation Sciences.\n2020:\nDeepSeg:\n                    Deep-learning-based activity segmentation framework for activity recognition using WiFi.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Yue Lei, Yongsen Ma, Fan Zhou, Zhiguang Qin.\nIEEE Internet of Things Journal.\nTime\n                    sensitivity-based popularity prediction for online promotion on Twitter.\nChunjing Xiao\n, Chun Liu, Ying Ma, Zheng Li, Xucheng Luo.\nInformation Sciences.\nReliability on Deep\n                    Learning Models: A Comprehensive Observation.\nYuhong Zhang,\nChunjing Xiao\n.\n2020 6th International Symposium on System and Software Reliability (ISSSR).\n本课题组注重学生能力提升和实践培养，2024届研究生都在行业内顶级会议和期刊发表了学术论文，\n        其中2人的论文发表在CCF-A类国际会议KDD，1人的论文发表在中科院一区期刊。\n        课题组的研究生毕业论文荣获2024年“河南省优秀硕士学位论文”，毕业研究生入职小米、比亚迪等科技名企。\n课题组与美国University of Maryland和Iowa State University，以及英国University College London的教授保持紧密的学术合作。\n       组内研究氛围浓厚，注重理论实践结合，有助于同学们的学业提升。欢迎对人工智能、大数据领域有兴趣的同学加入课题组，共同进行学习和研究。\n邮箱：9310028@qq.com\n微信号："
  },
  "serper::Molei Tao": {
    "homepage": "https://mtao8.math.gatech.edu/",
    "emails": [
      "mtao@gatech.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Molei Tao\nwelcome\nhome\nbio\npublication\ngroup\nteaching\nservice\nc.v. (2023)\nblog\nMolei Tao\n(full) Professor, Richard Duke Fellow\nSchool of Mathematics\nGeorgia Institute of Technology\n(sorry I don't use LinkedIn, but I use X (Twitter))\nFollow @MoleiTaoMath\nOffice: Skiles 214A\nAddress: 686 Cherry St NW, Atlanta GA 30332, USA\nPhone: +1-404-894-3711\nmtao at gatech dot edu\nsome other affiliations:\nGT Machine Learning Center\nAlgorithms & Randomness Center (ARC)\nAlgorithms, Combinatorics & Optimization (ACO) Program\nGT Decision & Control Lab\nTech AI\n(Internal Technical Advisory Board)\nGT AI4Science Center\n(Associate Director)\nWhat do I do?\nMy current interest is mainly the\ntheoretical and algorithmic foundation of machine learning\n. This includes\nprobabilistic ML, including sampling, measure transport, and (diffusion) generative modeling\ndeep learning theory, optimization, and geometric methods in ML; I advocate an emerging direction we call ‘dynamical systems for machine learning’\nAI4Sciences (astronomy, quantum sciences, bioengineering, scientific computing, mechanical engineering, material sciences, chemistry, …)\nPre-history I worked on structure preserving numerics (a.k.a. geometric integration), stochastic methods, and multiscale modeling/analysis.\nA subset of what I'm thankful for.\n(sorry if I forget to update!)\nJan 2026: Fortunate to have amazinging collaborators. 8 x ICLR’26 main track.\nSep 2025: Congrats to Kijung, Yuchen, Wei, Jaemoo, Avrajit, Lianghe, Yinuo and Haoxuan. 6 x NeurIPS’25 main track well deserved.\nSep 2025: Honored and grateful to have received Richard Duke Fellowship, and generous supports from 2 x DOE + 1 x NSF.\nAug 2025:\nGT AI4Science Center\nlaunched. Delighted to serve as an Associate Director.\nJul 2025: Our NeurIPS 2025\nDynaFront (Dynamics at the Frontiers of Optimization, Sampling, and Games) Workshop\nwas accepted. If you care about dynamical aspects and foundations of machine learning, please consider submitting and/or attending!\nMar 2025: Congrats to Yuqing - Sigma Xi Award for Best Ph.D. Thesis in Georgia Tech (2024)!\nMar 2025: Congrats to Ye - multiple tenure track offers! Proud of you, and best wishes to your future endeavor!\nMar 2025: Full prof.\nJan 2025: Congrats to Yuchen, Wei, and Kevin. 3 x ICLR’25 + 1 x AISTATS’25 well deserved.\nOct 2024: Congrats to Wei for winning a Best Poster Award at international conference “Recent Advances and Future Directions for Sampling” held at Yale!\nSep 2024: Congrats to Yuqing, Ye, Lingkai, and Zhenghao. 4 x NeurIPS’24 led by us are not too shabby as theorists.\nSummer 2024: Congrats to Dr. Yuqing Wang - Ph.D. in Math! Proud of you, and best wish to your next journey as a prestigious Research Fellow at the Simon's Institute at UC Berkeley!\nSummer 2024: Very grateful to have received SONY Faculty Innovation Award.\nâ¦(prehistory by ML timescale)\nInterested in joining our group?\n2 PhD student positions and 1 postdoc position are available. The currently planned areas are\nAI4Science\n(especially AI for quantum),\ndeep learning theory\nand\noptimization\n, but exceptional candidates in other areas can also be considered. Due to the large volume of inquiries, I may not be able to reply, but I will read emails carefully. If applying to PhD, please apply to one of the following Ph.D. programs: Math, CSE, Machine Learning, ACO; choose Math as the home unit, and include my name as one of your interested faculty members. Thank you for your interest."
  },
