    "homepage_text": "Tianyu Ding\nTianyu Ding\nBiography\nPublications\nPreprints\nMentoring\nTeaching\nServices\nTianyu Ding, PhD\nPrincipal Researcher\nMicrosoft\nRedmond, Washington, USA\nEmail: tianyuding [At] microsoft [Dot] com\nGitHub\n|\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nLinkedIn\n|\nCV\nBiography\nI am currently a Principal Researcher in\nApplied Sciences Group\nat\nMicrosoft\n, Redmond. I earned my PhD in Applied Mathematics and Statistics from\nJohns Hopkins University\n(JHU) in 2021, where I was advised by\nDr. Daniel P. Robinson\nand\nDr. René Vidal\n. Prior to my PhD, I received my Master's degrees in Computer Science and Financial Mathematics from JHU in 2020 and 2016, respectively. I began my academic journey with a Bachelor's degree in Mathematics from\nSun Yat-sen University\nin 2014.\nThroughout my career, I have focused on improving efficiency in machine learning and artificial intelligence, especially in areas like computer vision and generative models. I am constantly seeking new ways to push the boundaries of these fields and make contributions to the world of applied science.\nI would appreciate\nAnyverse Anonymous Feedback\nfrom\nanyone\non\nanything\n. Feel free to ping me!\nSelected Publications\n(\n*\nindicates equal contribution,\n†\nindicates corresponding authorship)\nProCrop: Learning Aesthetic Image Cropping from Professional Compositions\nKe Zhang,\nTianyu Ding\n†\n, Jiachen Jiang, Tianyi Chen, Ilya Zharkov, Vishal M. Patel, and Luming Liang\n†\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2026\nAC rate = 17.6%\ncomming soon...\nEfficient Last-Iterate Convergence in Solving Extensive-Form Games\nLinjian Meng, Tianpei Yang, Youzhi Zhang, Zhenxing Ge, Shangdong Yang,\nTianyu Ding\n, Wenbin Li, Bo An, and Yang Gao\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2025\nAC rate = 24.52%\npdf\ncode\nbibtex\nLast-Iterate Convergence of Smooth Regret Matching\n+\nVariants in Learning Nash Equilibria\nLinjian Meng, Youzhi Zhang, Zhenxing Ge,\nTianyu Ding\n, Shangdong Yang, Zheng Xu, Wenbin Li, and Yang Gao\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2025\nAC rate = 24.52%\npdf\ncode\nbibtex\nCoT-VTM: Visual-to-Music Generation with Chain-of-Thought Reasoning\nXikang Guan, Zheng Gu, Jing Huo,\nTianyu Ding\n, and Yang Gao\nAssociation for Computational Linguistics (\nACL\n), 2025\nAC rate = 20.3%\npdf\nproject page\nbibtex\nDistiLLM-2: A Contrastive Approach Boosts the Distillation of LLMs\nOral, top 1%\nJongwoo Ko, Tianyi Chen, Sungnyun Kim,\nTianyu Ding\n, Luming Liang, Ilya Zharkov, and Se-Young Yun\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2025\nAC rate = 26.9%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nbibtex\nONNXPruner: ONNX-Based General Model Pruning Adapter\nDongdong Ren, Wenbin Li,\nTianyu Ding\n, Lei Wang, Qi Fan, Jing Huo, Hongbing Pan, and Yang Gao\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nTPAMI\n), 2025\npdf\narXiv\nbibtex\nEnhancing Few-Shot Class-Incremental Learning via Training-Free Bi-Level Modality Calibration\nYiyang Chen,\nTianyu Ding\n, Lei Wang, Jing Huo, Yang Gao, and Wenbin Li\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2025\nAC rate = 22.1%\npdf\ncode\nsupplemental\nbibtex\nAutomated Joint Structured Pruning and Quantization for Efficient Neural Network Training and Compression\nXiaoyi Qu, David Aponte, Colby Banbury, Daniel Robinson,\nTianyu Ding\n, Kazuhito Koishida, Ilya Zharkov, and Tianyi Chen\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2025\nAC rate = 22.1%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nsupplemental\nbibtex\nOFER: Occluded Face Expression Reconstruction\nPratheba Selvaraju, Victoria Fernandez Abrevaya, Timo Bolkart, Rick Akkerman,\nTianyu Ding\n, Faezeh Amjadi, and Ilya Zharkov\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2025\nAC rate = 22.1%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nproject page\nbibtex\n3D Gaussian Splatting: Survey, Technologies, Challenges, and Opportunities\nYanqi Bao,\nTianyu Ding\n, Jing Huo, Yaoli Liu, Yuxin Li, Wenbin Li, Yang Gao, and Jiebo Luo\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (\nTCSVT\n), 2025\npdf\narXiv\nproject page\nbibtex\nStructSR: Refuse Spurious Details in Real-World Image Super-Resolution\nYachao Li, Dong Liang,\nTianyu Ding\n, and Sheng-Jun Huang\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (\nAAAI\n), 2025\nAC rate = 23.4%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nproject page\nbibtex\nCaesarNeRF: Calibrated Semantic Representation for Few-shot Generalizable Neural Rendering\nHaidong Zhu\n*\n,\nTianyu Ding\n*†\n, Tianyi Chen, Ilya Zharkov, Ram Nevatia, and Luming Liang\n†\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (\nECCV\n), 2024\nAC rate = 27.9%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nsupplemental\nproject page\nbibtex\nSafe and Robust Subgame Exploitation in Imperfect Information Games\nZhenxing Ge, Zheng Xu,\nTianyu Ding\n, Linjian Meng, Bo An, Wenbin Li, and Yang Gao\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2024\nAC rate = 27.5%\npdf\nbibtex\nDREAM: Diffusion Rectification and Estimation-Adaptive Models\nJinxin Zhou\n*\n,\nTianyu Ding\n*†\n, Tianyi Chen, Jiachen Jiang, Ilya Zharkov, Zhihui Zhu, and Luming Liang\n†\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2024\nAC rate = 23.6%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nproject page\nbibtex\nExploiting Inter-sample and Inter-feature Relations in Dataset Distillation\nWenxiao Deng, Wenbin Li,\nTianyu Ding\n, Lei Wang, Hongguang Zhang, Kuihua Huang, Jing Huo, and Yang Gao\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2024\nAC rate = 23.6%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nbibtex\nInsertNeRF: Instilling Generalizability into NeRF with HyperNet Modules\nYanqi Bao,\nTianyu Ding\n, Jing Huo, Wenbin Li, Yuxin Li, and Yang Gao\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2024\nAC rate = 30.96%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nbibtex\nEfficient Subgame Refinement for Extensive-form Games\nZhenxing Ge, Zheng Xu,\nTianyu Ding\n, Wenbin Li, and Yang Gao\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2023\nAC rate = 26.1%\npdf\nsupplemental\nbibtex\nWhere and How: Mitigating Confusion in Neural Radiance Fields from Sparse Inputs\nYanqi Bao, Yuxin Li, Jing Huo,\nTianyu Ding\n, Xinyue Liang, Wenbin Li, and Yang Gao\nACM International Conference on Multimedia (\nACMMM\n), 2023\nAC rate = 29.3%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nbibtex\nOTOv2: Automatic, Generic, User-Friendly\nTianyi Chen, Luming Liang,\nTianyu Ding\n, Zhihui Zhu, and Ilya Zharkov\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n), 2023\nAC rate = 31.79%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nbibtex\nOn the Optimization Landscape of Neural Collapse under MSE Loss: Global Optimality with Unconstrained Features\nSpotlight\nJinxin Zhou\n*\n, Xiao Li\n*\n,\nTianyu Ding\n, Chong You, Qing Qu, and Zhihui Zhu\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2022\nAC rate = 21.9%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nbibtex\nRSTT: Real-time Spatial Temporal Transformer for Space-Time Video Super-Resolution\nZhicheng Geng\n*\n, Luming Liang\n*\n,\nTianyu Ding\n, and Ilya Zharkov\nComputer Vision and Pattern Recognition (\nCVPR\n), 2022\nAC rate = 25.3%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nsupplemental\nbibtex\nA Geometric Analysis of Neural Collapse with Unconstrained Features\nSpotlight, top 3%\nZhihui Zhu\n*\n,\nTianyu Ding\n*\n, Jinxin Zhou, Xiao Li, Chong You, Jeremias Sulam, and Qing Qu\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2021\nAC rate = 25.7%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nsupplemental\nbibtex\nOnly Train Once: A One-Shot Neural Network Training and Pruning Framework\nTianyi Chen, Bo Ji,\nTianyu Ding\n, Biyi Fang, Guanyi Wang, Zhihui Zhu, Luming Liang, Yixin Shi, Sheng Yi, Xiao Tu\nNeural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n), 2021\nAC rate = 25.7%\npdf\ncode\narXiv\nsupplemental\nbibtex\nDual Principal Component Pursuit for Robust Subspace Learning: Theory and Algorithms for a Holistic Approach\nTianyu Ding\n, Zhihui Zhu, René Vidal, and Daniel P. Robinson\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n), 2021\nAC rate = 21.5%\npdf\ncode\nposter\nslides\nbibtex\nCDF