    "homepage_text": "Jiatao Gu - The Stars My Destination\nToggle navigation\nThe Stars My Destination\nHome\nAbout\nTeam\nPublications\nActivities\nWelcome!\nI am an Assistant Professor in the\nDepartment of CIS\nat the\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\n.\nI am also a primary faculty member of the\nGRASP Lab\nand member of the\nASSET Center\n.\nI also work part-time as a Staff Research Scientist at\nApple (MLR)\nand was a full-time researcher since 2022.\nPrior to joining Apple, I was a Research Scientist at\nMeta AI (FAIR Labs)\n.\nI obtained my Ph.D. degree at\nthe department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, University of Hong Kong\nin 2018 and I was supervised by\nProf. Victor O.K. Li\n. My doctoral work explored\nefficient neural machine translation systems\n.\nI also spent a wonderful time visiting the\nCILVR Lab, New York University\nworking with\nProf. Kyunghyun Cho\n.\nBefore that, I obtained my Bachelor’s degree at\nthe Electronic Engineering Department, Tsinghua University\nin 2014.\nProspective Students\nI will be recruiting self-motivated PhD students, visiting students and research interns for this graduate application cycle.\nI encourage to use this\nform\n.\nResearch Interests\nMy research goal is to advance the capabilities of AI agents to interact with the physical world, with a special emphasis on leveraging generative machine learning approaches for world modeling, iterative reasoning, and effective decision-making. I am particularly interested in developing multi-modal generative models that span natural language, images, videos, and 3D, ensuring these models are\nEfficient, Flexible, Scalable, and Knowledgeable\n. By bridging foundational machine learning research with real-world applications, my research seeks to create robust AI systems capable of operating seamlessly in complex and dynamic environments.\nJiatao Gu (顾佳涛)\n2018, Ph.D. EEE, HKU\n2014, B.Eng. EE, THU\nNews\n18 Sep, 2025\nFour paper was accepted by\nNeurIPS 2025\n..\n10 Aug, 2025\nOne paper was accepted by\nSIGGRAPH ASIA 2025\n..\n1 May, 2025\nOne paper was accepted by\nICML 2025\n..\n26 Feb, 2025\nTwo papers were accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n..\n... see all News\nI will be attending\n#ICML2025\nTue to Sat at Vancouver.\nPlease also come and check our oral presentation and spotlight poster on TARFlow on Thu:\nhttps://t.co/I3aQg3TDG5\nLooking forward to chatting with old and new friends on next-gen generative models and world models!!\n— Jiatao Gu (@thoma_gu)\nJuly 14, 2025\n© 2024 The Stars My Destination\nContact Jiatao via email:\njiataogu32_AT_gmail.com\n(personal)\njgu32_AT_apple.com\n(Apple)\njgu32_AT_upenn.edu\n(Penn)\nCoordinates:\n11 Penn Plaza, New York, NY, 10001, United States\n3333 Chestnut Street, Philadelphia, PA, 19104, United States"
  },
  "serper::M. Zhou": {
