    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/yujiamu/",
    "homepage_text": "Cong Shen\nCong Shen\nHome\nBiography\nPublications\nBy Topics\nBy Years\nMisc\nResearch\nProjects\nGroup\nTutorials\nTeaching\nUVA\nCong Shen\nAssociate Professor\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nUniversity of Virginia\nOffice: E-317 Thornton Hall\nMail: 351 McCormick Road, P.O. Box 400743, Charlottesville, VA 22904\nPhone: (434) 924-8940\nEmail:\ncong at virginia dot edu\nGoogle Scholar Profile\nI am an Associate Professor in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering of University of Virginia. I am also a member of the UVA\nLink Lab\n, and an active faculty in the\nComputer Engineering program\n. I got my B.S. and M.S. from Tsinghua University, and Ph.D. from UCLA. I received the NSF CAREER award in 2022.\nMy research interests span a number of interdisciplinary topics in AI/ML and its engineering applications. Some of my current research topics are:\nIn-context learning and Transformers\nReinforcement learning and multi-armed bandits\nDistributed and decentralized learning\nAI/ML for wireless\nNews\nJan. 2026: Area Chair for ICML 2026.\nDec. 2025: We successfully organized the 1st\nAI4NextG Workshop @ NeurIPS’25\n. All the talks are freely available\nonline\n.\nNov. 2025:\nYujia Mu\nsuccessfully defended her dissertation. Congratulations, Dr. Mu!\nOct. 2025: Co-organzing\nAAAI 2026 Workshop on AI for Time Series Analysis (AI4TS): Theory, Algorithms, and Applications\n.\nSept. 2025: PhD student\nZihan Chen\nreceived the McVey Fellowship, and PhD student Wei Shen received the Wilson Bicentennial Grad Fellowship. Congratulations!\nAug. 2025: Area Chair for AISTATS 2026 and ICLR 2026.\nAug. 2025: Lead organizer for\nAI4NextG Workshop @ NeurIPS’25\n. Submission deadline: August 29, 2025. Check our website for more details.\nMay 2025: I started the role of\nDeputy Director of Collaboration at SpectrumX\n.\narchived news\nPage generated 2026-02-24, by\njemdoc\n."
  },
  "serper::Yunpeng Shi": {
