    "homepage_text": "Yu Inatsu  - Home(English)\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nYu Inatsu\nHome(English)\nYu Inatsu (Ph.D.)\nAssociate\nProfessor\nDepartment of Computer Science, Nagoya Institute of Technology\n#40\n2\nA, Bldg.2, Nagoya Institute of Technology,\nGokiso-cho, Showa-ku, Nagoya, Aichi, 466-8555, Japan\nE-mail: inatsu.yu[at]nitech.ac.jp\nAffiliated Academic Society ：The Japan Statistical Society\nResearch：\n1. Asymptotic theory for longitudinal data\n2. Hypothesis testing and model selection for non-regular model\n3. Active learning for level set estimation\n4. Bayesian optimization under input uncertainty\nKey Words:\nActive learning; Asymptotic expansion; Asymptotic theory; Bayesian optimization; Generalized estimation equation; Information criterion; Input uncertainty; Level set estimation; Model selection; Simple ordering; Tree ordering.\nBiography：\n2012.4 -2014.3   Master course student at the Department of Mathematics, Graduate School of Science, Hiroshima University.\n2014.4 -2017.3   Ph.D. student at the Department of Mathematics, Graduate School of Science, Hiroshima University.\n2017.4 -2020.10 Postdoctoral Researcher, RIKEN Center for Advanced Intelligence Project, Data-Driven Biomedical Science Team.\n2020.11-2025.3\nAssistant Professor, Department of Computer Science, Nagoya Institute of Technology.\n2025.4-\nAssociate\nProfessor\n,\nDepartment of Computer Science, Nagoya Institute of Technology.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
