    "homepage_text": "Adam Liu\nIou-Jen (Adam) Liu\nMy research centers around reinforcement learning and multi-modal foundation models. I hold a PhD in ECE from UIUC, supervised by Professor\nAlexander Schwing\n. Prior to UIUC, I received my M.S. and B.S, both in EE, from National Taiwan University, working with Professor\nYao-Wen Chang\n.\nEmail\n/\nCV\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGitHub\nAffiliations\nNational Taiwan University\n2008 - 2015\nUniversity of Illinois\n2015 - 2022\nMicrosoft Research Montreal\nSummer 2021\nGoogle\n2022 - present\nGoogle DeepMind\n2025 - present\nPublications\nAsking for Knowledge: Training RL Agents to Query External Knowledge Using Language\nIou-Jen Liu\n*,\n              Xingdi Yuan*,\n              Marc-Alexandre Côté*,\n              Pierre-Yves Oudeyer,\n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(ICML'22)\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning, 2022\n[pdf]\n[project]\nBridging the Imitation Gap by Adaptive Insubordination\nLuca Weihs*,\n              Unnat Jain*,\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Jordi Salvador,\n              Svetlana Lazebnik, \n              Aniruddha Kembhavi, \n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(NeurIPS'21)\nNeural Information Processing Systems, 2021\n[pdf]\n[project]\nGridToPix: Training Embodied Agents with Minimal Supervision\nUnnat Jain,\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Svetlana Lazebnik, \n              Aniruddha Kembhavi, \n              Luca Weihs*,\n              Alexander G. Schwing*\n(ICCV'21)\nInternational Conference on Computer Vision\n, 2021\n[pdf]\n[project]\nSemantic Tracklets: An Object-Centric Representation for Visual Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning\nIou-Jen Liu\n*,\n              Zhongzheng Ren*,\n              Raymond A. Yeh*,\n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(IROS'21)\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems\n, 2021\nAlso presented in\nRL for Real Life Workshop\nat ICML 2021\n[pdf]\n[project]\nCooperative Exploration for Multi-Agent Deep Reinforcement Learning\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Unnat Jain,\n              Raymond A. Yeh,\n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(ICML'21)\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning, 2021\nLong Talk (Top 3%)\n[pdf]\n[project]\nHigh-Throughput Synchronous Deep Reinforcement Learning\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Raymond A. Yeh,\n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(NeurIPS'20)\nNeural Information Processing Systems, 2020\n[pdf]\n[project]\nPIC: Permutation Invariant Critic for Multi-Agent Deep Reinforcement Learning\nIou-Jen Liu\n*,\n              Raymond A. Yeh*,\n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(CoRL'19)\nConference on Robot Learning, 2019\n[pdf]\n[project]\nAccelerating Distributed Reinforcement Learning with In-Switch Computing\nYoujie Li,\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Yifan Yuan,\n              Deming Chen,\n              Alexander G. Schwing,\n              Jian Huang\n(ISCA'19)\nInternational Symposium on Computer Architecture, 2019\nAlso presented in\nNSDI'19 (poster)\n[pdf]\n[video]\nKnowledge Flow: Improve upon Your Teachers\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Jian Peng,\n              Alexander G. Schwing\n(ICLR'19)\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations,2019\n[pdf]\nOverlay-Aware Detailed Routing for Self-Aligned Double Patterning Lithography Using the Cut Process\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Shao-Yun Fang,\n              Yao-Wen Chang\n(TCAD'16)\nIEEE Transactions on Computer-Aided Design of Integrated Circuits and Systems, Vol. 35, 2016\n[pdf]\n(DAC'14)\nDesign Automation Conference, 2014\n[pdf]\nStitch-Aware Routing for Multiple E-Beam Lithography\nIou-Jen Liu\n,\n              Shao-Yun Fang,\n              Yao-Wen Chang\n(TCAD'15)\nIEEE Transactions on Computer-Aided Design of Integrated Circuits and Systems, Vol. 34, 2015\n[pdf]\n(DAC'13)\nDesign Automation Conference, 2013\n[pdf]\nTeaching\nECE220 Computer Systems and Programming\nUIUC, Head Teaching Assistant, Sp17, Fa17, Sp18, Su18, Fa18, Sp19, Su19, Fa19, Sp20, Fa20, Sp21, Fa21, Sp22\nTeachers Ranke