    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhimei Ren\nZhimei\nRen\nContact:\nzren at wharton.upenn.edu\nWelcome to my homepage!\nI am an assistant professor in the\nDepartment of Statistics and Data Science\nat the Wharton School,\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\n.\nFrom 2021-2023, I was a postdoctoral researcher in the Statistics Department at the University of Chicago, advised by Professor\nRina Foygel Barber\n. I obtained my Ph.D. in Statistics from Stanford University, advised by Professor\nEmmanuel Candès\n. Prior to this, I received my Bachelor’s degree in Statistics from Peking University. Here is a copy of my\nCV\n. You can also find me on\nGoogle scholar\nand\nGitHub\n.\nI am currently a co-organizer of the\nInternational Seminar on Selective Inference\n(with Will Fithian, Jelle Goeman, Nikos Ignatiadis and Lihua Lei).\nI am co-organizing a\nworkshop on high-dimensional data analysis\nat the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania, scheduled for Aug 11-13, 2026. PhD students are welcome to apply."
  },
