    "homepage_text": "Biao Zhang 张彪 - Homepage\nBiao Zhang 张彪\nKAUST\nLearning as always\nEmail\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nMy research interest includes machine learning, generative models, computer grahics, and computer vision… I am an incoming Professor of Xi’an Jiaotong University. I obtained PhD Degree in KAUST, working with\nPeter Wonka\n. Before that, I obtained the BSc and MSc from Xi’an Jiaotong University.\nOpenings: I am always looking for self-motivated students to work with me. If you are interested in my research, feel free to contact me with your CV and a brief research statement.\n🔥 News\n2025.12\n: I will be attending SIGGRAPH Asia 2025 in Hong Kong (China) from Dec 14 to Dec 19.\n2025.10\n: I will be attending ICCV 2025 in Hawaii (USA) from Oct 18 to Oct 24.\n2025.06\n: I will be co-organizing the workshop\nInd3D: Enforcing Inductive Bias in 3D Generation\non June 12, 2025, during CVPR. Feel free to drop by to chat.\n2025.06\n: I will be assisting Professor Wonka with his talk at the\n2nd Workshop on Urban Scene Modeling\non June 11, 2025, during CVPR. Feel free to drop by to chat.\n2025.04\n: I will be attending ICLR 2025 in Singapore.\n📝 Publications\nCVPR 2026\nFACE: A Face-based Autoregressive Representation for High-Fidelity and Efficient Mesh Generation\nHanxiao Wang, Yuan-Chen Guo, Ying-Tian Liu, Zi-Xin Zou,\nBiao Zhang\n, Weize Quan, Ding Liang, Yan-Pei Cao, Dong-Ming Yan\nCVPR 2026\nCVPR 2026\nHuman Geometry Distribution for 3D Animation Generation\nXiangjun Tang,\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nCVPR 2026\nCVPR 2026\nLumiX: Structured and Coherent Text-to-Intrinsic Generation\nXu Han,\nBiao Zhang\n, Xiangjun Tang, Xianzhi Li, Peter Wonka\nProject\nCVPR 2026\nCVPR 2026\nPoseGAM: Robust Unseen Object Pose Estimation via Geometry-Aware Multi-View Reasoning\nJianqi Chen,\nBiao Zhang\n, Xiangjun Tang, Peter Wonka\nProject\nCVPR 2026\nICLR 2026\nGenerative Human Geometry Distribution\nXiangjun Tang,\nBiao Zhang\n📧, Peter Wonka\nICLR 2026\n(Oral)\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025\nBrepGPT: Autoregressive B-rep Generation with Voronoi Half-Patch\nPu Li, Wenhao Zhang, Weize Quan,\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka, Dongming Yan\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025 (ToG)\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025\nAutoregressive Generation of Static and Growing Trees\nHanxiao Wang,\nBiao Zhang\n, Jonathan Klein, Dominik L. Michels, Dongming Yan, Peter Wonka\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2025 Conference\nICCV 2025\nGeometry Distributions\nBiao Zhang\n, Jing Ren, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\n,\nICCV\nICCV 2025\n(Highlight)\nICCV 2025\nV2M4: 4D Mesh Animation Reconstruction from a Single Monocular Video\nJianqi Chen,\nBiao Zhang\n, Xiangjun Tang, Peter Wonka\nProject\nICCV 2025\nSIGGRAPH 2025\nMatCLIP: Light-and Shape-Insensitive Assignment of PBR Material Models\nMichael Birsak, John Femiani,\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nSIGGRAPH 2025 Conference\nICLR 2025\nLaGeM: A Large Geometry Model for 3D Representation Learning and Diffusion\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\n,\nOpenReview\nICLR 2025\nNeurIPS 2024\nVivid-ZOO: Multi-View Video Generation with Diffusion Model\nBing Li*, Cheng Zheng*, Wenxuan Zhu*, Jinjie Mai,\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka, Bernard Ghanem\nProject\n,\nCode\nNeurIPS 2024\nCVPR 2024\nFunctional Diffusion\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\nCVPR 2024\nCVPR 2024\nMotion2VecSets: 4D Latent Vector Set Diffusion for Non-rigid Shape Reconstruction and Tracking\nWei Cao*, Chang Luo*,\nBiao Zhang\n, Matthias Niessner, Jiapeng Tang\nProject\n,\nCode\nCVPR 2024\nSIGGRAPH 2023 (ToG)\n3DShape2VecSet: A 3d shape representation for neural fields and generative diffusion models\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\n(Legacy)\n,\nCode\n(Latest)\n,\nToG\nThe work has been integrated into some large 3D foundation models, such as VAST/Tripo, CLAY, and Hunyuan3D.\nI gave a talk about this work in\nTowards 3D Foundation Models: Progress and Prospects\nOnline talk\nMeshy\n,\nGAMES Webinar 1\n,\nGAMES Webinar 2\nSIGGRAPH 2023 (ToG)\nNeurIPS 2022\n3DILG: Irregular Latent Grids for 3D Generative Modeling\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\nNeurIPS 2022\nICLR 2022\nTraining Data Generating Networks: Shape Reconstruction via Bi-level Optimization\n(\nICLR 2022\n)\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nSiggraph Asia 2021 (ToG)\nIntuitive and Efficient Roof Modeling for Reconstruction and Synthesis\nJing Ren,\nBiao Zhang\n, Bojian Wu, Jianqiang Huang, Lubin Fan, Maks Ovsjanikov, Peter Wonka\nCode\nSIGGRAPH Asia 2021 (ToG)\nCVPR 2021\nPoint cloud instance segmentation using probabilistic embeddings\nBiao Zhang\n, Peter Wonka\nFeatured in\nCVPR 2021 ScanNet workshop\n.\nCVPR 2021\n📚 Preprints\narxiv 2025\nLaRI: Layered Ray Intersections for Single-view 3D Geometric Reasoning\nRui Li,\nBiao Zhang\n, Zhenyu Li, Federico Tombari, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\narxiv 2025\niFlame: Interleaving Full and Linear Attention for Efficient Mesh Generation\nHanxiao Wang,\nBiao Zhang\n📧, Weize Quan, Dong-Ming Yan, Peter Wonka\nProject\n,\nCode\n📝 Notes\nNotes\nNotes on Muon\nBiao Zhang\n👪 Collaborators\nPeople I have worked with (we have at least submitted one paper):\nWei Cao\n(TU Munich)\nBing Li\n(KAUST)\nRui Li\n(KAUST)\nMatthias Niessner\n(TU Munich)\nJing Ren\n(ETH Zurich)\nJiapeng Tang\n(TU Munich)\nHanxiao Wang\n(CASIA)\nPeter Wonka\n(KAUST)"
  },
