    "homepage_text": "Xuelian Cheng\nDr. Xuelian Cheng\nADJUNCT LECTURER,\nDepartment of Data Science & AI,\nFaculty of Information Technology,\nMonash University\nOffice: 8th Floor, Building 2, No 1 Chuangyuan Road, SIP, Suzhou, Jiangsu Province, China\n中国江苏省苏州市工业园区华云路1号科创园2号楼8层\nEmail: xuelian.cheng@monash.edu\nLinkedin\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\nAbout me\nI am currently a Research Fellow at Monash Suzhou and an Adjunct Lecturer (Assistant Professor) at Monash University Australia. Prior to this role, I completed my PhD at Monash University under the guidance of\nA/Prof. Zongyuan Ge\n,\nA/Prof. Mehrtash Harandi\n, and\nProf. Tom Drummond\n.\nMy research interests include visual geometry and low-level vision tasks,\ni.e.\n, Depth Estimation, Stereo Matching, 3D Reconstruction; AutoML,\ni.e.\n, Neural Architecture Search (NAS); Video Interpretation, XR for Medical Education, and Robotic Surgery.\n[2024 Hold] Accepting prospective\nPhD students\n. If you're interested in working with me, please send an email including your CV and transcripts.\n.\nTeaching\nInterested in becoming a\npaid tutor\n? Please reach out to me!\nFIT5226 Multi agent systems and collective behaviour, S1, Monash University (Suzhou), 2025↝\nFIT5216\tModelling discrete optimization problems, S1, Monash University (Suzhou), 2024↝2025\nFIT5037\tNetwork security, T3, Monash University (Suzhou), 2024↝\nFIT5222\tPlanning and automated reasoning, T3, Monash University (Suzhou), 2024↝\nNews\nOne paper is accepted to MICCAI 2023 (oral, top 3%).\nBack to Monash University, after a 6-month intern at Tencent XR Lab (Canberra).\nOne paper is accepted by MICCAI 2022.\nOne paper is accepted by CVPR 2022!\nCheck my talk on TechBeat, regarding\na review of stereo matching\n(Chinese).\nOur LEAStereo achieves Umero Uno in\nKITTI challenge\n. Find PR here:\n[English]\n[Chinese]\n.\nSelected Publications\nEndoSurf: Neural Surface Reconstruction of Deformable Tissues with Stereo Endoscope Videos\nRuyi Zha*,\nXuelian Cheng*\n, Hongdong Li, Mehrtash Harandi, Zongyuan Ge\nMICCAI 2023 (\nOral\n, Student Travel Award, Top 3%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nDeep laparoscopic stereo matching with transformers\nXuelian Cheng\n, Yiran Zhong, Mehrtash Harandi, Tom Drummond, Zhiyong Wang, Zongyuan Ge\nMICCAI 2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nImplicit Motion Handling for Video Camouflaged Object Detection\nXuelian Cheng\n, Huan Xiong, Deng-Ping Fan, Yiran Zhong,\nMehrtash Harandi, Tom Drummond, Zongyuan Ge\nCVPR 2022\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Dataset]\nLearning Network Architecture for Open-Set Recognition\nXuelin Zhang,\nXuelian Cheng\n, Donghao Zhang, Paul Bonnington, Zongyuan Ge\nAAAI 2022\n[Paper]\nHierarchical Neural Architecture Search for Deep Stereo Matching\nXuelian Cheng\n*, Yiran Zhong*, Mehrtash Harandi, Yuchao Dai,\nXiaojun Chang, Hongdong Li, Tom Drummond, Zongyuan Ge\nNeurIPS 2020\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Talk]\nNoise-Aware Unsupervised Deep Lidar-Stereo Fusion\nXuelian Cheng\n*, Yiran Zhong*, Yuchao Dai, Pan Ji, Hongdong Li\nCVPR 2019\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Demo]\nProfessional activities\nConference Reviewer for NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, MICCAI and IEEE RA-L.\nInterests\nBesides the research study, I love to spend time in swimming pool. I am also a beginner of skateboarding and badminton. Except for outdoor activities, I do also love watching animation,\ni.e.\n魁拔(Kuiba)\nand\nRick and Morty\n. I really recommend one Chinese animation,\nKuiba\n. Both the series of animated films and books are fantastic!\nWebsite template from\nJon Barron"
  },
