    "homepage_text": "Researcher's Homepage\nResearcher\nHome\nGroup\nTeaching\nService\nResearch\nPublications\nCodes & Data\nAwards & honours\nHome\nDr. Renqiang Luo\nAssistant Professor of College of Computer Science and Technology\nJilin University\nEmail:\nlrenqiang@jlu.edu.cn\nOffice:\n[Computer Building, Qianwei South Campus, A427]\n📝 About Me\nWelcome to my academic homepage! I am a assistant professor at Jilin University. My research focuses on Trustworthy AI and Graph Learning, particularly applying fairness-aware encoding to address challenges in Graph Transformer.\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n] | \n        [\nORCID\n] | \n        [\nGitHub\n]\n📢 News\nMar 2026:\nOne paper entitled:\nFairGC: Fairness-aware Graph Condensation\naccepted by\nIJCNN'26\n.\nMar 2026:\nOne paper entitled:\nMoC-KT: Mixture of Convolutions for Knowledge Tracing\naccepted by\nACM Transactions on Information Systems (TOIS)\n.\nJan 2026:\nFive papers entitled:\nEnergy-Efficient Training-Free Zero-Inflation Correction for Rainfall Forecasting with Time-Series Foundation Models\n,\nWhen to Invoke: Refining LLM Fairness with Toxicity Assessment\n,\nFairGU: Fairness-aware Graph Unlearning in Social Networks\n,\nBridging Semantic Understanding and Popularity Bias with LLMs\n, and\nFairGE: Fairness-Aware Graph Encoding in Incomplete Social Networks\naccepted by\nWWW '26\n.\nJan 2026:\nOne paper entitled:\nDebising Large Language Models via Adaptive Causal Prompting with Sketch-of-Thought\naccepted by\nEACL'26\n.\nDec 2025:\nOne paper entitled:\nGraph Learning\naccepted by\nFoundations and Trends in Signal Processing\n.\nDec 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nIJCAI-ECAI '26\n.\nOct 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nACM Web Conference '26\n.\nSep 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nPAKDD '26\n.\nAug 2025:\nOne paper entitled:\nUnbiased Reasoning for Knowledge-Intensive Tasks in Large Language Models via Conditional Front-Door Adjustment\naccepted by\nCIKM'25\n.\nAug 2025:\nServe as reviewer of\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (TNNLS)\n.\nJul 2025:\nServe as reviewer of\nKDD '26\n.\nJul 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nAAAI '26\n.\nJun 2025:\nOne paper entitled:\nRMTrans: Robust Multimodal Transformers for Patient Prognosis under Backdoor Threats\naccepted by\nTIST\n.\nJun 2025:\nAwarded the Outstanding Reviewer at\nKDD '25\n.\nApr 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nECAI '25\n.\nMar 2025:\nOne paper entitled:\nMulti-type Social Patterns-based Graph Learning\naccepted by\nNeurocomputing\n.\nFeb 2025:\nServe as reviewer of\nKDD '25\n.\nFeb 2025:\nNew position started in the College of Computer Science and Technology at\nJilin University\n.\nFeb 2025:\nThe paper\nFairGP: A Scalable and Fair Graph Transformer Using Graph Partitioning\nhas been invited to be presented at an oral session at\nAAAI'25\n.\nJan 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nIJCAI '25\n.\nJan 2025:\nOne paper entitled:\nFactor Graph-based Interpretable Neural Networks\naccepted by\nICLR'25\n.\nJan 2025:\nServe as PC member of\nACM Web Conference '25 - Web for Good\n.\nJan 2025:\nServe as reviewer of\nACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology (TIST)\n.\nDec 2024:\nServe as PC member of\nACM Web Conference '25\n.\nDec 2024:\nServe as reviewer of\nInformation Processing & Management (IPM)\n.\nDec 2024:\nTwo paper entitled:\nFairGP: A Scalable and Fair Graph Transformer Using Graph Partitioning\nand\nCognitive Fluctuations Enhanced Attention Network for Knowledge Tracing\naccepted by\nAAAI'25\n.\nJul 2024:\nAwarded the Student Travel Award for attending\nKDD'24\n.\nMay 2024:\nOne paper entitled:\nFUGNN: Harmonizing Fairness and Utility in Graph Neural Networks\naccepted by\nKDD'24\n.\nMay 2024:\nServe as reviewer of\nACM Transactions on Probabilistic Machine Learning (TOPML)\n.\nApr 2024:\nOne paper entitled:\nFairGT: A Fairness-aware Graph Transformer\naccepted by\nIJCAI'24\n.\nMar 2024:\nServe as reviewer of\nIJCAI '24\n."
  },
  "serper::Z. Fan": {
