    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nhomepage\nData Mining Group\nQi Li\nAssociate Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science\nIowa State University\n0102 Atanasoff Hall, Ames, IA 50011\nemail:\nqli@iastate.edu\nI am broadly interested in data mining and natural language processing with a focus on text mining and applied machine learning, especially in information extraction, data management for crowdsourcing, and weakly supervised machine learning. I have contributed several key methods and is recognized as an expert in these fields. I am recognized by AMiner as 2022 AI 2000 Most Influential Scholar Honorable Mention in Database, and by Baidu as one of the 2022 Global Top Chinese Young Scholars in AI.\nFor motivated PhD student:\nCandidates are to work with Dr. Qi Li towards Ph.D. degrees at Computer Science Department at Iowa State University, conducting research in data mining and applied machine learning.\nCompetitive applicants will have a strong computer science background with exposure to applied math and statistics. Applicants from other disciplines with strong math background and motivations will also be considered (including but not limited to Information and Computational Sciences, Electrical Engineering, etc). Successful candidates will receive financial support. For interested applicants, please forward your CV, research plan, and transcripts in an email with a short statement of interests, using an email subject of “ISU Grad App. <your name>”. Also, complete the ISU Graduate School online application for Computer Science.\nGeneral guidelines for admissions can be found at\nhttps://www.cs.iastate.edu/computer-science-graduate-admissions\nand\nhttps://www.cs.iastate.edu/computer-science-international-graduate-admissions\n.\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  },
