    "homepage_text": "Weiyi ZHANG | School of Optometry\nSkip to main content\nFaculty of Health and Social Sciences\nOpen Site Search Popup\nShare\nFacebook\nLinkedin\nTwitter\nWeibo\nMail\nCopy Link\nInformation For\nStaff (Intranet)\nCurrent Students\nAlumni\nRPg Students (Intranet)\nQuick Access\nQuick Access\nGiving to SO\nOptometry Clinic Online Booking\nResearch Centre for SHARP Vision (RCSV)\nEmail\nLearn@PolyU (Blackboard)\nmyPolyU\neStudent\nAcademic Calendar\nLibrary\nStaff Directory\nAbout PolyU\nCampus Map\nPolyU A to Z\nResearch at PolyU\nStudy at PolyU\nMenu\nPeople\nOpen / close\nback\nPeople\nAcademic Staff\nAdjunct, Honorary and Visiting Staff\nAcademic Advisor and Advisory Committee\nOptometry Clinic Staff\nOpen / close menu\nOptometrists\nCustomer Service Officers\nOphthalmic Dispensers\nOphthalmic Assistants\nResearch Staff\nResearch Students\nSupporting Staff\nStudy\nOpen / close\nback\nStudy\nUndergraduate Programmes\nOpen / close menu\nBSc (Hons) in Optometry\nAcademic Advising\nGUR Subjects\nSchool of Optometry Student Ambassador Scheme\nTaught Postgraduate Programmes\nOpen / close menu\nDoctor of Optometry\nMaster of Science in Vision Science and Innovation\nFast-track Integrated BSc and MSc Degree Programme\nResearch Postgraduate Programmes\nOpen / close menu\nProjects Recruiting Research Students\nWords from HKPFS Awardees\nDoctor of Health Science (Optometry)\nOther Post-qualification Education\nOpen / close menu\nGeorge L. Spaeth International Fellowship Programme – Hong Kong/ Asian-based Fellows\nResidency Programme\nContinuing Professional Development (CPD) Activities\nTeaching Innovations & Facilities\nOpen / close menu\nTeaching Innovations\nTeaching Facilities\nInnovative Projects\nResearch\nOpen / close\nback\nResearch\nResearch Foci\nResearch Areas\nPublic Health Research Group\nResearch Achievement\nOpen / close menu\nResearch Outcome\nResearch Awards and Achievement\nClinical Trial Unit for Vision\nResearch Centres and Laboratories\nOpen / close menu\nCentre for Myopia Research\nPolyU-Stanford Joint Research Centre for Longitudinal Deep Omics\nResearch Centre for SHARP Vision\nJC STEM Lab of Innovative Light Therapy for Eye Diseases\nOptometry Research Clinic\nMajor Research Facilities\nUniversity-level Facilities\nResearch Collaboration\nImpactful Knowledge Transfer\nResearch Subject Recruitment\nOptometry Clinic\nOpen / close\nback\nOptometry Clinic\nMake an Appointment\nPrimary Eye Care Consultation\nSpecialty Clinics\nOpen / close menu\nMyopia Management\nChildren Vision & Binocular Vision\nOpen / close menu\nHealthy Seed Articles\nSpecialty Contact Lens Fitting\nDry Eye Management\nVision Rehabilitation\nOther Services\nOpen / close menu\nContact Lens Service\nGlaucoma Investigation\nOcular Health Service\nOphthalmic Dispensing Service\nVisual Electrodiagnostic Service\nFee\nOur Optometrists\nClinic Equipment\nService User Notes\nOpen / close menu\nBad Weather Arrangement\nPersonal Information Collection Statement (“PICS”) for Optometry Clinic\nReferrals\nCommunity Engagement\nOpen / close\nback\nCommunity Engagement\nCommunity Eye Care Centres\nOpen / close menu\nThe Integrative Community Health Centre at Lai King\nSik Sik Yuen – The Hong Kong Polytechnic University Optometry Centre (Wong Tai Sin Teaching and Learning Centre)\nVision of Love Mobile Eye Care Project\nVision Screening\nEye Care Publicity\nEye Health Info Gallery\nNews and Events\nOpen / close\nback\nNews and Events\nNews\nEvents\nMedia Coverage\nNewsletter\nPhoto Gallery\nVideo Gallery\nAbout SO\nOpen / close\nback\nAbout SO\nMessage from Head\nVision and Mission\nSO Affiliations\nContact Us\nJob Opportunities\nGiving to SO\nStaff (Intranet)\nCurrent Students\nAlumni\nRPg Students (Intranet)\nQuick Access\nStart main content\nHome\nPeople\nResearch Students\nWeiyi ZHANG\nResearch Students\nWeiyi ZHANG\nPhD Student\nmail\nwei-yi.zhang@connect.polyu.hk\nORCID ID\nBiography\nChief Supervisor\nProf. HE Mingguang\nProject Title\nAdvancing optometric problem solving through deep learning techniques\nSynopsis\nI propose a comprehensive investigation into the utilization of deep learning techniques to tackle a range of intricate issues within the field of optometry. These challenges encompass several crucial areas, including but not limited to, the generation and segmentation of fluorescein fundus angiography, the prediction of cardiovascular ailments through analysis of retinal images, the enhancement and refinement of fundus image datasets, as well as the creation of extensive models capable of captioning optometric images and answering visual queries.\nMy primary objective is to leverage the power of deep learning algorithms in order to significantly improve the accuracy and efficiency of medical image processing and analysis in the context of optometry. By doing so, I aim to transcend the limitations of traditional manual approaches and overcome challenges that have persisted thus far. Through the fusion of advanced deep learning methodologies with the intricacies of optometry, I aspire to unveil innovative solutions that have the potential to make a transformative impact across academic and clinical settings alike.\nWe use Cookies to give you a better experience on our website. By continuing to browse the site without changing your privacy settings, you are consenting to our use of Cookies. For more information, please see our\nPrivacy Policy Statement\n.\nAccept\nYour browser is not the latest version. If you continue to browse our website,  Some pages may not function properly.\nYou are recommended to upgrade to a newer version or switch to a different browser. A list of the web browsers that we support can be found\nhere\nWhat are you looking for?\nSite Search\nSearch\nInternal Document Search\nPopular Search\nEye Exam\nEvents\nPublication"
  },
