    "homepage_text": "Shuo Yang Homepage\nShuo Yang\nMy research focuses on ensuring the\nsafety of AI-enabled robots\n, allowing them to complete complex\n            tasks while remaining robust to real-world uncertainty. \n            My research draws on tools from formal methods, statistics, and game theory. I am particularly interested in the following areas:\nSafe, adaptive and efficient\n(reinforcement & imitation) learning-based control\nin (mainly non-cooperative)\nmulti-agent systems\nEfficient policy learning\n(e.g. diffusion policy) for robotics control\nUncertainty-aware safe control\nfor learning-enabled systems (e.g. using conformal prediction)\nFormal verification and synthesis for learning-enabled systems\nI completed my Ph.D. at the University of Pennsylvania\nGRASP Lab\n, advised by Professor\nGeorge J. Pappas\n, \n          and Bachelor's degree (Summa Cum Laude) from Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2021 \n          where I worked closely with Professor\nXiang Yin\n.\n          I have spent time in both tech (Toyota Research, Tencent AI) and quant finance (Point72/Cubist).\nEmail\n/\nLinkedin\n/\nGithub\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGRASP Page\nSelected Publication\n(* indicates equal contribution, see full list on\nGoogle Scholar\n)\nDynamic Rank Adjustment in Diffusion Policies for Efficient and Flexible Training\nXiatao Sun,\nShuo Yang\n, Yinxing Chen, Francis Fan, Yiyan (Edgar) Liang, Daniel Rakita\nRobotics: Science and Systems (RSS) 2025 [\nwebpage\n][\narxiv\n][\ncode\n]\nKey words: Online Imitation Learning, Diffusion Model\nMulti-Agent Reinforcement Learning Guided by Signal Temporal Logic Specifications\nJiangwei Wang,\nShuo Yang\n, Ziyan An, Songyang Han, Zhili Zhang, Rahul Mangharam, Meiyi Ma, Fei Miao\nIEEE/RSJ International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS) 2025 [\narxiv\n]\nKey words: Reinforcement Learning, Multi-Agent Systems, Safety\nSTLGame: Signal Temporal Logic Games in Adversarial Multi-Agent Systems\nShuo Yang\n, Hongrui Zheng, Cristian-Ioan Vasile, George J. Pappas, Rahul Mangharam\nLearning for Dynamics & Control Conference (L4DC) 2025 [\nwebpage\n][\narxiv\n][\ncode\n]\nKey words: Multi-Agent Systems, Game Theory, Formal Methods\nMEGA-DAgger: Imitation Learning with Multiple Imperfect Experts\nXiatao Sun*,\nShuo Yang\n*, Mingyan Zhou, Kunpeng Liu, Rahul Mangharam\nIEEE International Conference on Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITSC) 2024 [\narxiv\n][\ncode\n]\nKey words: Imitation Learning, Autonomous Racing, Safety\nLearning Adaptive Safety for Multi-Agent Systems\nLuigi Berducci,\nShuo Yang\n, Rahul Mangharam, Radu Grosu\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA) 2024 [\narxiv\n][\ncode\n]\nKey words: Reinforcement Learning, Multi-Agent Systems, Safety\nSafe Perception-based Control under Stochastic Sensor Uncertainty using Conformal Prediction\nShuo Yang\n, George J. Pappas, Rahul Mangharam, Lars Lindemann\nIEEE Conference on Decision and Control (CDC) 2023 [\narxiv\n]\nKey words: Safety, Uncertainty Quantification, Perception\nSecure Your Intention: On Notions of Pre-Opacity in Discrete-Event Systems\nShuo Yang\n, Xiang Yin\nIEEE Transactions on Automatic Control (TAC) 2022 [\narxiv\n]\nKey words: Information Privacy, Automata Theory\nSelected Honors\n2024, L-CSS Outstanding Reviewer Award (top 1%) [\nLetter\n]\n2024, DAAD AInet Fellow (Safe and Secure AI)\n2023, ACC Travel Grant\n2021, The Dean's Fellowship from Penn\n2021, Solomon M. Swaab Fellowship from Penn\n2021, Outstanding Graduate of SJTU\n2021, Outstanding Bachelor Thesis Award from SJTU (top 1%)\n2020, Person of the Year of SJTU [\nSJTU News Spotlight\n]\n2018 & 2019, Outstanding Academic Scholarship from SJTU\nService\nCo-organizer: the 2nd Workshop on\nMAD-Games: Multi-Agent Dynamic Games\n@ ICRA 2024\nArea Chair:\nTiny Papers @ ICLR 2024, 2023\nI also serve as a CPHS'2024 mentor.\nReviewer:\nAmerican Control Conference (ACC)\nIEEE Conference on Decision and Control (CDC)\nInternational Conference on Cyber-Physical Systems (ICCPS)\nAdvances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\nIEEE Transactions on Automatic Control (TAC)\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters (RA-L)\nIEEE Control Systems Letters (L-CSS)\nIEEE Transactions on Intelligent Vehicles (TIV)\nNonlinear Analysis: Hybrid Systems (NAHS)\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (ICRA)\nIROS 2023 Workshop on Multi-agent Dynamic Games (MAD-Games)\nNeurIPS 2023 AI for Science Workshop (AI4Science)\netc.\nTemplate from\nhere\n.\nLast updated Aug 2025."
  },
