    "homepage_text": "Welcome to Yan Chen's Home Page\nYan Chen\nProfessor\nDepartment\n\n\n\r\n                of Computer Science\nRobert R.\r\n                McCormick School of Engineering and Applied Science\nNorthwestern University\n3007 Mudd Hall\n2233 Tech Drive, Third Floor\nEvanston, IL 60208\n(847) 491-4946 (Office)\n(847) 491-2789 (Fax)\nE-mail :\nychen\r\n                AT northwestern.edu\n|\nPublications\n|\nTeaching\n|\nResearch\n|\nCV\n|\nStudents\n|\nI received my Ph.D. in\nComputer\n\n\n\r\n      Science\nfrom\nUniversity of\r\n      California at Berkeley\nin Dec. 2003 under the supervision of\nProf. Randy H. Katz\nand joined the faculty at\nNorthwestern University\nin Jan. 2004.\nTeaching\nEECS 340 - Introduction to Networking (\nWinter 2004\n,\nWinter 2006\n,\nWinter 2008\n,\nSpring 2010\n,\nWinter 2012\n,\nWinter 2014\n)\nDeveloped EECS 350 - Introduction to Computer Security (\nWinter 2005\n,\nWinter 2007\n)\nDeveloped EECS 354 - Network Penetration and Security (Fall\r\n        2007, Fall 2008, Fall 2009, Fall 2010, Fall 2011, Fall 2012,\r\n        Fall 2013, Fall 2014, Fall 2015,\nFall 2016\n).\nDeveloped EECS 450 - Internet Security (\nSpring 2004\n,\nSpring 2005\n,\nSpring 2007\n,\nWinter 2009\n,\nSpring 2010\n,\nSpring 2012\n,\nWinter 2013\n,\nSpring 2014\n,\nWinter 2015\n,\nFall 2016\n)\nDeveloped EECS 395/495 - Mobile Apps and Systems (\nSpring 2015\n)\nDeveloped EECS 395/495 - Programming Languages and Analysis\r\n        for Security (\nSpring 2013\n)\nDeveloped\nMSIT\n458 Information Security and Assurance (\nSpring 2007\n,\nSpring 2008\n,\nSpring 2009\n,\nWinter 2010\n,\nFall 2010\n,\nFall 2011\n,\nFall 2012\n,\nFall 2013\n,\nWinter 2015\n,\nFall 2015\n,\nFall 2016\n)\nResearch\nMy research interests are in security and measurement for networking\r\n    and large-scale distributed systems, especially in the AI-empowered system security recently. I lead the\nNorthwestern LIST (Lab for\r\n      Internet and Security Technology)\n.   I won the DOE Early\r\n    CAREER Award in 2005, the DOD (Air Force of Scientific Research)\r\n    Young Investigator Award in 2007, and the Most Influential Paper award of ASPLOS in 2018.\n    Based on\nGoogle\n\n\r\n      Scholar\n(papers from different authors with the same names are\r\n    removed), my papers have been cited over 17,000 times, and the\nh-index\nof\r\n    my publications is 63 as of Jan 2026. I am a Fellow of IEEE.\nCurrent Graduate Students and Research Staff\nZiyi Guo (Ph.D. student), won the Google Fellowship 2025.\nYuhao Jiang (Ph.D. student)\nRobin Luo\n(Ph.D. student)\nLingzhi Wang\n(Ph.D. student)\nGraduated Ph.D. Students and Postdocs\nSherwin Shen\n(Ph.D. 2025, First job: Assistant Professor\nat Hofstra University)\nMohammad Kavousi\n(Ph.D. 2025,\nFirst job: Assistant Professor of Instruction at Vandebilt University)\nKaiyu Hou\n(Ph.D. 2022, First job: Research Scientist at Ali\nCloud)\nWon both Star of Alibaba and Star of Huawei Awards for offers\nXutong Chen (Ph.D. 2021, First job: Research Scientist at Facebook)\nHaitao Xu\n(Postdoc,\n\r\n        2018, First job: Assistant Professor at Arizona State\r\n        University)\nZhenyang Qu\n(Ph.D. 2017, First job: Research Scientist at Facebook)\nXiang Pan\n(Ph.D. 2017, First job: Software Engineer at Google)\nXitao Wen\n(Ph.D. 2016. First job: Software Engineer at Google)\nVaibhav\r\n          Rastogi\n(Ph.D. 2015. First job: Postdoctal Scientis at\r\n        University of Wisconsin at Madison)\nYinzhi Cao\n(Ph.D. 2014. First job: Postdoctal Scientist at Columbia\r\n        University; Now: Assistant Professor at Johns Hopkins\r\n        University)\nHongyu Gao\n(Ph.D. 2013. First job: Software Engineer at Google. Now: Shape\r\n        Security)\nKai Chen\n(Ph.D. 2012. First job and now: Professor at Hongkong\r\n        University of Science and Technology)\nZhichun Li\n(Ph.D.\r\n        2009. First job and now: Researcher at NEC Labs America.)\nYao Zhao\n(Ph.D. 2009. First job: Researcher at Bell Labs. Now: Shape\r\n        Security)\nWon the 2009 EECS Best Dissertation Award of\r\n          Northwestern\n.\nGuohan Lv\n(Ph. D. of Tsinghua University China, 2008, co-advised\r\n        with Prof. Xing Li at Tsinghua. First job: Researcher at\r\n        Microsoft Research Asia.)"
  },
