    "homepage_text": "Jackson (Kuan-Chieh) Wang | The Movement Lab\nSkip to main content\nSkip to secondary navigation\nStanford University\n(link is external)\nMain content start\nJackson (Kuan-Chieh) Wang\nMy research focuses on 3D human modelling from visual inputs, with a focus on applications in sports.  For more details, please visit my website.\nEducation\nPh.D, University of Toronto, 2021\nMaster of Science, University of Toronto, 2016\nBachelor in Applied Science and Engineering, University of Toronto, 2014\nContact\nLocation\nGates 376\n353 Jane Stanford Way, Stanford, CA 94305\nWebsite\nPublications\nWang, K.-C., Weng, Z., Xenochristou, M. ., Araujo, J., Gu, J., Liu, C. K., & Yeung, S. (2023).\nNeMo: 3D Neural Motion Fields from Multiple Video Instances of the Same Action\n.\nConference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023\n.\nBack to Top"
