  "serper::Junyu Cao": {
    "homepage": "https://junyucao.com/",
    "emails": [
      "junyu.cao@mccombs.utexas.edu",
      "junyucao18@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Junyu Cao - Junyu Cao\nJunyu Cao\nThe University of Texas at Austin\nAbout Me\nI am an Assistant Professor in the Department of Information, Risk, and Operations Management (Decision Science Group) at McCombs School of Business, The University of Texas at Austin. I received my Ph.D. in the Department of Industrial Engineering and Operations Research (IEOR) from University of California, Berkeley in 2020.\nMy research interests include:\nAI-driven decision-making, with a focus on sequential decision-making (online learning, active\ndata acquisition), human-AI collaboration (model alignment, reinforcement learning from human\nfeedback), and trustworthy decision-making (enhancing interpretability, safety, and adaptability\nin decision-making processes).\nSmart-city analytics and urban operations, with an emphasis on agile logistics, transportation\nsystems including ride-hailing platforms, and autonomous mobility solutions.\nContact:\njunyucao18 AT gmail.com\njunyu.cao AT mccombs.utexas.edu (UT-related correspondence only)\nCopyright 2026 Junyu Cao 曹隽羽"
  },
  "serper::Guanbin Li": {
    "homepage": "https://guanbinli.com/",
