    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Guanbin Li (æå å½¬)\nBiography\nI am currently a\nfull Professor\nin School of Computer Science and Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University. I received my PhD degree in computer science from the University of Hong Kong, advised by\nProf. Yizhou Yu\n. I also hold a MS degree and a BE degree in computer science and technology from Sun Yat-sen University in 2009 and 2012 respectively. I have more than 150 publications in international conferences and journals, including TPAMI, TNNLS, TIP, CVPR, ICCV, ICML, AAAI and IJCAI, etc. My current research interests include computer vision, machine learning and medical image analysis.\nI am co-supervising the\nHCP-I2\nLab: Human-Cyber-Physical Intelligence Integration, SYSU.\nI am recruiting self-motivated Ph.D / Master students in computer vision and machine learning. If you are interested in, please directly send me your resume.\nEmail: liguanbin(at)mail.sysu.edu.cn\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n][\nä¸­æç\n]\nNews\n2025-06: 12 papers are accepted by ICCV2025\n2025-06: One paper is accepted by T-MI\n2025-06: One paper is accepted by T-KDE\n2025-05: Two papers are accepted by MICCAI2025\n2025-05: One paper is accepted by ICML 2025 and is selected as spotlight\n2025-04: One paper is accepted by ICME2025 and is selected as oral\n2025-03: One paper is accepted by T-MM\n2025-02: Seven papers are accepted by CVPR2025\n2025-01: One paper is accepted by T-IP\n2025-01: One paper is accepted by ISBI2025\n2024-12: Two papers are accepted by AAAI2025\n2024-10: One paper is accepted by T-PAMI\n2024-10: One paper is accepted by JBHI\n2024-09: Two papers are accepted by NeurIPS 2024, with one Spotlight paper\n2024-07: Two papers are accepted by ACM MM 2024\n2024-07: Three papers are accepted by ECCV2024\n2024-06: One paper is accepted by MICCAI2024\n2024-04: One paper is accepted by T-MI\n2024-03: One paper is accepted by Siggraph2024 for Journal track\n2024-02: Seven papers are accepted by CVPR2024, with one oral paper\n2024-02: Five papers are accepted by ISBI 2024\n2023-12: Five papers are accepted by AAAI2024\n2023-11: One paper is accepted by Medical Image Analysis(MIA)\n2023-11: One paper is accepted by T-IP\n2023-10: One paper is accepted by WACV 2023\n2023-10: One paper is accepted by T-NNLS\n2023-10: One paper is accepted by PR\n2023-10: One paper is accepted by T-IP\n2023-10: One paper is accepted by BioInformatics\n2023-09: One paper is accepted by Siggraph Asia\n2023-08: I am honered to be sponsored by NSFC for excellent youth scholars (å½å®¶ä¼é)\n2023-07: One paper is accepted by ACM MM 2023 and is selected as Oral representation.\n2023-07: Eight papers are accepted by ICCV2023\n2023-06: One paper is accepted by T-PAMI\n2023-06: One paper is accepted by T-NNLS\n2023-06: One paper is accepted by JBHI\n2023-06: Six papers are accepted by MICCAI2023, with two Early Accept papers\n2023-06: Two papers are accepted by IJCAI2023\n2023-03: Eight papers are accepted by CVPR2023, with two Highlight papers\n2023-03: One paper is accepted by T-IP\n2023-01: One paper is accepted by ISBI 2023\n2023-01: One paper is accepted by T-PAMI\n2022-11: Two papers are accepted by AAAI 2023\n2022-11: One paper is accepted by Computers in Biology and Medicine\n2022-11: Two papers are accepted by Journal of Software\n2022-09: One paper is accepted by NeurIPS 2022\n2022-07: Two papers are accepted by ECCV 2022\n2022-06: Two papers are accepted by ACM MM 2022\n2022-06: One paper is accepted by T-MI\n2022-05: One paper is accepted by T-PAMI\n2022-05: One paper is accepted by IEEE Transactions on Industrial Informatics\n2022-05: Six papers are provisionally accepted by MICCAI2022\n2022-04: Two papers are accepted by IJCAI 2022\n2022-03: Two papers are accepted by CVPR 2022, including one oral paper\n2022-03: Three papers are accepted by ICME 2022\n2022-01: Four papers are accepted by ISBI 2022, including two oral papers\nResearch Interest\nComputer Vision\nImage Understanding, including saliency detection, multi-label image classification, visual captioning, visual question answering.\nImage Processing, including image super-resolution, color sketch generation, image inpainting.\nOther Applications, including visual tracking, person re-identification and crowd counting.\nMachine Learning\nDeep Learning, including deep CNN, LSTM, Attention Modeling, Generative Adversarial Network, Reinforcement Learning\nClassic Machine Learning Branches, including SVM, Random forest, Boosting, etc.\nWeakly supervised learning\nAcademic Services\nI serve as an area chair of CVPR 2024.\nI serve as an associate editor of \"\nThe Visual Computer\n\".\nI serve as an area chair of\nVISAPP2019\n.\nI serve as a program committee member of CVPR2017~2022, NeurlPS2020~2021, ECCV2020 && 2022, ICCV2019 && 2021, IJCAI2018~2022, AAAI2018~2022.\nReviewer for:\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (T-PAMI)\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (IJCV)\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing (T-IP)\nIEEE Transactions on Neural Networks and Learning Systems (T-NNLS)\nIEEE Transactions on Multimedia (T-MM)\nIEEE Transactions on Cybernetics (T-Cyb)\nACM SIGGRAPH2017/SIGGRAPH Asia 2018\nSelected Honors & Awards\n2023 National Science Fund for Excellent Young Scholars by NSFC (å½å®¶ä¼é)\n2021 ICMR Best Poster Paper Award\n2020 Wu Wenjun Outstanding Youth Award for Artificial Intelligence (å´æä¿äººå·¥æºè½ä¼é)\n2019 Guangdong Natural Science Funds for Distinguished Young Scholar (å¹¿ä¸çæ°é)\n2019 ICCV Best Paper Nomination\n2019 ACM China Rising Star Nomination Award\n2019 The First Prize of Science and Technology awarded by CSIG\n2018 Excellent Award of CCF-Tencent Research Fund\n2012 Hong Kong PhD Fellowship"
  },
