    "homepage_text": "Yurong You | NVIDIA Research\nYurong\nYou\nI am research scientist at\nAutonomous Vehicle Research Group\nin NVIDIA Research. I received my Ph.D. degree in Computer Science from Cornell University in 2023, advised by\nKilian Q. Weinberger\nand\nBharath Hariharan\n. Before I came to Cornell, I received my bachelor’s degree from Shanghai Jiao Tong University (ACM Honors class). My research interest lies in computer vision and machine learning.\nPublications\nNeurIPS\nDiffuBox: Refining 3D Object Detection with Point Diffusion\nXiangyu Chen\n,\nZhenzhen Liu\n,\nKatie Z. Luo\n, Siddhartha Datta, Adhitya Polavaram,\nYan Wang\n,\nYurong You\n,\nBoyi Li\n,\nMarco Pavone\n,\nWei-Lun Chao\n,\nMark E. Campbell\n,\nBharath Hariharan\n, and\nKilian Q. Weinberger\nIn the Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)\n, Dec 2024\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\nxiangyu2024diffuBox\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Chen, Xiangyu and Liu, Zhenzhen and Luo, Katie Z. and Datta, Siddhartha and Polavaram, Adhitya and Wang, Yan and You, Yurong and Li, Boyi and Pavone, Marco and Chao, Wei-Lun and Campbell, Mark E. and Hariharan, Bharath and Weinberger, Kilian Q.}\n,\nbooktitle\n=\n{the Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)}\n,\ntitle\n=\n{DiffuBox: Refining 3D Object Detection with Point Diffusion}\n,\nyear\n=\n{2024}\n,\nmonth\n=\ndec\n,\n}\nICLR\nPre-training LiDAR-based 3D Object Detectors through Colorization\nTai-Yu Pan\n, Chenyang Ma, Tianle Chen,\nCheng Perng Phoo\n,\nKatie Z Luo\n,\nYurong You\n,\nMark Campbell\n,\nKilian Q Weinberger\n,\nBharath Hariharan\n, and\nWei-Lun Chao\nIn the International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR)\n, Jun 2024\nBib\nPDF\n@inproceedings\n{\npan2024pretraining\n,\ntitle\n=\n{Pre-training Li{DAR}-based 3D Object Detectors through Colorization}\n,\nauthor\n=\n{Pan, Tai-Yu and Ma, Chenyang and Chen, Tianle and Phoo, Cheng Perng and Luo, Katie Z and You, Yurong and Campbell, Mark and Weinberger, Kili