    "homepage_text": "Lei  Han's Homepage\nLei Han (é©ç£)\nCo-Founder & Chief Scientist\nNoitom Robotics\nShenzhen, China\nGmail:\nleihan DOT cs AT gmail DOT com\nNR Email:\nlhan AT noitomrobotics DOT com\nPrevious email addresses:\nlxhan@tencent.com;\nlei.han@msstate.edu;\nlhan@stat.rutgers.edu;\nleihan@comp.hkbu.edu.hk;\nhanlei@cis.pku.edu.cn\nBrief Biography\n2025-now: Co-Founder & Chief Scientist, Noitom Robotics\n2019-2025: Director of Embodied Intelligence, Principal Research Scientist, Tencent Robotics X\n2017-2019: Senior Research Scientist, Tencent AI Lab\n2016-2017: Assistant Research Professor, Mississippi State University, USA\nI was the director of embodied intelligence and principal research scientist at Tencent Robotics X, where I spent 6 fantastic years with a group of exceptionally talented researchers on many great projects under the supervision of Dr.\nZhengyou Zhang\n. Thanks to the entire team!\nI was an assistant research professor at the Department of Basic Science, Mississippi State University, USA. I received my Ph.D from Peking University (advised by Professor\nKunqing Xie\n) and spent two years in Hong Kong Baptist University (advised by Professor\nYu Zhang\n) and Rutgers University (advised by Professor\nTong Zhang\n) as postdoctoral researcher. I was the winner of the Best Dissertation Award of Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence (CAAI) (ä¸­å½äººå·¥æºè½å­¦ä¼ä¼å).\n        My research interests mainly focus on machine learning, artifical intelligence, and applications in robotics and game.\nWe are hiring AI researchers and interns at Noitom Robotics. If you're interested in working closly with me to develop cutting-edge embodied intelligence models, built upon large amount of high-quality data, please feel free to contact me.\nSelected Publications\n[\nGoogle Scholar\n]\nLong-Term Projects\n[5]\nTencent Robotics X Team & Futian Laboratory\n.\nTAIROS: An Embodied AI Platform for Robotics Applications.\n[\nTAIROS official site\n][\npdf\n], 2025.\n[4]\nLei Han\n*\n, Qingxu Zhu\n*\n, Jiapeng Sheng\n*\n, Chong Zhang\n*\n, Tingguang Li\n*\n, Yizheng Zhang\n*\n, He Zhang\n*\n, Yuzhen Liu, Cheng Zhou, Rui Zhao, \n            Jie Li, Yufeng Zhang, Rui Wang, Wanchao Chi, Xiong Li, Yonghui Zhu, Lingzhu Xiang, Xiao Teng, Zhengyou Zhang.\n            (* Equal contribution)\nLifelike Agility and Play in Quadrupedal Robots using Reinforcement Learning and Generative Pre-trained Models. [\nproject page\n][\nnature\n][\narxiv\n][\ncode & data\n]\nIn:\nNature Machine Intelligence\n, Vol. 6, No. 7, 2024. \n            (\nCover Story\n)\n[3]\nLei Han\nâ\n, Jiechao Xiong\nâ\n, Peng Sun\nâ\n, Xinghai Sun, Meng Fang, Qingwei Guo, Qiaobo Chen, Tengfei Shi, Zhengyou Zhang. (* Equal contribution. Correspondence to the first three authors.)\nTStarBot-X: An Open-Sourced and Comprehensive Study for Efficient League Training in StarCraft II Full Game. [\narxiv\n]\n(\nGrandmaster-Level AI\n)\narXiv preprint arXiv:2011.13729, 2020.\n[2]\nPeng Sun\nâ\n, Jiechao Xiong\nâ\n,\nLei Han\nâ\n, Xinghai Sun, Shuxing Li, Jiawei Xu, Meng Fang, Zhengyou Zhang. (* Equal contribution. Correspondence to the first three authors.)\nTLeague: A Framework for Competitive Self-Play based Distributed Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning. [\narxiv\n]\narXiv preprint arXiv:2011.12895, 2020.\n[1]\nPeng Sun\n*\n, Xinghai Sun\n*\n,\nLei Han\n*\n, Jiechao Xiong\n*\n, Qing Wang, Bo Li, Yang Zheng, Ji Liu, Yongsheng Liu, Han Liu, Tong Zhang. (*Equal contribution)\nTStarBots: Defeating the Cheating Level Builtin AI in StarCraft II in the Full Game. [\narxiv\n]\narXiv:1809.07193 [cs.AI], 2018.\n2026\n[74]\nBangguo Yu, Yuzhen Liu,\nLei Han\n, Hamidreza Kasaei, Tingguang Li, Ming Cao.\nVLN-Game: Vision-Language Equilibrium Search for Zero-Shot Semantic Navigation.\nIn:\nIEEE Transactions on Robotics (\nT-RO\n)\n, 2026.\n[73]\nRui Zhao, Xihui Li, Yizheng Zhang, Yuzhen Liu, Zhong Zhang, Yufeng Zhang, Cheng Zhou, Zhengyou Zhang,\nLei Han\n.\nCooperative-Competitive Team Play of Real-World Craft Robots.\nIn:\n2026 IEEE International Conference on Robotics & Automation (\nICRA\n)\n, 2026.\n2025\n[72]\nGaolin Zhao, Shuo Yang, Jinqiu Fan, Ran Song, qi jiang,\nLei Han\n, Wei Zhang.\nShapeAfford: Reconstructing 3D Shape with Manipulation Affordance via Geometry-Affordance Synergy.\nIn:\nThe IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters Submission and Review Management System (\nRA-L\n)\n, 2025.\n[71]\nFengshuo Bai, Rui Zhao, Hongming Zhang, Sijia Cui, Shao Zhang, Ying Wen, Yaodong Yang, Bo Xu,\nLei Han\n.\nSTAR: Efficient Preference-based Reinforcement Learning via Dual Regularization.\nIn:\nThe Thirty-ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2025.\n[70]\nYufan Dang, Chen Qian, Xueheng Luo, Jingru Fan, Zihao Xie, Ruijie Shi, Weize Chen, Cheng Yang, Xiaoyin Che, Ye Tian, Xuantang Xiong,\nLei Han\n, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun.\nMulti-Agent Collaboration via Evolving Orchestration.\nIn:\nThe Thirty-ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2025.\n[69]\nSiyuan Zhou, Yilun Du, Yuncong Yang,\nLei Han\n, Peihao Chen, Dit-Yan Yeung, Chuang Gan.\nLearning 3D Persistent Embodied World Models.\nIn:\nThe Thirty-ninth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2025.\n[68]\nZhuoyun Du, Chen Qian, Wei Liu, Zihao Xie, YiFei Wang, Rennai Qiu, Yufan Dang, Weize Chen, Cheng Yang, Ye Tian, Xuantang Xiong,\nLei Han\n.\nMulti-Agent Collaboration via Cross-Team Orchestration.\nIn:\nThe 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL\n)\n, 2025.\n[67]\nKangyang Luo, Yuzhuo Bai, Cheng Gao, Shuzheng Si, Zhu Liu, Yingli Shen, Zhitong Wang, Cunliang Kong, Wenhao Li, Yufei Huang, Ye Tian, Xuantang Xiong,\nLei Han\n, Maosong Sun.\nGLTW: Joint Improved Graph Transformer and LLM via Three-Word Language for Knowledge Graph Completion.\nIn:\nThe 63rd Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (\nACL\n)\n, 2025.\n[66]\nFengyuan Liu, Rui Zhao, Shuo Chen, Guohao Li, Philip Torr,\nLei Han\n, Jindong Gu.\nCan an Individual Manipulate the Collective Decisions of Multi-Agents?\nIn:\nThe 2025 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (\nEMNLP\n)\n, 2025.\n[65]\nYizheng Zhang, Zhenjun Yu, JiaXin Lai, Cewu Lu,\nLei Han\n.\nAgentWorld: An Interactive Simulation Platform for Scene Construction and Mobile Robotic Manipulation. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nThe 9th Annual Conference on Robot Learning (\nCoRL\n)\n, 2025.\n[64]\nTao Zhang, Yuenan Zhao, Xiaoyu Xu, Ran Song,\nLei Han\n, Wei Zhang.\nVCADNet: Vision-Based Circular Accessible Depth Prediction for UGV Perception.\nIn:\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (\nIROS\n)\n, 2025.\n[63]\nYinduo Xie, Yuenan Zhao, Ran Song, Zhiheng Li,\nLei Han\n, Wei Zhang.\nALVO: Adaptive Learning with Velocity Obstacles for UGV Navigation in Dynamic Scenes.\nIn:\nInternational Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (\nIROS\n)\n, 2025.\n[62]\nJiawei Xu, Rui Yang, Shuang Qiu, Feng Luo, Meng Fang, Baoxiang Wang,\nLei Han\n.\nTackling Data Corruption in Offline Reinforcement Learning via Sequence Modeling. [\nPDF\n]\nIn:\nThe Thirteenth International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2025.\n2024\n[61]\nXinyu Xu, Yizheng Zhang, Yong-Lu Li,\nLei Han\n, Cewu Lu.\nHumanVLA: Towards Vision-Language Directed Object Rearrangement by Physical Humanoid. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nThe Thirty-eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2024.\n[60]\nYe Tian, Baolin Peng, Linfeng Song, Lifeng Jin, Dian Yu,\nLei Han\n, Haitao Mi, Dong Yu.\nToward Self-Improvement of LLMs via Imagination, Searching, and Criticizing. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nThe Thirty-eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2024.\n[59]\nPengyu Cheng, Tianhao Hu, Han Xu, Zhisong Zhang, Yong Dai,\nLei Han\n, Nan Du, Xiaolong Li.\nSelf-playing Adversarial Language Game Enhances LLM Reasoning. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nThe Thirty-eighth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (\nNeurIPS\n)\n, 2024.\n[58]\nLei Han\n*\n, Qingxu Zhu\n*\n, Jiapeng Sheng\n*\n, Chong Zhang\n*\n, Tingguang Li\n*\n, Yizheng Zhang\n*\n, He Zhang\n*\n, Yuzhen Liu, Cheng Zhou, Rui Zhao, \n            Jie Li, Yufeng Zhang, Rui Wang, Wanchao Chi, Xiong Li, Yonghui Zhu, Lingzhu Xiang, Xiao Teng, Zhengyou Zhang.\n            (* Equal contribution)\nLifelike Agility and Play in Quadrupedal Robots using Reinforcement Learning and Generative Pre-trained Models. [\nproject page\n][\nnature\n][\narxiv\n][\ncode & data\n]\nIn:\nNature Machine Intelligence\n, Vol. 6, No. 7, 2024.\n[57]\nYingru Li, Jiawei Xu,\nLei Han\n, Zhiquan Luo.\nQ-Star Meets Scalable Posterior Sampling: Bridging Theory and Practice via HyperAgent. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (\nICML\n)\n, 2024.\n[56]\nChong Zhang, Jiapeng Sheng, Tingguang Li, He Zhang, Cheng Zhou, Qingxu Zhu, Rui Zhao, Yizheng Zhang,\nLei Han\n.\nLearning Highly Dynamic Behaviors for Quadrupedal Robots. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n)\n, 2024.\n[55]\nHaojie Shi, Tingguang Li, Qingxu Zhu, Jiapeng Sheng,\nLei Han\n, Max Q.-H. Meng.\nAn Efficient Model based Approach on Learning Agile Motor Skills without Reinforcement. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n)\n, 2024.\n[54]\nJiyuan Shi, Chenjia Bai, Haoran He,\nLei Han\n, Dong Wang, Bin Zhao, Mingguo Zhao, Xiu Li, Xuelong Li.\nRobust Quadrupedal Locomotion via Risk-Averse Policy Learning. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nIEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation (\nICRA\n)\n, 2024.\n[53]\nRui Yang, Han Zhong, Jiawei Xu, Amy Zhang, Chongjie Zhang,\nLei Han\n, Tong Zhang.\nTowards Robust Offline Reinforcement Learning under Diverse Data Corruption. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nThe Twelfth International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2024. (\nSpotlight\n)\n[52]\nYucheng Yang, Tianyi Zhou, Qiang He,\nLei Han\n, Mykola Pechenizkiy, Meng Fang.\nTask Adaptation from Skills: Information Geometry, Disentanglement, and New Objectives for Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning. [\narxiv\n]\nIn:\nThe Twelfth International Conference on Learning Representations (\nICLR\n)\n, 2024. (\nSpotlight\n)\n[51]\nYucheng Yang, Tianyi Zhou,\nLei Han\n, Meng Fang an...[truncated]"
