  "serper::Bowen Zhou": {
    "homepage": "https://web.ee.tsinghua.edu.cn/zhoubowen/en/index.htm",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "æ¸åå¤§å­¦ Bowen Zhou--Home--Home\nä¸­æ\nPersonal Homepage\nä¸­æ\nBowen Zhou\nProfessional Title: Professor\nZipCodeï¼\n62bda03a21f6be47d99c58a3772613a27075eef9c35da2856ed9b226889e41867227c6d5288df5775bdffa3e06db6496816d5d6cd700f5bb35d04d0728684ae30a8db31218d4e25b1fea65356f3cb4d4662cc1d728d84e751699278cde613657cae6afc0fea1e743a48b12e1db617e89a267dbcbcf6612307f12c01734616445\nPostalAddressï¼\n5fd7f4038c44888a493b653c830fcb8cbeff904dedf60bf21119d461ee97944678cd258e92201309b98ac24df9ead530872e3586febd620631ccb7b0989ef8e5a12624fe19ce4925c4a566b6e6983622afa17fb04506b56f6fe6057e06181498b623882a94961d9c51c049c4ca9137950e7d23109a661f17233ac2254b5b900e\nEmailï¼\nc67724a655b3d4eef00ba45eaceb1eb6d1ace3fea74b3307a19f550fafd795e126222d93dff9a051a937dab03207e7e87148af3a5419753982a65bd68ea6bec59e9107bdcd06b3eae89e733fe00b08ead35c3089918651893b809b84e7b0b269cdc570ae793f050d304f2c5ae39eaf9fb75a923636c16054be88752a5cd27966\nRead more >\nProfile\nBowen Zhou is a Huiyan Chair Professor at Tsinghua University, a tenured Professor in the Department of Electronic Engineering, the Director of the Center for Collaborative and Cognitive Interaction Intelligence (C3I), and the Founder of Xianyuan Technology. He is also a Fellow of IEEE and CAAI.\nProfessor Zhou brings a wealth of experience from both cutting-edge research and industry. He previously served as Director of the AI Foundation Lab at IBM Research, Chief Scientist of the IBM Watson Group, IBM Distinguished Engineer, Senior Vice President of JD.com, Chairman of the JD Group Technology Committee, and President of JD Cloud & AI. In 2022, he returned to academia from industry.\nHis research interests include speech and natural language processing, multimodal and knowledge representation, understanding, generation, reasoning, human-computer dialogue, and trustworthy AI. He has published over 100 papers with more than 21,000 citations and holds dozens of domestic and international patents.\nHe proposed a self-attentive multi-head fusion mechanism for natural language representation, which later became one of the core ideas of the Transformer architecture and has been cited over 2,000 times by papers such as Transformer and GAT. He also proposed two natural language generation model architectures and algorithms in the field of AIGC, which have been cited more than 3,000 times.\nLab homepage:\nhttp://c3i.ee.tsinghua.edu.cn\n(including latest publications)\nResearch Focus\nNext-generation artificial intelligence models and theories\nWork Experience\nEducational Experience\nXianyuan Technology\n                    \n                    \n                     , Founder\nJD.com Group\n                    \n                    \n                     , Senior Vice President of JD.com Group, Chairman of the Technology Committee of JD.com Group, President of JD Cloud & AI, and Founding Dean of JD AI Research Institute\nIBM\n                    \n                    \n                     , Director of AI Foundations Labs, IBM Researchï¼Chief Scientist of IBM Watson Groupï¼IBM Distinguished Engineer\nUniversity of Science and Technology of China\n                     , Electronic Information Engineering\n                     , University graduated\n                     , Bachelor's degree\nChinese Academy of Sciences\n                     , Information and Signal Processing\n                     , Postgraduate (Master's Degree)\n                     , Master's degree\nUniversity of Colorado, USA\n                     , Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering\n                     , With Certificate of Graduation for Doctorate Study\n                     , Doctoral degree\nSocial Affiliations\nDirector and Chief Scientist of Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory\nIEEE/CAAI Fellow\nVice Chairman of the Artificial Intelligence Standardization Technical Committee of the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology\nMember of the Expert Committee of the National New Generation Artificial Intelligence Governance\nMember of the Expert Committee of the National New Generation Artificial Intelligence Development Research Center\nExecutive Director of the National Major Science and Technology Special Project for New Generation Artificial Intelligence\nMember of the Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Strategic Consulting Expert Committee; Science and Technology Advisor for cities like Beijing, Guangzhou, and Chengdu\nVisiting Professor at Peking University, University of Science and Technology of China, and Shanghai Jiao Tong University\nPart-time Professor & Ph.D. Supervisor at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (Shenzhen) and Harbin Institute of Technology\nScientific Research\nPapers\nBo Li, Peng Qi, Bo Liu, Shuai Di, Jingen Liu, Jiquan Pei, Jinfeng Yi, Bowen Zhou. Trustworthy AI: From principles to practices. ACM Computing Surveys 2023/1\nBiqing Qi, Bowen Zhou, Weinan Zhang, Jianxing Liu, Ligang Wu. Improving robustness of intent detection under adversarial attacks: A geometric constraint perspective. IEEE transactions on neural networks and learning systems. 2023/8\nBiqing Qi, Junqi Gao, Jianxing Liu, Ligang Wu, Bowen Zhou. Enhancing adversarial transferability via information bottleneck constraints. IEEE Signal Processing Letters. 2024/4\nBiqing Qi, Yiang Luo, Junqi Gao, Pengfei Li, Kai Tian, Zhiyuan Ma, Bowen Zhou. Exploring adversarial robustness of deep state space models. NeurIPS 2024\nNing Ding, Yulin Chen, Bokai Xu, Yujia Qin, Zhi Zheng, Shengding Hu, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun, Bowen Zhou. Enhancing chat language models by scaling high-quality instructional conversations. EMNLP 2023\nKaiyan Zhang, Ning Ding, Biqing Qi, Xuekai Zhu, Xinwei Long, Bowen Zhou. CRaSh: Clustering, Removing, and Sharing Enhance Fine-tuning without Full Large Language Model. EMNLP 2023\nNing Ding, Xingtai Lv, Qiaosen Wang, Yulin Chen, Bowen Zhou, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. Sparse low-rank adaptation of pre-trained language models. EMNLP 2023\nBowen Zhou, Ning Ding. Generative ai for complex scenarios: Language models are sequence processors. International Journal of Artificial Intelligence and Robotics Research. 2024/3\nXuekai Zhu, Biqing Qi, Kaiyan Zhang, Xinwei Long, Zhouhan Lin, Bowen Zhou. PaD: Program-aided distillation can teach small models reasoning better than chain-of-thought fine-tuning. NAACL 2024\nChe Jiang, Biqing Qi, Xiangyu Hong, Dayuan Fu, Yang Cheng, Fandong Meng, Mo Yu, Bowen Zhou, Jie Zhou. On Large Language Models' Hallucination with Regard to Known Facts. NAACL 2024\nKaiyan Zhang, Sihang Zeng, Ermo Hua, Ning Ding, Zhang-Ren Chen, Zhiyuan Ma, Haoxin Li, Ganqu Cui, Biqing Qi, Xuekai Zhu, Xingtai Lv, Hu Jinfang, Zhiyuan Liu, Bowen Zhou. Ultramedical: Building specialized generalists in biomedicine. NeurIPS 2024\nKaiyan Zhang, Jianyu Wang, Ermo Hua, Biqing Qi, Ning Ding, Bowen Zhou. Cogenesis: A framework collaborating large and small language models for secure context-aware instruction following. ACL 2024\nBiqing Qi, Junqi Gao, Kaiyan Zhang, Dong Li, Jianxing Liu, Ligang Wu, Bowen Zhou. Smr: State memory replay for long sequence modeling. ACL 2024\nBiqing Qi, Kaiyan Zhang, Kai Tian, Haoxiang Li, Zhang-Ren Chen, Sihang Zeng, Ermo Hua, Hu Jinfang, Bowen Zhou. Large language models as biomedical hypothesis generators: a comprehensive evaluation. COLM 2024\nDayuan Fu, Biqing Qi, Yihuai Gao, Che Jiang, Guanting Dong, Bowen Zhou. MSI-Agent: Incorporating Multi-Scale Insight into Embodied Agents for Superior Planning and Decision-Making. EMNLP 2024\nXiangyu Hong, Che Jiang, Biqing Qi, Fandong Meng, Mo Yu, Bowen Zhou, Jie Zhou. On the token distance modeling ability of higher RoPE attention dimension. EMNLP 2024\nXingtai Lv, Ning Ding, Kaiyan Zhang, Ermo Hua, Ganqu Cui, Bowen Zhou. Scalable Efficient Training of Large Language Models with Low-dimensional Projected Attention. EMNLP 2024\nYulin Chen, Ning Ding, Hai-Tao Zheng, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun, Bowen Zhou. Empowering private tutoring by chaining large language models. CIKM 2024\nLifan Yuan, Ganqu Cui, Hanbin Wang, Ning Ding, Xingyao Wang, Jia Deng, Boji Shan, Huimin Chen, Ruobing Xie, Yankai Lin, Zhenghao Liu, Bowen Zhou, Hao Peng, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun. Advancing llm reasoning generalists with preference trees. ICLR 2025\nKaiyan Zhang, Jiayuan Zhang, Haoxin Li, Xuekai Zhu, Ermo Hua, Xingtai Lv, Ning Ding, Biqing Qi, Bowen Zhou. OpenPRM: Building Open-domain Process-based Reward Models with Preference Trees. ICLR 2025\nå¨ä¼¯æ. ä»¥éä¸èåæ¹å¼æå»ºAGIââè·¯å¾ä¸å³é®é®é¢[J]. ä¸­å½è®¡ç®æºå­¦ä¼éè®¯, 2025, 21(1): 54-62.\nResearch Group\nFoundation Models\nGeneralization algorithms based on reinforcement learning\nPhysically interpretable model mechanism analysis and architecture design\nMultimodal Understanding and Representation\nImage/video understanding and controllable generation\nLanguage model-augmented proteomics analysis\nHuman-Machine / Multi-Agent Collaboration\nRobot control and computer operation driven by vision-language models\nMulti-agent collaborative reasoning based on reinforcement learning\nAI for Science and Innovation\nAI-driven hypothesis generation and frontier theoretical validation in biology, chemistry, physics, and mathematics\nHonors and Titles\n2021\nFellow of the Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence\n2020\nWu Wenjun Artificial Intelligence Outstanding Contribution Award\n2019\nIEEE Fellow\nAll rights reserved. Department of electronic engineering, Tsinghua University Address: Tsinghua University, Haidian District, Beijing, 100084\nThe Last Update Time:\n-\n-\nClick:"
