    "homepage_text": "Jinshuo Dong\nMenu\nHome\nLinks\nBlog\nJinshuo Dong\nAbout me:\nI'm a postdoc at Northwestern University. I did my PhD in applied math (\nAMCS\n) at the University of Pennsylvania, advised by Aaron Roth.\nPrior to Penn, I obtained my bachelor's degree\nin mathematics from Peking University in 2014. My CV can be found\nhere\n.\nContact:\nEmail:\nfirst name\n@northwestern.edu\nSeeley Mudd 3527, 2233 Tech Drive\nEvanston, IL 60208\nNews:\nI'm on the academic job market this year\nResearch\nI study privacy and reliability of modern data science. My work is best represented\nby two lines of research: differential privacy and accountable machine learning in legal context. For more information, see my\nresearch statement\n.\nBeyond that, I'm also generally interested in the science and mathematics of information and computation.\nPapers\n[Selected Publications]\n[Full publication list]\nError-tolerant e-discovery protocols\nJinshuo Dong, Jason Hartline, Liren Shan, Aravindan Vijayaraghavan.\nTo appear in the 3rd ACM CSLAW Symposium\n[arXiv]\nGaussian Differential Privacy\nJinshuo Dong, Aaron Roth, Weijie Su.\nDiscussion paper\nin Journal of the\nRoyal Statistical Society Series B: Statistical Methodology (JRSSB), 84(1):3â37, 02 2022\n[blog post]\n[arXiv]\n[talk at Simons Institute]\n[RSS discussion introductory pre-meeting]\n[RSS discussion recording]\nA Central Limit Theorem for Differentially Private Query Answering\nJinshuo Dong, Weijie J Su, Linjun Zhang\nIn the Proceedings of NeurIPS 2021 (selected as\nspotlight\n)\n[arXiv]\n[slides]\n[recording/OpenReview]"
