    "homepage_text": "Huazhe Xu\nHuazhe Xu（许华哲）\n[Google Scholar]\n[Twitter]\nHome\nPublication\nGroup\nContact\nMisc\nI am a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor at\nInstitute for Interdisciplinary Information Sciences (IIIS), Tsinghua University\n. I am leading the Tsinghua Embodied AI Lab (TEA Lab,\nlogo\n), where we build robots and then bring intelligence to robots.\nI was a postdoctoral researcher at\nStanford Vision and Learning Lab (SVL)\nadvised by Prof.\nJiajun Wu\n. I obtained my Ph.D. in\nBerkeley AI Research (BAIR)\nadvised by Prof.\nTrevor Darrell\n. I obtained my bachelor degree from Tsinghua University (major in EE, minor in Management).\nI am hiring self-motivated Postdocs, Ph.D. students, Undergrads, and Research Interns at Tsinghua (base: Beijing, Shanghai). See more details in Chinese\nhere\n.\nI am also hiring talented engineers and interns in an embodied AI startup.\nPlease email me (+ tealab_hire@163.com) with your CV directly.\nI support\nSlow Science\n.\nResearch Topics\nI am interested in\nEmbodied AI\n:\nReinforcement Learning\n,\nRobotics\n, and\nComputer Vision/Touch\n. Specifically, my research focuses on modeling the dynamics of the world, leveraging/finding human priors for policy learning, and further enabling algorithms to learn in a sample-efficient manner and generalize to unseen scenarios. I am also interested in solving complex real robot applications with deep learning and reinforcement learning.\nNews\nTwo papers (\nDemoSpeedUp\n,\nFACET\n) are accepted by CoRL'25.\nOur paper\nRDP\nwon\nbest student paper finalist\nat RSS'25.\nOur paper\nRDP\nwon\nbest paper\nat ICRA'25 Beyond Pick and Place Workshop.\nOur paper\nDemonGen\nwon\nbest long paper\nat CVPR'25 Syn4CV Workshop.\nI gave three invited talks at RSS workshops.\nI won AI100 Pioneers from DeepTech and MIT Tech Review in China.\nI served as a session chair and a mentor in ICLR'25.\nTwo papers (\nMENTOR\n,\nFoG\n) are accepted by ICML'25.\nFour papers (\nDemoGen\n,\nDOGlove\n,\nRDP\n,\nMeopheus\n) are accepted by RSS'25.\nThe paper\nTwoByTwo\nis accepted by CVPR'25.\nDLLM\nis accepted by NAACL'25.\nI am invited to Boao Forum for Asia as a roundtable speaker.\nFour papers (\nDenseMatcher\n(\nspotlight\n),\nStem-OB\n(\nspotlight\n),\nRobots Pre-Train Robots\n,\nLooking Backward\n) are accepted by ICLR'25.\nTwo papers (\nCatch It!\n,\nPower-Saving Quadruped\n) are accepted by ICRA'25.\nI serve as an area chair for IJCAI'25.\nTwo papers (\nMake-An-Agent\n,\nKeyGrid\n) are accepted by NeurIPS'24.\nI serve as an associate editor for ICRA'25.\nThree papers (\nManiwhere\n,\nRiEMann\n,\nGenSim2\n) are accepted by CoRL'24.\nI serve as an area chair for ICLR'25.\nI won Yunfan \"Brilliant Star\" Award in World Artificial Intelligence Conference (WAIC) 2024.\nTwo papers (\nRoboABC\n,\nDiffusion Reward\n) are accepted by ECCV'24.\nV-Loco-Manip\nis accepted by IROS'24.\nACE\nand\nOMPO\nare selected as\noral\npresentations in ICML'24.\nDP3\nis accepted by RSS'24.\nSix papers (\nRethinking Transformers in Solving POMDPs\n,\nOMPO\n,\nPremier-TACO\n,\nBEE\n,\nOBAC\n,\nACE\n) are accepted by ICML'24.\nI serve as a meta-reviewer in\nPioneers Workshop\nin RSS'24.\nThree papers (\nArraybot\n,\nDeformNet\n,\nHIRO Hand\n) are accepted by ICRA'24.\nSix papers (\nDrM (\nspotlight\n)\n,\nGenSim(\nspotlight\n)\n,\nUni-O4\n,\nLaMo\n,\nCOPlanner\n,\nMorphMaze\n) are accepted by ICLR'24.\nI serve as a reviewer in Science Robotics.\nI serve as a Senior PC in IJCAI'24.\n9DTact\nis accepted by RA-L with a presentation at ICRA'24.\nI served as session chairs at DAI and X-AGI conference. I also will give a tutorial on RL at DAI.\nI gave a talk about Embodied AI at\nYiXi\n@Shenzhen.\nRoboCraft (3D version) is accepted by IJRR.\nOur paper\nRoboCook\nwon\nbest system paper award\nat CoRL'23.\nOur paper\nGenSim\nwon\noutstanding paper award\nin LangRob workshop at CoRL'23.\nI serve as an associate editor in ICRA'24.\nSix papers (\nRL-ViGen\n,\nTACO\n,\nLfVoid\n,\nMoVie\n,\nH-InDex\n,\nCEIL\n) are accepted by NeurIPS'23 including 1 in dataset and benchmark track.\nOTAS\nis accepted by WACV'24.\nRoboCook is accepted by CoRL'23 (\noral\n).\nPretrain-or-not-pretrain\nis accepted by ICML'23.\nI will serve as an SPC member in IJCAI'23.\nFour papers (\nDeFog\n,\nEAR\n,\nScalingDiffPlanning\n,\nno-ensemble-mbrl\n) are accepted by ICLR'23.\nFour papers(\nUSEEK\n,\nDTact\n,\nEIL\n,\nBimanual Handover\n) are accepted by ICRA'23.\nTwo papers are accepted by NeurIPS'22 (\nPIE-G\n,\nEMAPP\n, 2\nspotlights\n).\nOne paper (\nsee-hear-feel\n) is accepted by CoRL'22.\nOur paper\nSUMMON\nis accepted by Siggraph Asia'22.\nOur paper \"Towards Learning to Play Piano with Dexterous Hands and Touch\" is accepted by IROS'22.\nOur RSS paper \"RoboCraft\" is covered by\nMIT Tech Review\nand\nHAI\n.\nTwo papers are accepted by ICML'22.\nOur paper \"Don't Touch What Matters\" is accepted by IJCAI'22.\nI gave a talk at UC San Diego.\nOur paper RoboCraft is accepted by RSS'22.\nOne paper is accepted by ICLR'22 (\nspotlight\n).\nTwo papers are accepted by NeurIPS'21.\nI became Dr. Xu on May 15, 2021.\nI gave a talk at MSRA, March 10, 2021.\nOne paper is accepted by CVPR'21.\nTwo papers are accepted by ICRA'21.\nTwo papers are accepted by ICLR'21.\nI gave a talk at Nvidia, Nov, 2020.\nOne papers is accepted by NeurIPS'20.\nOne papers is accepted by ECCV'20.\nOne papers is accepted by ICML'20 (\noral\n)."
  },
  "serper::Yan Yan": {
    "homepage": "https://tomyan555.github.io/",
    "emails": [
