    "homepage_text": "Yan Yan | Personal Webpage\nYan Yan\nAssociate Professor\nDepartment of Computer Science\nUniversity of Illinois Chicago\noffice: LIB3-190G\nemail: yyan55 [AT] uic.edu\nNews:\n[Top] In Fall 2026 and Spring 2027, I have multiple openings for postdocs and Ph.D students in the fileds of computer vision, biomedical image analysis, multimedia and machine learning. Feel free to contact me with your CV.\nBio\nDr. Yan Yan is currently a tenured Associate Professor in the Department of Computer Science at the University of Illinois Chicago. \n\tHe received his Ph.D. in Computer Science at the University of Trento.\n\tHe has published 200+ research papers in the fields of computer vision, multimedia and machine learning. \n\tHe received IBM Best Student Paper Award in ICPR 2014, Best Paper Award in ACM Multimedia 2015 and Best Paper Finalist in ACM Multimedia 2018. \n\tHe has served as the General Chair for ACM ICMR 2025 and as Area Chairs for major computer vision and multimedia conferences including CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, BMVC, ACM Multimedia, ICLR and NeurIPS.\n\tHe also served as associate editors in Neurocomputing, Computer Vision and Image Understanding (CVIU), Machine Vision and Applications (MVA), Image and Vision Computing (IVC), \n\tand guest editors in IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (TPAMI), \n\tComputer Vision and Image Understanding (CVIU) and ACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications (TOMM). \n\tKnow more information please check the\nCVM-LAB\n.\nPublications\nMost recent publications on\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nSelected\nMIM4DD: Mutual Information Maximization for Dataset Distillation\nYuzhang Shang, Zhihang Yuan, Yan Yan\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2023\nPaper\nBoundary Guided Mixing Trajectory for Semantic Control with Diffusion Models\nYe Zhu, Yu Wu, Zhiwei Deng, Olga Russakovsky, Yan Yan\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS), 2023\nPaper\nCode\nTowards Saner Deep Image Registration\nBin Duan, Ming Zhong, Yan Yan\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2023\nPaper\nCode\nCausal-DFQ: Causality Guided Data-free Network Quantization\nYuzhang Shang, Bingxin Xu, Gaowen Liu, Ramana Kompella, Yan Yan\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2023\nPaper\nPost-training Quantization on Diffusion Models\nYuzhang Shang, Zhihang Yuan, Bin Xie, Bingzhe Wu, Yan Yan\nIEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2023\nPaper\nCode\nDiscrete Contrastive Diffusion for Cross-Modal Music and Image Generation\nYe Zhu, Yu Wu, Kyle Olszewski, Jian Ren, Sergey Tulyakov, Yan Yan\nInternational Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR), 2023\nPaper\nCode\nLipschitz Continuity Retained Binary Neural Network\nYuzhang Shang, Dan Xu, Bin Duan, Ziliang Zong, Liqiang Nie, Yan Yan\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nLearning Omnidirectional Flow in 360-degree Video via Siamese Representation\nKeshav Bhandari, Bin Duan, Gaowen Liu, Hugo Latapie, Ziliang Zong, Yan Yan\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nNetwork Binarization via Contrastive Learning\nYuzhang Shang, Dan Xu, Ziliang Zong, Liqiang Nie, Yan Yan\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nQuantized GAN for Complex Music Generation from Dance Videos\nYe Zhu, Kyle Olszewski, Yu Wu, Panos Achlioptas, Menglei Chai, Yan Yan, Sergey Tulyakov\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2022\nPaper\nCode\nLipschitz Continuity Guided Knowledge Distillation\nYuzhang Shang, Bin Duan, Ziliang Zong, Liqiang Nie, Yan Yan\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2021\nPaper\nCode\nDescribing Unseen Videos via Multi-Modal Cooperative Dialog Agents\nYe Zhu, Yu Wu, Yi Yang, Yan Yan\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV), 2020\nPaper\nCode\nTeaching\nUIC CS 512: Advanced Machine Learning (Fall 2025)\nUIC CS 594: Energy Efficient Deep Learning (Spring 2025)\nIIT CS 577: Deep Learning (Fall 2023)\nIIT CS 584: Machine Learning (Spring 2024, Spring 2023, Fall 2022, Fall 2021, Spring 2021)\nIIT CS 595: Advanced Topics on Computer Vision and Multimedia (Spring 2022)\nMembers\nComputer Vision and Multimedia Lab on\nCVM-LAB\nCurrent PhD students:\nChangchang Sun\n(Fall 2021-current, B.S./M.S.: Shandong University)\nZhenghao Zhao\n(Fall 2022-current, M.S.: IIT)\nWeitai Kang\n(Fall 2022-current, B.S.: Sun Yat-sen University)\nJunyi Wu\n(Spring 2023-current, B.S.: Sun Yat-sen University)\nGengyu Zhang (Spring 2023-current, M.S.: University of Georgia)\nHaoxuan Wang\n(Fall 2023-current, B.S./M.S.: Shanghai Jiao Tong University)\nFeiran Wang\n(Spring 2024-current, M.S.: University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign)\nJiachen Tao (Fall 2024-current, B.S.: Zhejiang University)\nBingxin Xu (Part-time, Spring 2023-current, working at Discover Financial Services)\nAlumni:\nPostdocs and PhDs:\nGaowen Liu\n(Postdoc 2018-2020, First Employment: Research Scientist at Cisco Research)\nKeshav Bhandari\n(PhD 2018-2022, First Employment: Sr. Software Engineer at Tesla)\nYe Zhu\n(PhD 2019-2023, First Employment: Postdoctoral Researcher at Princeton University)\nBin Duan\n(PhD 2019-2024, First Employment: Postdoctoral Researcher at the University of Michigan)\nYuzhang Shang\n(PhD 2021-2025, First Employment: Assistant professor at the University of Central Florida)\nVisitings:\nHao Tang\n(Visiting PhD 2018-2019 from University of Trento, Next: Postdoc at ETH Zürich)\nYutian Lin\n(Visiting PhD 2018-2019 from University of Technology Sydney, Next: Associate Professor at Wuhan University)\nXianjin Han\n(Visiting PhD 2019-2020 from Shandong University, Next: Postdoc at National University of Singapore)\nNa Zheng\n(Visiting PhD 2019-2020 from Shandong University, Next: Postdoc at National University of Singapore)\nAihua Zheng\n(Visiting Professor 2019-2020 from Anhui University)\nSongsong Wu\n(Visiting Professor 2018-2019 from Nanjing University of Posts and Telecommunications)\nMasters with Thesis:\nCastaneda Lopez Luis (Master 2022, First Employment: Software Engineer at NextShift)\nChaguer Reda (Master 2022, First Employment: Software Engineer at Meta)\nElomari Alaoui Ismail (Master 2022, First Employment: Software Dev Engineer at Amazon)\nJorge Cervera Perez (Master 2021, First Employment: Senior Software Engineer at Qualcomm)\nDe Miguel Juan Carlos (Master 2021, First Employment: Data Scientist at Caterpillar Inc)\nAli Issaoui (Master 2021, First Employment: Software Engineer at Amazon Web Services)\nNikhil Sharma (Fall 2023-Spring 2025, M.S.: IIT)\nUndergraduates:\nMario A. DeLaGarza (Undergraduate 2019, First Employment: Software Engineer at Google)\nTheo William Guidroz (Undergraduate 2021-2022, First Employment: Software Engineer at Google)\nChengyuan Xue (University of Toronto REU 2023, Next: University of Toronto)\nWilliam Zhu (UChicago High School Student 2022, Next: Yale University)\nKavya Uppal (Illinois Mathematics and Science Academy High School Student 2023)\nMisc\nThis website was built with\njekyll\nbased on a template by\nMartin Saveski\n.\nYan Yan\nemail: yyan55 [AT] uic.edu"
