  "serper::Zaiwei Chen": {
    "homepage": "https://sites.google.com/view/zaiweichen/home",
    "emails": [
      "chen5252@purdue.edu"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zaiwei Chen\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nZaiwei Chen\nZaiwei Chen\nI am an Assistant Professor in the Edwardson School of Industrial Engineering at Purdue University, where I was appointed as a Solberg Academic Excellence Scholar. I am also affiliated with the\nInstitute for Control, Optimization and Networks\n(ICON)\nPrior to joining Purdue, I was a CMI Postdoctoral Fellow in the Department of Computing and Mathematical Sciences at the California Institute of Technology. I hold a Ph.D. in Machine Learning, an M.S. in Mathematics, and an M.S. in Operations Research from the Georgia Institute of Technology. I received my B.S. in Electrical Engineering from the Chu Kochen Honors College at Zhejiang University. Here is my\nCV\n.\nI am actively recruiting motivated Ph.D. students with strong mathematical backgrounds. Prospective students are encouraged to apply to the\nPh.D. program\nin the School of Industrial Engineering at Purdue University.\nResearch Interests\nReinforcement Learning\nMulti-Agent Systems and Learning in Games\nStochastic Approximation\nConcentration Inequalities\nRecent News\nI will chair an invited session (Applied Probability Society cluster) at the INFORMS Annual Meeting, October 26–29, 2025, in Atlanta, Georgia, titled “Reinforcement Learning: Theory and Algorithms.”\nI will give a talk titled “Non‑asymptotic analysis of average‑reward Q‑learning with adaptive stepsizes” at ICCOPT 2025 (International Conference on Continuous Optimization), July 21–24, 2025, in Los Angeles, California.\nI will jointly give a tutorial titled “Structure‑Exploiting Reinforcement Learning for Networked Systems” at ACC 2025 (American Control Conference), July 8–10, 2025, in Denver, Colorado.\nI will give two talks titled “Seminorm Lyapunov Stability: From Deterministic to Stochastic Approximation Algorithms” and “Non-asymptotic Guarantees of Average-Reward Q-Learning with Adaptive Stepsizes”, and chair the poster lightning‑talk session at the INFORMS APS Conference in Atlanta (June 30 – July 3, 2025).\nI will jointly give a tutorial titled “Recent Advances of Reinforcement Learning in Dynamic Games” at SIGMETRICS 2025, June 9–13, 2025, at Stony Brook University, New York.\nContact Information\nEmail\n:\nchen5252\n@purdue.edu\nOffice\n: Grissom Hall 264\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
  "serper::Byoung-Tak Zhang": {
    "homepage": "https://en.snu.ac.kr/research/highlights?md=v&bbsidx=122871",
    "emails": [
      "gurume0221@snu.ac.kr",
      "morningcalm2@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Professor ZHANG Byoung-Tak, a Pioneer Scientist of Artificial Intelligence - Research Highlights - Research Highlights - Research - Seoul National University\nSkip to content\nGwanak Campus\nYeongeon Campus\nPyeongchang Campus\nSiheung Campus\nColleges\nOffice of Global Affairs\nOpen Mobile Navigation\nInput Keywords\nSearch\nClose\nAdmissions Information\nCampus Map\nResearch Highlights\nResearch Highlights\nCOVID-19\nStats & Report\nResearch Profiles(PURE)\nResearch Units\nResearch Institutes\nGovernment-funded Research Centers\nBK21 FOUR Groups\nResearch Support\nSupport for Academic Activities\nSupport for Internal Projects\nSupport for Research Activities\nSNU 10-10 Project\nResearch Ethics\nInstitutional Review Board\nCommittee on Research Integrity\nInstitutional Animal Care and Use Committee\nSNU R&DB Foundation\nResearch\n/\nResearch Highlights\nResearch Highlights\nResearch Highlights\n/\nResearch Highlights\nProfessor ZHANG Byoung-Tak, a Pioneer Scientist of Artificial Intelligence\nShare this to Kakao Talk\nShare this to Facebook\nCopy URL\nProfessor ZHANG Byoung-Tak>\nProfessor Zhang Byoung-Tak (Department of Computer Science and Engineering), a pioneer in the field of artificial intelligence, had an interview with\nMaeil Business Newspaper\n. “When I returned to Korea in 1995 after receiving my doctorate degree, people asked me why I studied artificial intelligence. Today there are smartphones, robots, IoT and cloud computing,” he said. Professor Zhang is currently developing ‘Pororobot,’ and ‘home robot.’ Pororobot is an artificial intelligence robot that can have conversations (even in English) with children. Home robot would help working mothers by waking children up in the morning, memorizing their class schedules and taking care of school supplies. “My goal is to make robots that can absorb and apply information by themselves,” said Professor Zhang. “Not many Korean companies are interested in artificial intelligence. Korean companies should invest in artificial intelligence R&D as other global companies do.”\nPublished in\nMaeil Business Newspaper\nSummary by LEE Hee Un, SNU English Editor, gurume0221@snu.ac.kr\nProofread by Melora Brett Briana Johnson, morningcalm2@gmail.com"
  },
