    "homepage_text": "Quan Yuan's Homepage\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nQuan Yuan's Homepage\nQuan YUAN's Homepage\nYUAN Quan 袁 泉\nI am currently an associate researcher at School of Cyber Science and Technology, Shandong University\n.\nMy research interest is cryptography, especially digital signatures, zero-knowledge proofs, hash-based constructions, quantum security, and blockchain.\nEmail:\nyuanquansdu at gmail.com\nGoogle Scholar\n,\nORCID\n,\nResearchGate\n,\ndblp\nEducation\nPhD: Guaduate School of Informatics, Kyoto University. Supervisors: Mehdi Tibouchi & Masayuki Abe.\nDegree Thesis: A Study on Hash-based Signature Schemes.\nLink\nB&M: Department of Mathematics, Shandong University. Supervisor: Puwen Wei.\nDegree Thesis: Security of the Blockchain Against Long Delay Attack.\nWork Experience\nAssociate Researcher.\nSchool of Cyber Science and Technology, Shandong University. 2024.10\n~\nProject Researcher.\nMathematical Informatics 1st Laboratory\n, t\nhe University of Tokyo,\n2022-2024\nPublications\nQuan Yuan, Chao Sun, Tsuyoshi Takagi. Revisiting the Security of Fiat-Shamir Signature Schemes under Superposition Attacks. ACISP 2024: 164-184 (2024)\nShichen Wu, Zhiying Song, Puwen Wei, Peng Tang, Quan Yuan\n. Improving privacy of anonymous proof-of-stake protocols. CANS 2023: 368-391 (2023)\nQuan Yuan, Mehdi Tibouchi, Masayuki Abe. Quantum-Access Security of Hash-Based Signature Schemes. ACISP 2023: 343-380 (2023)\nQuan Yuan, Mehdi Tibouchi, Masayuki Abe. On subset-resilient hash function families. Des. Codes Cryptogr. 90(3): 719-758 (2022)\nQuan Yuan, Mehdi Tibouchi, Masayuki Abe. Security notions for stateful signature schemes. IET Inf. Secur. 16(1): 1-17 (2022)\nQuan Yuan, Puwen Wei, Keting Jia, Haiyang Xue: Analysis of blockchain protocol against static adversarial miners corrupted by long delay attackers. Sci. China Inf. Sci. 63(3) (2020)\nPuwen Wei, Quan Yuan, Yuliang Zheng. Security of the Blockchain Against Long Delay Attack. ASIACRYPT (3) 2018: 250-275 (2018)\nProceedings\nQuan Yuan, Tsuyoshi Takagi. Quantum-access Security of\nProbabilistic\nFiat-Shamir Signature Schemes.  4A2\n-3, 2024.\nQuan Yuan, Tsuyoshi Takagi. Revisiting Fiat-Shamir Signatures under Superposition Attacks. SCIS 2023, 1A2-5, 2023.\nQuan Yuan, Mehdi Tibouchi, Masayuki Abe. Quantum-Accessible Security of Stateless Hash-based Signature Schemes. SCIS 2022.\nQuan Yuan, Mehdi Tibouchi, Masayuki Abe. Security Notions of Stateful Signature Schemes. SCIS 2021\nTalks\nOpportunities and challenges of hash-based digital signatures in a post-quantum environment. Hainan University, 2024.12\nQuantum Security of Hash-based Signature Schemes. Xiamen University 2024.\nSecurity of Fiat-Shamir Signature Schemes under Superposition Attacks. Crypto-Math Workshop. Tokyo Institute of Technology, 2023.5\nQuantum Security of Modern Digital Signature Schemes. Shandong University, 2023.5\nActivities\nProgram Committee Member:\nACISP 2023\n, ICICS 2025\n(Sub-)Reviewer: ASIACRYPT 2023, ProvSec 2023, ACNS 2024,\nCT-RSA 2022 & 2020,\nTCC 2021,\nIWSEC 2021, PKC 2020,\nJournal of Cryptology, Frountiers of Computer Science, IEICE Transactions.\nProject Member:\nCrypto-Math CREST\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
