    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jingyuan Deng\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nJingyuan Deng\nHi! My name is Jingyuan (Jean) Deng. I am a fourth year (Jan 2022~) Ph.D. student in Information Systems at the\nDepartment of Information Systems and Analytics\n,\nNational University of Singapore\n.\nI am fortunate to be advised by\nProf. Dandan Qiao\n.\nBefore starting the PhD journey, I obtained my Bachelor's degree and Master's degree in Management Information Systems at Beijing Normal University and National University of Singapore in 2020 and 2021.\nMy current research centers on\nplatform-incentives, and the intermediary role of digital platforms. Particularly, I focus on exploring\nhow digital platforms 1) shape consumer behaviors in purchase, word-of-mouth and review evaluation and 2) facilitate value co-creation\nin innovation\nbetween different actors.\nYou may contact me at\ndeng.jingyuan\nat\nu.nus.edu\n.\nWorking Papers\nExploring the Impact of Platform-Incentivized Reviews on Product Sales and the Role of Review Inconsistency\njoint\nwith Prof. Warut Khern-am-nai\n,\nProf. Dandan Qiao\nConference\n:\nCSWIM\n2023\n(\nChangsha, China)\nSSRN Manuscript\nUnraveling the Role of Public Crowds in Driving Innovation for Technology Product Development\njoint\nwith Prof. Grace Gu,\nProf. Dandan Qiao\nConferences\n:\nSCECR\n2022\n(\nMadrid, Spain)\n;\nSMS Annual Conference\n2022\n(London, UK)\n;\nCIST\n2022\n(Indianapolis, USA)\nSSRN Manuscript\nConnecting People and Spreading Ideas: Unravelling the Impact of Ride-Hailing on Local Knowledge Flows\njoint\nwith Prof. Aditya Karanam,\nProf. Dandan Qiao\nConferences\n:\nAOM\n2025\n(Copenhagen, Denmark)\n; SCECR\n2025\n(\nPaphos, Cyprus)\n; CIST\n2025\n(Atlanta\n,\nUSA);\nICIS\n2025\n(\nNashville\n, USA)\nSee\nAbstract\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
  },
