    "homepage_text": "Zhengqing Zhou\nHome\nResearch\nZhengqing Zhou   å¨æ­£æ¸\nAbout me\nI am currrently working as a quantitative researcher at\nSusquehanna International Group\n. I received my PhD in Mathematics from\nStanford\n(2021),  advised by\nProf. Peter Glynn\n,\nProf. Jose Blanchet\n, and\nProf. George Papanicolaou\n(co-advise). I was a member in\nAdvanced Financial Technologies Laboratory (AFTLab)\n. Prior to Stanford, I obtained my bachelor's degree in\nSchool of Mathematical Science\nfrom\nUSTC\n(2016).\nContact\nEmail: zqzhou [at] stanford [dot] edu\nLinkedIn\nGoogle Scholar\nResearch Interests\nAlgorithmic Trading\nApplied Probability\nDistributionally Robust Optimization\nStatistical Machine Learning\nResearch\nPreprints\nSequential Batch Learning in Finite-Action Linear Contextual Bandits\nYanjun Han,\nZhengqing Zhou\n, Zhengyuan Zhou, Jose H. Blanchet, Peter W. Glynn, Yinyu Ye\nUnbiased Optimal Stopping via the MUSE\nZhengqing Zhou\n†\n, Guanyang Wang\n†\n, Jose H. Blanchet, Peter W. Glynn\nDistributionally Robust Martingale Optimal Transport\nZhengqing Zhou\n, Jose H. Blanchet, Peter W. Glynn\nPublished Papers\nMultivariate Distributionally Robust Convex Regression under Absolute Error Loss\nJose H. Blanchet, Peter W. Glynn, Jun Yan,\nZhengqing Zhou\n*\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS), 2019\n[Slides]\n[Poster]\n[Code]\nBatched Multi-armed Bandits Problem\nZijun Gao, Yanjun Han, Zhimei Ren,\nZhengqing Zhou\n*\nConference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n(NeurIPS)(\nOral\n), 2019\n[Slides]\n[Poster]\n[Code]\nFinite-Sample Regret Bound for Distributionally Robust Offline Tabular Reinforcement Learning\nZhengqing Zhou\n, Zhengyuan Zhou, Qinxun Bai, Linhai Qiu, Jose H. Blanchet, Peter W. Glynn\nInternational Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics\n(AISTATS), 2021\nOptimal Communication Rates for Zero-Error Distributed Simulation under Blackboard Communication Protocols\nYanjun Han, Kedar Tatwawadi, Gowtham Kurri,\nZhengqing Zhou\n, Vinod Prabhakaran, Tsachy Weissman\nIEEE Transactions on Information Theory\n(to appear), 2021\n* stands for alphabetical order,\n†\nstands for equal contribution.\nTalks\nDistributionally Robust Martingale Optimal Transport\nAFTLab Doctoral Conference\n, June 2019, Stanford, CA\nDistributionally Robust Convex Regression\nINFORMS Annual Meeting\n, October 2019, Seattle, WA\nDistributionally Robust Offline Reinforcement Learning\nINFORMS Annual Meeting\n, November 2020, Online\nProfessional Activities\nJournal reviewing: Mathematics of Operations Reserach, Advances in Applied Probability, Latin American Journal of Probability and Mathematical Statistics, Journal of the American Statistical Association.\nConference reviewing: NeurIPS 2019 Workshop on Information Theory and Machine Learning, NeurIPS 2020-2022, ICLR 2021-2022, ICML 2021."
