    "homepage_text": "Wenliang Zhong's Homepage\nWenliang Zhong\nProfile\nBiography\nResearch\nPublications\nTeaching\nHonors\nExperience\nWenliang Zhong\nPhD Student in Computer Science\nUniversity of Texas at Arlington\nArlington, TX\nEmail:\nwxz9204@mavs.uta.edu (preferred); wenliang.zhong@uta.edu\n[GitHub]\n[Google Scholar]\n[Curriculum Vitae]\nBiography\nI am a fifth-year PhD student in Computer Science at the University of Texas at Arlington. My PhD advisor is\nProf. Junzhou Huang\n. I received my B.S. in Computer Science and Technology from Jilin University.\nResearch\n- Instruction-Aware Models\n- Computer Vision\n- Multimodal Learning\n- Deep Graph Learning\nSelected Publications\nWenliang Zhong\n, Haiqing Li, Thao M. Dang, Feng Jiang, Hehuan Ma, Yuzhi Guo, Jean Gao, Junzhou Huang, \"Learning from Guidelines: Structured Prompt Optimization for Expert Annotation Tasks\", AAAI 2026\nWenliang Zhong\n, Rob Barton, Weizhi An, Feng Jiang, Hehuan Ma, Yuzhi Guo, Abhishek Dan, Shioulin Sam, Karim Bouyarmane, Junzhou Huang,\n\"Zero-Shot Composed Image Retrieval via Dual-Stream Instruction-Aware Distillation\"\n, ICCV 2025\nWenliang Zhong\n, Weizhi An, Feng Jiang, Hehuan Ma, Yuzhi Guo, and Junzhou Huang,\n\"Compositional Image Retrieval via Instruction-Aware Contrastive Learning\"\n, Preprint\nWenliang Zhong\n, Wenyi Wu, Qi Li, Rob Barton, Boxin Du, Karim Bouyarmane, Shioulin Sam, Ismail Tutar, and Junzhou Huang,\n\"Enhancing Multimodal Large Language Models with Multi-instance Visual Prompt Generator for Visual Representation Enrichment\"\n, SIGIR workshop on Multimodal Representation and Retrieval 2024\nWeizhi An,\nWenliang Zhong\n, Feng Jiang, Hehuan Ma and Junzhou Huang,\n\"Causal Subgraphs and Information Bottlenecks: Redefining OOD Robustness in Graph Neural Networks\"\n, ECCV 2024\nQifeng Zhou,\nWenliang Zhong\n, Yuzhi Guo, Michael Xiao, Hehuan Ma, and Junzhou Huang,\n\"PathM3: A Multimodal Multi-Task Multiple Instance Learning Framework for Whole Slide Image Classification and Captioning\"\n, MICCAI 2024\nWenyi Wu, Qi Li,\nWenliang Zhong\n, Junzhou Huang,\n\"MIVC: Multiple instance visual component for visual-language models\"\n, WACV 2024.\nFeng Jiang, Yuzhi Guo, Hehuan Ma, Saiyang Na,\nWenliang Zhong\n, Yi Han, Tao Wang, and Junzhou Huang,\n\"GTE: a graph learning framework for prediction of T-cell receptors and epitopes binding specificity\"\n, Briefings in Bioinformatics 2024.\nYucheng Shi*, Hehuan Ma*,\nWenliang Zhong*\n, Qiaoyu Tan, Gengchen Mai, Xiang Li, Tianming Liu, Junzhou Huang,\n\"Chatgraph: Interpretable text classification by converting chatgpt knowledge to graphs\"\n, ICDM Workshop 2023\nWenliang Zhong\n, Hehuan Ma, Yu Rong, Yatao Bian, Long-Kai Huang, Yuzhi Guo, Peilin Zhao, Junzhou Huang, \"CoSSL: A Context-based Semi-Supervised Framework for Molecular Property Prediction\", ICML workshop on Computational Biology 2023\nIndustry Experience\nApplied Scientist Intern, Amazon.com;\nSummer 2023, 2024, 2025\nHonors\nOutstanding undergraduate thesis in Jilin University (~ 5%), 2021\nProvincial First Prize in National College Student Mathematical Modeling Contest in China, 2019\nTeaching\nCSE-6367 Computer Vision;\nFall 2024,\nSpring 2023, Fall 2023\nCSE-6319 Game Theory;\nSpring 2024\nCSE-5311 Design and Analysis of Algorithms;\nFall 2022\nCSE-5321 Software Testing;\nSpring 2022\n*Last updated on Aug 2025."
  },
  "serper::Zenglin Xu": {
    "homepage": "https://faculty.fudan.edu.cn/xuzenglin/en/index.htm",
    "emails": [
      "zenglin@gmail.com",
      "zenglinxu@fudan.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zenglin Xu Home--Home\nPersonal Homepage\nQr code\n中文\nZenglin Xu\n教授\nName (English):\nZenglin Xu\nE-Mail:\nzenglin@gmail.com\nDate of Employment:\n2024-05-23\nSchool/Department:\nArtificial Intelligence Innovation and Incubation Institute\nAdministrative Position:\nProfessor\nEducation Level:\n博士研究生\nBusiness Address:\nZhangjiang Campus, Fudan University, Pudong, Shanghai\nContact Information:\nzenglinxu@fudan.edu.cn\nDegree:\n博士学位\nProfessional Title:\n教授\nStatus:\nOthers\nAlma Mater:\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\nDiscipline:\nComputer Software and Theory\nMOBILE Version\nClick:\nThe Last Update Time:\n.\n.\nHome\nEducation and Teaching\nCourse Information\nStudent Information\nScientific Research\nAcademic Achievements\nResearch Projects\nPatent Commercialization\nSocial Service\nAcademic Organizations\nSocial Positions\nOthers\nAwards and Honors\nAdmissions Information\nPhoto Album\nFaculty Blog\nProfile\nZenglin Xu received a Ph.D. degree in computer science and engineering from the Chinese University of Hong Kong. He is currently a full professor at Fudan University, and also affiliated with Shanghai Academy of AI for Science. He has been working at Michigan State University, the Cluster of Excellence at Saarland University and the Max Planck Institute for Informatics, Purdue University, and the University of Electronic Science and Technology of China, and Harbin Institute of Technology Shenzhen. Dr. Xu's research interests include Trustworthy machine learning and AI for Science. He is the recipient of the outstanding student paper honorable mention at AAAI 2015, the best student paper runner up at ACML 2016, the best paper final list of ICONIP 2023, and the 2016 young researcher award from APNNS. He currently serves as an associate editor of Neural Networks. He is currently the vice president for education in International Neural Network Society.\nEducational Experience\n2005.8 --\n               2009.2\n香港中文大学\n计算机科学与工程\n博士\nWork Experience\nNo content\nSocial Affiliations\nNo content\nOther Contact Information:\nPostalAddress : 308 Computer Building\nemail : zenglinxu@fudan.edu.cn\nResearch Focus\nNo content\n220 Handan Rd., Shanghai(200433)  © 2019 FUDAN UNIVERSITY."
  },
