    "homepage_text": "Aodong Li's Homepage\n李傲冬\nAodong Li\nApplied Scientist, AWS AI\nEmail\n:\naodongli6@gmail.com\n[Research Interest]\n[Education]\n[GitHub]\n[Google Scholar]\n[Research]\n[Academic Activities]\n[Myself]\nI'm an Applied Scientist at\nAWS AI\n, where I design and deploy solutions for real-world problems across multiple products, including adaptive modeling and optimization for\nRedshift query scaling prediction\n, code-generation agents (Text-to-SQL/CLI) for\nSageMaker\nand\nAmazon Ads\n.\nI obtained my PhD in Computer Science at University of California, Irvine, advised by\nProf. Stephan Mandt\n.\nProf. Padhraic Smyth\n,\nProf. Maja Waldron\n, and\nProf. Marius Kloft\nalso provided valuable feedback on my research.\n    Before, I got my master degree from New York University, where I worked with\nProf. Rajesh Ranganath\nand\nProf. Yao Wang\n. I got my bachelor degree from Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications, and I also worked closely with\nProf. Dong Wang\nat Tsinghua University.\nHere is my\nCV\n.\nResearch Interest\nMy research interests lie in machine learning and safety, including anomaly detection, changepoint detection, adaptation, etc. I'm also interested in solving machine learning problems from a probabilistic perspective.\nEducation\n2019.9 - 2024.6: PhD in Computer Science, University of California, Irvine, US\n2017.9 - 2019.6: MSCS, New York University, US\n2014.9 - 2017.3: M.E., Bejing University of Posts and Telecommunications, China\n2010.9 - 2014.6: B.E., Bejing University of Posts and Telecommunications, China\nResearch\nAcademic Activities\nAwards\nComputer Science Department’s M.S. Thesis/Research Fellowship, Fall 2018, NYU\nAcademic Services\nTop reviewer for ICML, NeurIPS.\nReviewer for ICML (2021-2024), NeurIPS (2021-2023), ICLR (2022-2023), AISTATS (2021, 2024).\nOthers\nTeaching assistant:\nDeep Generative Models, Fall 2021, Spring 2023, UCI\nIntroduction to Machine Learning, Fall 2019, UCI\nMachine Learning, Spring 2019, NYU\nFoundamental Algorithms, Fall 2018, NYU\nMyself\nMy hobby is\nbasketball\n.\nMy Hometown:\nNanyang\n,\nHenan\n,\nChina\nlast updated: 2025/11/05"
  },
