    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/whalenian",
    "homepage_text": "Zhichao Lu\nAssistant Professor\nCity University of Hong Kong (CityU)\nluzhichaocn [at] gmail [dot] com\nZhichao Lu received Ph.D degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering from\n                                Michigan State University under the supervision of Prof.\nKalyanmoy Deb\n(\nFIEEE, FACM\n),\n                                where he studied bilevel optimization, evolutionary multi-objective optimization,\n                                and neural architecture search.\nIn the broad context of AI, his current research focuses on the intersections of\n                                evolutionary computation, learning, and optimization, notably on developing efficient\n                                and automated ML/DL algorithms and systems, with the overarching goal of making\n                                AI accessible to everyone.\nProspective Students: I am always looking for\nself-motivated\nstudents with strong\n                        mathematical and programming background. Please refer to\nopenings\nfor potential\n                        opportunities.\nRecent News\n06/2023:\nTutorial on\n\"Multi-Objective Optimization for Deep Learning\"\nis accepted to CVPR 2023!\n05/2023:\nOne paper accepted to IEEE ICWS '23!\n03/2023:\nTwo papers accepted to CVPR '23! Congratulations to\nShihua Huang\n,\nChuntao Ding\nand all collaborators!\n09/2021:\nOur HZL team won the\nExcellent Award\n(ranked 6/566) of\n                                Glaucoma grAding from Multi-Modality imAge (GAMMA) Challenge at the\nMICCAI OMIA workshop'21\n!\n08/2021:\nThanks National Natural Science Foundation of China\n                                to fund our surrogate-assisted evolutionary neural architecture search project\n                                (国家自然科学基金青年科学基金项目)!\n07/2021:\nTwo papers accepted to ICCV '21! Congratulations to\nShihua Huang\n,\nTeng Wang\nand all collaborators!\n06/2021:\nOur team is the\nRunner-Up Winner\nof the\n2021 CVPR ActivityNet Event Dense-Captioning Challenge\n.\n                                Congratulations to\nTeng Wang\nand\nZhu Liu\nfor leading the project!\nOral presentation at CVPR\n                                    21 Workshop\n.\n06/2021:\nThanks China Postdoctoral Science Foundation to\n                                fund our evolutionary multi-objective neural architecture search project\n                                (中国博士后科学基金面上资助项目)!\n02/2021:\nOur paper titled \"\nA New\n                                    Many-Objective Evolutionary Algorithm Based on Generalized Pareto Dominance\n\"\n                                is accepted to\nIEEE T-CYB\n! Congratulations to\nShuwei Zhu\nfor leading the paper!\n01/2021:\nOur paper titled \"\nNeural Architecture Transfer\n\"\n                                is accepted to\nIEEE T-PAMI\n!\n09/2020:\nOur paper titled \"\nMultiobjective Evolutionary Design of Deep Convolutional Neural\n                                    Networks for\n                                    Image Classification\n\"\n                                is accepted to\nIEEE T-EVC\n!\n07/2020:\nNSGANetV2\nis accepted as\nOral (top 2%)\nat ECCV '20!\n06/2020:\nNSGA-Net\nis invited to\nIJCAI '20 as an\n                                    extended abstract\n.\n04/2020:\nMUXConv\nis accepted to CVPR '20!\n07/2019:\nNSGA-Net\nwon the\nBest Paper Award\nat\nGECCO '19 (Evolutionary Machine Learning Track)\n.\nExpand\nSelected Research\nRethinking Code Similarity for Automated Algorithm Design with LLMs\nRui Zhang\n,\nZhichao Lu\nICLR\n, 2026\narXiv\n/\ncode\nA new way to distinguish algorithms from the perspective of problem-solving behavior,\n                                    laying the groundwork for automated algorithm design with LLMs.\nDEIM: DETR with Improved Matching for Fast Convergence\nShihua Huang\n,\nZhichao Lu\n,\nXiaodong Cun\n,\nYongjun Yu\n,\nXiao Zhou\n,\nXi Shen\nCVPR\n, 2025\n(Shenzhen AI Open-source\n                                Software Award)\narXiv\n/\nslides\n/\ncode\nIntroduce a dense one-to-one matching strategy,\n                                    by incorporating additional targets via data augmentations,\n                                    to accelerate convergence of Transformers (DETR)\n                                    in real-time object detection.\nEvolution of Heuristics: Towards Efficient Automatic Algorithm\n                                        Design Using Large Language Model\nFei Liu\n,\nXialiang Tong\n,\nMingxuan Yuan\n,\nXi Lin\n,\nFu Luo\n,\nZhenkun Wang\n,\nZhichao Lu\n,\nQingfu Zhang\nICML\n, 2024\n(Oral presentation,\n                                IEEE CIS FLAME Technical Challenge 2024 Runner-up)\narXiv\n/\nslides\n/\ncode\nA new paradigm that combines evolutionary computation and LLMs to search in the space of\n                                    language (e.g., ideas and codes) for automated algorithm design.\nNeural architecture search as multiobjective optimization benchmarks:\n                                        Problem formulation and performance assessment\nZhichao Lu\n,\nRan Cheng\n,\nYaochu Jin\n,\nKay Chen Tan\n,\nKalyanmoy Deb\nIEEE TEVC\n, 2023\narXiv\n/\nslides\n/\ncode\nTransforming Neural Architecture Search (NAS) into multiobjective optimization\n                                    problems. A benchmark suite for testing evolutionary algorithms in deep learning.\nRevisiting Residual Networks for Adversarial Robustness\nShihua Huang\n,\nZhichao Lu\n,\nKalyanmoy Deb\n,\nVishnu N. Boddeti\nCVPR\n, 2023\narXiv\n/\nposter\n/\ncode\nA holistic study on the impact of architectural design on adversarial robustness,\n                                    showing that\narchitecture\ncontributes as much as, if not more than,\n                                    adversarial training to adversarial robustness.\nNeural Architecture Transfer\nZhichao Lu\n,\nGautam Sreekumar\n,\nErik Goodman\n,\nWolfgang Banzhaf\n,\nKalyanmoy Deb\n,\nVishnu N. Boddeti\nIEEE TPAMI\n, 2021\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\ncode\nImprove practical utilities of neural architecture search through\n                                        many-objective optimization, iterative surrogate modeling, and transfer\n                                        learning.\nNSGANetV2: Evolutionary Multi-Objective\n                                            Surrogate-Assisted Neural Architecture Search\nZhichao Lu\n,\nKalyanmoy Deb\n,\nErik Goodman\n,\nWolfgang Banzhaf\n,\nVishnu N. Boddeti\nECCV\n, 2020\n(Oral\n                                            Presentation)\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\ncode\nAn efficient multi-objective neural architecture search framework.\n                                        It can be easily integrated with most of search spaces.\nNSGA-Net: Neural Architecture Search\n                                            using Multi-Objective Genetic Algorithm\nZhichao Lu\n,\nIan Whalen\n,\nVishnu N. Boddeti\n,\nYashesh Dhebar\n,\nKalyanmoy Deb\n,\nErik Goodman\n,\nWolfgang Banzhaf\nGECCO\n, 2019\n(Oral Presentation,\n                                            Best Paper Award)\narXiv\n/\nvideo\n/\ncode\n/\nextended abstract\n                                        (invited by IJCAI '20)\nAn evolutionary multi-objective search algorithm for evolving\n                                        DNN architectures automatically."
  },
  "serper::Zhangyue Yin": {
    "homepage": "https://yinzhangyue.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "yinzhangyue@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/yinzhangyue",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Zhangyue Yin | Fudan University\nZhangyue Yin\n印张悦\nPh.D. Candidate in Computer Science at\nFudan University\nAdvised by\nProf. Xipeng Qiu\n&\nProf. Xuanjing Huang\nEmail\nGoogle Scholar\nSemantic Scholar\nGitHub\nAbout\nI am a final-year Ph.D. candidate in Computer Science at\nFudan University\n(expected June 2026), working with\nProf. Xipeng Qiu\nand\nProf. Xuanjing Huang\nat the\nFudanNLP Group\n.\n      I received my B.S. in Data Science from East China Normal University in 2021.\nMy research focuses on building\nmore reliable and capable reasoning systems\nfor large language models. Key directions include:\n◈ LLM Reasoning\n— uncertainty-aware guidance, cross-model communication, and hierarchical answer aggregation for complex multi-step reasoning.\n◈ Reward Design\n— dynamic, generalizable process reward models with fine-grained multi-dimensional criteria for robust supervision.\n◈ Evaluation\n— adaptive metrics for test-time scaling, error classification frameworks, and self-knowledge assessment of LLMs.\nNews\n2026.01\nStarted internship at\nTencent HY\n, working on reward design.\n2025.09\nInterned at\nOptiver AI\nas an Alpha Researcher (Sep–Nov 2025).\n2025\n2 papers accepted to\nACL 2025\n: DG-PRM and financial bias in LLMs.\n2024.12\nAwarded the\nNational Scholarship\n(国家奖学金).\n2024\nPapers accepted to\nACL, CVPR, EMNLP, LREC-COLING, NAACL, ICML, COLM, AAAI\nin 2024–2025.\nSelected Publications\n* denotes equal contribution. See full list on\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nFirst Author\nDo Large Language Models Know What They Don't Know?\nZhangyue Yin\n, Qiushi Sun, Qipeng Guo, Jiawen Wu, Xipeng Qiu, Xuanjing Huang\nACL 2023\nIntroduced SelfAware, a dataset and automated methodology to evaluate LLMs' ability to recognize unanswerable questions, revealing intrinsic self-knowledge capabilities.\nExchange-of-Thought: Enhancing LLM Capabilities through Cross-Model Communication\nZhangyue Yin\n, Qiushi Sun, Cheng Chang, Qipeng Guo, Junqi Dai, Xuanjing Huang, Xipeng Qiu\nEMNLP 2023\nA novel framework enabling cross-model communication through four paradigms (Memory, Report, Relay, Debate) with confidence evaluation.\nReasoning in Flux: Enhancing LLM Reasoning through Uncertainty-aware Adaptive Guidance\nZhangyue Yin\n, Qiushi Sun, Qipeng Guo, Zhiyuan Zeng, Xiaonan Li, Junqi Dai, Qinyuan Cheng, Xuanjing Huang, Xipeng Qiu\nACL 2024\nIntroduced UAG, a plug-and-play approach that dynamically identifies uncertainty signals and intervenes by retracting to reliable states with certified reasoning clues.\nExplicit Memory Learning with Expectation Maximization\nZhangyue Yin\n, Qiushi Sun, Qipeng Guo, Zhiyuan Zeng, Qinyuan Cheng, Xipeng Qiu, Xuanjing Huang\nEMNLP 2024\nIntroduced EM², a framework treating memory as a latent variable with EM algorithm for explicit memory updates in continual learning.\nDynamic and Generalizable Process Reward Modeling\nZhangyue Yin\n, Qiushi Sun, Zhiyuan Zeng, Qinyuan Cheng, Xipeng Qiu, Xuanjing Huang\nACL 2025\nProposed DG-PRM with reward trees for fine-grained multi-dimensional criteria and Pareto dominance estimation, achieving superior cross-domain generalization.\nAggregation of Reasoning: A Hierarchical Framework for Enhancing Answer Selection in LLMs\nZhangyue Yin\n, Qiushi Sun, Qipeng Guo, Zhiyuan Zeng, Xiaonan Li, et al.\nLREC-COLING 2024\nCo-First Author\nRethinking Label Smoothing on Multi-hop Question Answering\nZhangyue Yin*\n, Yuxin Wang*, Xiannian Hu, Yiguang Wu, et al.\nCCL 2023\n🏆 Best Paper\nError Classification of LLMs on Math Word Problems: A Dynamically Adaptive Framework\nZhangyue Yin*\n, Yuhong Sun*, Xuanjing Huang, Xipeng Qiu, Hui Zhao\nEMNLP 2025\nPixel-level Semantic Correspondence through Layout-aware Representation Learning\nYixuan Sun*,\nZhangyue Yin*\n, Haibo Wang, Yan Wang, Xipeng Qiu, Weifeng Ge, Wenqiang Zhang\nCVPR 2024\nScaling of Search and Learning: A Roadmap to Reproduce o1 from RL Perspective\nZhiyuan Zeng*, Qinyuan Cheng*,\nZhangyue Yin*\n, Bo Wang*, et al.\narXiv 2024\nSelected Co-authored Papers\nCorex: Pushing the Boundaries of Complex Reasoning through Multi-Model Collaboration\nQiushi Sun,\nZhangyue Yin\n, Xiang Li, Zhiyong Wu, Xipeng Qiu, Lingpeng Kong\nCOLM 2024\nRevisiting the Test-Time Scaling of o1-like Models\nZhiyuan Zeng, Qinyuan Cheng,\nZhangyue Yin\n, Yunhua Zhou, Xipeng Qiu\nACL 2025\nContextual Structure Knowledge Transfer for Graph Neural Networks\nZhiyuan Yu, Wenzhong Li,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nAAAI 2025\nCan AI Assistants Know What They Don't Know?\nQinyuan Cheng, Tianxiang Sun, ...,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nICML 2024\nLlatrieval: LLM-Verified Retrieval for Verifiable Generation\nXiaonan Li, Changtai Zhu, Linyang Li,\nZhangyue Yin\n, Tianxiang Sun, Xipeng Qiu\nNAACL 2024\nScienceBoard: Evaluating Multimodal Autonomous Agents in Realistic Scientific Workflows\nQiushi Sun, ...,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nICLR 2025\nVLABench: A Large-Scale Benchmark for Language-Conditioned Robotics Manipulation\nShiduo Zhang, ...,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nICCV 2025\nAre LLMs Rational Investors? Detecting and Reducing Financial Bias in LLMs\nYuhang Zhou, Yuchen Ni, ...,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nACL 2025\nWhat Dense Graph Do You Need for Self-Attention?\nYuxin Wang, Chu-Tak Lee, Qipeng Guo,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nICML 2022\nA Survey of Reasoning with Foundation Models\nJiankai Sun, ...,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nACM Computing Surveys 2025\nThe Rise and Potential of Large Language Model Based Agents: A Survey\nZhiheng Xi, ...,\nZhangyue Yin\n, et al.\nScience China Info. Sci. 2025\nThe Dual-edged Sword: AI's Evolving Role in Academic Peer Review\nXuanjing Huang, Shihan Dou,\nZhangyue Yin\nScience China Info. Sci. 2025\nShow all publications ↓\nExperience\nTencent HY\nResearch Intern — Reward Design\nJan 2026 – Present\nOptiver AI\nResearch Intern — Alpha Factor Mining with LLM Agents & RL\nSep 2025 – Nov 2025\nHonors & Awards\n🏅 National Scholarship\nMinistry of Education, China · Dec 2024\n🏆 Best Paper Award\nCCL 2023 — 22nd China National Conference on Computational Linguistics\n⭐ Outstanding Student\nFudan University · Nov 2022\nEducation\nFudan University\nPh.D. in Computer Science · GPA: 3.82/4.0\nSep 2021 – Jun 2026 (expected)\nEast China Normal University\nB.S. in Data Science\nSep 2017 – Jun 2021"
  },
