    "homepage_text": "Qi Guo's Homepage\nQi Guo 郭琦\nPh.D Student in Computer Science\nDepartment of Internet Architecture\nMax Planck Institute for Informatics\nSaarbrücken, Germany\nEmail\n:\nqiguo@mpi-inf.mpg.de\nGoogle Scholar\n|\nX\n|\nGitHub\n|\nLinkedIn\n|\nBlueSky\nAbout me\n.\n                        I am a Ph.D student in computer science at\nMax Planck Institute for Informatics\n, advised by\nProf. Anja Feldmann\nand\nProf. Balakrishnan Chandrasekaran\n.\nResearch Interests\n.\n                        I am broadly interested in\nsystems\nand\nnetworking\n. Currently, my research focuses on cost-efficient video streaming and partially reliable transport.\nPrior to MPI\n. \n                        I got my B.S. degree in the joint program between\nQueen Mary University of London\nand\nBeijing University of Posts and Telecommunications\nin 2020.\nNews\n[March 2024]\nAlterEgo\nis accepted to\nEdgeSys 2024\n!\n[Sep 2023]\nI will be a teaching assistant for the seminar\nHot Topics in Data Networks\nnext semester.\n[April 2023]\nQSDP\nis accepted to\nICML 2023\n!\n[April 2023]\nI will be a teaching assistant for the core courses\nData Networks\nand\nDistributed Systems\nnext semester.\n[Sep 2022]\nStart my Ph.D. study at\nINET group\n,\nMPI for Informatics\n.\n[April 2022]\nLinkGuardian\nis accepted to\nAPNet 2022\n!\nPublications\nSee my\nGoogle Scholar\nfor the full publication list.\nConference Papers\nAlterEgo: A Dedicated Blockchain Node For Analytics\n.\nQi Guo\n, Mahdi Alizadeh, Ali Falahati, Laurent Bindschaedler.\nInternational Workshop on Edge Systems, Analytics and Networking (EdgeSys) (Co-located with EuroSys)\n, 2024.\nQuantized Distributed Training of Large Models with Convergence Guarantees\n.\nIlia Markov, Adrian Vladu,\nQi Guo\n, Dan Alistarh.\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n, 2023.\nLinkGuardian: Mitigating the impact of packet corruption loss with link-local retransmission\n.\nRaj Joshi,\nQi Guo\n, Nishant Budhdev, Ayush Mishra, Mun Choon Chan, Ben Leong.\nAsia-Pacific Workshop on Networking (APNet)\n, 2022.\nApplication and Experiments of 5G Technology Powered Industrial Internet\n.\nFangmin Xu, Fan Yang, Xinya Wu,\nQi Guo\n, Chenglin Zhao.\nInternational Conference on Communications (ICC) Workshops\n, 2019.\nJournal Papers\nPredicting spatial visualization problems' difficulty level from eye-tracking data\n.\nXiang Li, Rabih Younes, Diana Bairaktarova,\nQi Guo\n.\nSensors\n, 2020.\nTeaching and Supervision\nSaarland University:\nHot Topics in Data Networks\n(2023-24 Winter as teaching assistant, 2024-25 Winter as tutor)\nDistributed Systems\n(2022-23 Summer as teaching assistant)\nData Networks\n(2022-23 Summer as tutor)\nThesis Supervision\nMaster Thesis\n, Topic: Layered Video Streaming, Jaideep More, Saarland University (2025), co-advised with\nDr. Taha Albakour\nand\nDr. Tiago Heinrich\n.\nBachelor Thesis\n, Topic: Video Streaming ABR Evaluation in Mobile Network, Erin Elagöz, Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam (2025), co-advised with\nProf. Balakrishnan Chandrasekaran\n.\nMaster Thesis\n, Topic: Partially Reliable Transport with QUIC Datagram, Punit Lodha, Saarland University (2024-25), co-advised with\nProf. Balakrishnan Chandrasekaran\n.\nMaster Thesis\n, Topic: Web Browsing with Partially Reliable Transport, Aditya N. Srivastava, Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam (2024), co-advised with\nProf. Balakrishnan Chandrasekaran\n.\nExperiences\nEducation:\nPh.D. in Computer Science\n,\nMax Planck Institute for Informatics\nand\nSaarland University\n(Sep 2022 - Present)\nB.S. in Telecommunication Engineering\n,\nQueen Mary University of London\nand\nBeijing University of Posts and Telecommunications\n(Sep 2016 - July 2020)\nAcademic:\nNSDI '26\nArtifacts Evaluation Committee\nIndustrial:\nPhD Intern\n,\nBell Labs\n, Stuttgart, Germany (September 2025- December 2025)\nSoftware Development Engineering Intern\n,\nAmazon\n, Beijing, China (October 2020- July 2021)\nSoftware Development Engineering Intern\n,\nDiDi\n, Beijing, China (October 2019 - May 2020)"
