ppointments\nNeuroscience\nAssociate Research Scientist\nPrimary\nNeuroscience\nOther Departments & Organizations\nAll Institutions\nNeuroscience\nEducation & Training\nPhD\nFudan University (2014)\nResearch\nCopy Link\nResearch at a Glance\nYale Co-Authors\nFrequent collaborators of Shengtao Yang's published research.\nPublications Timeline\nA big-picture view of Shengtao Yang's research output by year.\nDibyadeep Datta\nView Full Profile\nView 7 Common Publications\nMin Wang, PhD\nView Full Profile\nView 7 Common Publications\nAlvaro Duque, PhD\nView Full Profile\nView 6 Common Publications\nAmy Arnsten, PhD\nView Full Profile\nView 6 Common Publications\nElizabeth Woo\nView Full Profile\nView 5 Common Publications\nChristopher van Dyck, MD\nView Full Profile\nView 3 Common Publications\n16\nPublications\n463\nCitations\nPublications\n2025\nKynurenic acid signaling expands in human and nonhuman primates and impairs dorsolateral prefrontal cortical cognition that is key to mental illness\nYang S\n,\nDatta D\n, Krienen F,\nWoo E\n, May A,\nAnderson G\n, Galvin V, Gonzalez-Burgos G, Lewis D, Ling E, McCarroll S,\nArnsten A\n,\nWang M\n.\nKynurenic acid signaling expands in human and nonhuman primates and impairs dorsolateral prefrontal cortical cognition that is key to mental illness\n. Molecular Psychiatry 2025, 1-11.\nPMID: 41413200\n,\nDOI: 10.1038/s41380-025-03425-y\n.\nPeer-Reviewed Original Research\nAltmetric\nConcepts\nHigher cognitive deficits\nCognitive deficits\nPrimate dlPFC\nKAT II\nKynurenic acid\nNeuronal firing\nDorsolateral prefrontal cortex\nAged macaques\nPlasma kynurenine/tryptophan ratio\nSystemic administration of agents\nSystemic administration\nHuman dlPFC\nPrefrontal cortex\nWorking memory\nDlPFC neurons\nAged monkeys\nKynurenic acid production\nCognitive performance\nDLPFC\nCognitive function\nMental illness\nKynurenine/tryptophan ratio\nNonhuman primates\nDeficits\nApplication of kynurenic acid\nDysregulated calcium signaling in the aged pr