    "homepage_text": "Hongming Zhang\nHongming Zhang\nBiography\nHongming Zhang is currently a senior researcher at Tencent AI Lab, Seattle. He leads the research\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ton\nSelf-Evolving LLM Agents\nat Tencent AI Lab. Before that, He\n                                was a research scholar at University of Pennsylvania, working with\nProf. Dan Roth\n. In 2021, He got his\n                                Ph.D. degree from HKUST, supervised by\nProf.\n                                Yangqiu Song\n. Before that, He received his MPhil. degree from the TLE program, HKUST\n                                in 2018 and B.E.degree from the ECE department, HKUST in 2016.\n\n                                Hongming's research interest is primarily on LLM Agents and Self-evolving LLMs.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSpecifically, Hongming aims at building a general purpose LLM agent system that could finish autopilot tasks and learn during deployment.\n\n                                You can find Hongming at hzhangal [AT] cse.ust.hk or learn more about Hongming with\nGoogle\n                                Scholar\n,\nGithub\n, and\nCV\n(Dec, 2022).\nCurrent\n                    Research Focus\nLLM Agents\nSelf-evolving LLM Systems\nAdvanced RAG Systems\nInformation Retrieval\nInformation Extraction\nNews\n01/2025: Two papers are accepted to ICLR 2025. Topics cover MLE agents and code agents.\n09/2024: Five papers are accepted to EMNLP 2024 (and findings). Topics cover theory-of-mind, RAG, and complex reasoning capabilities of LLMs\n05/2024: Five papers are accepted to ACL 2024 (and findings). Topics cover complex reasoning capability of LLMs and agents.\n03/2024: Five papers are accepted to NAACL 2024 (and findings). Topics cover complex reasoning capability of LLMs and fine-grained information retrieval.\n01/2024: Three papers are accepted to EACL 2024 findings.\n12/2023: Our paper on sentence representation has been awarded the outstanding paper of EMNLP 2023.\n10/2023: Five papers are accepted to EMNLP 2023. Topics including Open-world Information Extraction, Sentence Embedding for Information Retrieval, and story-level commonsense reasoning.\n09/2023: Our paper \"Thrust: Adaptively Propels Large Language Models with External Knowledge\" has been accepted to Neurips 2023.\n07/2023: Our paper \"Video State-changing Object Segmentation\" has been accepted to ICCV 2023.\n05/2023: Invited to serve as the reviewer for EMNLP 2023.\n05/2023: Invited to serve as the Area Chair for AACL 2023.\n05/2022: Two papers about event causal relation induction and faithful reasoning with LM are accepted to ACL 2023 main conferences.\n01/2022: Our paper \"Knowledge-in-Context: Towards Knowledgeable Semi-Parametric Language\n                            Models\" has been accepted as ICLR 2023 Spotlight.\n01/2022: Four papers have been accepted by EACL 2023. Topics including event relation\n                            extraction, commonsense reasoning, event argument extraction, and sentence key semantics\n                            identification.\n12/2022: Invited to serve as the PC for IJCAI 2023 and ACL 2023.\n11/2022: Invited to serve as the PC for CVPR 2023.\n10/2022: Seven papers are accepted to EMNLP 2022 (including findings).\n09/2022: Our paper \"Learning Event Extraction From a Few Guideline Examples\" has been\n                            accepted to IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing.\n08/2022: Our paper \"Multilingual Word Sense Disambiguation with Unified Sense\n                            Representation\" has been accepted to COLING 2022.\n08/2022: Invited to serve as the senior PC for AAAI 2023.\n05/2022: One paper about acquiring commonsense causality between daily events has been\n                            accepted to ICML 2022.\n05/2022: Our ASER paper has been accepted to Artificial Intelligence.\n05/2022: Invited to serve as the reviewer for ECCV 2022.\n04/2022: Our zero-shot topic classification system has been accepted as one of the NAACL\n                            2022 Demo paper.\n04/2022: Two papers about reasoning over KGs and explainable QA systems were accepted to\n                            NAACL 2022 Findings.\n04/2022: One paper about pronoun coreference resolution was accepted to LREC 2022.\n02/2022: I am happy to received the HKUST Engineering PhD Research Excellence Finalist\n                            Award.\n02/2022: Two papers about commonsense knowledge and word sense disambiguation are accepted\n                            by ACL 2022.\n01/2022: One paper about applying coreference resolution for better dialogue understanding\n                            is accepted to Pattern Recognition.\n[Selected\n                    Publications]\n[Full\n                    Publications by Year]\nHongming Zhang\n, Xiaoman Pan*, Hongwei Wang, Kaixin Ma, Wenhao Yu, and Dong Yu.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCognitive Kernel: An Open-source Agent System towards Generalist Autopilots. Technical Report. 2024.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE & DATA]\nHongming Zhang\n, Xin Liu, Haojie Pan, Yangqiu Song, and Cane Wing-Ki Leung.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tASER: A Large-scale Eventuality Knowledge Graph. The Web Conference (WWW). 2020.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE & DATA]\n[PPT]\nHongming Zhang\n, Daniel Khashabi, Yangqiu Song, and Dan Roth.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTransOMCS: From Linguistic Graphs to Commonsense Knowledge. International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI). 2020.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE & DATA]\n[PPT]\nHongming Zhang\n, Xinran Zhao, and Yangqiu Song.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWinoWhy: A Deep Diagnosis of Essential Commonsense Knowledge for Answering Winograd Schema Challenge. Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL). 2020.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE & DATA]\n[PPT]\nHongming Zhang\n, Liwei Qiu, Lingling Yi, and Yangqiu Song.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tScalable Multiplex Network Embedding.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tInternational Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI). 2018.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE]\n[PPT]\nJournal Publications\n2022\nHongming Zhang*\n, Xin Liu*, Haojie Pan*, Haowen Ke, Tianqing Fang, Jiefu Ou, Yangqiu Song.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tASER: Towards Large-scale Commonsense Knowledge Acquisition via Higher-order Selectional Preference over Eventualities.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tArtificial Intelligence.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE & DATA]\nXintong Yu,\nHongming Zhang\n, Ruixing Hong, Yangqiu Song, and Changshui Zhang.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCD-PCR: Improving Visual Dialog with Pronoun Coreference Resolution.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPattern Recognition (PR). 2022.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE]\nRuixin Hong,\nHongming Zhang\n, Xintong Yu, and Changshui Zhang.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearning Event Extraction From a Few Guideline Examples.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tIEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing (TASLP). 2022.\n[PAPER]\n[CODE]\nConference Publications\n2025\nLiqiang Jing, Zhehui Huang, Xiaoyang Wang, Wenlin Yao, Wenhao Yu, Kaixin Ma,\nHongming Zhang\n, Xinya\nDu, and Dong Yu. DSBench: How Far Are Data Science Agents from Becoming Data Science Experts? (ICLR 2025)\nSiru Ouyang, Wenhao Yu, Kaixin Ma, Zilin Xiao, Zhihan Zhang, Mengzhao Jia, Jiawei Han,\nHongming Zhang\n,\nand Dong Yu. RepoGraph: Enhancing AI Software Engineering with Repository‑level Code Graph. (ICLR 2025)\n2024\nWenhao Yu,\nHongming Zhang\n, Xiaoman Pan, peixin cao, Kaixin Ma, Jian Li, Hongwei Wang, and Dong Yu. Chain-of-Note: Enhancing Robustness in Retrieval-Augmented Language Models. (EMNLP 2024)\nFengyu Cai, Xinran Zhao, Tong Chen, Sihao Chen,\nHongming Zhang\n, Iryna Gurevych, and Heinz Koeppl. MixGR: Enhancing Retriever Generalization for Scientific Domain through Complementary Granularity. (EMNLP 2024)\nTong Chen, Hongwei Wang, Sihao Chen, Wenhao Yu, Kaixin Ma, Xinran Zhao,\nHongming Zhang\n, and Dong Yu. Dense X Retrieval: What Retrieval Granularity Should We Use? (EMNLP 2024)\nRuixin Hong,\nHongming Zhang\n, Xiaoman Pan, Dong Yu, and Changshui Zhang. Abstraction-of-Thought Makes Language Models Better Reasoners. (Findings of EMNLP 2024)\nChunkit Chan, Cheng Jiayang, Yauwai Yim, Zheye Deng, Wei Fan, Haoran Li, Xin Liu,\nHongming Zhang\n, Weiqi Wang, and Yangqiu Song. NegotiationToM: A Benchmark for Stress-testing Machine Theory of Mind on Negotiation Surrounding. (Findings of EMNLP 2024)\nZhaowei Wang, Wei Fan, Qing Zong,\nHongming Zhang\n, Sehyun Choi, Tianqing Fang, Xin Liu, Yangqiu Song, Ginny Wong, and Simon See. AbsInstruct: Eliciting Abstraction Ability from LLMs through Explanation Tuning with Plausibility Estimation. (ACL 2024)\nYinya Huang, Ruixin Hong,\nHongming Zhang\n, Wei Shao, Zhicheng YANG, Dong Yu, Changshui Zhang, Xiaodan Liang, and Linqi Song.\n CLOMO: Counterfactual Logical Modification with Large Language Models. (ACL 2024)\nHongliang He, Wenlin Yao, Kaixin Ma, Wenhao Yu, Yong Dai,\nHongming Zhang\n, Zhenzhong Lan, and Dong Yu. WebVoyager: Building an End-to-End Web Agent with Large Multimodal Models. (ACL 2024)\nXinran Zhao,\nHongming Zhang\n, Xiaoman Pan, Wenlin Yao, Dong Yu, Tongshuang Wu, and Jianshu Chen. Fact-and-Reflection (FaR) Improves Confidence Calibration of Large Language Models. (Findings of ACL 2024)\nFengyu Cai, Xinran Zhao,\nHongming Zhang\n, Iryna Gurevych, and Heinz Koeppl. GEOHard: Towards Measuring Class-wise Hardness through Modelling Class Semantics. (Findings of ACL 2024)\nRuixin Hong,\nHongming Zhang\n, Xinyu Pang, Dong Yu, and Changshui Zhang. A Closer Look at the Self-Verification Abilities of Large Language Models in Logical Reasoning. (NAACL 2024)\nSihao Chen,\nHongming Zhang\n, Tong Chen, Ben Zhou, Wenhao Yu, Dian Yu, Baolin Peng, Hongwei Wang, Dan Roth, and Dong Yu. Sub-Sentence Encoder: Contrastive Learning of Propositional Semantic Representations. (NAACL 2024)\nHangfeng He,\nHongming Zhang\n, and Dan Roth. SocREval: Large Language Models with the Socratic Method for Reference-free Reasoning Evaluation. (Findings of NAACL 2024)\nTianqing Fang, Zhaowei Wang, Wenxuan Zhou,\nHongming Zhang\n, Yangqiu Song, and