    "homepage_text": "Pilhyeon Lee, Ph.D.\nPilhyeon Lee\n(이필현)\nAssistant Professor at Inha University\nFollow\nGitHub\nGoogle Scholar\nLinkedIn\nEmail\nCV\nBiography\nI am an assistant professor in Dept. of Artificial Intelligence at\nInha University\n. Before joining it, I was a postdoctoral researcher in Dept. of Computer Science at\nYonsei University\n. In the past, I collaborated as a visiting researcher with the video understanding team at\nCLOVA AI Research\n, hosted by Dr.\nTaeoh Kim\n. Also, I was fortunate to visit\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nas a research intern, working with Dr.\nYan Lu\nand Dr.\nJinglu Wang\n. I obtained my PhD in Computer Science at Yonsei University under the supervision of Prof.\nHyeran Byun\n.\nMy research interests include computer vision, multimodal learning, video understanding, label-efficient training, model robustness, and generative models.\nNotice:\nThis homepage will rarely be updated. Please visit our\nMultimodal AI Lab\nfor the latest news and updates.\nNews\n2024.09\nI have recently taken the role of an assistant professor in\nDept. of Artificial Intelligence\nat\nInha University\n!\n2024.07\nOne paper\n[1]\nwas accepted to ECCV 2024. I am working on the camera-ready version and code refactoring. Please stay tuned for the following update!\n2024.04\nI gave an invited talk titled \"Weakly-supervised Learning in Computer Vision\" at Chung-Ang University, hosted by Prof.\nChanho Eom\n.\n2023.12\nBAM-DETR\n[link]\nis now on arXiv! It resolves two core issues each regarding moment formulation and proposal scoring in DETR-based approaches for temporal sentence grounding.\n2023.09\nI am now working as a postdoctoral researcher at Yonsei University.\n2023.08\nI gave a presentation in Doctoral Colloquium at KCCV 2023.\n2023.07\nTwo papers were accepted to ICCV 2023.\n2023.06\nI successfully completed my PhD defense.\n2023.03\nOne paper was accepted to Neurocomputing (IF: 5.779) (JCR Top-30%).\n2023.02\nOne paper was accepted to CVPR 2023.\n2023.01\nOne paper was accepted to BCI 2023 as Oral presentation.\nEducation\nMar. 2018 - Aug. 2023\nYonsei University, South Korea\nPhD in Computer Science\nMar. 2014 - Feb. 2018\nChung-Ang University, South Korea\nBSc in Computer Science & Engineering\nExperiences\nSep. 2024 - Present\nInha University\nAssistant Professor\nSep. 2023 - Aug. 2024\nYonsei University\nPostdoctoral Researcher\nFeb. 2022 - Jan. 2023\nClova AI Research, NAVER Corp.\nVisiting Researcher\nDec. 2019 - Jun. 2020\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nResearch Intern\nSelected Publications\nA full publication list can be found\nhere\n.\nBAM-DETR: Boundary-Aligned Moment Detection Transformer for Temporal Sentence Grounding in Videos\nPilhyeon Lee\n†, Hyeran Byun († Corresponding author)\nEuropean Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nECCV\n), 2024\n(Acceptance rate: 2395 / 8585 ≈ 27.9%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nAesPA-Net: Aesthetic Pattern-Aware Style Transfer Networks\nKibeom Hong, Seogkyu Jeon, Junsoo Lee, Namhyuk Ahn, Kunhee Kim,\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Daesik Kim, Youngjung Uh, Hyeran Byun\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n), 2023\n(Acceptance rate: 2160 / 8068 ≈ 26.8%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nImproving Diversity in Zero-Shot GAN Adaptation with Semantic Variations\nSeogkyu Jeon, Bei Liu,\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Kibeom Hong, Jianlong Fu, Hyeran Byun\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n), 2023\n(Acceptance rate: 2160 / 8068 ≈ 26.8%)\n[Paper]\nDecomposed Cross-modal Distillation for RGB-based Temporal Action Detection\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Taeoh Kim, Minho Shim, Dongyoon Wee, Hyeran Byun\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n), 2023\n(Acceptance rate: 2360 / 9155 ≈ 25.8%)\n[Paper]\n[Poster]\n[Slides]\nFair Contrastive Learning for Facial Attribute Classification\nSungho Park, Jewook Lee,\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Sunhee Hwang, Dohyung Kim, Hyeran Byun\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\n(\nCVPR\n), 2022\n(Acceptance rate: 2067 / 8161 ≈ 25.3%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nExploiting Shape Cues for Weakly Supervised Semantic Segmentation\nSungpil Kho*,\nPilhyeon Lee\n*, Wonyoung Lee, Minsong Ki, Hyeran Byun (* Equal contributions)\nPattern Recognition\n(\nPR\n), 2022\nJCR Top-10%\n(Impact Factor: 8.0)\n[Paper]\nLearning Action Completeness from Points for Weakly-supervised Temporal Action Localization\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Hyeran Byun\nIEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision\n(\nICCV\n), 2021\nOral Presentation\n(Acceptance rate: 210 / 6236 ≈ 3.3%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\n[Slides]\nFeature Stylization and Domain-aware Contrastive Learning for Domain Generalization\nSeogkyu Jeon, Kibeom Hong,\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Jewook Lee, Hyeran Byun\nThe 29th ACM International Conference on Multimedia\n(\nMM\n), 2021\nOral Presentation\n(Acceptance rate: 179 / 1942 ≈ 9.2%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\nWeakly-supervised Temporal Action Localization by Uncertainty Modeling\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Jinglu Wang, Yan Lu, Hyeran Byun\nThe 35th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nAAAI\n), 2021\n(Acceptance rate: 1692 / 7911 ≈ 21.4%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]\nBackground Suppression Network for Weakly-supervised Temporal Action Localization\nPilhyeon Lee\n, Youngjung Uh, Hyeran Byun\nThe 34th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence\n(\nAAAI\n), 2020\nSpotlight Presentation\n(Acceptance rate: 1591 / 7737 ≈ 20.6%)\n[Paper]\n[Code]\n[Poster]"
