    "homepage_text": "ï»¿\nHanzi Wang\nChinese Version\nMy E-mail Address:\nWang.Hanzi@gmail.com\nHanzi.Wang@xmu.edu.cn\nVacancies\n:\nWe have several vancant positions at the level of Associate/Assistant professorship at\nthe Center for PAMI, XMU\n. We also recruit Postdocs and international PhD students to join in our group. For those who are interested in our research, please send your CV to Wang.Hanzi@gmail.com.\nAbout Me (\nChinese Version\n):\nHanzi Wang is currently a\nDistinguished Professor of \"Minjiang Scholars\"\nin Fujian province and a\nFounding Director\nof the\nCenter for Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(CPAMI) at XMU. He is also the\nDeputy Director\nof the\nFujian Key Laboratory of Sensing and Computing for Smart City\nin Fujian province. He was an Adjunct Professor (2010-2012) and a Senior Research Fellow (2008-2010) at\nthe University of Adelaide\n, Australia; an Assistant Research Scientist (2007-2008) and a Postdoctoral Fellow (2006-2007) at\nthe Johns Hopkins University\n; and a Research Fellow at\nMonash University\n, Australia (2004-2006). He received his Ph.D degree in Computer Vision from Monash University where he was awarded the\nDouglas Lampard Electrical Engineering Research Prize and Medal\nfor the best PhD thesis. His students have been awarded three best PhD theses in Fujian Province and won one best PhD thesis award in the China Society of Image and Graphics. His research interests are concentrated on computer vision and pattern recognition including visual tracking, object detection, action recognition, video segmentation, robust statistics, model fitting, classification and clustering, 3D structure from motion, image analysis and related fields. He has published more than 100 papers in top-level journals (such as IEEE TPAMI(7), IJCV(7), IEEE TIP, IEEE TCYB, IEEE TCSVT, IEEE TMM, etc.) and conferences (such as ICCV, CVPR, ECCV, AAAI, ACM MM, etc.)\nHe is a senior member of the IEEE. He was an Associate Editor for\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology\n(from 2010-2015) and he was a Guest Editor of\nPattern Recognition Letters\n(September 2009). He is the General Chair for\nIEEE Conference of Future Media Technology 2018\nand\nACM ICIMCS2014\n, Program Chair for\nCVRS2012\n, Area Chair for PRCV2020, PRCV2019,\nICPR2018\n,\nACCV2016\nand\nDICTA2010\n, Tutorial Chair for\nVALSE2017\n, Publicity Chair for\nICIG2015\nand\nIEEE NAS2012\n. He has also served on the program committee\n(\nPC) of\nICCV,\nECCV, CVPR, IJCAI, SIGGRAPH, AAAI, etc, and he has served on the reviewer panel for more than 40 jounrals and conferences.\nRECENT NEWS\n:\n2024-Jul\n: One paper accepted by\nIJCV\n. Congratulations to Qiang Qi!\n2024-Jul\n: Three paper accepted by\nACM MM\n. Congratulations to Xiying, Wenyu, Guangyao!\n2024-Mar\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TCSVT\n. Congratulations to Xiao Wang!\n2024-Feb\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TIP\nand one paper accepted by\nIEEE TMM\n. Congratulations to Yuanling!\n2024-Jan\n: One paper accepted by\nIJCV\n. Congratulations to Shuyuan!\n2023-Dec\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TIP\n. Congratulations to Xiao Wang!\n2023-Dec\n: One\nBest Master Thesis award in Fujian Province\n. Congratulations to Rongyun!\n2023-Dec\n: Two papers accepted by\nAAAI\n. Congratulations to Chenlin and Ziqiang!\n2023-Nov\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TNNLS\n. Congratulations to Runqing!\n2023-Jul\n: Winning the\nSecond Prize of National Teaching Achievement Award\n!\n2023-Jul\n: One paper accepted by\nICCV\n. Congratulations to Yiliang!\n2023-Jun\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TMM\n. Congratulations to  Qiang Qi!\n2023-May\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TIP\n. Congratulations to  Qiang Qi!\n2023-May\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TCSVT\n. Congratulations to Wenxin!\n2023-Mar\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TCSVT\n. Congratulations to Xiao Wang!\n2023-Mar\n: One paper accepted by\nIJCV\n. Congratulations to Shuying!\n2023-Feb\n: Two papers accepted by\nCVPR\n. Congratulations to Jinyan and Yukang!\n2023-Jan\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TCSVT\n. Congratulations to  Qiang Qi!\n2023-Jan\n: Winning the\nFirst Prize of Fujian Provincial Science and Technology Progress Award\n!\n2022-Dec\n: Winning the\nFirst Prize of Outstanding Academic Paper in Natural Science of Fujian Province\n!\n2022-Nov\n: Winning one\nBest PhD thesis award\nand one\nBest Master thesis award in Fujian Province\n. Congratulations to Shuyuan and Delian!\n2022-Nov\n: One paper accepted by\nAAAI\n. Congratulations to Yukang!\n2022-Oct\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TIP\n. Congratulations to Shuyuan!\n2022-Jul\n: One paper accepted by\nPR\n. Congratulations to Rongyun!\n2022-Jul\n: One paper accepted by\nECCV\n. Congratulations to Xinyi!\n2022-Jun\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TNNLS\n. Congratulations to Runqing!\n2022-May\n: One paper accepted by\nIEEE TCYB\n. Congratulations to Youze!\n2022-Apr\n: One paper accepted by\nIJCAI\n. Congratulations to Xinyi!\nArchived ...\nVideo Demos:\nWe propose a novel CNN based correlation filter tracker with shepherded instance-aware proposals to automatically estimates the\ntarget scale in each frame and re-detects the target when distortion happens.(See our\nACM MM'18\npaper)\nResearch Interests:\nEffective Appearance Model and Similarity Measure for Tracking\nTracking and Segmenting Objects with Occlusions\nProbabilistic Multiple Cue Fusion\nBackground Initialization and Modeling\nFace Detection and Recognition\nObject Detection in Images and Videos\nRobust Parametric Model Estimation and Its Application to Computer Vision\nRobust Optical Flow Calculation and Motion Estimation\nImage Segmentation (Range Image Segmentation and Color Image Segmentation)\nRobust Fundamental Matrix Estimation\nFeature Detection, Matching, and Tracking\nMotion Estimation\nScene Graph Generation and Image Caption, etc.\nGroup Members: (\nPhoto2023\nï¼\nPhoto2019\nï¼\nPhoto2017\nï¼\nPhoto2014\n)\nOur group\nincludes a Professor (Dr.\nYan Yan\n) and an Assistant Professor  (Dr.\nYang Lu\n) , 1 research assistant, 1 postdoctor, 6 PhD students and more than 30 Master students. We welcome excellent young researchers and postdoctors, PhD and master students, who are interested in Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, to join in our group at XMU.\nSelected Papers\n(\nCopyright             Statement\n)\nâ\nQ. Qi, Z. Qiu, Y. Yan, Y. Lu,\nH. Wang\nIMC-Det: Intra-Inter Modality Contrastive Learning for Video Object Detection\n.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n),\n2024 (accepted)\n.\n(pdf)\nâ\nS. Lin, F. Huang, T. Lai, J. Lai,\nH. Wang\n, J. Weng\n.\nRobust Heterogeneous Model Fitting for Multi-source Image Correspondences\n.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), pages 1-26, 2024 (accepted)\n.\n(pdf)\nâ\nY. Yan, Y. Shu, S. Chen, J. Xue, C. Shen,\nH. Wang\nSPL-Net: Spatial-Semantic Patch Learning Network for Facial Attribute Recognition with Limited Labeled Data\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), Vol 131, No. 8, pages 2097-2121, 2023.\n(pdf)\nâ\nD. Ruan, R. Mo, Y. Yan, S. Chen, J. Xue,\nH. Wang\nAdaptive Deep Disturbance-Disentangled Learning for Facial Expression Recognition\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n),\nVol 130, No. 2, pages 455-477, 2022\n.\n(pdf)\nâ G. Xiao,\nH. Wang\n, J. Ma, D. Suter.\nSegmentation by Continuous Latent Semantic Analysis for Multi-structure Model Fitting.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), Vol 129, No. 7, pages 2034-2056, 2021.\n(pdf)\nâ\nH. Wang\n, G. Xiao, Y. Yan, and D. Suter\nSearching for Representative Modes on Hypergraphs for Robust Geometric Model Fitting\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nPAMI\n), Vol 41, No. 3, pages 697-711, 2019.\n(pdf)\n(Early version appeared in ICCV'15)\nâ G. Xiao,\nH. Wang\n, Y. Yan, and D. Suter\nSuperpixel-guided Two-view Deterministic Geometric Model Fitting\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), Vol 127, No. 4, pages 323-339, 2019.\n(pdf)\n(Early version appeared in ECCV'16)\nâ X. Li, A. Dick, C. Shen, A. van den Hengel,and\nH. Wang\nIncremental Learning of 3D-DCT Compact Representations for Robust Visual Tracking\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nPAMI\n), Vol 35, No. 64, pages 863 - 881, Apr. 2013.\nâ\nH. Wang\n, T.-J. Chin, and D. Suter\nSimultaneously Fitting and Segmenting Multiple-Structure Data with Outliers\nIEEE Transactions Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(PAMI)\n, Vol 34, No. 6, pages 1177 - 1192, June 2012.\n(pdf)\n(Partial data and ground truth are available:\nhere\n)\nâ C. Shen, P. Wang, F. Shen and\nH. Wang\nUBoost: Boosting with the Universum\nIEEE Transactions Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n(PAMI)\n, Vol 34, No. 4, pages 825 - 832, June 2012.\n(pdf)\nâ\nH. Wang,\nD. Mirota and G. Hager\nA Generalized Kernel Consensus Based Robust Estimator.\nIEEE Transactions Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nPAMI\n), Vol 32, No. 1, pages 178-184, 2010.\n(pdf)\nâ K. Schindler, D. Suter and\nH. Wang\nA Model-selection Framework for Multibody Structure-and-Motion of Image\nSequences.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), Vol 79, No. 2, pages 159-177, 2008.\n(pdf)\nâ\nH. Wang,\nD. Suter, K. Schindler and C. Shen\nAdaptive Object Tracking Based on an Effective Appearance Filter.\nIEEE Transactions Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nPAMI\n), Vol 29, No. 9, pages 1661-1667, 2007.\n[Featured article from the September issue 2007]\n(pdf)\n(Early version appeared in ECCV'06)\nâ\nH. Wang\nand D. Suter\nRobust Adaptive-Scale Parametric Model Estimation for Computer Vision.\nIEEE Transactions Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence (\nPAMI\n), Vol. 26, No.11, pages 1459-1474, 2004.\n(pdf)\n,\n(abstract)\nâ\nH. Wang\nand D. Suter\nMDPE: A Very Robust Estimator for Model Fitting and Range Image Segmentation.\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision (\nIJCV\n), Vol. 59, No.2, pages 139-166, 2004.\n(pdf)\n,\n(abstract)\nAcademic Journal Papers:\nS Lin, A Yang, T Lai, J Weng,\nH Wang\nMulti-Motion Segmentation via Co-Attention-Induced Heterogeneous Model Fitting\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems for Video Technology (\nIEEE TCSVT\n), Vol 34, No 3, Pages 1786-1798, 2024.\nX Fan, Y Zhang, Y Lu,\nH Wang\nPARFormer: Transformer-Based Mult...[truncated]"
