    "homepage_text": "About me - Homepage\nDeyu Bo / 薄德瑜\nPostdoc @ NUS\ndeyu.bo [AT] nus.edu.sg\nFollow\nSingapore\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nI am currently a research fellow at National University of Singapore (NUS), collaborating with Prof.\nXinchao Wang\n. I obtained my doctoral degree in the School of Computer, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications (BUPT), supervised by Prof.\nChuan Shi\n. I also collaborated with Prof.\nXiao Wang\nat Beihang University. Before that, I got my B.E. in the School of Information and Telecommunication Engineering at BUPT.\nI am interested in graph machine learning, especially spectral graph neural networks and graph signal processing.\nResearch Highlights (\nMore\n)\nUnified Dataset Distillation:\nUniDD (ICLR 2026)\nSpectral Graph Distillation:\nGDEM (ICML 2024)\nScalable Positional Encoding:\nEigenMLP (NeurIPS 2023)\nSet-to-Set Graph Filter:\nSpecformer (ICLR 2023)\nAdaptive Graph Filter:\nFAGCN (AAAI 2021)\nDeep Graph Clustering:\nSDCN (WWW 2020)\nExperience\nVisiting student (2022.12-2023.6), Singapore Management University\nSupervisor: Yuan Fang\nRemote visiting student (2021.12 - 2022.12), University of British Columbia\nSupervisors: Renjie Liao & Lele Wang\nResearch intern (2020.12 - 2021.06), Ant Financial Service\nMentor: Binbin Hu\nResearch intern (2019.02 - 2019.08), Tencent Inc.\nMentor: Emiao Lu\nAcademic Service\nHonor\n: NeurIPS 2024 Top Reviewer\nJournal Reviewer\n: IEEE TPAMI  /  TSP  /  TIP  /  TKDE  /\nConference Reviewer\n: NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, KDD, WWW"
