    "homepage_text": "Namkyeong  Lee\nNamkyeong\nLee\nSenior Machine Learning Scientist @ Genentech\n''Hi, my name is Louis, fifth year Bichon Frise! I'm the first dog of AFGRL.''\nHi, I’m Namkyeong Lee. I am Senior Machine Learning Scientist at Genentech, dedicated to developing Foundation Models for biology and drug discovery.\nBefore joining Genentech, I earned my Ph.D. from the Industrial and Systems Engineering Department at KAIST, advised by\nProf. Chanyoung Park\nat the\nData Science and Artificial Intelligence Lab (DSAIL)\n. \nMy doctoral research, deeply rooted in the collaboration with the Korea Research Institute of Chemical Technology (KRICT), focused on bridging the gap between AI and molecular science.\nMy research topics of interest include, but are not limited to, the following:\nFoundation Models for scientific discovery\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) for scientific discovery\nLLM Agent Systems for scientific discovery\nNews\nFeb 20, 2026\nI have officially completed my doctoral studies at KAIST! Beyond the completion of my degree, my dissertation “Understanding Science through the Lens of AI” was recognized with the\nKAIST Presidential Best Ph.D. Thesis Award\n.\nFeb 11, 2026\nI gave a research talk at\nUNIST IE\nopen seminar titled ‘Artificial Intelligence for Molecular Science’\nJan 26, 2026\nA paper got accepted at\nICLR 2026\n.\nNov 7, 2025\nA paper got accepted at\nAAAI 2026\n.\nOct 27, 2025\nI gave a research talk at\nUNIST AIGS\nopen seminar titled ‘Artificial Intelligence for Molecular Science’\nYou can even add a little note about which of these is the best way to reach you."
  },
