    "homepage_text": "Pinhao Song — Robotics\nPinhao Song\nMechanical Engineering - Division PMA\nCelestijnenlaan 300\n- box\n2420\n3001 Leuven\nBelgium\nroom:\n02.19\ncontact\nPublications\nquery=user:U0161364 year:[2006 TO 2026] &institution=lirias&from=1&step=20&sort=scdate\nshowing 1 to 17 of 17\nSort\nnewest first\n|\nauthor\n|\ntitle\n|\npopularity\nType\nall\n|\narticles\n|\npresentations\n|\nconferences\n|\nchapters\n|\nother\n|\nreports\n|\nphd theses\n|\nbook reviews\n|\nbooks\n|\noutreach\n|\nedited books\n|\ninvited lectures\njournal-article\nHu, Yutong;Song, Pinhao;Wen, Kehan;Detry, Renaud;\n2026.\nMini Diffuser: Fast Multi-task Diffusion Policy Training Using Two-level Mini-batches.\nIEEE Robotics and Automation Letters; 2026; Vol. 11; iss. 1; pp. 938 - 945\nkeyboard_arrow_down\nLIRIAS4280342\ndescription\nWe present a method that reduces, by an order of magnitude, the time and memory needed to train multi-task vision-language robotic diffusion policies. This improvement arises from a previously underexploreddistinction between action diffusion and the image diffusion techniques that inspired it: In image generation, the target is high-dimensional. By contrast, in action generation, the dimensionality of the target is comparatively small, and only the image condition is high-dimensional. Our approach, Mini Diffuser, exploits this asymmetry by introducing two-level minibatching, which pairs multiple noised action samples with each vision-language condition, instead of the conventional one-to-one sampling strategy. To support this batching scheme, we introduce architectural adaptations to the diffusion transformer that prevent information leakage across samples while maintaining full conditioning access. In RLBench simulations, Mini-Diffuser achieves 95% of the performance of state-of-the-art multi-task diffusion policies, while using only 5% of the training time and 7% of the memory. Real-world experiments further validate that Mini-Diffuser preserves the key strengths of diffusion-based policies, including the ability to model multimodal action distributions and produce behavior conditioned on diverse perceptual inputs.\nPublisher: Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers\nPublished\npresentation\nSong, Pinhao;Li, Pengteng;Detry, Renaud;\n2025.\nGrasp Planning: Combining Dense Prediction and Sampling-based Methods.\nLIRIAS4218432\ndescription\nAccepted\njournal-article\nDai, Linhui;Liu, Hong;Song, Pinhao;Tang, Hao;Ding, Runwei;Li, Shengquan;\n2024.\nEdge-guided representation learning for underwater object detection.\nCAAI Transactions on Intelligence Technology; 2024; Vol. 9; iss. 5; pp. 1078 - 1091\nLIRIAS4155353\ndescription\nPublisher: Wiley\nPublished\nconference\nSong, Pinhao;Li, Pengteng;Detry, Renaud;\n2024.\nImplicit Grasp Diffusion: Bridging the Gap between Dense Prediction and Sampling-based Grasping.\nProceedings of Machine Learning Research; 2024; Vol. 270; pp. 2948 - 2964\nPublisher: JMLR\nkeyboard_arrow_down\nLIRIAS4187789\ndescription\nThere are two dominant approaches in modern robot grasp planning: dense prediction and sampling-based methods. Dense prediction calculates viable grasps across the robot’s view but is limited to predicting one grasp per voxel. Sampling-based methods, on the other hand, encode multi-modal grasp distributions, allowing for different grasp approaches at a point. However, these methods rely on a global latent representation, which struggles to represent the entire field of view, resulting in coarse grasps. To address this, we introduce \\emph{Implicit Grasp Diffusion} (IGD), which combines the strengths of both methods by using implicit neural representations to extract detailed local features and sampling grasps from diffusion models conditioned on these features. Evaluations on clutter removal tasks in both simulated and real-world environments show that IGD delivers high accuracy, noise resilience, and multi-modal grasp pose capabilities.\nPublished online\njournal-article\nKong, Bin;Qian, Jing;Song, Pinhao;Yang, Jing;Hussain, Amir;\n2024.\nUnderwater image clarifying based on human visual colour constancy using double-opponency.\nCAAI Transactions on Intelligence Technology; 2024; Vol. 9; iss. 3; pp. 632 - 648\nLIRIAS4098016\ndescription\nPublisher: Wiley\nPublished\njournal-article\nDai, Linhui;Liu, Hong;Song, Pinhao;Liu, Mengyuan;\n2024.\nA gated cross-domain collaborative network for underwater object detection.\nPattern Recognition; 2024; Vol. 149\nLIRIAS4142808\ndescription\nPublisher: Elsevier\nPublished\njournal-article\nChen, Yang;Liu, Hong;Song, Pinhao;Li, Wenhao;\n2024.\nNeural ordinary differential equation for irregular human motion prediction.\nPattern Recognition Letters; 2024; Vol. 178; pp. 76 - 83\nLIRIAS4145166\ndescription\nPublisher: Elsevier\nPublished\nconference\nLi, Pengteng;He, Ying;Yu, F Richard;Song, Pinhao;Zhou, Xingchen;Zhou, Guang;\n2024.\nOTOcc: Optimal Transport for Occupancy Prediction.\nPROCEEDINGS OF THE THIRTY-THIRD INTERNATIONAL JOINT CONFERENCE ON ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, IJCAI 2024; 2024; pp. 1010 - 1019\nPublisher: IJCAI-INT JOINT CONF ARTIF INTELL\nLIRIAS4223712\ndescription\nPublished\nconference\nSong, Pinhao;Li, Pengteng;Aertbeliën, Erwin;Detry, Renaud;\n2024.\nRobot Trajectron: Trajectory Prediction-based Shared Control for Robot Manipulation.\nProceedings of IEEE International Conference on Robotics and Automation; 2024; pp. 5585 - 5591\nPublisher: Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers\nLIRIAS4142451\ndescription\nPublished online\nconference\nLi, Pengteng;He, Ying;Yu, F Richard;Song, Pinhao;Yin, Dongfu;Zhou, Guang;\n2023.\nIGG: Improved Graph Generation for Domain Adaptive Object Detection.\nProceedings of the 31st ACM International Conference on Multimedia; 2023; pp. 1314 - 1324\nPublisher: Association for Computing Machinery\nLIRIAS4127825\ndescription\nPublished online\njournal-article\nDai, Linhui;Liu, Hong;Tang, Hao;Wu, Zhiwei;Song, Pinhao;\n2023.\nAO2-DETR: Arbitrary-Oriented Object Detection Transformer.\nIeee Transactions On Circuits And Systems For Video Technology; 2023; Vol. 33; iss. 5; pp. 2342 - 2356\nLIRIAS4088289\ndescription\nPublisher: Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers\nPublished\njournal-article\nSong, Pinhao;Li, Pengteng;Dai, Linhui;Wang, Tao;Chen, Zhan;\n2023.\nBoosting R-CNN: Reweighting R-CNN samples by RPN?s error for underwater object detection.\nNeurocomputing; 2023; Vol. 530; pp. 150 - 164\nLIRIAS4081821\ndescription\nPublisher: Elsevier\nPublished\njournal-article\nChen, Yang;Song, Pinhao;Liu, Hong;Dai, Linhui;Zhang, Xiaochuan;Ding, Runwei;Li, Shengquan;\n2023.\nAchieving domain generalization for underwater object detection by domain mixup and contrastive learning.\nNeurocomputing; 2023; Vol. 528; pp. 20 - 34\nLIRIAS4070321\ndescription\nPublisher: Elsevier\nPublished\nconference\nLi, Pengteng;He, Ying;Yin, Dongfu;Yu, F Richard;Song, Pinhao;\n2023.\nBagging R-CNN: Ensemble for Object Detection in Complex Traffic Scenes.\nICASSP 2023 - 2023 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP); 2023\nPublisher: IEEE\nLIRIAS4082851\ndescription\nPublished online\nconference\nXvtao, Liang;Song, Pinhao;\n2022.\nExcavating RoI Attention for Underwater Object Detection.\n2022 IEEE International Conference on Image Processing (ICIP); 2022; pp. 2651 - 2655\nPublisher: IEEE\nLIRIAS4084108\ndescription\nPublished\nconference\nWang, Tao;Liu, Hong;Song, Pinhao;Guo, Tianyu;Shi, Wei;\n2022.\nPose-Guided Feature Disentangling for Occluded Person Re-identification Based on Transformer.\nTHIRTY-SIXTH AAAI CONFERENCE ON ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE / THIRTY-FOURTH CONFERENCE ON INNOVATIVE APPLICATIONS OF ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE / THE TWELVETH SYMPOSIUM ON EDUCATIONAL ADVANCES IN ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE; 2022; pp. 2540 - 2549\nPublisher: AAAI Press\nLIRIAS4070322\ndescription\nPublished\nconference\nLiu, Hong;Song, Pinhao;Ding, Runwei;\n2020.\nTOWARDS DOMAIN GENERALIZATION IN UNDERWATER OBJECT DETECTION.\n2020 IEEE INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON IMAGE PROCESSING (ICIP); 2020; pp. 1971 - 1975\nPublisher: IEEE\nLIRIAS4070323\ndescription\nPublished\nkeyboard_arrow_up\nTo homepage kuleuven.be"
  },
