  "serper::Zhaowei Wang": {
    "homepage": "https://zhaowei-wang-nlp.github.io/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": "https://github.com/Elvin-Yiming-Du",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/zhaowei-wang-571943221",
    "homepage_text": "Zhaowei (James) Wang\nZhaowei (James) Wang\nE-mail:\nzwanggy # cse dot ust dot hk\nI am currently a research intern with the Seed VLM team at ByteDance. Previously, I was a visiting scholar at\nEdinburghNLP\n, working with\nMark Steedman\n. I am pursuing my PhD in\nthe Department of Computer Science and Engineering (CSE)\nat HKUST as a recipient of\nthe Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS)\n, supervised by\nYangqiu Song\n. I received my MPhil degree from the Department of CSE at HKUST in August 2023.\nMy current research interests mainly focus on the long-context ability of MLLMs, as well as on the long-term memory of MLLMs, which is a highly relevant application of long-context understanding. Prior to the advent of LLMs, I worked on event understanding, such as discourse relation and event abstraction.\nI am always open to new collaborations. Please feel free to reach out via email.\nResearch Highlights by Topic\nMultimodal Long Context\narXiv\nRethinking Memory in AI: Taxonomy, Operations, Topics, and Future Directions\nYiming Du, Wenyu Huang, Danna Zheng,\nZhaowei Wang\n, Sebastien Montella, Mirella Lapata, Kam-Fai Wong, and Jeff Z. Pan\narXiv\nCode\nNeurIPS\nMMLongBench: Benchmarking Long-Context Vision-Language Models Effectively and Thoroughly\n(*spotlight)\nZhaowei Wang\n, Wenhao Yu, Xiyu Ren, Jipeng Zhang, Yu Zhao, Rohit Saxena, Liang Cheng, Ginny Wong, Simon See, Pasquale Minervini, Yangqiu Song, and Mark Steedman\nIn The 39th (2025) Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\narXiv\nCode\nWebsite\nAbstraction Knowledge\nACL\nAbsInstruct: Eliciting Abstraction Ability from LLMs through Explanation Tuning with Plausibility Estimation\nZhaowei Wang\n, Wei Fan, Qing Zong, Hongming Zhang, Sehyun Choi, Tianqing Fang, Xin Liu, Yangqiu Song, Ginny Y. Wong, and Simon See\nIn The 62nd (2024) Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics\narXiv\nCode\nNews\nSep 19, 2025\nMMLongBench is accepted as a\nspotlight\nat NeurIPS 2025!!!\nSep 19, 2025\nTwo papers are accepted at NeurIPS 2025!\nAug 20, 2025\nThree papers accepted at EMNLP 2025.\nJun 9, 2025\nThe workshop version of our MMLongBench has been accepted by the LCFM Workshop at ICML 2025.\nMay 20, 2025\nOur new paper about Multimodal Long Context is now available: MMLongBench: Benchmarking Long-Context Vision-Language Models Effectively and Thoroughly.\nMay 16, 2025\nOur new paper about LLM memory is now available: Rethinking Memory in AI: Taxonomy, Operations, Topics, and Future Directions.\nMay 15, 2025\nTwo papers on entailment and factual knowledge have been accepted by ACL2025.\nDec 1, 2024\nOne paper on entailment has been accepted by NAACL2025.\nSelected Awards\nMajor Awards:\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship    2023\nNational Scholarship (top 2%)    2018-2019\nNational Scholarship (top 2%)    2017-2018\nNational Scholarship (top 2%)    2016-2017\nOther Awards:\nHKUST RedBird Academic Excellence Award for Continuing PhD Students    2025\nHKUST Overseas Research Award    2025\nHKUST RedBird PhD Award    2023-2024\nMerit Student in Heilongjiang Province (top 2.5%)    2017-2018\nService\nArea Chair:\nACL ARR 2024 (all rounds); ACL ARR 2025 Feb, May, July\nConference Reviewer:\nNeurIPS 2024, 2025; ICLR 2025, 2026; ICML 2025; ICCV 2025; ACL 2023, 2024; EMNLP 2022, 2023; NAACL 2024; KDD 2023; SIGIR 2025; CIKM 2023; AAAI 2024; ACL ARR 2023 (all rounds); ACL ARR 2024 Feb, Apr; ACL ARR 2025 May; COLM 2024, 2025; EACL 2023, 2024; COLING 2022, 2025; LREC-COLING 2024; SDM 2023; AACL 2022, 2023; AKBC 2022; WiNLP@EMNLP 2024\nExternal Journal Reviewer:\nJAIR 2023 Apr"
  },
