    "homepage_text": "Zhenhailong Wang\nZhenhailong Wang\nPh.D. in CS at UIUC\nFollow\nChampaign, Illinois\nEmail\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nGithub\nGoogle Scholar\nHi there! I’m\nZhenhailong Wang\n(王镇海龙). I am a final year Ph.D. in Computer Science at\nUniversity of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)\nadvised by Prof.\nHeng Ji\n. Expected graduation in May 2026. Before that, I got my M.S. in Computer Science and Civil Engineering from\nUIUC\nand B.S. from\nZhejiang University\n. I am a recipient of the 2025 Amazon AICE PhD Fellowship.\nMy Research\nMy research focuses on building large multimodal models (LMMs) and LMM-brained agents with human-like perception and reasoning. I aim to equip these models with the capability for system-2 reasoning, as well as efficient decision-making in dynamic and complex environments. For my most recent publications, please check my\nGoogle Scholar\n.\nSelected Publications\nMultimodal Policy Internalization for Conversational Agents\n[\nProject Page\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Jiateng Liu, Amin Fazel, Ritesh Sarkhel, Xing Fan, Xiang Li, Chenlei Guo, Heng Ji, Ruhi Sarikaya\nICLR 2026\nPerception-Aware Policy Optimization for Multimodal Reasoning\n[\nProject Page\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n*, Xuehang Guo*, Sofia Stoica, Haiyang Xu, Hongru Wang, Hyeonjeong Ha, Xiusi Chen, Yangyi Chen, Ming Yan, Fei Huang, Heng Ji\nICLR 2026\nDyMU: Dynamic Merging and Virtual Unmerging for Efficient VLMs\n[\nProject Page\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n*, Senthil Purushwalkam*, Caiming Xiong, Silvio Savarese, Heng Ji, Ran Xu\nNeurIPS 2025\nMobile-Agent-E: Self-Evolving Mobile Assistant for Complex Tasks\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Haiyang Xu, Junyang Wang, Xi Zhang, Ming Yan, Ji Zhang, Fei Huang, Heng Ji\nNeurIPS 2025\nSEA Workshop\n(\nOral\n)\nMultiAgentBench: Evaluating the Collaboration and Competition of LLM agents\n[\nPaper\n][\nCode\n]\nKunlun Zhu, Hongyi Du, Zhaochen Hong, Xiaocheng Yang, Shuyi Guo, Zhe Wang,\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Cheng Qian, Xiangru Tang, Heng Ji, Jiaxuan You\nACL 2025 Main\nInfogent: An Agent-Based Framework for Web Information Aggregation\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nRevanth Gangi Reddy*, Sagnik Mukherjee*, Jeonghwan Kim*,\nZhenhailong Wang\n*, Dilek Hakkani-Tur, Heng Ji\nNAACL 2025 Findings\nVisually Descriptive Language Model for Vector Graphics Reasoning\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Joy Hsu, Xingyao Wang, Kuan-Hao Huang, Manling Li, Jiajun Wu, Heng Ji\nTMLR; CVPR 2025\nMAR Workshop\n(\nSpotlight\n)\nDo LVLMs Understand Charts? Analyzing and Correcting Factual Errors in Chart Captioning\n[\nPaper\n] [\nProject Page\n]\nKung-Hsiang Huang, Mingyang Zhou, Hou Pong Chan, Yi R. Fung,\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Lingyu Zhang, Shih-Fu Chang, Heng Ji\nACL 2024 Findings\nUnleashing Cognitive Synergy in Large Language Models: A Task-Solving Agent through Multi-Persona Self-Collaboration\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Shaoguang Mao, Wenshan Wu, Tao Ge, Furu Wei, Heng Ji\nNAACL 2024 main\nPaxion: Patching Action Knowledge in Video-Language Foundation Models\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Ansel Blume, Sha Li, Genglin Liu, Jaemin Cho, Zineng Tang, Mohit Bansal, Heng Ji\nNeurIPS 2023 (\nSpotlight\n)\nRCOT: Detecting and Rectifying Factual Inconsistency in Reasoning by Reversing Chain-of-Thought\n[\nPaper\n]\nTianci Xue, Ziqi Wang,\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Chi Han, Pengfei Yu, Heng Ji\narXiv:2305.11499\nZemi: Learning Zero-Shot Semi-Parametric Language Models from Multiple Tasks\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Xiaoman Pan, Dian Yu, Dong Yu, Jianshu Chen, Heng Ji\nACL 2023 Findings\nA Language First Approach for Procedural Planning\n[\nPaper\n]\nJiateng Liu, Sha Li,\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Manling Li and Heng Ji\nACL 2023 Findings\nLanguage Models with Image Descriptors are Strong Few-Shot Video-Language Learners\n[\nPaper\n][\nVideo\n] [\nCode\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Manling Li, Ruochen Xu, Luowei Zhou, Jie Lei, Xudong Lin, Shuohang Wang, Ziyi Yang, Chenguang Zhu, Derek Hoiem, Shih-Fu Chang, Mohit Bansal, Heng Ji\nNeurIPS 2022\nNewsClaims: A New Benchmark for Claim Detection from News with Background Knowledge\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nRevanth Gangi Reddy, Sai Chetan,\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Yi R. Fung, Kathryn Conger, Ahmed Elsayed, Martha Palmer, Preslav Nakov, Eduard Hovy, Kevin Small, Heng Ji\nEMNLP 2022 main\nOpen Vocabulary Electroencephalography-To-Text Decoding and Zero-shot Sentiment Classification\n[\nPDF\n] [\nCode\n]\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Heng Ji\nAAAI 2022\nThe Future is not One-dimensional: Complex Event Schema Induction by Graph Modeling for Event Prediction\n[\nPaper\n] [\nCode\n]\nManling Li, Sha Li,\nZhenhailong Wang\n, Lifu Huang, Kyunghyun Cho, Heng Ji, Jiawei Han and Clare Voss\nEMNLP 2021 main\nExperience\n05/2025 - 08/2025,\nAmazon Alexa AI\nApplied Scientist Intern\nMentor: Amin Fazel, Ritesh Sarkhel, Xiang Li, Xing Fan, Heng Ji\nFocus: Multimodal Instruction Following and Policy Internalization\n06/2024 - 01/2025,\nSalesforce AI Research\nResearch Intern\nMentor:\nSenthil Purushwalkam\n,\nCongying Xia\n,\nRan Xu\n.\nFocus: Efficient Variable-length Visual Encoding\n05/2023 - 08/2023,\nMicrosoft Research Asia\nResearch Intern\nMentor:\nTao Ge\n,\nShaoguang Mao\n,\nWenshan Wu\n.\nFocus: Large Language Models, Multi-persona Collaboration\n05/2022 - 08/2022,\nTencent AI Lab\nResearch Intern\nMentor:\nXiaoman Pan\n,\nDian Yu\n,\nJianshu Chen\n.\nFocus: Retrieval Augmented Generation\n01/2022 - 05/2022,\nMicrosoft Research\nCollaboration on project\nVidIL\nWorking with\nRuochen Xu\n,\nLuowei Zhou\n,\nShuohang Wang\n,\nZiyi Yang\n,\nChenguang Zhu\n.\nFocus: Video-Language Understanding\n07/2020 - Present,\nBLENDER Lab\nGraduate Research Assistant\nAdvisor: Prof.\nHeng Ji\nFocus: Large Multimodal Models and Multimodal Agents\n09/2019 - 08/2020,\nRAAMAC Lab\nUndergraduate Research Assistant\nAdvisor: Prof.\nMani Golparvar-Fard\nFocus: Robotics\nEducation\nUniversity of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\nPh.D. in Computer Science, 2023 - Present; Advisor: Prof.\nHeng Ji\nM.S. in Computer Science, 2021 - 2023; Advisor: Prof.\nHeng Ji\nM.S. in Civil Engineering, 2019 - 2021; Advisor: Prof.\nMani Golparvar-Fard\nGPA: 3.98/4.0\nZhejiang University\nB.S. in Civil Engineering, 2016 - 2020\nGPA: 3.92/4.0\nZhejiang Province Government Scholarship\n(<2%)\nAcadamic Scholarship\n(<8%)\nInvited Talk, Service\n12/6/2022: Microsoft Research NLP PhD Student Invited Talk (Knowledge and Language Team)\n2/16/2023:\nAI-Time\nNeurips 2022 Event\n3/9/2024:\nLLM and AI Agent Reading Group\nFall 2024: Teaching Assistant for\nCS 546: Advanced Topics in Natural Language Processing\n, with a guest lecture on LLM-based Agents.\n7/20/2025:\nTalk at Ploutos AI\nMiscellaneous\nA\nshort film\nwritten and directed by me, ft.\nITP\n(dialogue in Chinese :)"
