      "pfwang@cnic.cn",
      "wpf2106@gmail.com"
    ],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Home\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nPengfei Wang\nFull Professor\nComputer Network Information Center, Chinese Academy of Sciences\nEmail:\npfwang[AT] cnic[DOT]cn;\nwpf2106\n[AT]\ngmail\n[DOT]\ncom\nGoogle Scholar\nShort Biography\nDr. Pengfei Wang received his B.S. degree from Jilin University and received his Ph.D. degree from the Chinese Academy of Sciences.\nHe has published over 50 papers in renowned international conferences and journals in the fields of data mining and artificial intelligence, including Cell Research, ACM SIGKDD, IJCAI, WWW, IEEE ICDM, AIJ, IEEE TKDE, and ACM TWEB.\nHe is a PC member for some top academic conferences such as KDD, NeurIPS, ICLR, WWW, IJCAI, and AAAI.\nResearch Interests\nDr. Pengfei Wang has broad interests in data mining and machine learning, especially in Spatial-Temporal Graph Data Mining, Reinforcement Learning, Large Language Models (LLM), and AI for Science (AI4S). Most of the methods are motivated by real-world applications, such as flow predictions and behavior analysis.\nInter\nThe research group works closely with esteemed professors from both domestic and international institutions, such as Arizona State University, the University of Wisconsin-Madison, Portland State University, the University of Kansas, the University of Macau, Tsinghua University, and the Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (Guangzhou). Students can be recommended for advanced studies.\nThe group maintains strong collaborations with research teams from leading internet companies, including Alibaba, Tencent, ByteDance, and Meituan, offering recommendations for outstanding individuals seeking internships or full-time positions.\nNews\n1\n1\n/2025 One paper on\nsingle-cell analysis\nis accepted by\nAAAI'26\n.\n10/2025 One paper on\nScientific Topic\nis accepted by IEEE\nBig Data'25 (\nBest Paper Shortlist\n)\n.\n10\n/2025 One paper on\nData Augmentation\nis accepted by\nIEEE TKDE\n.\n0\n6\n/2025 One paper on\nAI for Science\nis accepted by Advanced Science.\n05/2025\nOne\npaper\non Data augmentation\nis\naccepted by\nACL\n'25.\n0\n5\n/2025\nFour\npapers are accepted by IJCAI'25. One is on\nscRNA-seq\nclustering, one is on feat\nure generation. The other two are on graph learning.\n04/2025 One paper on AI-ready dataset is accepted by Advanced Science.\n12\n/2024 One paper on\nDrug-drug interaction\nis accepted by\nAAAI\n'2\n5\n.\n09/2024 One paper on\nSemi-supervised Multi-label Learning\nis accepted by\nNeurIPS\n'24.\n09/2024 One paper on single-cell\nfoundation model\nis accepted by\nCell Research (cover story).\n0\n9\n/2024\nOne\npaper on\nefficient\nuniversity courses\nis\naccepted by\nICDM\n'24.\n0\n7\n/2024 Two papers are accepted by\nCIKM'24.\nOne is on  multi-modal learning (regular), and the other is on drug-drug interaction  (short).\n0\n7\n/202\n4\nOne\npaper on\ngene regulatory networks is\naccepted by Briefings\nIn Bioinformatics.\n04/2024 Three papers are accepted by IJCAI'24.\n0\n3\n/2024\nTwo\npapers are accepted by\nDASFAA\n'24.\n01/2024 One paper on temporal knowledge reasoning is accepted by Artificial Intelligence (AIJ).\n01/2024 One paper on\nspatial-temporal delay effects\nis accepted by\nWWW'24.\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nGoogle Sites\nReport abuse"
