    "homepage_text": "Lichao Sun, Lehigh University\nLichao Sun\nHome\nResearch\nPublication\nPeople\nTeaching\nAssistant Professor\nOffice: 325, Building C, MT\nLehigh University\nComputer Science &\n                        Engineering\nEmail: lis221 at lehigh dot edu\nGoogle Scholar\nAbout me\nLichao Sun an Assistant Professor in\nComputer Science and Engineering\nat\nLehigh University\n. Meanwhile, He also an Adjunct Professor at Mayo Clinc. Before that, I received my Ph.D. degree in Computer Science at University of Illinois, Chicago in 2020, under the supervision of Prof.\nPhilip S. Yu\n. Further before, I obtained M.S. and B.S. from University of Nebraska Lincoln. He was the recipients of 2024 Microsoft Accelerate Foundation Models Research Award, 2024 OpenAI Researcher Award and NSF CRII Award.\nI also have long-term research intern experience in the industrial research labs, including Microsoft Research, Salesforce Research, Samsung Research America, Amazon Web Service, and LinkedIn. Looking forward to any collaborations from both academia and industrial research lab too.\n[Open Positions] We are recruiting Ph.D. students, undergraduate students, and visiting scholars/students. Please feel free to send me an email with your CV.\nNews and Highlights\nI am now looking for highly motivated remote or onsite visiting students:\nIf you are interested in working with me, please feel free to email me.\n[2024.05] OpenAI Researcher Access Program is awarded\n[2024.01] Microsoft Accelerate Foundation Models Research is awarded\n[2023.11] Invited talk at University of Notre Dame, South Bend, Indiana\n[2023.08] SIGIR Best Paper Honorable Mention Award!\n[2023.07] Invited talk at NEC Lab, NJ\n[2023.06] NSF CRII is awarded\n[2023.05] Invited talk at University of Nevada, Las Vegas, Google CSR\n[2023.04] Invited talk at Florida Internatonal University of Nevada\n[2023.04] Invited talk at Harvard Medical School, MGH\nServices\nPC members\n2023 NeurIPS, ICML, CVPR, KDD, ICCV, AAAI, IJCAI (SPC)\n2022 NeurIPS, ICML, KDD, CVPR, ECCV, AAAI, IJCAI\n2021 NeurIPS, ICML, KDD, CVPR, ICCV, AAAI, IJCAI, WSDM"
  },
  "serper::Liang-Jian Deng": {
    "homepage": "https://liangjiandeng.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "liangjian.deng@uestc.edu.cn"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/liangjiandeng",
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Liang-Jian Deng | UESTC\nLiang-Jian Deng\n(邓良剑)\nUniversity of Electronic Science and Technology of China\nEmail: liangjian.deng@uestc.edu.cn\nOffice: Innovation Center A-401, Qingshuihe Campus, Chengdu, Sichuan, China\nI am a professor in the School of Mathematical Sciences of\nUESTC (电子科技大学)\n.\nI was born in Xichang, a small city in Liangshan Prefecture of Sichuan Province. In 2010 and 2016, I got my B.S. and Ph.D. degrees from the School of Mathematical Sciences, University of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC), under the supervision of Prof. Ting-Zhu Huang. As a Joint-Training Ph.D. student, I worked with\nProf. Weihong Guo\nat Case Western Reserve University (CWRU) in Cleveland, Ohio, from September 2013 to September 2014. In 2017, I was a postdoctoral researcher at HKBU under\nProf. Xue-Cheng Tai\n(Hong Kong, China). I also paid short visits to the Isaac Newton Institute for Mathematical Sciences (University of Cambridge) and HKBU. My research interest is mainly focusing on Machine learning, Variational image modeling & computing, and various image and vision tasks, e.g., image fusion, image analysis, etc. \nIn recent years, I have published over 40 journal papers as the first or corresponding author in SIAM J. Imag. Sci., Int. J. Comput. Vis., Info. Fusion, Inverse Prob. Imag., J. Sci. Compt, IEEE TPAMI/GRSM/TIP/TCyber/TNNLS/TMM/TGRS/TCSVT/TSMC, and over 20 papers at top-tier conferences (CCF-A) such as ICML/NeurIPS/CVPR/ICCV/AAAI/ACM MM/IJCAI.\nTeaching\nLinks\nPublications (Full)\nResearch Projects (Click logos):\nPublications (Selected):\nMore papers info., please visit:\nGoogle Scholar Profile\n(4500+ citations)\nA New Operator Splitting Method for the Euler Elastica Model for Image Smoothing\nLiang-Jian Deng\n, Roland Glowinski, Xue-Cheng Tai\nSIAM Journal on Imaging Sciences\n, 12(2):1190-1230, 2019. (\nOur Lie-Operator splitting algorithm, as an independent paradigm compared to the mainstream ADMM and Primal-Dual algorithms, has successfully and efficiently solved various complex variational optimization models, e.g., L1 mean curvature problem, Gaussian curvature problem, Willmore energy problem, color Elastica model, obstacle problem, etc.\n)\n[PDF]\n[Code]\nAn Efficient Image Fusion Network Exploiting Unifying Language and Mask Guidance\nZi-Han Cao#, Yu-Jie Liang#,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\n, Gemine Vivone\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n, 2025 (\nFirst efficient image fusion network with unified language and mask guidance, validated on 6 tasks (12 datasets) and applied to detection, depth estimation, segmentation, etc\n)\n[PDF]\n[Supp]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{caotpami2025,\n  title={An Efficient Image Fusion Network Exploiting Unifying Language and Mask Guidance},\n  author={Zi-Han Cao, Yu-Jie Liang, Liang-Jian Deng, Gemine Vivone},\n  journal={IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},\n  volume={},\n  number={},\n  pages={},\n  year={2025},\n  doi={}\n  }\n[Code]\nFully-Connected Transformer for Multi-Source Image Fusion\nXiao Wu, Zihan Cao, Ting-Zhu Huang*,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\n, Jocelyn Chanussot, Gemine Vivone\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n, 2025 (\nA unified multilinear-algebra-based framework for generalized self-attention, subsuming all mainstream variants​\n)\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{wu2025fully,\n    title={Fully-Connected Transformer for Multi-Source Image Fusion},\n    author={Wu, Xiao and Cao, Zi-Han and Huang, Ting-Zhu and Deng, Liang-Jian and Chanussot, Jocelyn and Vivone, Gemine},\n    journal={IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},\n    volume={47},\n    number={3},\n    pages={2071-2088},\n    year={2025}\n  }\n[Code]\nDynamic Evolution of Complex Networks: A Reinforcement Learning Approach Applying Evolutionary Games to Community Structure\nBin Pi,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\n, Minyu Feng*, Matjaž Perc, Jürgen Kurths\nIEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence\n, 2025 (\nThe first to introduce the concepts of game theory and birth-death processes into reinforcement learning-based complex network research\n)\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{pitpami2025,\n    title={Dynamic Evolution of Complex Networks: A Reinforcement Learning Approach Applying Evolutionary Games to Community Structure},\n    author={Bin Pi, Liang-Jian Deng, Minyu Feng, Matjaž Perc, Jürgen Kurths},\n    journal={IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence},\n    volume={},\n    number={},\n    pages={},\n    year={2025},\n    doi={10.1109/TPAMI.2025.3579895}\n  }\n[Code]\nUnsupervised Coefficient Learning Framework for Variational Pansharpening\nJin-Liang Xiao, Ting-Zhu Huang*,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\n, Huidong Jiang, Qibin Zhao, Gemine Vivone\nInformation Fusion\n, 2025\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{xiaoif2025,\ntitle={Unsupervised coefficient learning framework for variational pansharpening},\nauthor={Jin-Liang Xiao, Ting-Zhu Huang, Liang-Jian Deng, Huidong Jiang, Qibin Zhao, Gemine Vivone},\njournal={Information Fusion},\nvolume={127},\npages={103790},\nyear={2026},\ndoi={https://doi.org/10.1016/j.inffus.2025.103790}\n}\n[Code]\nLoss-Driven Dynamic Weight and Residual Transformation in Physics-Informed Neural Network\nYabin Zhang,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\nNeural Networks\n, 2025\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{zhangnn2025,\ntitle={ Loss-driven dynamic weight and residual transformation in physics-informed neural network},\nauthor={Yabin Zhang, Liang-Jian Deng },\njournal={Neural Networks},\nvolume={191},\nnumber={6},\npages={107841},\nyear={2025},\ndoi={ https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neunet.2025.107841}\n}\n[Code]\nMMAIF: Multi-task and Multi-degradation All-in-One for Image Fusion with Language Guidance\nZihan Cao#, Yu Zhong, Ziqi Wang,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)\n, 2025\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@article{cao2025mmaif,\n  title={MMAIF: Multi-task and Multi-degradation All-in-One for Image Fusion with Language Guidance},\n  author={Cao, Zihan and Zhong, Yu and Wang, Ziqi and Deng, Liang-Jian},\n  journal={IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)},\n  year={2025}\n}\n[Code]\nTaming Flow Matching with Unbalanced Optimal Transport into Fast Pansharpening\nZihan Cao#, Yu Zhong#,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\nIEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)\n, 2025\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@article{cao2025taming,\n  title={Taming Flow Matching with Unbalanced Optimal Transport into Fast Pansharpening},\n  author={Cao, Zihan and Zhong, Yu and Deng, Liang-Jian},\n  journal={IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)},\n  year={2025}\n}\n[Code]\nAdaptive Rectangular Convolution for Remote Sensing Pansharpening\nXueyang Wang, Zhixin Zheng, Jiandong Shao, Yule Duan\nLiang-Jian Deng\nIEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)\n, 2025\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{wxycvpr2025,\n  title={Adaptive Rectangular Convolution for Remote Sensing Pansharpening},\n  author={Xueyang Wang, Zhixin Zheng, Jiandong Shao, Yule Duan, Liang-jian Deng},\n  journal={IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)},\n  year={2025},\n  url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.00467},\n  }\n[Code]\nA General Adaptive Dual-level Weighting Mechanism for Remote Sensing Pansharpening\nJie Huang#, Haorui Chen#, Jiaxuan Ren, Siran Peng,\nLiangjian Deng\nIEEE/CVF Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (CVPR)\n, 2025\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{jiecvpr2025,\n  title={A General Adaptive Dual-level Weighting Mechanism for Remote Sensing Pansharpening},\n  author={Jie Huang, Haorui Chen, Jiaxuan Ren, Siran Peng, Liangjian Deng},\n  journal={IEEE/CVF Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference (CVPR)},\n  volume={},\n  number={},\n  pages={},\n  year={2025},\n  doi={}\n  }\n[Code]\nWavelet-Assisted Multi-Frequency Attention Network for Pansharpening\nJie Huang#, Rui Huang#, Jinghao Xu, Siran Peng, Yule Duan,\nLiangjian Deng*\nAAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)\n, 2025 (#: equal contribution) (\nOral, 4.7%\n)\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{jieaaai2025,\ntitle={Wavelet-Assisted Multi-Frequency Attention Network for Pansharpening},\nauthor={Jie Huang, Rui Huang, Jinghao Xu, Siran Peng, Yule Duan, Liangjian Deng},\njournal={AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence (AAAI)},\nvolume={},\nnumber={},\npages={},\nyear={2025},\ndoi={}\n}\n[Code]\nA General Paradigm with Detail-Preserving Conditional Invertible Network for Image Fusion\nWu Wang,\nLiang-Jian Deng*\n, Ran Ran, Gemine Vivone\nInternational Journal of Computer Vision\n, 2024\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{wangijcv2024,\ntitle={A General Paradigm with Detail-Preserving Conditional Invertible Network for Image Fusion },\nauthor={ Wu Wang, Liang-Jian Deng, Ran Ran, Gemine Vivone },\njournal={ International Journal of Computer Vision},\nvolume={13},\nnumber={},\npages={1029–1054},\nyear={2024},\ndoi={10.1007/s11263-023-01924-5}\n}\n[Code]\nFusionMamba: Efficient Remote Sensing Image Fusion with State Space Model\nSiran Peng, Xiangyu Zhu, Haoyu Deng,\nLiang-Jian Deng\n, Zhen Lei\nIEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing\n, 2024\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@ARTICLE{pengtgrs2024,\n  title={Fusionmamba: Efficient remote sensing image fusion with state space model},\n  author={Peng, Siran and Zhu, Xiangyu and Deng, Haoyu and Deng, Liang-Jian and Lei, Zhen},\n  journal={IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing},\n  volume={62},\n  number={},\n  pages={1-16},\n  year={2024},\n  doi={10.1109/TGRS.2024.3496073}\n  }\n[Code]\nExploring the Low-Pass Filtering Behavior in Image Super-Resolution\nHaoyu Deng, Zijing Xu, Yule Duan, Xiao Wu, Wenjie Shu\nLiang-Jian Deng*\nInternational Conference on Machine Learning (ICML)\n, 2024\n[PDF]\n[BibTeX]\n@article{deng2024exploring,\n  title={Exploring the Low-Pass Filtering Behavior in Image Super-Resolution},\n  author={Deng, Haoyu and Xu, Zijing and Duan, Yule and Wu, Xiao and Shu, Wenjie and Deng, Lia