    "github": "https://github.com/ChiYeungLaw",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ziyang-luo-681a17192/",
    "homepage_text": "Ziyang's Page\nZiyang Luo\nResearch Scientist\nSalesforce Research\nGitHub\nGoogle Scholar\nX\nLinkedIn\nAbout Me\nI am an AI Research Scientist (Large Language Models) at\nSalesforce Research, working under\nDr. Junnan Li\n.\nI obtained my PhD in Computer Science at\nHong Kong Baptist University (2025). Previously, I was a visiting researcher at\nthe National University of Singapore (2024), collaborating with\nProf. Mohan Kankanhalli\n. I have also interned at\nMicrosoft Research and\nAlibaba. I was deeply involved in the development of the well-known open-source project\nWizardLM\n, served as the first author of\nWizardCoder\n, and contributed to the first commercial-scale diffusion LLM,\nMercury\n.\nMy research focuses on foundation models and artificial intelligence, with a particular emphasis on\ndeveloping trustworthy intelligent agents that can effectively interact with real-world environments\n. I have published over 30 papers at top-tier AI conferences, including ICLR, CVPR, ICCV, ACL, and EMNLP. For academic collaboration or inquiries, please reach out via email at zluo AT salesforce.com or WeChat (ID: chiyeunglaw).\nLatest News\nJanuary 2026\n2 papers are accepted by ICLR 2026.\nDecember 2025\nI am invited to serve as an SAC (Code Models Track) for ACL 2026.\nI have also been invited to serve as an Industry Day speaker for ACM MM Asia 2025.\nMay 2025\nI am invited to serve as an SAC (Code Models Track) for EMNLP 2025 and as an AC for NeurIPS 2025.\n4 papers are accepted by ACL 2025 (2 main, 2 findings).\nMarch 2025\nVideoAutoArena\nis accepted by CVPR 2025.\nJanuary 2025\nRelease popular GUI grounding benchmark\nScreenSpot-Pro\n(ACM Multimedia 2025)."
  },
