    "homepage_text": "Niranjan Damera-Venkata\nNIRANJAN DAMERA-VENKATA\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata (HP Labs Web page)\nHewlett-Packard Laboratories\n   1501 Page Mill road, MS 4U-6\n   Palo Alto, CA 94304 USA\n   Work Phone: (+1 650) 857-4788\n   Home Phone: (+1 408) 720-8821\n   E-mail: damera@exch.hpl.hp.com\nResearch Interests\n-\nEducation\n-\nPublications\n-\nSoftware\nCurrent Research Interests\nWobulation: Theory and algorithms\nSignal processing for projector pipelines\nProjector-camera systems\nDigital Halftoning and inverse halftoning\nDigital camera image processing\nMultidimensional System theory\nHilbert Transforms in communication and signal processing\nSymbolic design and analysis tools\nImage and video quality assessment\nDigital image watermarking and information embedding\nEducation\nThe University of Texas at Austin\n, \n   Austin, Texas\nPhD in\nElectrical \n   Engineering\n, Dec. 2000\nG.P.A.: 4.0/4.0\nArea:\nTelecommunications and Information Systems Engineering\nSupervisor:\nDr. Brian L. Evans\nThe University of Texas at Austin\n, \n   Austin, Texas\nM.S in\nElectrical \n   Engineering\n, May 1999\nG.P.A.: 4.0/4.0\nArea:\nTelecommunications and Information Systems Engineering\nSupervisor:\nDr. Brian L. Evans\nThe University of Madras, Madras, INDIA\nB.S in Electronics and Communication \n   Engineering, May 1997\nEquivalent G.P.A.: 9.8/10.0\nArea: Multidimensional Digital Signal Processing\nThesis title: \"\nStabilization and Stability Testing of \nMultidimensional recursive digital filters\n\"\nSupervisor: Dr. P. S Reddy\nPublications\nJournal Articles\nVishal Monga,\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n, and Brian L. Evans,\n\"Image Halftoning by Error Diffusion: A Survey of Methods for\nArtifact Reduction\",\nSPIE Journal of Electronic Imaging\n, submitted.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n, Jonathan Yen, Vishal Monga, and\nBrian L. Evans,\n\"Hardcopy Image Barcodes Via Block Error Diffusion\",\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n, submitted.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nBrian L. Evans\n, and\nVishal Monga,\n\"Color Error Diffusion Halftoning\",\nIEEE Signal Processing Magazine\n,\nvol. 20, no. 4, pp. 51-58, July 2003, invited paper.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Design\nand Analysis of Vector Color Error  \nDiffusion Halftoning  Systems\"\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n, vol. 10, no. 10,\npp. 1552-1565, October 2001.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Adaptive\nThreshold Modulation for Error Diffusion Halftoning\"\n,\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n, vol. 10, no. 1, pp.\n104-116, January 2001.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n, Mahalakshmi Venkataraman,\nM. S. Hrishikesh, and P. S. Reddy,\n\"A New Transform for the Stabilization and Stability Testing of\nMultidimensional Recursive digital Filters\",\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems-II\n, vol. 47, no. 9, pp. 965-968, \nSeptember 2000.\nThomas\nD. Kite\n,\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nBrian L. Evans\nand\nAlan\nC. Bovik\n, \n\"A Fast, High Quality Inverse Halftoning Algorithm for Error Diffused\nHalftoned images,\"\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing,\n,\nvol. 9, no. 9, pp. 1583-1593, September 2000.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nBrian L. Evans\n, and\n Shawn R. McCaslin, \n     \"Design of Optimal Minimum Phase Digital FIR Filters Using Discrete \n        Hilbert Transforms\",\nIEEE Transactions on  Signal Processing\n, vol. 48, no. 5,\n  pp. 1491-1495, May 2000.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nThomas\nD. Kite\n,\nWilson\nS. Geisler\n,\nBrian\nL. Evans\nand\nAlan\nC. Bovik\n, \"Image Quality Assessment Based on a Degradation Model\",\nIEEE Transactions on Image Processing\n, vol. 9, no. 4,\npp. 636-651, April 2000.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"An Automated Framework for Multi-criteria Optimization of Analog\nFilter Designs\",\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems-II\n, vol. 46,\nno. 8, pp 981-990, August 1999.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n, Mahalakshmi Venkataraman,\n M. S. Hrishikesh and   \n P. S. Reddy,\n \"Stabilization of 2-D Recursive Digital Filters by the DHT method\",\nIEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems-II\n, vol. 46, no. 1,\n  pp 85-89, January 1999.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n, Srikanth Gummadi, and\nBrian L. Evans\n, \n \"Comments on `Description of FIR Digital Filters in the form of\nParallel Connection of Linear Phase FIRs' \",\nElectronics Letters,\nvol. 34, no. 9, pp. 866-867, April 30, 1998.\nConference Papers\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Color Error Diffusion with Generalized Optimum Noise Shaping\",\nProc.\nIEEE International Conference on Image\nProcessing\n,Oct. 7-10, 2001, Thessaloniki, Greece, to appear.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"FM Halftoning Via Block Error Diffusion\",\nProc.\nIEEE International Conference on Image\nProcessing\n,Oct. 7-10, 2001, Thessaloniki, Greece, to appear.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Matrix Gain Model for Vector Color Error Diffusion\",\nProc.\nIEEE-EURASIP Workshop on Nonlinear Signal and Image\nProcessing\n,June 3-5, 2001, Baltimore, MD, invited paper.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Parallel Implementation of Multifilters\", Proc.\nIEEE Conf. on\nAcoustics, Speech, and Signal Processing\n, vol. 6, pp. 3335-3338,\nJune 2000, Istanbul, Turkey.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Optimal Design of Real and Complex Minimum Phase Digital FIR\nFilters\",\nProc. IEEE Conf. on Acoustics, Speech, and Signal\nProcessing\n, vol. 3, pp. 1145-1148, March 15-19, 1999, Phoenix, AZ.\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nBrian L. Evans\n,\nMiroslav D. Lutovac\nand\nDejan V. Tosic\n,\n\"Joint Optimization of Multiple Behavioral and Implementation\nProperties of Analog Filter Designs\"\n,\nProceedings,\nIEEE International Symposium on Circuits and\nSystems,\nvol. 6, pp. 286-289, Jun. 1998, Monterey, CA\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nThomas D. Kite\n, Mahalakshmi Venkataraman\nand\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Fast\nBlind Inverse Halftoning\"\n, \nProceedings,\nIEEE International Conference on Image\nProcessing,\n, vol. 2, pp. 64-68, Oct. 4-7, 1998, Chicago, IL.\nThomas\nD. Kite\n,\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata\n,\nBrian L. Evans\nand\nAlan C. Bovik\n,\n\"A High Quality, Fast Inverse Halftoning Algorithm for Error Diffused\nHalftoned images,\"\nProceedings,\nIEEE International Conference on Image Processing,\n,\nvol. 2, pp. 59-63, Oct. 4-7, 1998, Chicago, IL.\nPublished Software\nThomas D. Kite, Niranjan Damera-Venkata and Brian L. Evans,\n\"Fast Inverse Halftoning Package\"\n, copyright © 1998-\nThe University of Texas.\nC packages to implement fast inverse halftoning. Unix and PC versions,\nPGM and raw greylevel supported. Blind inverse halftoning from\nerror-diffused halftones. Inverse halftoning from fixed cluster and\ndispersed dot dither screens.\nVersion 1.0 (Oct. 1998) will be available on the Web at\nhttp://www.ece.utexas.edu/~bevans/projects/inverseHalftoning.html\nNiranjan Damera-Venkata and\nBrian L. Evans\n,\n\"Filter Optimization Packages for  \n        Mathematica 1.1\"\n,\n        copyright © 1993-1998,\n        The Regents of the University of California.\n        Mathematica packages to generate Matlab software to perform\n        a joint optimization of several characteristics of pole-zero analog\n        infinite impulse response filters.\n        Supported characteristics are magnitude response,\n        phase response, step response, and quality factors.\n        New characteristics can be easily added.\n        Version 1.1 (June 22, 1998) is available on the Web at\nhttp://www.ece.utexas.edu/~bevans   \n        /projects/syn_filter_software.html\nLast modified:\nMay 26, 2000"
  },
  "serper::Jan-Peter Calliess": {
    "homepage": "https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~jan/",
    "emails": [],
    "github": null,
    "linkedin": null,
    "homepage_text": "Jan-Peter Calliess\nJan-Peter Calliess\nSenior Research Fellow\nOxford-Man Institute\nUniversity of Oxford\nEagle House, Walton Well Road\nOxford, OX2 6ED\nUnited Kingdom\nT: +44 (0)1865 616600\nE: jan “at” robots “dot”ox”dot” ac “dot” uk\nMINI BIO\nJan-Peter Calliess is a Senior Research Fellow at the Oxford-Man Institute of Quantitative Finance and the Department of Engineering Science at the University of Oxford, UK. His main research interests focus on the intersection of machine learning, adaptive decision making\nand uncertainty quantification, as well as on applications to finance, and control.\nPrior to joining Oxford in his current post, he had repeated stays at Carnegie Mellon University, USA, had received his undergraduate degrees from University of Karlsruhe, Germany (now KIT), a DPhil in Engineering Science from Oxford University and had been a research associate at the Control Group and the Computational and Biological Learning Lab at the University of Cambridge, UK.\nRESEARCH INTERESTS\nMy research interests include topics pertaining to machine learning and decision making with applications to finance, computational mechanism design, multi-agent coordination, inference, control and dynamical systems.\nTEACHING & SEMINARS\nC24: Advanced Probability\nFourth Year Projects (4YPs)\nMachine Learning for Finance Reading Group Series (suspended)\nMachine Learning, Dynamics and Finance Study Group\nSERVICE\nI have served on the programme comittee /as a reviewer for\n Automatica, IEEE Trans. on Automatic Control, IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters, ICAIF, ICRA, ICML, NIPS, IROS, Multidimensional Signals and Systems,  ACC, ECC, CDC, NMPC as well as\nfor the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF).\nPAPERS\nPublications\nJ. W. Huang, S. J. Roberts, J. Calliess.\nOn the Sample Complexity of Lipschitz Constant Estimation\n. Transactions on Machine Learning Research, 2023. [Awarded a \"Featured\" Certification.]\n[LINK]\nHuang, Julien W.; Roberts, Stephen J.; Calliess, Jan-Peter.\nFirst Hitting Time Guarantees for Contractive Nonlinear Systems. Conference on Decision and Control (CDC)\n, 2023.\nPeer Nagy, Jan-Peter Calliess, Stefan Zohren,\nAsynchronous Deep Double Dueling Q-learning for trading-signal execution in limit order book markets\n. Front. Artif. Intell., 2023.\nShi, Danni; Calliess, Jan-Peter; Cucuringu, Mihai.\nMultireference Alignment for Lead-Lag Detection in Multivariate Time Series and Equity Trading\n. Proceedings of the Fourth ACM International Conference on AI in Finance (ICAIF), 507-515, 2023.\nP. Belcak, J. Calliess and S. Zohren.\nFast Agent-Based Simulation Frame- work of Limit Order Books with Applications to Pro-Rata Markets and the Study of Latency Effects,\nThe 23rd International Work- shop on Multi-Agent-Based Simulation, ABS 2021, Springer Nature, LNAI 13128, 2022.\nXingchen Wan, Jie Yang, Slavi Marinov, Jan-Peter Calliess, Stefan Zohren and Xiaowen Dong,\nSentiment correlation in financial news networks and associated market movements,\nNature Sci. Rep., 2021.\nM. Ahrens J. Ashwin, J. Calliess , V. Nguyen.\nBayesian Topic Regression,\nProc. of the Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP), 2021.\nF. Krause and J. Calliess,\nNeural Policy Learning of Interpretable Trading Strategies.\nACM ICAIF 2021 Workshop on Explainable AI in Finance, 2021. Also available as an [SSRN preprint].\nJ. M. Manzano, D. Munoz de la Pena, J. -P. Calliess and D. Limon.\nComponentwise Hoelder inference for robust learning-based MPC,\nIn IEEE Transactions on Automatic Control, doi: 10.1109/TAC.2021.3056356.\n[LINK]\n, 2021.\nCamilla Sterud, Signe Moe, Mads Valentin Bram, Stephen Roberts and Jan Calliess.\nRecurrent neural network structures for learning control valve behaviour.\nAutomation, Robotics and Communications for Industry 4.0 (ARCI' 2021), 2021.\nJ. Huang, J. Calliess,\nFirst Hitting Time Guarantees for Nonlinear Time Series Models, Time Series Workshop,\nICML, 2021.\nJ.M. Manzano, D. Munoz de la Pena, J. Calliess, D. Limon.\nOnline learning constrained MPC based on double prediction.\nManzano, J.M., Munoz de la Pena, D., Calliess, J. and Limon, D., 2021. Online learning constrained model predictive control based on double prediction. International Journal of Robust and Nonlinear Control, 31(18), 2021.\nJ. Calliess, S. J. Roberts, C. E. Rasmussen, J. Maciejoswki\nLazily Adapted Constant Kinky Inference for nonparametric regression and model-reference adaptive control\n. Automatica, 2020.\n[LINK]\nJ.M. Manzano, D. Limon, D. Munoz de la Pena, J. Calliess.\nRobust learning-based MPC for nonlinear constrained systems.\nAutomatica, 117:01, 2020.\nK. Polymenakos, L. Laurenti, A. Patane, J. Calliess, L. Cardelli, M. Kwiatkowska, A. Abate and S. Roberts.\nSafety Guarantees for Iterative Predictions with Gaussian Processes.\nConference on Decision and Control (CDC), 2020.\nMads Valentin Bram, Jan-Peter Calliess, Stephen Roberts, Dennis Hansen, Zhenyu Yang.\nAnalysis and Modeling of State-Dependent Delay in Control Valves.\nIFAC World Congress, 2020.\nJ.M. Manzano, J. Calliess, D. Munoz de la Pena and D. Limon.\nOnline learning robust MPC: an exploration-exploitation approach.\nIFAC World Congress, 2020.\nJ.M. Manzano, D. Limon, D. Munoz de la Pena and J. Calliess.\nData-based Robust MPC with Componentwise Hoelder Kinky Inference.\nProc. of the CDC, 2019.\nA. Alvi, B. Ru, J. Calliess, S. Roberts, M. A. Osborne.\nAsynchronous Batch Bayesian Optimisation with Improved Local Penalisation.\nProc. of the International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), PMLR 97:253-262, 2019.\nJ.M. Manzano, D. Limon, D. Munoz de la Pena and J. Calliess.\nOutput Feedback MPC based on Smoothed Projected Kinky Inference.\nIET Control Theory & Applications, 2019.\nA. Blaas, J. M. Manzano, D. Limon and J. Calliess.\nLocalised Kinky Inference.\nProc. of the ECC, 2019.\nJ. Calliess.\nOnline Optimisation for Online Learning and Control -- From No-Regret to Generalised Error Convergence.\nProc. of the ECC, 2019.\nJ. Calliess, A. Papachristodoulou and S. J. Roberts.\nBayesian nonparametrics and\nfeedback-linearisation of discretised control-affine\nsystems\n. Proc. of the Conf. on Decision and Control (CDC), 2018.\nJ. M. Manzano, D. Limon, D. Munoz de la Pena and J. Calliess.\nRobust Data-Based Model Predictive Contol for Nonlinear Constrained Systems\n. IFAC-PapersOnLine, Vol. 51, Issue 20, Elsevier, 2018.\n[LINK]\nA. Edwards, J. Calliess and K. Margellos.\nDistributed Optimization for Energy Management in Building Networks.\nControl 2018.\nJ. Calliess, S. J. Roberts, C. E. Rasmussen  and J. Maciejoswki.\nNonlinear Set Membership Methods with Hyperparameter Estimation for Online Learning and Control.\nProc. of the ECC, 2018.\nA. Blaas, A. Cobb, J. Calliess and S. J. Roberts.\nScalable Bounding of Predictive Uncertainty in Regression Problems with SLAC.\nLNAI 11142, Springer, 2018.\nJ. Calliess\nLipschitz Optimisation for Lipschitz Interpolation\n. Proc. of the ACC, 2017.\n[LINK]\nD. Limon, J. Calliess and J. Maciejowski.\nLearning-based Nonlinear Model Predictive Control\n. IFAC-PapersOnLine, Vol. 50, Issue 1, (Proc. of the 2017-IFAC World Congress), 2017.\n[LINK]\nJ. Calliess, N. Korda, G. J. Gordon.\nA Distributed Mechanism for Multi-Agent Convex Optimisation and Coordination with No-Regret Learners.\nWorkshop on Learning, Inference and Control of Multi-Agent Systems, Neural Information Processing Systems (NIPS), 2016.\n[LINK]\nJ. Calliess.\nBayesian Lipschitz Constant Estimation and Quadrature\n, Workshop on Probabilistic Integration, NIPS, 2015.\nJ. Calliess, M. Osborne and S. J. Roberts.\nConservative collision prediction and avoidance for stochastic trajectories in continuous time and space\n. Proc. Autonomous Agents and Multi-agent Systems (AAMAS), 2014.\nJ. Calliess A. Papachristodoulou and S. J. Roberts.\nStochastic processes and feedback-linearisation for online identification and Bayesian adaptive control of fully-actuated mechanical systems\n, WS- Advances in Machine Learning for Sensorimotor Control, NIPS, 2013.  (Also submitted to Arxiv)\nJ. Calliess, M. Osborne and S. J. Roberts.\nNonlinear adaptive hybrid control by combining Gaussian process system identification with classical control laws\n, WS- Novel Methods for Learning and Optimization of Control Policies and Trajectories for Robotics, ICRA, 2013.\nJ. Calliess and S. J. Roberts.\nMulti-agent planning with mixed-integer programming and adaptive interaction constraint generation\n. (Extended Abstract), Symposium on Combinatorial Search (SOCS), 2013.\nJ. Calliess, M. Osborne and S. J. Roberts.\nTowards auction-based multi-agent collision-avoidance under continuous stochastic dynamics\n. Presented at workshop: Markets, Mechanisms, and Multi-Agent Models — Examining the Interaction of Machine Learning and Economics, (ICML 2012).\nD. Lyons, J. Calliess and U. Hanebeck.\nChance-constrained Model Predictive Control for Multi-Agent Systems\n. Proc. of the American Control Conference (ACC 2012).\nJ. Calliess, D. Lyons and U. Hanebeck.\nLazy auctions for multi-robot collision avoidance and motion control under uncertainty\n. LNAI 7068, Springer, 2011.\nJ. Calliess, M. Mai, S. Pfeiffer.\nOn the Computational Benefit of Tensor Separation for High-Dimensional Discrete Convolutions\n. Multidimensional Systems and Signal Processing, Springer, 2010.\nJ. Calliess.\nOn Fixed Convex Combinations of No-Regret Learners. 6th International Conference on Machine Learning and Data Mining\nin Pattern Recognition\n. In LNAI 5632, Springer, 2009.\nS. Pfeiffer, M. Mai, W. Globcke, J. Calliess.\nOn generalized separation and the speed-up of local operators on multi-dimensional signals\n. 6th International Workshop on\nMultidimensional (nD) Systems (NDS ’09). (IEEE-XPLORE).\nA. Porbadnigk, M. Wester, J. Calliess, T. Schultz.\nEEG-based Speech Recognition – Impact of Temporal Effects\n. International Conference on Bio-inspired Systems and Signal Processing, Biosignals 2009.\nJ. Calliess and G. J. Gordon.\nNo-regret Learning and a  Mechanism for Distributed Multiagent Planning.\nProc. of the 7th International\nConference on Autono...[truncated]"
