    "homepage_text": "Min-hwan Oh | Seoul National University\nMin-hwan Oh is an Associate Professor in\nthe Graduate School of Data Science\nat\nSeoul National University\n.\nHis primary research interests are in\nsequential decision making, reinforcement learning, bandit algorithms, optimization, statistical machine learning,\nand their various applications.\n→\nRecent News\nJan 2026\n4 papers accepted at\nICLR\n2026\nNov 2025\nRecognized as a\nTop Area Chair\nat NeurIPS 2025\nOct 2025\nSelected as a finalist for the\nINFORMS JFIG Paper Award\nSep 2025\n9 papers accepted at\nNeurIPS\n2025 (including 1 Spotlight) in the main track, and 1 paper accepted in the position track\nJune 2025\nReceived the\nAmazon Research Award\nMay 2025\n5 papers accepted at\nICML\n2025, and 1 paper at\nCOLT\n2025\nJan 2025\n5 papers accepted at\nICLR\n2025\nSep 2024\n5 papers accepted at\nNeurIPS\n2024\nAug 2024\nOur paper won an Outstanding Paper Award at 2024 Korea Artificial Intelligence Association.\nMay 2024\n1 paper accepted at\nCOLT\n2024\nJan 2024\n1 paper accepted at\nICLR\n2024\nDec 2023\n3 papers accepted at\nAAAI\n2024\nSep 2023\n1 paper accepted at\nNeurIPS\n2023\nJul 2023\nOur papers won a Best Paper Award and an Outstanding Paper Award at 2023 Korea Artificial Intelligence Association.\nApr 2023\n3 papers accepted at\nICML\n2023\nJan 2023\n1 paper accepted at\nAISTATS\n2023\nNov 2022\n1 paper accepted at\nAAAI\n2023\nAug 2022\nOur paper won an Outstanding Paper Award at 2022 Korea Artificial Intelligence Association.\nMar 2022\n1 paper accepted at WWW 2022\nSep 2021\nMin-hwan has been selected as a Creative-Pioneering Researcher at SNU.\nMay 2021\n1 paper accepted at\nICML\n2021\nJan 2021\n1 paper accepted at\nAAAI\n2021\nNov 2020\nMin-hwan's Ph.D. thesis received a finalist recognition for\nGeorge B. Dantzig Dissertation Award\n.\nSee more"
