  "serper::Ariel Ortiz-Bobea": {
    "homepage": "https://arielortizbobea.github.io/",
    "emails": [
      "ao332@cornell.edu"
    ],
    "github": "https://github.com/arielortizbobea",
    "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ariel-ortiz-bobea-a904637/ ",
    "homepage_text": "Ariel Ortiz-Bobea\nhome\n450B warren |\nao332@cornell.edu\n| 607.255.0220\ngoogle scholar\n|\ngithub\n|\nbluesky\n|\ntwitter\n|\nlinkedin\nI'm an Associate Professor of Applied Economics and Policy at Cornell University with appointments in the\nCharles H. Dyson School of Applied Economics and Management\nand the\nJeb E. Brooks School of Public Policy\n. I'm also Faculty Fellow at the\nCornell Atkinson Center for Sustainability\nand serve on the\nCornell Research Integrity Council\n.\nI'm broadly interested in how people cope and adapt to environmental change. The core of my research program focuses on fundamental agricultural sustainability issues, particularly related to climate change and natural resources. I also work on non-agricultural topics often when working with students. I often collaborate with non-economists across and beyond our campus.\nI have editorial responsabilities at various academic journals including the\nJournal of the Association of Environmental and Resource Economists\n,\nClimatic Change\n,\nEnvironmental Research: Food Systems\nand the\nJournal of Wine Economics\n.\nI served on the author team for the Sixth National Climate Assessment (NCA6) until the team was disbanded in April 2025."
  },
